1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Vincent-Cento/6000000218565580891, fruit dealer in Quincy, Illinois, was the husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Victoria-Cento/6000000218563202821?through=6000000218565580891, sister of https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/people/Salvatore-Giovanni-Gaetano-Riggitano-John-R-Prevost/6000000218366187822?through=6000000218563202821.  He was interviewed by reporters for the ''Quincy Daily Herald'', published in two parts on  19 March 1917:  ([ht
2 CONC tps://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000218628585878&graph_node_id=profile-34843006110&mode=tagged “Riggitano in Triangle.”]). Cento claimed that he and Riggitano knew the Fontaine family when they came to Italy during the
2 CONC  Pan-European War around 1896-97. When [https://www.geni.com/people/Suzanne-Prevost/6000000218366242821 Suzanne] Immigrated to the US she sought out Riggitano in Chicago. Riggitano brought Suzanne to Quincy for a week for a visit,
2 CONC  but was cut short when a detective showed up with an arrest warrant for Suzanne and Riggitano.  It is not currently (May 2025) known which, if any, of her details Cento described were true.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The “Suzana Fountan” and “Giovanni Riggitano” (later known as John R. Prevost) of the article became the grandparents of [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Leo-XIV/6000000218365400850?through=6000000218365690853 Robert Francis Prev
2 CONC ort], elected pope on 8 May 2025.
2 CONT ----
