1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mildred Agnes Martinez''', the youngest of the seven daughters of Joseph N. Martinez and his wife Louise Baquie, was born 30 December 1911 in Chicago.  She was baptized 4 February 1912 at the Holy Name Cathedral, and died on 18
2 CONC  June 1990 of cancer.  She was buried in the Assumption Catholic Cemetery and Mausoleum in Glenwood next to her husband.  She who was also deeply involved in Catholic parish life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mildred Martinez Prevost was the mother of Robert Prevost, elected the Catholic Pope on 8 May 2025, and who took the name [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Leo_XIV Pope Leo XIV].
2 CONT
2 CONT Mildred was known as "Millie".  Her parents were [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_Creole_people Louisiana Creoles] from the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7th_Ward_of_New_Orleans 7th ward of New Orleans] who had moved to C
2 CONC hicago around 1911.  Her father, the mixed-race Joseph Martínez (1864-1926) was born in Hispianola;  Joseph’s mother, Maria Ramos, was from Cuba.  Mildred’s mother was New Orleans-born mixed-race Louise Baquié (1868-1945) (also re
2 CONC ndered Baquiex).
2 CONT
2 CONT Millie grew up in Chicago with five sisters, two of whom became nuns, and graduated from all-girls [https://media.geni.com/p14/46/df/39/27/53444868cbdc52f2/1929_-_immaculata_high_school_graduation__original.png?hash=6da270a1ae855a
2 CONC 06bbe0b5f65d40e10ad29f3b521fdae14fb77299a28636ba09.1747205999 Immaculata High School] in 1929.  She graduated from DePaul University with a bachelor’s in education in 1947, and attended the same masters of education program at DeP
2 CONC aul University  as [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-Prevost/6000000218365690853?through=6000000218365739839 Louis Prevost] (1920-1997).  They married on 25 January 1949 in Cook County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She had waited until she was in her mid-30s before marrying the educator, who was eight years her junior. So she was in her late 30s and early 40s when she had children, three boys born in a span of just over four years.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Louis Martin Prevost
2 CONT # John Joseph Prevost
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Leo-XIV/6000000218365400850?through=6000000218365739839 Robert Francis Prevost], born 14 September 1955 at Mercy Hospital in Chicago, an Augustinian priest who became Pope Leo XIV on 8 May 2025;
2 CONC  the first Pope born in the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Prevosts raised their family in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolton,_Illinois Dolton, Illinois], a suburb bordering Chicago's far South Side. The boys attended school at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Mary_of_the_Assum
2 CONC ption_Church_(Chicago)  St. Mary of the Assumption Parish].  It was located in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverdale,_Chicago Riverdale] neighborhood of South Side Chicago and is now closed.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the librarian at Von Stuben and Mendel Catholic High Schools in the Chicago area. President of the St. Mary of the Assumption Church's Altar & Rosary Society and the Mendel Catholic High School Mothers Club. Member of the 
2 CONC St. Mary's Choir.  She loved to sing.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT “PREVOST Mildred Prevost, nee Martinez, beloved wife of Louis M. Prevost, retired Superintendent of School District #167 &amp; Mount Carmel School, Chicago Heights; loving mother of Louis Martin, John J. and Rev. Robert Prevost, O
2 CONC SA; dear grandmother of … ; fond sister of Sister Mary Sulpice, RSM. Funeral Thursday 11:00 a.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: United States, Illinois, Chicago Chicago Tribune 1990-Jun-20 Page 70
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' In 1950, newly married https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-Prevost/6000000218365690853 and  https://www.geni.com/people/Mildred-Prevost/6000000218365739839 were living at 212 East 141st Place, Dolton, Illinois. Their cen
2 CONC sus record shows a foster son, Raymond Fuller, aged 15.  He was probably this https://www.geni.com/people/Raymond-Fuller-Sr/6000000218648273840, but confirmation and further details are sought.  See [https://www.geni.com/discussio
2 CONC ns/298917?msg=1769392 discussion].
2 CONT
