2 CONC eferred to as "Hayti" outside of the country, as the western side of Hispaniola had been occupied by the Haiti between 1822 and 1844.” (Comment at [https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/collaborate/L5J2-C9G FamilySearch].)
