1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Louise Baquié''', daughter of Ferdinand David Baquié and Eugenie Granbois, was born 4 February 1868 in New Orleans, Louisiana, and died 17 November 1945 in Chicago, Illinois. She was buried on 21 November 1945 in the All Saints
2 CONC  Catholic Cemetery and Mausoleum, Des Plaines, Cook, Illinois, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise married Joseph N. Martinez (1864-1926) at Our Lady of Sacred Heart in New Orleans on 17 September 1887. Their children Irma, Marguerite, Lydia, Louise, Hilda, and Ethel were born in New Orleans. The family moved from New Or
2 CONC leans to Chicago about 1911, and their daughter Mildred was born there on 30 December 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''Chicago Tribune'', November 19, 1945, Page 24. < [https://www.newspapers.com/article/chicago-tribune-louise-martinez/171979247/ via Newspapers.com] > Accessed May 8, 2025: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >MARTINEZ-Louise Martinez, wife of the late Joseph N. mother of Sister Mary Sulpice, R. S. M., late Sister Mary Amarita, BVM Marguerite Shinnick. Lydia Plum, Irma Meyers and Mildred Martinez. Funeral from home for funerals. Erie a
2 CONC nd Wabash, Wednesday. Nov. 21. at 9:30 a. m.. to Holy Name becathedral. Interment All Saints' cemetery.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Martinez and Louise Baquié were married at Our Lady of the Sacred Heart in New Orleans; 1872 building at Annette & N. Claiborne.  Undated photo.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000218536038838&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: Uncredited for the Archdiocese of New Orleans via  < [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Our_Lady_of_the_Sacred_Heart_Church_New_Orleans_1872_Building.jpg?uselang=en#Licensing Wikimedia Commons] >. Public domain.
2 CONT
