0 @I6000000218368560821@ INDI
1 NAME Jacques /Martinez/
2 GIVN Jacques
2 SURN Martinez
2 NICK Martines
2 NICK James
2 NICK Jacques Manuel Theodore Martinez
2 NICK Martines
2 NICK Martiner
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 FEB 1823
2 PLAC New Orleans, Orleans, Louisiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 FEB 1891
2 PLAC New Orleans, Orleans, Louisiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 OCCU tailor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Martinez was born about 1822 in  New Orleans, Louisiana, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques married Marie Rose Ramos (born about September 24, 1826 in New Orleans, Orleans; daughter of George Pantaleon Ramos and Julienne Montreuil) on 14 Jul 1848 in New Orleans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children included Joseph Narvale Martinez (1864–1926).  It appears Joseph was born in “Hayti” (Hispaniola)  with a birth registered in New Orleans, where he was living with his family in 1870.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, Jacques was living in New Orleans Ward 7, Orleans, Louisiana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques died on February 23, 1891 in Orleans, aged 68.  His death record lists both his own parents as Cuban-born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph Martinez 
2 CONT # 	Marie Martinez
2 CONT # Nisida Martinez
2 CONT # Chéne Martinez
2 CONT # James Martinez
2 CONT # Michael Martinez
2 CONT # Gerard Martinez
2 CONT # Joseph Norval Martinez
2 CONT # Adele Martinez
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Census reports
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1840, he lived in New Orleans Ward 1 with his family and two enslaved persons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Venus, slave of Mr Jacques Martinez was incarcerated in 1848 for being a runaway and not having a pass.[3]In 1850, Jacques owned a 26 year old female slave, possibly Venus (Unknown) Martinez (abt.1824-aft.1850)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1850 census Jacques, tailor, was in New Orleans Ward 1, Orleans, Louisiana, United States. He was described as a Mulatto.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family can be found in the 1870 U.S. census in New Orleans with their children, including Michel Martinez and Joseph Norval Martinez (Pope Leo XIV’s maternal grandfather). In the record, Jacques’s occupation is tailor and the 
2 CONC family is identified as “mulatto.”
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000218518418852&size=large}}
2 CONT > Image: 1870 U.S. census / MyHeritage
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1880 census Joegue (age 58), tailor, was the married head of household in New Orleans, Orleans, Louisiana, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
