2 CONC e it Remembered, That on this day , to wit: the Twenty Fourth of February in the year of our Lord One Thousand Eight Hundred and ninety one and the One Hundred and fifteenth of the Independence of the United States of America,  be
2 CONC fore me, S. R. OLLIPHANT , M. D., President Board of Health and Ex - Officio Recorder of Births , Deaths and Marriages in and for the Parish of Orleans , personally appeared Ernest M. Rougan, a native of this city residing at No 5
2 CONC 9 New St Bernard St. who hereby declares that '''Jacques Martinez''' a native of this city, aged 68 years & 9 days, departed this life Yesterday (25 Feb. 1891) at New St Bernard Near Celestine Street in this city.  Cause of Death:
2 CONC  Abscess of  liver. Certificate of Death: Dr J. Tricke. Deceased was married,  a tailor by occupation.  Birth place of parents: Cuba.  This done at New Orleans. in the presence of the aforesaid E. M. Rougan, as also in that of Mes
2 CONC srs H Lanigan, both of this City witnesses, by me requested so to be , who have hereunto set their hands , together with me , after reading hereof , this day , month and year first above written. E. R. Oliphant MD President,  Boar
2 CONC d of Health and Ex-Officio Recorder.  Ernest W. Rouzan.
