2 CONC  09 Sep 1864. Spouse's Mother's Name	Odile Copele  
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/LRZG-LBM "Eugenie Parentage. I think it very likely that Eugene Grambois is Eugenie's father. Her mother, Odile Copele, lived at 127 Esplanade in 1861 -- seen in the New Orlean
2 CONC s Director. At 121 Esplanade is Eugene Grambois office - an apothecary / doctor. Odile named her daughter very literally to make it clear who her birth father was."
2 CONT * Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/282457159/eug%C3%A9nie-baqui%C3%A9: accessed May 12, 2025), memorial page for Eugénie Grambois Baquié (1838–8 Jul 1907), Find a Grave Memorial ID 282457159; 
2 CONC Burial Details Unknown; Maintained by us_airforcewife (contributor 48584417).
2 CONT * “Family of Pope Leo XIV” < [https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Family_of_Pope_Leo_XIV&oldid=1290731780 ''Wikipedia''] > revision of 16 May 2025; accessed 16 May 2025. “Ferdinand David Baquie, [https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Pope-Leo-XIV/6000000218365400850 Leo XIV's] great-grandfather, was born in New Orleans on October 10, 1837.[29] He married Eugenie Grambois on September 19, 1864.[30] Ferdinand's mother and Leo XIV's great-great-grandmother was C
2 CONC eleste Lemelle. Celeste was the daughter of Louis Lemelle and Celeste Olimpie Grandpres, who were married in Opelousas, Louisiana, in 1798. Louis and Celesete were classified as quadroons, meaning they were either one-fourth Afric
2 CONC an or Native American ancestry.[29]”
