2 CONT # “Family of Pope Leo XIV” < [https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Family_of_Pope_Leo_XIV&oldid=1290731780 ''Wikipedia''] > revision of 16 May 2025; accessed 16 May 2025. “Ferdinand David Baquie, [https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Pope-Leo-XIV/6000000218365400850 Leo XIV's] great-grandfather, was born in New Orleans on October 10, 1837.[29] He married Eugenie Grambois on September 19, 1864.[30] Ferdinand's mother and Leo XIV's great-great-grandmother was C
2 CONC eleste Lemelle. Celeste was the daughter of Louis Lemelle and Celeste Olimpie Grandpres, who were married in Opelousas, Louisiana, in 1798. Louis and Celesete were classified as quadroons, meaning they were either one-fourth Afric
2 CONC an or Native American ancestry.[29]”
