1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Death certificate for https://www.geni.com/people/Jacques-Martinez/6000000218368560821?through=6000000218368957860 (1823-1891) lists his parents as born in Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marguerite Cadenette''' is likely Jacques Martinez's mother. She is present in the 1850 and 1860 censuses with him. In addition, he declares her death. Furthermore, in the 1870 census, we find a Marguerite Martinez, who died in
2 CONC  April 1870 from "Chronic Diarrhea." She was born in Cuba according to the 1870 census, and according to Jacques Martinez's death certificate, her parents were born in Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT It's likely that her son Jacques was the son of the Jacques Martinez born in New Orleans in June 1789, son of Jacques and Françoise Panquinette. https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/L58X-FV4
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a Marie Joseph Fenelise who died in NOLA 1834, daughter of Joseph Lazare and Margueritte Mimi Cadenet. In the 1850 and 1860 census she is listed in the household of Jacques Martinez, and in that same household is a Joseph
2 CONC ine/Mary Lazarde or Lazares.
2 CONT < [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSPG-9CW3?view=fullText&keywords=Marie+Joseph+Fenelise&lang=en link] >
2 CONT
2 CONT Native of Cuba or New Orleans?
2 CONT
2 CONT Records that list Marguerite as native of New Orleans:
2 CONT - 1850 Census.
2 CONT - 1860 Census.
2 CONT - 1870 Death record
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “Pope Leo’s Maternal Roots”
2 CONT Posted by Sean Daly on May 22, 2025
2 CONT https://en.geneanet.org/genealogyblog/post/2025/05/pope-leos-maternal-roots
2 CONT
2 CONT Contrary to what his name might suggest, it is not certain that the MARTINEZ family is of Spanish origin. Indeed, a mystery surrounds Jacques MARTINEZ (1823-1891), husband of Maria Rosa RAMOS (1826-1904). His death certificate men
2 CONC tions parents from Cuba, but it is likely this refers to his wife’s family because his mother, Marguerite CADNET or CADENETTE, came from a family from New Orleans. His father, also called Jacques MARTINEZ, was at one point thought
2 CONC  to be an Italian named Jacques MARTINO (~1808-1852), but Antonio A. Herrera-Vaillant, honorary president of the Venezuelan Academy of Genealogy, has shown that the latter married and had other children [PDF]. It is more likely th
2 CONC at Jacques MARTINEZ senior was himself born in New Orleans, to Françoise Rosalie PANQUINETTE and a father whose original name was… Jacob MARTINE. Having become Santiago MARTIN and then MARTINEZ, his name was Hispanicized, like tho
2 CONC se of many people during the period of Spanish domination of Louisiana (1763-1803).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Comments'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo formerly attached to profile could have been Agathe Solilele LEMELLE and Henry Alexandre PARLONGUE.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # "United States, Census, 1850", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MCJZ-TFX : Fri Jan 17 01:32:13 UTC 2025), Entry for Jacques Martines (son of) Margeritta Cadenett, 1850.
2 CONT # "United States, Census, 1860", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MFP8-WDG : Sun May 11 01:56:37 UTC 2025), Entry for J Martinez and Mary Martinez, 1860. Marguerite Martinez.  Also in household: Marguerite
2 CONC  Martinez, age 52, birth year estimated 1808 in  New Orleans.  White.  
2 CONT #"United States Census (Mortality Schedule), 1850-1880", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6PF7-TLMG : Tue Apr 22 18:11:29 UTC 2025), Entry for Margth Martinez, Apr 1870.
2 CONT # "Louisiana, Orleans, Death Records and Certificates, 1835-1954", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:CGX7-6WPZ : Thu Mar 07 23:34:00 UTC 2024), Entry for Mrs Margurit Cadnet, 20 Apr 1870.
2 CONT # "Louisiana, State Museum Historical Center, Cemetery Records, 1805-1944", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CS4L-241T?cc=4234528 : 23 May 2025),  > image 1 of 1. The original record has Jacques
2 CONC  Martinez listed as declaring the death. This is the correct Marguerite.
2 CONT #Avoyelles Today.  “The new pope’s Louisiana roots,” (Thu, 05/08/2025) < [https://www.avoyellestoday.com/news/new-popes-louisiana-roots link] > Jacques Martino (1806-1852), 2nd great-grandfather of the Pope, was a native of San Re
2 CONC mo, Genova, Italy [sic: disproved] who migrated to New Orleans where he died. His wife Martuerite Cadeneth who was a native of East Feliciana Parish, Louisiana.
2 CONT # Ortiz, Ana María.  (9 May 2025). ''El Mundo''.  “Martínez, Ramos y Bastos, los 10 antepasados del Papa con apellido español hasta su origen en Cuba.”  < [https://www.elmundo.es/espana/2025/05/09/681e4093fc6c8334478b45b5.html lin
2 CONC k] > Accessed 20 May 2025.
2 CONT # González, Mirelis Peraza.  (16 May 2025).  ''Cuban Genealogy Club of Miami, Fl, Inc''. “Cuban Ancestry of Pope Leo XIV.” < [https://www.cubangenclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/POPE-LEO-XIV-FINAL-REPORT.pdf PDF] > Accessed 20
2 CONC  May 2025
2 CONT # “Pope Leo’s Maternal Roots.” ''Geneanet.org/blog''. Posted by Sean Daly on May 22, 2025.  < [https://en.geneanet.org/genealogyblog/post/2025/05/pope-leos-maternal-roots link] > Accessed 24 May 2025.
2 CONT #”RAÍCES CUBANAS DE SU SANTIDAD, EL PAPA LEÓN XIV” Por Antonio A. Herrera-Vaillant1 Académico Correspondiente. ''REAL ACADEMIA MATRITENSE DE HERÁLDICA Y GENEALOGÍA.'' (Madrid, 2025) < [https://ramhg.es/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/2
2 CONC 50514_herrera_vaillant_raices_cubanas_santidad_papa_leon_xiv.pdf PDF] >. Accessed 24 May 2025.
2 CONT # https://gw.geneanet.org/gntstarxivleon?lang=en&pz=robert+francis&nz=prevost&p=marguerite&n=cadenette Il s'agit vraisemblablement de la mère de Jacques MARTINEZ. Elle est présente aux recensement de 1850 et 1860 avec lui. En outr
2 CONC e, il déclare son décès. En outre, au recensement de 1870, on retrouve bien une Marguerite MARTINEZ, décédée en avril 1870 d'une "Chronic Diarrhea". Elle est native de Cuba selon le recensement de 1870 et selon l'acte de décès de 
2 CONC Jacques MARTINEZ, ses parents sont nés à Cuba.
2 CONT # https://gw.geneanet.org/lecentredegenealogie
