1 NAME Eugène /Grambois/
2 GIVN Eugène
2 _MARNM Grambois
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1815
2 ADDR
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY New Orleans
3 STAE Louisiana
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU druggist
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Eugene Grambois [not Granbois] was born on 6 September 1806 in Carcés, Var, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur in France, a son of Jean Joseph Augustin Grambois and Marie Theres (Paul) Grambois. [1] In the 1850 Census, he is described as 
2 CONC White[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Eugene owned an Apothecary on the corner of Esplanade and Craps (Burgundy) Streets in New Orleans. [3] As an "apothecary," his address in 1867 was 121 Esplanade Street.[4] His occupation was given as "druggist," -- these Apothecar
2 CONC ies were the pharmacies of their day. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “We published the Grambois tree in France after confirmation of the name of Eugene Grambois appearing on the mariage record of Eugenie. The record was disclosed by the archives of the diocese of New Orleans (records are not availa
2 CONC ble online after 1815). This was the piece we needed to confirm our hypothesis. This hypothesis was based on the singularity of the surname Grambois in New Orleans at the time (as per the directories available) and its proximity t
2 CONC o the only other person bearing it: the apothecary and drugstore owner Eugene Grambois. Confirmed by the donation Eugene made to Odile Coppel in 1843. We just needed the baptism and mariage act to be 100% sure.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *"United States, Census, 1840", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XHTD-GYF : Sun Mar 10 09:38:31 UTC 2024), Entry for Eugene Grandbois, 1840.
2 CONT *Eugene Grambois donation to Odile Coppel 1843; New Orleans, Orleans, Louisiana, United States [https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/memories/GW8M-2TF jpg] 
2 CONT *"United States, Census, 1850", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MCJZ-69M : Tue Jan 14 20:01:18 UTC 2025), Entry for E Grambois and Monier, 1850.
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/LRZG-LBM "Eugenie Parentage. I think it very likely that Eugene Grambois is Eugenie's father. Her mother, Odile Copele, lived at 127 Esplanade in 1861 -- seen in the New Orlean
2 CONC s Director. At 121 Esplanade is Eugene Grambois office - an apothecary / doctor. Odile named her daughter very literally to make it clear who her birth father was."
2 CONT * "United States City and Business Directories, ca. 1749 - ca. 1990", FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:68DD-Z4XH : Sat Mar 09 23:01:44 UTC 2024), Entry for Eugene Grambois, 1861. "Grambois Eugene, Burgundy
2 CONC  Esplaade"
2 CONT *https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/GT8S-SDZ
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Granbois-8
