1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Odile is Louise Bacquie’s grandmother, and Eugenie Grambois’s mother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is a free woman of color who lived in New Orleans — first record that appears is Eugenie’s baptism in 1838. It was not uncommon for fpc to “own slaves,” but some of them were family members. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Was Odile born into slavery? - there is record of an Odile/Adele who was born a slave, the right age as our Odile. Her mother, Manette, was involved in a whole family court case, and the last I have found her is being purchased by
2 CONC  Adolph Ducros in 1820.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
