1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find A Grave:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Thereze Rancurel Baquie should not be mistaken for Marie Therese Corine Baquie, daughter of Catherine Elisabeth Mathilde Baquie and Joseph Aristide Baquie. Marie Therese Corine Baquie was born in New Orleans on August 28, 18
2 CONC 40 in New Orleans, Louisiana. According to Marie Thereze Baquie's obituary, which matches the inscription on the tombstone, she died at the age of 83 on August 11, 1857. This puts her date of birth circa 1774. She also could not h
2 CONC ave possibly been the wife of William Conrad Reinhard Quenttell who married Marie Therese Corine Baquie as they were married on February 6, 1860 at which point the Marie Thereze Rancuel Baquie was already deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is NOT the wife or placee of Jean Rose Joseph Baquie who was born circa 1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT A document provided to me by a genealogy contributor from France shows that her two children were born from her union with Jean Pierre Baquie. The two sons were born:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Aristide Joseph Fleury Baquie, who also went by the name Joseph Aristide Fleury. 
2 CONT # The second son was Augustus Baquie.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY From Courrier de la Louisiane - Aug 11, 1857
2 CONT
2 CONT Last night at 12 o'clock, at the age of 83 years, Mrs. Thereza Baquie, mother of Augustus and Joseph Aristide Baquie. The friends and acuaintances of her sons and of the family are requested to attend, without further notice, her 
2 CONC funeral, which will take place this afternoon at 4 1/2 o'clock from Villere Street near Esplanade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomb reads, Marie Therese Baquie
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Thereze Rancurel married Henry Bontemps in 1794 in Marseille, France. It was after the loss of her husband that a union between her and Jean Pierre Baquie produced her two sons August and Aristide Baquie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her baptism record in Marseilles, Saint-Martin parish
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archives13.fr/ark:/40700/vta48123918eb05129f/daogrp/0/118
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfather Firmain RANCUREL, trader
2 CONT Godmother Therese VERNIN (signature Marie Therese VERNIN
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://www.rfgenealogie.com/infos/les-racines-francaises-du-nouveau-pape-leon-xiv
2 CONT
2 CONT Les racines françaises du nouveau pape Léon XIV
2 CONT
2 CONT Google translate 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Finally, on the BACQUIÉ side, we come to Guadeloupe, where the great-great-grandfather, Aristide, was born in Pointe-à-Pitre in 1811, the son of an apparently unmarried couple: he, Jean-Pierre BACQUIÉ, Béarnais, born in Monein, s
2 CONC on of a local bourgeois (Jean-Baptiste, husband of Marguerite (de) GANOSSE, daughter of a GANOSSE/MAUBOURGUET couple, whose ancestors are known) and she, Marie-Thérèse RANCUREL, daughter of a Marseille bourgeois, son of a Antoine/
2 CONC Marguerite HANCY couple. He, son of Antoine and Marie Madeleine GIRAUD; she, sister of a churchwarden, daughter of Ignace César HANCY, Italian musician born in Modena, and of Marie-Thérèse CRAVEZAN, with a beautiful family tree, p
2 CONC ut online by Thierry Musset, giving ancestors in Monaco and Menton (GROSSO, notables, known from the 13th century).
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
