1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Marie Cathalina Guesnon    
2 CONT * Gender:	Female  
2 CONT * Birth:	October 26, 1756 
2 CONT * New Orleans, Orleans Parish, Louisiana, United States  
2 CONT * Death:	August 14, 1799 (42) New Orleans, Orleans Parish, Louisiana, United States (Childbirth of a baby boy who also passed away)
2 CONT Parents:	
2 CONT * Pierre Guesnon
2 CONT * Andrea Perinne Guesnon (born D'Auville)
2 CONT Spouses:
2 CONT # 	D. Manuel José de Ramos y Tadino
2 CONT # D. Juan Ventura de Morales Hidalgo y Perez de Merida
2 CONT Children:	
2 CONT
2 CONT # Rosa Lynd (born Ramos Guesnon)
2 CONT # D. Pedro Carlos Ramos Guesnon
2 CONT # Vicente Ignacio Santiago de Ramos y Geusnon
2 CONT # Ana Mathilde Martina Phillipe de Marigny de Mandeville (born Morales y Guesnon)
2 CONT # Francisco Morales Gesnon
2 CONT # unknown name de Morales Guesnon
2 CONT
2 CONT GUESNON [@GUENON, GUENONT]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (Pierre, royal master gunner, and Andre Perinne DOVILE), b. Oct. 27, 1756, s. Pierre GUENON and Marie CHAUVIN (SLC, B3, 65)
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sponsers/Godparents: brother Pierre and maternal aunt Marie Jeanne DOUVILLE (var) CHAUVIN<
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT GUESNON
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Catalina (Pedro and Andrea Petronila D’AUVILLE) native of this city, 39 yr. widow of Manuel Jose RAMOS, sp. Juan Ventura MORALES, proprietary accountant for the army and royal household, presently interim intendant of the pr
2 CONC ovince, i. Aug. 14, 1799, d. during childbirth with a premature male infant who was b. simply and buried with his mother (SLC, F4, 70)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT We have to go up one more branch on the family tree, to Marie Rosa Ramos's great-grandfather—six generations behind the Pope—to find the ancestor who emigrated to New Orleans. This is Manuel José Ramos , who, like the Martínez/Mar
2 CONC tino branch, did so from Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Havana in 1760, he was already living in the United States by the age of 18, having married Marie Catherine there. Manuel José's life was very short, dying in 1789 at the age of 29. According to records, he was the only so
2 CONC n of Vicente Ignacio Ramos and María Bastos . Their birth dates are around 1730 in what was then Spanish Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Ortiz, Ana María.  (9 May 2025). ''El Mundo''.  “Martínez, Ramos y Bastos, los 10 antepasados del Papa con apellido español hasta su origen en Cuba.”  < [https://www.elmundo.es/espana/2025/05/09/681e4093fc6c8334478b45b5.html lin
2 CONC k] > Accessed 20 May 2025.
2 CONT # González, Mirelis Peraza.  (16 May 2025).  ''Cuban Genealogy Club of Miami, Fl, Inc''. “Cuban Ancestry of Pope Leo XIV.” < [https://www.cubangenclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/POPE-LEO-XIV-FINAL-REPORT.pdf PDF] > Accessed 20
2 CONC  May 2025
2 CONT # Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-593481892/marie-catherine-guesnon-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 18 2022, 18:
2 CONC 44:44 UTC''
