1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ramos-1785
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Jose Ramos was born in 1760 in La Havane, La Habana, Cuba, son of Vicente Ignacio Ramos (1730– ) and Maria Bastos (~1708– ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel (17) married Marie Catherine Guesnon (21) (born on October 26, 1756 in New Orleans, Louisiana, New France; daughter of Pierre Guesnon and Andrea Perrine Dauville) on April 25, 1778 in New Orleans, Louisiana, New Spain.[1] T
2 CONC heir son was Vincent Ignace Jacques Ramos (1786–1842).
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel died in 1789 in La Nouvelle Orléans, Louisiane, Louisiana, aged 29.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT We have to go up one more branch on the family tree, to Marie Rosa Ramos's great-grandfather—six generations behind the Pope—to find the ancestor who emigrated to New Orleans. This is Manuel José Ramos , who, like the Martínez/Mar
2 CONC tino branch, did so from Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Havana in 1760, he was already living in the United States by the age of 18, having married Marie Catherine there. Manuel José's life was very short, dying in 1789 at the age of 29. According to records, he was the only so
2 CONC n of Vicente Ignacio Ramos and María Bastos . Their birth dates are around 1730 in what was then Spanish Cuba.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
