1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Dalakov, Georgi.  “William Quentell” < [http://www.computer-timeline.com/timeline/william-quentell/ link] > Accessed 19 May 2025
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm Quentell was born in Bremen, Germany, on 1 March 1823, and came to America in the 1830s together with his family—father: Wilhelm (1784-1840), mother: Anna Luise Wilhelmine Conradine (1794–1880), and brothers: Friedrich The
2 CONC odore (1828-1848), and Franz Carl (1830-1858).
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm and Marie Therese married on 6 February 1860 (Marie Therese was the widow of his brother, Franz Carl, who died on 23 Oct. 1858, and had one daughter, Marie Louise Wilhelmina (1857-1929), from his first marriage).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT QUENTELL
2 CONT On Friday, 12th January, at 3:30 o'clock P. M., WILLIAM CONRAD REINHARD QUENTELL, aged 54 years, a native of Bremen, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT His friends and acquaintances and those of the Baquie family, are respectfully invited to attend the funeral, which will take place from his late residence, 59 Chestnut street, corner of Josephine, This Afternoon, at 3 o'clock.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Daily Picayune
2 CONT New Orleans, Louisiana
2 CONT Saturday, January 13, 1877
2 CONT Page: 4
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Refs
2 CONT
