1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Dalakov, Georgi.  “William Quentell” < [http://www.computer-timeline.com/timeline/william-quentell/ link] > Accessed 19 May 2025
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Prehn Quentell''' (1861-1932) was a prolific inventor, a holder of at least 33 US patents (as well as many patents in Canada, Germany, France, and Great Britain), stretching over more than 40 years (the last was granted
2 CONC  in 1931, the year before he died). His first patent (and most of the others) was for a typewriter, but Quentell was also a holder of many patents for calculating machines.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Prehn Quentell was born in New Orleans on 8 January 1861, the first son of William (born Wilhelm) Reinhard Conrad Quentell and his wife, Marie Therese Corine Baquie Quentell (born 28 Aug. 1840 in New Orleans-died 1868).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 Feb. 1892, William Prehn married in Independence, Jackson County, Missouri, to Agness Roberts (b. 27 Apr. 1863 in Missouri-d. 17 Sep. 1949). They had two daughters, born in New York: Olga Marie (3 May 1900-30 Oct. 1953), and 
2 CONC Gladys Agnes (7 Aug. 1901-8 Feb. 1966).
2 CONT
2 CONT The remarkable inventor and businessman William Prehn Quentell died at Mineral Springs, Moore County, North Carolina, on 23 January 1932, two weeks after his 71st birthday. He was buried in Saint Louis Cemetery, New Orleans.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
