1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Antoine Rancurel''', son of Antoine Rancurel and Madeleine Marie Giraud, was born in 1727[1].  His parents married 20 Nov 1713 in Lançon-Provence, Bouches-du-Rhône, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine died in 1788 in Marseilles.[3]. He was buried in Saint-Martin parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Rancurel and Marguerite Hancy were married on February 1, 1770 in Marseille.[2] at the Notre-Dame des Accoules parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children included:
2 CONT # Marie Thérèse Rancurel Born 14 May 1776 in Marseille.  “She is 18 years old, daughter of the late Antoine RANCUREL and Marguerite HENCY. Henry BONTEMS is a merchant. He is 47 years old and a widower (former wife Marie LAUGIER).”
2 CONC  Her baptism was recorded  in Marseilles, Saint-Martin parish, Godfather Firmain RANCUREL, trader.  Godmother Therese VERNIN (signature Marie Therese VERNIN. < [http://www.archives13.fr/ark:/40700/vta48123918eb05129f/daogrp/0/118 
2 CONC link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine RANCUREL
2 CONT France, Vital Records Index
2 CONT Record type:	Death
2 CONT Birth:	Circa 1728
2 CONT Death:	Sep 5 1788 - Marseille, Bouches-du-Rhône, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France
2 CONT Wife:	Marguerite HENCHY
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Antoine Rancurel (1727-1788)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rancurel-2 : accessed 20 May 2025).
