1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT and in the Lemelle line there is almost an implex  between the 2 brothers Francois et Jacques et François son frère.
2 CONT Jacques LEMELLE fathered Marie Jeanne to Jacqueline. 
2 CONT And Marie Jeanne LEMELLE aka Tonton /aka Marie Jeanne DAVION had children with Francois, the brother of Jacques LEMELLE
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Individual Note===
2 CONT Occupation: Lieutenant, French Militia ; Master Baker Source: Book - Arch. of New Orleans Sacr. Rec. - V1, 1718-1750 - [book] - Woods, Earl, ed. p123 [Master baker] Witness: Marriage of Jacques L’Archeveque & Marie Philipaux. Jan 
2 CONC 29, 1760. Witness: Baptism of Félicité Marie Braud. May 15, 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT Index to French and Spanish Trans. of Orig. Doc., Louisiana Museum Lib., NOLA, Dec 25, 1744. Mar Cntr, Guillaume Vincent and Charlotte Labbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. LA. Mar Cntr, v. V, Mar Cntr of Attakapas Post, 1760-1803, p 19, no 59, OA, Book 9, No 29A.
2 CONT
2 CONT Le Poste les Opelousas by Gladys deVillier. LC 72-78170.
2 CONT
2 CONT LA Mar Cntr, 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Lemelle tranfers power of attorney to his brother François Lemelle, Dec 5, 1765. Source: - Periodical - Genesis - [serial] - New Orleans, LA - Book - Arch. of New Orleans Sacr. Rec. - V2, 1751-1771 - [book] - Woods, Earl, 
2 CONC ed. (P170,P33)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Slaveowner--31 July 1788 slave Eleanor freed, who had belonged to his mom 1st, and her children Victoire and Alexander freed
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT François Lemelle married Charlotte Christine Labbé, a daughter of Jean Labbé and Christine Allard, all of New Orleans–see François and Charlotte’s joint succession, dated 18 July 1789 in Opélousas: Louisiana State Archives and Rec
2 CONC ords (Bâton Rouge), Opelousas, 1789. See also another succession related to the community of François and Charlotte, both deceased, dated 14 December 1789, naming 3 legitimate children: Louisiana State University Archives, Opelous
2 CONC as, no. 15; and François’s last will and testament, dated 16 July 1789: Louisiana State University at Eunice, Opelousas, 1789.
2 CONT
