2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''Ursule Thibodeau''' was born 19 APR 1723 in Port Royal, Acadia. Shewas the daughter of [[Thibodeau-9|Pierre Thibodeau]] and [[Aucoin-6|Anne-Marie Aucoin]]. She was baptized the next day at Port Royal. Her godpare
2 CONC nts were Pierre L'Anou and Marie Brun.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 59) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/59?r=0&
2 CONC s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Ursule Thibaudault baptism RG 1 volume 26 page 190 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=941≤/ref>≤ref> Dic
2 CONC tionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes Title:  Stephen A. White, Dictionnaire Génalogique des Familles Acadiennes (2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes , 1999).  p. 1521≤/ref>
2 CONT She was married about 1745 in Acadia to Jean Savoie, widower of Marie Dupuis.≤ref>S Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes Title:  Stephen A. White, Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes (2 vols., Moncton, N
2 CONC ew Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes , 1999).  pp. 1458 & 1521≤/ref>   
2 CONT In at least 1752-1755 several siblings lived in Chipoudy: Marguerite, Olivier, Catherine Josephe and Ursule and Pierre together with their spouses.≤ref name=White>Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes - Dictionnaire Gé
2 CONC néalogique des Familles Acadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714 - Stephen A. White - 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick:Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999 - p. 1520-22≤/ref> 
2 CONT
