2 CONC mb I:42c-1 May 2, 1759  Three banns published.  Claude La Foret, sergeant in Bonnille's company, native of --ll-ry (Callery? Culsery?), bishopric of Chalons-sur-Saone, in the province of Bourgogne, son of Charles La Foret and Jean
2 CONC ne Marie Roy. '''Catherine Castel of the Cickachayay area1 of Louisiana, daughter of Pierre Castel and Maguerite Cecile Christophe'''. Witnesses signing: Castelle;2 Colomb;3 (Joseph) Bock, who married in 1760 (Mob. mb I:43); CL-f-
2 CONC a-(?);4 (Pierre Cajot dit) Faulevant or Fonlevant, spouse of Therese Christophe.
2 CONT ###On Danville's 1732 map, the "Tchikachaé, gros village" is shown above the Youanné village on the east bank of the Chickasawhay River, in Mississippi, due west of Choctaw County, Alabama. Early in 1739, Pierre Castel (and wife) 
2 CONC had contracted to trade with the Choctaw for two years. LHO, VI (1923), 302.
2 CONT ###This may be the bride's signature or that of someone in her family.
2 CONT ###Not identified. Probably one of the Collon-Finot sons, and a Colon-Praux grandson.
