2 CONT Marrige Contracts of French Colonial Louisiana 
2 CONT
2 CONT November 7, 1728 FRANCOIS LeMESLE called BELLEGARDE, native of Paris,Parish of St. Sulpice, son of the deceased FRANCOIS LeMESLE and of MARIE COQUELIN, and MARIE LOUISE MARIETTE, native of the City of Treve in Germany, daughter of
2 CONC  the deceased LOUIS MARIETTE, Surgeon Major of the Regiment of the Swiss, AND of MARGUERITTE ZERESSE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signing on the part of LeMESLE being Sieur BERANGER, Captain and Comander of the vessel LaBalein, Sieur CHAUANNES, Secretary of the Superior Council, his friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And for the Demoiselle MARIETTE, Hr. DELACHAISE, Commissioner for the King in this Colony, BUTELET and POMET also of the Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT A promise this marriage to be solemnized in the Holy Roman Catholic Church. Signed ROSSARD, Notary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note This marriage was solomnized in the St. Louis Parish Church on November 8, 1728, by F. Raphael, Capuchln priest, Vicar General.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
