2 CONT ===Individual Note===
2 CONT Occupation: Ship Captain (1768) ; Burgher, New Orleans (1759) Source: Book - Arch. of New Orleans Sacr. Rec. - V2, 1751-1771 - [book] - Woods, Earl, ed. p10 [burger of this city] ; p33 [ship captain] Witness: Marriage of Louis Bar
2 CONC beau Boisdoré & (Marie) Marguerite Doussin. Jan 15, 1759. Witness: Marriage of Jean Antoine Barbeau Boisdoré & Françoise Veillon. Mar 22, 1762. Witness: Baptism of Jacques Denis Braud. Apr 26, 1768.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Lemelle tranfers power of attorney to his brother François, Dec 5, 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard DeMarigny v. Victoire LeMelle, 1042, New Orleans City Court.
2 CONT
2 CONT > > *Louisiana Historical Quarterly
2 CONT > > Volume 29 – Issue 1
2 CONT > > January 1946*
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Agata (Agathe), Juana Francisca (Jeanne Françoise) and Maria Adelayda
2 CONT > > (Adelaide) Lemelle petition to be declared competent and authorized to
2 CONT > > administer their own affairs.*
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > No. 3052, 8 pp.
2 CONT > > Court of Alcalde - Nicolas Forstall
2 CONT > > Assessor - Juan del Postigo
2 CONT > > Escribano (Clerk of the Court) – Fernando Rodriquez
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *This procedure, brought for the emancipation of three minors, all free
2 CONT > > negresses, follows the procedure employed in similar cases brought for the
2 CONT > > emancipation of white minors. After the ages of the minors have been
2 CONT > > verified by the presentation of their baptismal certificates, and competent
2 CONT > > witnesses have testified to their ability to manage their property without
2 CONT > > the necessity of a curator, and to their good character, etc., the Court
2 CONT > > issues the decree of emancipation.*
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > The petitioners present their baptismal certificates which are as follows:
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > I, Father Antonio de Sedella, Capuchin monk, Vicar General of the Province
2 CONT > > of Louisiana and Parish Priest of the Church of St. Louis of New Orleans,
2 CONT > > certify in due form that in one of the Books of Baptisms in my charge, on
2 CONT > > page 23, there is an entry of the following tenor:
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Entry.*
2 CONT > > In the year one thousand seven hundred and seventy-one (1771), on the
2 CONT > > seventh of November, I, the undersigned have baptized, with the ordinary
2 CONT > > ceremonies of the Church, *Maria Adelaide*, born the eleventh of October
2 CONT > > of the present year, of Jacqueline, a mulatress slave of Mr. Lemelle; this
2 CONT > > child was declared free by Mr. Lemelle, her master, and of unknown father.
2 CONT > > The god-father was Mr. Carmuche, a merchant, and the god-mother was Miss
2 CONT > > Marie Braud, who signed with me on the day and year as above. (Signed)
2 CONT > > Father Dagobert; Marie Braud; Lemelle.
2 CONT > > This conforms to its original which remains in the books of this Parish,
2 CONT > > to which I refer, and to which I attest. New Orleans, on the twenty-sixth
2 CONT > > day of the month of July, of the year one thousand seven hundred and
2 CONT > > eight-five. (Signed) Fr. Antonio de Sedella. (Official Seal)
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Jeanne Francoise’s Baptismal Certificate.*
2 CONT > > I, Father Antonio de Sedella, Capuchin monk, Vicar General , ad interim,
2 CONT > > of the Province of Louisiana and Parish Priest of the Church of Saint Louis
2 CONT > > of New Orleans, certify in due form that in one of the Books of Baptisms,
2 CONT > > on page 58, there is an entry of the following tenor:
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Entry.*
2 CONT > > In the year one thousand seven hundred and sixty-nine (1769), on the
2 CONT > > seventh day of September, I, the undersigned, baptized, with the ordinary
2 CONT > > ceremonies of the Church, Jeanne Françoise, born the fourteenth day of the
2 CONT > > month of August of the present year of Jacqueline, a mulatress, a slave of
2 CONT > > Mr. Lemelle, the master, who has declared to me that he wishes the said
2 CONT > > Jeanne Françoise to be baptized as free. The god-father was Mr. Jean
2 CONT > > Baptiste Francois de Macarty, and the god-mother was Miss Jeanne Françoise
2 CONT > > de Macarty, who signed with me, the day and year as above. Father Dagobert,
2 CONT > > Parish Priest; Macarty; Le Bretton: Lemelle.
2 CONT > > This agrees with its original, which remains in the books of this Parish
2 CONT > > Church, to which I refer, and to which I attest. New Orleans, on July the
2 CONT > > twenty-sixth of the year one thousand seven hundred and eighty-five.
2 CONT > > (Signed) Father Antonio de Sedella. (Official Seal)
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Agata (Agathe) Lemelle’s Baptismal Certificate.*
2 CONT > > I, Father Antonio de Sedella, Capuchin monk, Vicar General, ad interim, of
2 CONT > > the Province of Louisiana and Parish Priest of the Parish Church of Saint
2 CONT > > Louis of New Orleans, certify in due form that in one of the Books of
2 CONT > > Baptisms of the said Parish Church in our charge there is an entry, on page
2 CONT > > 30, of the following tenor:
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Entry.*
2 CONT > > In the year one thousand seven hundred and sixty (1760), on the fifth day
2 CONT > > of May, we the undersigned Capuchin Priest, and Apostolic Missionary, have
2 CONT > > baptized with the ordinary ceremonies of the Church, Agathe, a mulatress,
2 CONT > > born yesterday of Jacqueline, a mulatress slave of Mr. Lemelle, Jr., and
2 CONT > > she had for her god-father, Charles Le Conte, a merchant of this city, and
2 CONT > > for her god-mother, Catherine Moreau, who have signed, and in faith of
2 CONT > > which I sign, the day, month and year, as above. This child has been
2 CONT > > declared free to us by Mr. Lemelle, the master of Jacqueline, his slave. I
2 CONT > > faith of which we have signed. Father Dagobert, Parish Priest: father
2 CONT > > Eustache, Capuchin: Lemelle: Charles Le Conte; Moreau Olivier.
2 CONT > > This agrees with its original that remains in the books of this Parish
2 CONT > > Church, to which I refer, and to which I attest. New Orleans, on July
2 CONT > > eighth of the year one thousand seven hundred and eighty-five. (Signed)
2 CONT > > Father Antonio de Sedella. (Official Seal.)
2 CONT > > *
2 CONT > > Agatha, Juana Francisca and Maria Adelayda Lemelle petition to present
2 CONT > > witnesses*.
2 CONT > > Agatha, Juana Francisca (Jean Françoise) and Maria Adelayda (Adelaide)
2 CONT > > Lemelle, free mulatress, less than twenty-five years of age, and more than
2 CONT > > fourteen, as their Baptismal Certificates duly presented, prove, set forth
2 CONT > > that it is convenient to them to present witnesses who will testify to
2 CONT > > their good conduct and that they are capable to work and make their own
2 CONT > > living and to increase the business they have entered, and done, deliver
2 CONT > > these depositions to them to use for their rights. Alcalde Forstall, on
2 CONT > > Assessor Postigo’s advice, rules: the Baptismal Certificates having been
2 CONT > > presented, let the testimony be received that these party’s offer. Entrust
2 CONT > > the taking of the depositions to the Escribano (Clerk), and done, deliver
2 CONT > > them to the petitioners.
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Declaration of the 1st witness.*
2 CONT > > In the city of New Orleans, on the day, month and year (July 29, 1785),
2 CONT > > Agatha, Adelaida and Juana Francisca Lemelle, for the testimony they have
2 CONT > > offered and have been ordered to give, presented as a witness Antonio
2 CONT > > Planchard, from whom the Escribano (Clerk), in virtue of the commission
2 CONT > > conferred upon him, received the oath, which he made by God, Our Lord, and
2 CONT > > a Sign of the Cross, according to law, under charge of which he promised to
2 CONT > > speak the truth, and when examined on the tenor of the foregoing written
2 CONT > > petition, he said that he knew the parties presenting him to be persons
2 CONT > > known for their good conduct, and capable to posses and administer their
2 CONT > > estate without the necessity of a curator , which is well known to the
2 CONT > > witness because he lives next to them. This is truth, under charge of his
2 CONT > > oath, he is 50 years of age, and he signed, to which the Escribano (Clerk)
2 CONT > > attests. (Signed) De Planchard.
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Declaration of the 2nd*
2 CONT > > Pedro Labatte (Labat), under oath, states that he is an immediate neighbor
2 CONT > > of the petitioners and knows them to be persons well known for their good
2 CONT > > conduct and capable to possess and manage their estate without a curator.
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > Agathe, Juana Francisca (Jean Françoise) and Maria Adelayda (Adelaide)
2 CONT > > Lemelle petition to be emancipated
2 CONT > > The three petitioners, free mulattresses, aver that as may be noted from
2 CONT > > the testimony of the witnesses have duly presented, they are capable of
2 CONT > > managing their own affairs, therefore they pray the Court, after examining
2 CONT > > the said testimony, to emancipate them and to concede to them sufficient
2 CONT > > authority to manage their own affairs. This petition is sighed Agathe
2 CONT > > Lemelle; Adelaide Lemelle; Jean Francoise Lemelle, Alcalde Forstall, on
2 CONT > > Assessor Postigo’s advice, receives this petition and later decrees.
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > *Decree.*
2 CONT > > In the city of New Orleans, on August 9, 1785, Nicolas Forstall, Regidor
2 CONT > > Perpetuo and Senior Alcalde Ordinario of this city and its jurisdiction for
2 CONT > > His Majesty, having examined these records, said that he must declare and
2 CONT > > does declare, as sufficient, the testimony given for Agueda (Agathe),
2 CONT > > Adelayde (Adelaide), and Juana Francisca (Jeanne Françoise) Lemelle, and
2 CONT > > orders that the aforenamed be emancipated, stating that they are able and
2 CONT > > capable to trade and make contracts that may be convenient to them. This is
2 CONT > > his decree, thus he has ordered, provided and signed. Fees 3 pesos,
2 CONT > > received. (Signed) Nicolas Forstall; Licenciado Postigo; before Fernando
2 CONT > > Rodriguez, Clerk of the Court.
2 CONT > > Source: - Note: (Oct 28, 2001 [http&|;&|;nujrias.org&|;~nopl&|;inv&|;citycourt&|;cC5.htm]) - Book - Arch. of New Orleans Sacr. Rec. - V2, 1751-1771 - [book] - Woods, Earl, ed. (P10,P9,P33) - Periodical - Genesis - [serial] - N
