1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antoine Jacques Philippe de Marigny de Mandeville (also known as Antoine James de Marigny and Mandeville DeMarigny) was the son of Bernard de Marigny de Mandeville and the son-in-law of William C. C. Claiborne, the
2 CONC  first governor of Louisiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended the Academy of St. Cyr in the 1830s before briefly serving in the French Army.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT During the American Civil War, he was a colonel in the 10th Louisiana Infantry Regiment (" French Brigade, French Legion") and served in Virginia.[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sophronia Louise Claiborne, daughter of the first Governor of Louisiana.[5]
