2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication and older brother also named Pierre. Please contact the Acadian Project
2 CONC  before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Pierre the younger was born around 1678 to parents Pierre Thibodeau and Jeanne Theriot. ≤ref name=White />≤ref name=Karen>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=pierr
2 CONC e+le+jeune&n=thibodeau Pierre the Younger] citing Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS, vols. 1-6; 1630-1775; Quebec, Le Conseil de la Vie Francaise en Amerique, 1965; p. 808 (Port Royal); own copy. Pierre was born 
2 CONC 1676, married at Port Royal on25 Nov 1706 to Marie-Anne AUCOIN, daughter of Martin & Marie GAUDET of the river "aux Canards, at Grand Pre." Ten children are listed, the last Pierre, born 1724 [when mother was about 38 years old].≤
2 CONC /ref>
2 CONT On November 25 1706 he married Anne-Marie Aucoin, daughter of Martin and Marie Gaudet.  Pierre Gaudet, Claude Thibodeau, de Goutin and the groom all signed their names.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds dela paroisse catholiq
2 CONC ue Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 124) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/124?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 170
2 CONC 2-1755 Pierre Tibeaudeau andMarie Anne Aucoin marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 280 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1215≤/ref>≤ref name=Karen /> Theyare found the next year in Port Royal.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcri
2 CONC ption of the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.
2 CONC lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Pierre THIBEAUDEAU and his wife; 1 arpent, 7 cattle, 13 shee
2 CONC p, 8 hogs, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had 11 children: ≤ref name=White />
2 CONT #Marguerite
2 CONT #Paul
2 CONT #Marie Rose
2 CONT #Brigitte
2 CONT #Olivier
2 CONT #Elisabeth
2 CONT #Jeanne
2 CONT #Catherine Josephe
2 CONT #Ursule
2 CONT #Anne Marie
2 CONT #Pierre
2 CONT By 1714 they moved to Riviere des Canards of Grand Pre, where Marie Anne grew up.   Since he is the only Pierre Thibodeau listed in the 1714Census, presumably that is him.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census, 
2 CONC at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian C
2 CONC ensus microfilm C-2572 of theNational Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”,Images 239-261.≤blockquote> Pierre THIBODEAU and his wife, 2 sons, 3 daughters.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Pierre died before 14 October 1734 (his son Oliver's marriage).≤ref name=White>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. ''Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadi
2 CONC ennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p1508-1511; 1520-1522.≤/ref>≤ref> Karen Theriot Reader [ ] citing AadianChurch Records, vol. II - Milton P. and Norma Gaudet Rieder - Metairie, LA: Authors, 1976 - Covers year 1712-1748. 
2 CONC Also available as microfiche #6087649. Includes transcripts of Beaubassin, Acadia church registers, now at the Archives of the Mayor of La Rochelle, Charente Maritime, France. - Family History Library, 35 North West Temple, Salt L
2 CONC ake City UT 84150  V2d - p. 48 ≤blockquote>He was deceased before the marriage of his son Olivier.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
