2 CONT Brief Life History of Olivier
2 CONT
2 CONT When Olivier Thibodeau was born in 1713, in Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, British North America, his father, Pierre Thibodeau le Jeune, was 36 and his mother, Anne Marie Aucoin, was 26. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Melanson on 14 October 1734, in Beaubassin, Acadia, New France. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 3 daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 21 December 1757, in Notre-Dame de Québec, Quebec City, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 44, and was buried in Notre-Dame de Québec, Quebec City, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT Note: Olivier, his wife Elizabeth, and newborn daughter Marguerite all died within a 3 day period (reportedly of smallpox).
2 CONT
