2 CONT == Biography =='''Anne Savoye''' was born 28 April 1724. She was the daughter of [[Savoie-67|Jean Savoie]] and [[Dupuis-295|Marie Dupuis]]. She was baptized the next day at Port Royal. Her godparents were Jean Dupuis, the sonand M
2 CONC arie Joseph Savoye.≤ref> Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 67) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/67?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An A
2 CONC cadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Anne Savoye baptism RG 1 volume 26 page 198 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=987≤/ref>
2 CONT She married Olivier Saulnier, son of Pierre and Madeleine Comeau about1750.≤ref>Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes: 1715  1780780 - Stephen A. White - Moncton, NB: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, draft version - Centre 
2 CONC d'Études Acadiennes - Centre d'Études AcadiennesUniversity of Moncton - Centre d'Études Acadiennes - 1 University of Moncton - SAULNIER no. 4 e.≤/ref>
2 CONT == Sources ==
