2 CONT {{Acadian}} [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spellings and attempts to add unsourced parents. Please 
2 CONC contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT ----:Marie Breau was born about 1662 in Port-Royal, Acadie. <ref name="DGFA">"Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes"; Stephen A. White; 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p. 1457; Note: 
2 CONC BIRTH-PARENTS-CENSUS-MARRIAGE-DEATH-BURIAL.: [died] Age around 90 years (sic). Present were Charles SAVOIE; Pierre SAVOIE & Amand SAVOIE.</ref>She was age 9 on the census of 1671. Herparents were [[Breau-18|Vincent Breau]] and [[B
2 CONC ourg-38|Marie Bourg]].She married [[Savoie-15|Germain Savoie]] about 1678. <ref name="DGFA"/> <ref Name="PRDH">Programme de Recherche en Démographie Historique (PRDH); [http://www.genealogy.umontreal.ca/en/main.htm University of M
2 CONC ontreal] 7160 famille & couple</ref>Together they had 12 children:
2 CONT # [[Savoie-64|Germain Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-65|François Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[DeSavoie-6|Marie Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-168|Pierre Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-67|Jean Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-68|Marie Madeleine Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-171|Marie Jeanne Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-69|Paul Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-172|Claude Savoy Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-173|Charles Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-174|Marie Josephe Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-175|Marguerite Savoie]] :Marie Breau died October 23, 1749 in Port-Royal and was buried there the next day.<ref name="DGFA"/> 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Recensements/Censuses ===:[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671cens.htm 1671 Census] at Port-Royal, age 9, father's name spelled BROT.<ref>1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie The original census can be found at [http://her
2 CONC itage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 3-14. Also: [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671a.htm Scan of orig
2 CONC inal]; [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671cens.htm TimHebert transcription]</ref>
2 CONT ::Vincent BROT, 40, wife Marie BOURG 26; ::Children: Marie 9, Antoine 5, Marguerite 3, Pierre 1; cattle 9, sheep 7. :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1678cens.htm 1678 Census] at Port Royal, married, no children yet.<ref>Hebert, Tim.
2 CONC  “Recensement 1678, Port-Royal, Acadie.” Edited by Clarence d'Entremont. Acadian-Cajun Genealogy & History. Rootsweb.com. [https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm. 1678]</ref> ::Germain Savoye & Marie B
2 CONC eraud-4 acres   4 cattle :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1686cens.htm 1686 Acadian Census] at Port-Royal. Marie BARAULT, age 21 [sic], living with Germain SAVOYE, age31, and two sons; Germain & Francois<ref>The original census can 
2 CONC be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Image 15-61</ref> :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com
2 CONC /1693cens.htm 1693 Acadian Census], at Port-Royal, Acadie.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Ca
2 CONC nada “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-]</ref>::Germain SAVOYE 37, Marie BEREAU 30, Germain 11, Francois 9, Marie 7,Jean 1; 8 cattle, 12 sheep, 6 pigs, 8 arpents, 1 gun :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1698cens.htm 1698 A
2 CONC cadian Census], at Riviere St. Jean.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 Acadian Censusmicrofilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada “Acadie Recensemen
2 CONC ts 1671 – 1752”, Images 107-109]</ref>:: Germain SAVOYE 46; Marie BRAULT (wife) 36; Germain 16; Francois 14,Marie 12; Pierre 8; Jean 5; Magdeleine 4; Paul 2; 12 cattle, 14 sheep, 13 hogs, 16 arpents, 12 fruit trees, 1 gun. :[http:
2 CONC //www.acadian-home.org/census1700.html 1700 Acadian census],  age 37 years.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National
2 CONC  Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements1671 – 1752”, Images 151-173.</ref>::Germain SAVOIE 44; Marie BREAU (wife) 37; Germain 18; François 16: Jean 8; Pierre 2; Charles 1; Marie 14; Madelaine 7; Marie 6; Jeanne 4;10 cattle, 15 s
2 CONC heep, arpents, 1 gun. :[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Acadian Census], Port-Royal], age 38.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572
2 CONC /2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.</ref>::Germain SAVOYE 47, Marie BROS (wife) 38; Germain 20, Francois 18, Pierre 15, Jean 10, Paul 5,
2 CONC  Claude 3, Marie 16, Magdeleine 7; 2 guns, 13cattle, 20 sheep, 12 hogs, 12 arpents.
