2 CONT Residence: a farm near the river in the seigneury of Belisle, 7 kilometers from Port Royal, Nova Scotia. Census: 1686 Port Royal, 1686 5a, 1693 11a, 1698 16a, 1700 18a, 1701 20a.  Census: 1714 Port Royal; 3 fils [3 sons]  Event: P
2 CONC resence 5 MAY 1720 godparent to Jean Baptiste Babinot, son of Clement & Renee Bourgeois, son of Clement & Renee Bourg, Port Royal (Annapolis Royal), Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada  Event: Presence 7 OCT 1706 godparent to his sister M
2 CONC arie Josephe Savoie  Event: Presence 9 MAR 1714/15 godparent to nephew Honore Savoie, son of Francois & Marie Richard, Port Royal (Annapolis Royal), Acadia, Nova Scotia, Can
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT P. 206 Les Savoie - Fidèle Thériault
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT P. 206 Les Savoie - Fidèle Thériault
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}} [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{One Name Study|name=Savoie|category=Canada, Savoie Name Study}} 
2 CONT == Biographie== 
2 CONT "Germain Savoie, l'aîné des douze enfants de ceux-ci, vit le jour vers 1682. Le 13 janvier 1709, à Port-Royal, il prit pour femme Geneviève Babineau, fille de Nicolas Babineau et de Marie -Marguerite Granger."<ref>“La généalogie d
2 CONC es trente-sept familles hôtesses des ‘Retrouvailles ‘94”; WHITE, Stephen A.; Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne, vol. 25, nos 2 et 3 (1994) [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/55 Genealogy of 37 Families] or [http:
2 CONC //www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac/wf/wf/pdf/37fam-Savoie.pdf Savoie]</ref>
2 CONT Translation of Biographie: "Germain Savoie, the eldest of the twelve children of these, was born around 1682. On January 13, 1709, in Port Royal, he took for wife Geneviève Babineau, daughter of Nicolas Babineau and Marie-Margueri
2 CONC te Granger." [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==Germain was born about 1681. He was the son of [[Savoie-15|Germain Savoie]] and [[Breau-9|Marie Breau]]. He was age 5 on the 1686 Census of Port Royal.
2 CONT Germain Savoye, son of Germain Savoye and Marie Brau married GenevieveBabinot, daughter of Nicolas Babinot and Marie Granger 16 January 1709 at Port Royal. Signed by De St Castin and Rene Babinot. There was dispensation for 4-4 co
2 CONC nsanguinity.<ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 135) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/135?r=0&s=5</ref><ref>An Acadian
2 CONC  Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Germain Savoye and Genevieve Babinot marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 291 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1243</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Children
2 CONT # Jean dit Djanne SAVOIE 1710-/1791
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste SAVOIE 1712-
2 CONT # Pierre SAVOIE 1714-
2 CONT # Joseph SAVOIE 1717-/1760
2 CONT # Marie Josephe SAVOIE 1719-
2 CONT # Marguerite SAVOIE 1722-
2 CONT # Francois SAVOIE 1724-1734
2 CONT # Amand Gregoire SAVOIE 1727-1763/
2 CONT # Anne SAVOIE 1729-/1763
2 CONT # Marie SAVOIE 1738- Germain was alive when daughter Marguerite was baptized 28 May 1722. He has children born from 1710-1738 on Karen Theriot READER's site https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&
2 CONC ocz=1&p=marguerite&n=savoie&oc=2
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away after 1710. 
