2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography =='''Paul Savoie''' was born about 1696. He was the son of [[Savoie-15|Germain Savoie]] and [[Breau-9|Marie Brau]]. He was age 2 on the 1698 census of Port Royal. 
2 CONT Paul Savoye married Judith Michel, daughter of Jacques Michel and Catherine Comeau 23 November 1722 at Port Royal, Acadia. The bride and groom made their marks and Joseph Leblanc signed.<ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de l
2 CONC a paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 182) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/182?r=0&s=5</ref><ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, A
2 CONC nnapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Paul Savoye and Judith Michel marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 332 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1367</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # male SAVOIE
2 CONT # Judith SAVOIE 1723-/1764
2 CONT # Marie Josephe Modeste SAVOIE 1726-1775
2 CONT # Marie Madeleine SAVOIE 1728-
2 CONT # Marguerite SAVOIE 1730-
2 CONT # Pierre SAVOIE 1741-1788
2 CONT # Anastasie SAVOIE ca 1743-1802
2 CONT
2 CONT == Residence ==
2 CONT CENSUS: 1698, Port Royal, Acadia, age 2 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT CENSUS: 1700, as Jeanne, age 4 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT CENSUS: 1701, age 5 years. Unlike his father and his brothers, who remained at Port-Royal, Paul and his family moved to Chepoudy probably in the 1720s.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away before 11 July 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />* BIRTH-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-RESIDENCES: Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS; 1625-1810; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, 6 vols.; p. 1572 (Chipoudy)
