2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Les Savoye d'Acadie s'établirent, pour la plupart, autour de la rivière Chipoudie, jusqu'au temps du "grand dérangement des Acadiens"... Loose translation of above....the Acadian Savoies settled mostly around the river Chipoudie u
2 CONC ntil the time of the "great disturbance of the Acadians
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT
2 CONT :: Date:  5 OCT 1706<ref>[https://www.genealogiequebec.com/membership/voir.aspx?id=L%3a%2fRegistres%2fAcadie%2fLieux+de+A+à+W%2fPort-Royal%2f1700%2f1706%2fd1p_33110051.jpg Registres du Fond Drouin, Collection Acadie A-Z, Port-Roya
2 CONC l, 1706, image d1p_33110051.jpg] - Marie Joseph Savoye</ref>
2 CONT :: Place:  Port Royal, Acadia, Canada :: Baptism: 7 OCT 1706
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT : Date: 14 OCT 1727<ref>[https://www.genealogiequebec.com/membership/voir.aspx?id=L%3a%2fRegistres%2fAcadie%2fLieux+de+A+à+W%2fPort-Royal%2f1720%2f1727%2fd1p_33110372.jpg Registres du Fond Drouin, Collection Acadie A-Z, Port-Royal
2 CONC , 1727, image d1p_33110372.jpg] - Jean Baptiste Poirier et Marie Josephe Savoye</ref>
2 CONT :: Place: Port-Royal, Acadia, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT :: Date:  29 DEC 1757:: Burial: 30 DEC 1757<ref>[https://www.genealogiequebec.com/Membership/LAFRANCE/acte/252795 Genealogie Quebec Burial Record 252795] - MaireJosephe Savoye</ref><ref>"Québec, registres paroissiaux catholiques,1
2 CONC 621-1979," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G99Q-MKZ7?cc=1321742&wc=HC3D-ZNL%3A17585101%2C19508101%2C26879601 : 16 July 2014), Québec > Notre-Dame-de-Québec >Baptêmes, mariages, sépu
2 CONC ltures 1757-1759 > image 126 of 259; Archives Nationales du Quebec (National Archives of Quebec), Montreal. Burial Marie Josephe Savoye 1757</ref> :: Place:  Québec (Notre-Dame-de-Québec), Canada, Nouvelle-France :: Name: Marie Sa
2 CONC voye :: Age: Approximately 60 :: Transcript: "Le trente de décembre mil sept cens cinquante sept a été inhumée Marie (annotation: Joseph) Savoye, acadienne, veuve de Jean-Baptiste Poirier, décédée le jour précédent, munie des sacr
2 CONC ements, âgée de soixante ans environ. Étaient présents Jean Vallée, Guillaume Taphorin et autres. J.F. Récher, curé". :: Loose translation: "The thirtieth of December 1757 was buried Marie(Joseph) Savoye, Acadian, widow of Jean-Ba
2 CONC ptiste Poirier, (she) died the previous day, provided the sacraments, aged sixty or so. Present were Jean Vallée, Guillaume Taphorin and others. J.F. Récher, pastor." :: Research notes: Someone mentioned she died of smallpox, but 
2 CONC the burial record makes no such mention.  There was a tremendous amount of death around this time period and their may have been an outbreak of smallpox at the time -- unless proven otherwise we cannot claim that she died of small
2 CONC pox based on the current evidence. Additional sources would be required. -- [[Poirier-1805|Dave Poirier]]
2 CONT
