1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography:'''
2 CONT *'''Marguerite Savoye''' was born 7 May 1709. She was the daughter of [[Savoie-15|Germain Savoie]] and [[Breau-9|Marie Breau]]. She was baptized the same day at Port Royal. Her godparents were François Savoye and Louise de Gannes 
2 CONC de Falaize who signed.<ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Marguerite Savoye baptism RG 1 volume 26 page 82 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=281</re
2 CONC f> She passed away in Jan 1711, aged 20 months and was buried 17 January 1711 in the cemetery of theSt-Laurent chapel, upriver.<ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds dela paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.
2 CONC )-1870 C-1870 (image 200) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/200?r=0&s=5</ref><ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Marguerite Savoye burial RG 1 volu
2 CONC me 26 page 355 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1492</ref>
2 CONT
