2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT '''Charles Savoie''', son of Germain Savoie and Marie dite Vincelotte Breau, was born in 1703 at Port-Royal, Acadie.<ref name=DGFA>Stephen A. White, ''Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes'' (Moncton, New Brunswick: Ce
2 CONC ntre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999)  p. 1458
2 CONT :Text: Sponsors: Yvon GURE (who signed) & Marie SAVOIE </ref>He was christened there on 24 June 1703. <ref>[https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=20 Public Archives of Nova Scotia - St. Jean Baptiste Ch. Register,
2 CONC  Annapolis 1702-1755; RG 1, vol. 26, p. 7]Text: Felix Pain, Priest; 24 June 1703 Baptism of Charles Savoy born 25 May 1703; Germain Savoy, Father;  Marie Vinalote, Mother; GodparentsYvone Quaine and Marie Savoy:Text: Charles SAVOY
2 CONC , son of Germain SAVOY & Marie VINALOTE. Sponsors:Yvone QUAINE & Marie SAVOY. </ref>  Charles Savoie and Francoise Martin, daughter of  Etienne Martin and Marie Jeanne Comeau, were married 16 January 1730 in Port-Royal. <ref>RG 1 
2 CONC Vol. 26a p.44 René Charles de Breslay, Priest; 16 January 1730 Marriage of Charles Savoye twenty-six years old Groom; Germain Savoye, Father; Marie Brau. Mother; Françoise Martin nineteen years old Bride;Etienne Martin, Father; Ma
2 CONC rie Comau, Mother; Paul Savoye brother of the groom, Jacques Michel, son of Jacques Michel, Joseph Landry son of Claude Landry, first cousin of the bride, Pierre Michel son of JacquesMichel, cousin of the bride, Witnesses. </ref> 
2 CONC :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/savoie.htm Children]:
2 CONT #Marie Josephe Savoie, b: 17 OCT 1730 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Francois Savoie, b: ABT 1732 in Chipoudy, Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Anne Savoie, b: 25 APR 1734 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Felicite Savoie, b: 1736 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Rosalie Savoie, b: 1739 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Marguerite Savoie, b: 1741 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Madeleine Savoie, b: 1743 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Guillaume Savoie, b: 1745 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Joseph Savoie, b: 1747 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Jean (dit Valois) Savoie, b: 1749 in Nova Scotia 
2 CONT #Ludevine Savoie, b: 1752 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia  Charles remained in Port Royal until the day he and his family were deported in late 1755. Charles, his wife Francoise Martin and eight of their eleven children were boarded on
2 CONC  the English vessel ''Experiment''on December 8, 1755 and deported to New York. Charles was 52 years old. <ref>Letter dated May 6, 1756, during the time of Gov. Hardy, namesFrench neutrals sent by Gov. Lawrence from Nova Scotia to
2 CONC  New York: Charles Savoit, wife, 8 children, New Rochelle, Westchester County, NY. </ref>Seven of the eight deported children survived the eight years of captivity. His wife did not. After the death of Francoise Martin, Charles re
2 CONC married Hugues Racle sometime before 1767.<ref name=DGFA /> In 1763, with the signing of the Treaty of Paris, the British authorities in the American colonies allowed the Acadians to go free. Most could not leave immediately, havi
2 CONC ng to earn money for passage elsewhere. Some may have stayed, but most chose to go north to Nova Scotia, west to Louisiana, or south to Martinique shortly thereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles died before the 1767 census.<ref name=DGFA />
2 CONT
