2 CONT Charles remained in Port Royal until the day he and his family were
2 CONT deported. Charles and his family were boarded on the English vessel
2 CONT Experiment on Dec. 8, 1775 and deported to New York. Charles was 52 years
2 CONT old when the Acadians were exiled. Charles and his wife Francoise Martin
2 CONT and 8 of his 11 children were exiled to New York (New Rochelle). 7 of the
2 CONT 13 children survived the 8 years of captivity. In 1763, the British
2 CONT authorities in the American colonies allowed the Acadians to go free, and
2 CONT some were shipped to Martinique the same year.
2 CONT Letter dated May 6, 1756, during the time of Gov. Hardy, names of French
2 CONT neutrals sent by Gov. Lawrence from Nova Scotia to New York;
2 CONT Charles Savoit, wife, 8 children, New Rochelle, Westchester County, NY.
