1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marguerite Cecile Christophe was born about 1723 to Jean Christophe and Marie Agnes Simon dite de L'espine, who were married prior to being deported to Biloxi together aboard Le Tilleul in 1720 .[1] Marguerite Ceci
2 CONC le's father was an "untrained ‘barber surgeon’ who cut limbs as well as hair while her mother was listed among 'forced laborers: bohèmes," a term equated with Roma or gypsies.[1]
2 CONT
