1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~thetells/genealogy/moran.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Moran III was born in 1805 at Seymour, on Back Bay of Biloxi, Mississippi. He married (#1) Virginia Fayard. She was born 26 March 1814 in Woolmarket, Harrison County, Mississippi. She died 9 March 1842 and is buried in Wool
2 CONC market by her parents. Joseph died in 1880 at Seymour and is buried in Moran Cemetery. He married (#2) Caroline (Coralie) Ladner (daughter of Joseph Ladner and Rosalie Fayard) about 1843. Caroline was born 22 Dec 1805.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Morans had a large kiln where they made charcoal. Back in 1865 after the "War with the States", Joseph with his son Jean Baptiste had a sailing schooner named "Clements" which they used to deliver their charcoal to New Orleans
2 CONC , Louisiana. All of Joseph Moran's children were born in Seymour, Harrison County, Mississippi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Moran and Virginia Fayard had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT SEVENTH GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.(F) Marie Louise Moran n. 26 Oct 1833 m. Bernard Sartain m. Francois Taltivall 2.(F) Victoria Moran n 3 March 1835 d. 15 Dec 1885 m. Celeste Fayard m. Richard Louis Boney 3.(M) Jean Baptiste Moran n. 6 Aug 1836 d. 1 June 1924 4.
2 CONC (F) Virginia Moran n. 20 April 1838 5.(F) Delphine Moran n. 25 Dec 1839 d. 24 Jan 1891 m. August W. Newman 6.(M) Joseph Moran IV n. 19 Feb 1841 d. 28 June 1914 m. Catherine Abbley
2 CONT
