1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tamelie Roselie CAVELIER Cook was born the daughter of Charles Louis Henri Cavelier, Sr. and Tamelie Adelaide MASCEY Cavelier. Her father's Cavelier family being long time New Orleans residents since the early year
2 CONC s of the city migrating from historic Rouen, Normandy, France in 1752.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tamelie's known siblings include: 1. Sophie Octavie CAVELIER Fossier b.1837 - (# 61840092) - married Theodule Fossier 2. Charles Cavelier, Jr. (1840-1893) - married Marie Clothilde ROUX Cavelier 3. Octave Catoire Louis Cavelier b.
2 CONC 1842 - (# 89705796) - married Mary GREEN Cavelier 4. Marie Estelle CAVELIER Smith b.1846 - (# 110796613) - married John Alexander Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT It is here in New Orleans where she met and later married a most interesting gentleman, he being a British child-immigrant named Frederick Henry Cook, Sr. Their young family would move around a good bit with her husband's work, bu
2 CONC t eventually settled back home with their family in New Orleans, LA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tamelia and Frederick's children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Frederick Charles Cook, Jr. b.1860 2. Alice Roselie H. COOK Richardson b.1867 - married Thomas Rice Richardson 3. Mathilde Marie COOK Posey - married Edward Lloyd Posey, Sr. 4. Walter Henry Cook - married Marie Leonie Aldige - 
2 CONC married Louise Marie Joubert de Villemarest 5. Sidney George Cook - married Daisy Isabelle Beebe - married Florence Falkenstein  - #30488332, Putnam Co, IN, 1906 - married Margaret H. O'Connor 6. Louise Amelia COOK Finley - marrie
2 CONC d Ridgely Finley
