2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Name: Marie Estelle Cavalier Smith   Event Type: Death   Event Date: 19 Jan 1926   Event Place: Grand Coteau, St. Landry, Louisiana   Gender: Female   Age: 78   Race: White   Birth Year (Estimated): 1848   Birthplace: New Orleans,
2 CONC  Louisiana   Father's Name: Charles Cavalier   Mother's Name: Tamelia Massey   Spouse's Name: John A Smith   Certificate Number: 1022  
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT  Sister of: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=61840092   Sophie Octavie Cavelier Fossier] Charles Antoine Cavelier, Jr. (1840-1893) married Marie Clothilde ROUX Cavelier [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.c
2 CONC gi?page=gr&GRid=135502807  Tamelie Roselie Cavelier Cook] [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=89705796  Octave Louis Cavelier]
2 CONT  Marie Estelle Cavelier Smith 
2 CONT *************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT  Died:  This afternoon at 12:30 o'clock,
2 CONT   Mrs. J. A. SMITH  born Estelle Cavalier, aged 78 years, 11 months and 15 days,
2 CONT    The funeral will take place from the family residence in Grand  Coteau,  tomorrow  (Wednesday)  afternoon  at  3 ' clock.  Services and interment at Sacred Heart Church and cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Friends and acquaintances are respectfully invited to attend.                            In BEHALF OF THE FAMILY Grand Coteau, La., Jan. 19, 1926
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  MRS. J. A. SMITH DIED WEDNESDAY AT HER HOME ______
2 CONT
2 CONT WAS 78 YEARS OLD AT THE TIME  OF HER DEATH AT GRAND COTEAU  ______
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. J. A. Smith of Grand Coteau passed into the great beyond last Wednesday at noon.  She was the wife of Judge Smith and one of the most beloved characters in St. Landry parish.  Widely connected, she leaves a host of relatives.
2 CONC   Before her marriage she was Miss Estelle Cavalier.  At the time of her death she was aged 78 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral took place from the home Wednesday and services and interment took place at the Sacred Heart Church and Cemetery.  Looked on by friends and relatives as the soul of beauty and refinement, she will be greatly missed by 
2 CONC the loved ones she has left behind.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturday, January 23, 1925 Clarion Progress [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=103560900  Edith Garland Dupré] Library, UL Lafayette.
2 CONT
2 CONT *************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT  50 Years Ago
2 CONT  CLARION-PROGRESS
2 CONT   November 4, 1922
2 CONT   GOLDEN WEDDING TO  BE OBSERVED IN GRAND  COTEAU
2 CONT  Judge and Mrs. J. A. Smith To Be Honored by 
2 CONT  Host of Friends Next Thursday
2 CONT   The whole commnity is looking forward to
2 CONT  the golden wedding anniversary of
2 CONT  Judge and Mrs. J.  A.  Smith (Estelle Cavilier)
2 CONT   which will be celebrated  November 9th. 
2 CONT  They were married in New Orleans,
2 CONT  Nov. 9, 1872.
2 CONT   They are the parents of ten children,
2 CONT  Alex, of New  Orleans,
2 CONT  Birdie (Mrs. William  Devalcourt) of Sunset,
2 CONT  Cook of Grand Coteau,  Temilia  (Mrs. Edgar Smith) of Arnaudville,
2 CONT  John of Grand Coteaux,
2 CONT  Zita (Mrs. James  Fox) of Grand Coteau,
2 CONT  Marie who is residing with her  parents,
2 CONT  Louise (Sister Estelle) of St. Louis, Mo.,
2 CONT   Walter of Opelousas, and
2 CONT  Electa (Mrs. Henry Richard) of Grand Coteau.
2 CONT
2 CONT They have forty-eight grandchildren and three great-grandchildren and  what is more remarkable, there has been no deaths in the family. Judge Smith has been justice of the peace here for the last thiry-five years.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  Will Celebrate Golden Wedding.   Grand Coteau. La., Nov. 1 or 4.- the golden wedding anniversary of Judge and Mrs. J. A. Smith (Estelle Cavilier) will be celebrated on Thursday of next week. They were married in New Orleans on No
2 CONC vember 9, 1872. A special mass of thanksgiving will be said at the Sacred Heart Catholic Church, after which they will receive their friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Times Picayune November 2, 1922 Page 19
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  GOLDEN WEDDING  TO BE OBSERVED IN GRAND COTEAU ______ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge and Mrs. J. A. Smith to Be Honored by Host of Friends Next Thursday. ______
2 CONT
2 CONT GRAND COTEAU, La., Nov. 2-- The whole community is looking forward to the golden wedding anniversary of Judge and Mrs. J. A. Smith, (Estelle Cavilier) which will be celebrated on Thursday of next week.  They were married in New Or
2 CONC leans, on November 9, 1872.  A special mass of thanksgiving will be said at half past seven o'clock at the Sacred Heart Catholic Church.  In the afternoon from three to five they will receive their friends.  The Jubilarians are in
2 CONC viting all their friends through the papers as no invitations will be sent.
2 CONT
2 CONT They are the parents of ten children, Alex, of New Orleans, Birdie, (Mrs. William Devalcourt) of Sunset, Cook of Grand Coteau, Temilia, (Mrs. Edgar Smith of Arnaudville), John of Grand Coteau, Zita, (Mrs. James Fox) of Grand Cotea
2 CONC u, Marie who is residing with her parents, and Louise (Sister Estelle) of St. Louis, Mo.  Walter of Opelousas, and Electa, (Mrs. Henry Richard) of Grand Coteau.  They have forty-eight grandchildren and three great-grandchildren, a
2 CONC nd what is most remarkable there has been no deaths in the family,  Judge Smith has been Justice of the peace here for the past thirty-five years.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAILY CLARION-PROGRESS OPELOUSAS, LOUISIANA, THURSDAY, NOVEMBER 2, 1922  
2 CONT *************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Hilda Smith of New Orleans is visiting her grandparents, Judge and Mrs. J. A. Smith.
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT The St. Landry Clarion Saturday, August 9, 1919. Opelousas Louisiana, Page 5, Column 1. 
2 CONT *********************** CAVELLIER, Estelle m. 6 Nov. 1872 John A. Smith (Opel.Ct.Hse.:Mar. #7121) Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. J. A. SMITH NOBLE WIFE AND MOTHER FEB. 04, 1847 JAN. 19, 1926
