2 CONT GUESNO, Joseph (Esteban, native of {*}, resident of this parish, and Victoria Alexandrina DUCAYET, native of Port-au-Prince on Santo Domingo, resident of this parish), b. May 4, 1818, bn [*] 1818, pgp, Santiago GUESNO and Maria Lu
2 CONC isa CARABY, mgp [*] DUGAYET and Juana Adalaida JOUANEL, s Juan Maria Joseph DUCAYET and Maria Luisa CARABY, infant's paternal grandmother (SLC, B31, 1).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Found in the 1850 and 1860 Census living with the family created with Gertrude.  In 1850 the family is listed as white by the census takers, the oldest is 6 years old.  In 1860 the family is listed as mulatto.  In 1870 the family 
2 CONC is scattered and Joseph has yet to be found in a census.  14 year old Ovide is living with sister Justine and her family.  Gertrude can not be found again.  In 1871 Joseph marries Elmire Bertonniere, a white woman, much younger th
2 CONC an he.
