2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT CENSUS-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; p. 41; own copy. #2: MartinAUCOIN, probably son of Martin
2 CONC  & Marie SALLE', born around 1651. He married around 1673 to Marie GAUDET, daughter of Denis & Martine GAUTHIER; nineteen children. He was on the 1686 census at Les Mines, Acadia, age 35 years; in 1693, age 46 years (sic). He died
2 CONC /was buried (Grand Pre' Register) 14/15 May 1711, age 60 years, "he died suddenly on Ascension day upon return from mass, having always lived strongly Christian, and with edification."**CENSUS: 1686, Baye des Mines, Acadia, age 35
2 CONC , with wife and 8 children. They have 1 gun, 15 cattle, 10 sheep and 6 pigs. No land is listed.**CENSUS: 1693, age 46 years.**BIRTH-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-RESIDENCES: Arsenault, H&G, p. 1086 (Grand Pre'). Born in 1651 in the parish of 
2 CONC Cougnes, in the La Rochelle region of France. A footnote from Genevieve MASSIGNON's Les parlers francais d'Acadie, vol. 1, p. 57: Michel AUCOIN [sic, meant for Martin?] was probably the nephew of Michelle AUCOIN, spouse of Michel 
2 CONC BOUDROT of Port Royal, and of Jeanne AUCOIN, spouse of Francois GIROUARD, also of Port Royal. Martin was at Beaubassin in 1684, at the river aux Canards in Grand-Pre' in 1714. He died suddenly on the day of the Ascension, on retur
2 CONC ning from mass "ayant toujours ve'cu fort chre'tiennement et avec e'dification." [Is this from his burial record at Saint-Charles-des-Mines?]**NAME-CHILDREN-CHRISTENING: Name spelled AUCOING on daugher Cecile's baptism in 1686 at 
2 CONC Mines (See DeVille, ACR, 1).**DEATH-BURIAL: On Pedigree Chart sent by Dwayne A. MONTZ in Apr 1996. Martin AUCOIN, born about 1651 at Riv. Aux Canards, Acadia, married about 1672 at Port Royal. He died on 14 May 1711 at Riv Aux Can
2 CONC ards; buried 15 May 1711 at Grand Pre' (Reference Diocese of Baton Rouge Records, v. 1, p. 4).**BURIAL: Diocese of Baton Rouge [LA], CATHOLIC CHURCH RECORDS; 1707-1769; vol. 1, Catholic Diocese of Baton Rouge, 1978; p. 4; Sutro, [
2 CONC CA] State Library, F377 B3 C3 V.1; contains the 3 registers of the church of St. Charles-aux [des]-Mines, Grand Pre', that were carried into exile by Acadians to St. Gabriel d'Iberville, LA. Martin [AUCOIN], age 60 years [so born 
2 CONC 1651?], native of River aux Canards, was buried on 15 May 1711. Recorded in (SGA-1, 26).
2 CONT
