1 NOTE Martin Aucoin of Cougnes, near La Rochelle, reached Port-Royal soon after the first census was taken and married Marie, a granddaughter of Jean Gaudet, in 1673.  They settled first at Beaubassin then moved to Minas.  Marie gave Ma
2 CONC rtin 19 children, including 10 sons, nine of whom created families of their own.
2 CONT Married about 1673 to Marie Jeanne Gaudet [#1988] at Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; sources: P. Girouard genealogy from the internet (copy filed L-14-30); "Genealogie de l'ancienne Acadie" shows family with 14 children.
2 CONT 1686 Census of Port Royal shows family as follows: Martin AUCOIN 35, Marie GAUDET 27; children: Martin 12, Marie10, Michel 9, Isabelle 7, Louis 6, Agnesse 4, Alexis 3, Cecille 7 months; 1 gun, 15 cattle, 10 sheep, 6 hogs.
2 CONT <http://www.genweb.net/acadian-cajun/aucion.htm> (copy filed L-14-30) shows him and his family.
2 CONT <http://www.geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga5.html>  (copy filed L-14-15 & L-14-30) shows family of 17 children.<http://www.geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga106.html>  (copy filed L-37-2).
2 CONT <http://perso.wanadoo.fr.froux/families/aucoin/aucoin2.htm> (copy filed L-38-2) shows the following about Martin Aucoin:  In 1686, Martin (3) Aucoin was listed in the bay of mines with his family, Martin Aucoin 35, Marie Gaudet 27
2 CONC , Martin 12, Marie 10, Michel 9, Isabelle 7, Louis 6, Agnesse 4, Alexis 3, and Cecille 3 months.  This source also gives a lot of conflicting information as to which Martin is who.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
