2 CONT The following was acquired from : <http://www.geocities.com/acadienne_99/AucoinMartin.htm>
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Aucoin and Marie Gaudet
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Aucoin is probably the son of Martin and Marie Sallé, born about 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie Gaudet, the daughter of Denis and Martine Gauthier, old around 16 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Martin Aucoin and Marie Gaudet:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Martin, born about 1674. He married about 1698, Catherine Thériot, daughter of Germain and Andrée Brun.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Marie, born about 1676. In 1693 at the Mines she was 18 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Michel, born about 1677. He married about 1699, Jeanne Bourg, daughter of Martin and Marie Potet.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Isabelle (Élisabeth), born in Beaubassin about 1679. She married about 1698, Jerome Giraud Guerin, son of François and Anne Blanchard.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Louise, born at Beaubassin, June 18, 1681. Her godfather was Antoine Morin and her godmother Marguerite Bourgeois. She married about 1708, François Gautrot son of François and Marie Sébastienne Brun.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Agnes, born in Beaubassin on October 20, 1682. Her godfather was Louis Morin and her godmother Francoise Chiasson. Married about 1703 to Claude Thériot son of Claude and Marie Gautrot. Deceased in October 1756 at Falmouth Engla
2 CONC nd.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Alexis (twin), born at Beaubassin, March 14, 1684. His godfather was Germain Girouard and his godmother Anne Morin. Married about 1707 to Anne-Marie Bourg daughter of Martin and Marie Potet. Burial at St-Nicolas of Boulogne sur
2 CONC  Mer on December 25, 1759, at the age of 75 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Augustin (twin), born in Beaubassin on March 14, 1684. His godfather was Jacques Blou and his godmother Madeleine Dugas. Note in margin of the baptismal certificate, deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Cecile, born in Beaubassin on 12 January 1686, baptized on May 13 of the same year. His godfather was Thomas Vincent and his godmother Cécile Landry. In 1693, he was 9 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Anne-Marie, born about 1687. Married at Port-Royal November 25, 1706, Pierre Thibodeau , the young person, son of Pierre and Jéhanne Thérriot. Deceased at Quebec the 16 Oct 1757, at the age of 75 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Pierre, born about 1689. In first wedding about 1716 he married, Marie Breau daughter of Pierre and Marie-Josèphe Bourgeois. In second wedding he married at Grand-Pre on  August 1718, Catherine Comeau daughter of Jean the youn
2 CONC g person and Catherine Babin. Deceased in Quebec on January 27, 1758, at the age of approximately 60 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Rene, born about 1690. He married about 1712, Madeleine Bourg, daughter of Martin and Marie Potet. Deceased after 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. Catherine, born about 1692. In 1693 she was 1 year old.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Antoine, born about 1694. Married at Grand-Pre November 20, 1713 to Anne Breau daughter of Pierre and Marie-Josèphe Bourgeois. Deceased at St-Suliac on June 5 1759 at the age of approximately 70 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15. Francoise, born about 1696. Married about 1719 to Jean-Baptiste Borough, son of Jean and Marguerite Martin , widower of Marie-Catherine Barrieau; deceased at sea in 1758 during the crossing to France.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16. Joseph born about 1698. He married about 1720, Anne Trahan daughter of Jean-Charles and Marie Boudrot. Deceased In Metairie Pommerais. Burial at Plouër, May 25, 1769, at the age of approximately 69 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Jean married about 1722 to Marguerite Pitre daughter of Claude and Marie Comeau.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. Charles, married at Grand-Pre January 28, 1726 to Marie (Anne-Marie) Dupuis, daughter of Martin and Marie Landry. Deceased before May 21, 1763.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19. girl born before 1707.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: S. White
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawsuit of Jean Campagna 1685, deposition of Martin Aucoin 34 years old. Deposition of Marie 28 years old Gaudet.
2 CONT
2 CONT December 2, 1705, expropriation of joining site a "on the side of the old man strong" and pertaining to Martin Aucoin or Sr of St-Castin, for the extension of the fort of Port-Royal.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is deceased at Grand-Pre May 14, 1711, at the age of 60. He died suddenly the day of the Ascension at the end of the mass, having always lived extremely chrétiennement and with construction.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
