2 CONC ue GUERIN was born in 1721, son of Jérome GUERIN & Elizabeth AUCION, married Anne LEBLANCE, born about 1726, died at the age 56 years, buried 11 May 1782 (St Jacques of Nantes. Issue (childern) are Joseph GUERIN born about 1752 in
2 CONC  Louisbourg in Canada, resident of St Similien of Nantes (SEE FLAMILY # 146. Francoise GUERIN was born about 1761 in the Parish of TrigavouDIOCESE of St Malo, was married 23 Nov 1784 (St Jacques of Nantes) to Jacques TERRIOT (SEE 
2 CONC FLAMILY # 282). Dominique GUERIN, Anne LEBLANC, his wife & family of 7 persons were in the Fourth Convoy leaving Châtellerault for Nantes from 6 Mar to 13 Mar 1776. Dominique GUERIN, widower, & his 2 daughters: Elizabeth & Brigitt
2 CONC e were passengers (Flamily # 8 aboard LA BERGERE which departed France on 12 May 1785 & arrived in Louisiana on 15 Aug 1785. *** FAMILY # 146 *** !INFORMATION: was obtainted from the following book: The Acadian Exiles in Nantes 17
2 CONC 75 to 1785 by Albert J ROBICHAUX Jr., pages 77 &78, Joseph GUERIN was born about 1752 in Louisbourg in Canada, resident of St Simiolien of Nantes, son of Dominique GUERIN & anne LEBLANC (SEE FAMILY # 145), married 30 Apr 1776 (St 
2 CONC Similien of Nantes, he married Agnes PITRE who was born about 1748 in the Parish of St Pierre & St Paul of Cobequid in Acadie, she is the daughter of Benjamin PITRE & Jeanne MOYSE, his first wife (SEE FAMILY # 259, ISSUE (childern
2 CONC ): Marie Jsoephine GUERIN was baptized on 12 Jan 1777 at St Similien of Nantes; Francoise GUERIN was baptized on 30 Apr 1874 (St Jacques of Nantes). Joseph GUERIN, Agnès PITRE, his wife &Francoise, his daughter were passengers (FA
2 CONC MILY # 9) aboard LA BERGERE, which departed France on 12 May 1785 & arrived in Louisiana on 15 Aug 1785.
