2 CONC  of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003–, accessed November 20, 2013]≤/ref>'':''1670’s-1690’s Available farmland decreases; some leave Port-Royal to establish new villages: Beaubassin (1671); Grand-Pré and Pigiguit (1680); Chipoudie (1
2 CONC 698), and Cobeguit and Petcoudiac (1699).≤ref>[http://www2.umoncton.ca/cfdocs/etudacad/1755/index.cfm?id=010102000&lang=en&style=G&admin=false&linking= Pioneer Families, in 1755 l'Histoire et les Histoires, University of Moncton]≤
2 CONC /ref>''
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1670''' birth, son Pierre the elder:'''1671''' residence, in Port-Royal≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 
2 CONC Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752 Image
2 CONC s 3-14.≤blockquote>Pierre THIBEAUDEAU, 40, wife Jeanne TERRIAU27; Children: Pierre 1, Marie 10, Marie 9, Marie 7, Anne Marie 6, Catherine 4; cattle 12, sheep 11.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :'''1672''' birth, son Jeanne
2 CONT :'''1674'' birth, son Jean
2 CONT :'''1676''' birth, son Antoine
2 CONT :'''1678''' residence, in Port-Royal
2 CONT :'''1678''' birth, son Pierre the younger
2 CONT :'''1680''' birth, son Michel
2 CONT :'''1680''' birth, daughter Cécile
2 CONT :'''1682''' birth, daughter Anne-Marie
2 CONT :'''1685''' birth, son Claude
2 CONT :'''1686''' residence, in Port-Royal
2 CONT :'''1686''' birth, daughter Catherine-Josèphe
2 CONT :''1687 War of the League of Augsburg (King William’s War) starts between England and France≤ref name=Griffiths2005>Griffiths, Naomi E.S.,From migrant to Acadian : a North-American border people, 1604-1755, Montreal (Québec), McGi
2 CONC ll-Queen's University Press, 2005, p147-151 (King William’s War); p 267-268 (oaths of allegiance)≤/ref>''
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1689''' birth, son Charles
2 CONT :''1690 Phipps captures and sacks Port-Royal, coerces inhabitants' oaths of allegiance to English Crown, sets up local Peacekeeping Council and leaves within 12 days.≤ref name=biophips>[http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/phips_william
2 CONC _1E.html C.P.Stacey, “PHIPS, SIR WILLIAM,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, University of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003, accessed November 20, 2013]≤/ref>≤ref name=biowikiphips>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Ph
2 CONC ips#Port_Royal_expeditionBiography of William Phipps]≤/ref>≤ref name=biotourasse>[http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/la_tourasse_charles_1E.html C.Bruce Fergusson,“LATOURASSE, CHARLES,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, Uni
2 CONC versity of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003, accessed November 20, 2013]≤/ref>'' Seaman from two ships later loot and burn between 28 and 35homes/habitations including the parish church.≤ref name=Dunn/>” 
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1693''' residence, in Port-Royal
2 CONT :''1693 Port-Royal raid with looting and burning.''≤ref name=Dunn>Dunn, Brenda. A History of Port Royal / Annapolis Royal 1605-1800. Nimbus Publishing, p vii,ix,1-12 (early European settlement); p13 (1629 Food abundance Scottish s
2 CONC ettlement); p32 (Church and School 1686));p 40,43 (1693 PR raid); p44-45 (1697 Treaty of Ryswick); p52-53(1702 Queen Anne’s War); p61-62 (Blockade of PR); p 71-73(1707 Attack on PR); p82-85(1710 Siege of PR).≤/ref>:''1697 Treaty o
2 CONC f Ryswick restores Acadia to France; Port-Royal is itscapital''≤ref name=Dunn/>
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1698''' residence, in Port-Royal
2 CONT :'''1698''' founder, Chipoudy
2 CONT :'''1700-1701''' residence, in Port-Royal
2 CONT :''1702 War of the Spanish Succession (Queen Anne’s War) starts between England and France''≤ref name=Dunn/>
2 CONT :'''1703''' residence, in Port-Royal≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1703cens.htm 1703 Census Transcription]. The original cens
2 CONC us can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 ofthe National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 212-220.≤blockquote>Pierre THIBAUDO
2 CONC T, his wife, 4 boys, 2 girls, 4 arms bearers. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :''1704 Blockade of Port Royal; no destruction of houses but some inhabitants taken prisoner''≤ref name=Dunn/>
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1704''' widowed, in Port-Royal 
2 CONT
2 CONT :''1707 Attack on Port-Royal; burning and pillaging''≤ref name=Dunn/>:''1710 Siege of Port-Royal; French surrender the Fort. Port-Royal, Acadia becomes Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia≤ref name=Dunn/>:''1713 Treaty of Utrecht. France 
2 CONC cedes Acadia to England. Permanent British rule. ≤ref>[http://www2.umoncton.ca/cfdocs/etudacad/1755/index.cfm?id=010201000&lang=en&style=G&admin=false&linking= The Neutrality: Political Context, in 1755 l'Histoire et les Histoires
2 CONC , University of Moncton]≤/ref>'':''1714-15 New English King requires oaths of allegiance.≤ref name=Griffiths2005/> Delegates from Port-Royal sign a [http://www2.umoncton.ca/cfdocs/etudacad/1755/index.cfm?id=010202000&overlay=doc&i
2 CONC dentifier=001461&bd=CEA&lang=en&style=P&admin=false&linking= '''conditional''' oath of allegiance], promising to stay true to the King of Great Britain for as long as they stayed in Nova Scotia, and to remain neutral in the event 
2 CONC of a conflict between France and Great Britain'' :''1720 and onward Acadians refuse to sign an '''unconditional''' oathof allegiance. This is tolerated by the British as they lack militarymeans to enforce the oath.≤ref name=oath>T
2 CONC he Neutrality, 1755 Histoire et Les Histoires, University of Moncton≤/ref>'' :''1713-1744 Golden Age≤ref name=Griffiths92>Griffiths, Naomie E.S. The Contexts of Acadian History 1686-1784.Published for the Center for Canadian Studi
2 CONC es Mount Allison University, Montreal: McGill-Queens University Press, 1992, p61 (golden age);≤/ref> of Acadian Growth and Prosperity” 
2 CONT
2 CONT
