2 CONT :Marie was born about 1661-1662 to [[Thibodeau-30|Pierre Thibodeau]] and [[Thériot-100|Jeanne Thériot]].  She married  [[Landry-80|AntoineLandry]] about 1681 and gave birth to about a dozen children. Detailsof her death are unknow
2 CONC n except that both she and Antoine were already deceased when their daughter [[Landry-524|Francoise Landry]] was married on February 16, 1711. ≤ref name="DGFA">"Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes"; Stephen A. White;
2 CONC  2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p. 1508≤/ref>≤ref>Dioceseof Baton Rouge Catholic Church Records: Acadian Records, 1707-1748, Volume 1a, revised, p. 109. :"Francoise Landry (Antoine Landry and Ma
2 CONC rie Tibeaudo, both decd., habitans des Mines) m. 16 Feb. 1711 Pierre Leblanc (Antoine Leblanc and Marie Bourgois, habitans de la Grand Pree)...."≤/ref>
2 CONT :DNA: Maternal relationship is confirmed, [Thériot-100|Jeanne Thériot aka Theriault] is a common ancestor, by a triangulated group consisting of [[Morales-671|Kevin Paul Morales]] GEDmatch M579136, [[Mageau-9|Barbara Ann Mageau]] 
2 CONC GEDmatch  A713327and [[Lajiness-24 |Kevin Charles Lajiness]] GEDmatch M658673 sharing segment on chromosome 20 from 12930672 - 34674266 (19.5089 cM)  Overlap with previous match 16540474 -34674266
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT :Marie Thibodeau, the second of several daughters named "Marie" was born about 1663 in Port Royal, Acadia to parents Pierre Thibodeau and Jeanne Theriot.  About 1678 she married Pierre Lejeune dit Briard II in Port Royale. ≤ref>So
2 CONC urce: [[#S14]]  p. 1508 
2 CONT :Text:  Married (Belle-Ile-en-Mer Declaration) before the 1678 census.
2 CONT :Text:  No place given for marriage. :Text:  Also recorded in Tanguay, vol. VII, p. 290.≤/ref>[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I2229 Children]
2 CONT
2 CONT === Residence ===
2 CONT :CENSUS:  '''1671''' Port Royal Census :: Pierre THIBEAUDEAU, 40, wife Jeanne TERRIAU 27; Children: Pierre 1,Marie 10, Marie 9, Marie 7, Anne Marie 6, Catherine 4; cattle 12, sheep 11.
2 CONT :CENSUS: '''1678''', Clarence J. d'Entremont, "Recensement de Por t-Royal," in MEMOIRES DE LA SOCIETE GENEALOGIQUE CANADIENNE -FRANCAISE; vol. 22, no. 4; p. 233; sent by PERSI in Jun 1999. On Folio 20: one of the five girls in the
2 CONC  household of Pierre THIBAUDEAU & Jeanne TERRIOT, ages 12 to 1. There are also three boys. [None were old enough?]
2 CONT ::Pierre Le Jeune & Marie Thibaudeau-3 acres   4 cattle
2 CONT :CENSUS: '''1686''', Port Royal, Acadia, age 23, listed in father 's entry, with two other sisters also named Marie, ages 25 and 21.
2 CONT :: Pierre Thibaudeau & Jeanne Terriot-12 acres   30 cattle
2 CONT :: 3 boys - 11   1669, 7   1671, 5   1673
2 CONT :: 5 girls - 12   1666, 8   1670, 4   1674, 3   1675, 1   1677
2 CONT :: Pierre TIBAUDEAU                  55
