2 CONT == Biography/Biographie ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spellings and attempts to add unsourced paren
2 CONC ts. Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT ----:'''Anne Marie Thibodeau''' was born about 1666 in Port-Royal, Acadie,Nouvelle-France. Her parents (Père et mère) were [[Thibodeau-30|Pierre Thibodeau]] and [[Thériot-100|Jeanne Thériot]]. ≤ref name="DGFA">"Dictionnaire Généal
2 CONC ogique des Familles Acadiennes"; Stephen A. White; 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; pp. 1508-1511
2 CONT :No place of birth given. - Born around 1666.
2 CONT :BOUDROT #4 No place given for marriage.:Anne-Marie died between 1698 & 1700.≤/ref> She married [[Boudrot-15|Claude Boudrot]], son of Michel Boudrot and Michelle Aucoin, in 1682 atPort-Royal. Vers 1682, à Port-Royal, Acadie, Canad
2 CONC a, elle épouse Claude Boudrot, fils de Michel Boudrot et de Michelle Aucoin. ≤ref name="DGFA"/>Together they had 8 children, birth order is estimated:
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-9|Claude Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-1|Michel Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-159|Joseph Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-8|Marie Anne Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-10|Marie Madeleine Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudreaux-11|Anne Boudreaux]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-211|Elisabeth Boudrot]]
2 CONT # [[Boudrot-61|Marguerite Boudrot]]
2 CONT :She died in 1699 in Grand-Pré, Acadie, Nouvelle-France.≤ref name="DGFA"/>. Anne Marie Thibodeau has a Find a Grave memorial citing burial at Saint-Charles-des-Mines, Grand Pré, but no gravestone photo or source is provided. There
2 CONC  are family links to both parents, spouse, one child and one sibling. ≤ref>Find A Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com : accessed 05 November 2019), memorial page for Anne-Marie Thibodeau (1665–1697), Find A Grav
2 CONC e Memorial no. 125959396, citing Saint-Charles-des-Mines, Grand Pré, Kings County, Nova Scotia,Canada ; Maintained by AW (contributor 47829810). Anne-Marie Thibodeau (1665-1697) on {{FindAGrave|125959396}} retrieved 05 November 20
2 CONC 19≤/ref>
2 CONT :'''DNA''' Maternal and Paternal relationship is confirmed, [Thériot-100|Jeanne Thériot aka Theriault] is a common ancestor, by a triangulated group consisting of Kevin Paul Morales GEDmatch M579136, Barbara Ann Mageau GEDmatch A7
2 CONC 13327and Kevin Charles Lajiness GEDmatch M658673sharing segment on chromosome 20 from 12930672 - 34674266 (19.5089 cM) Overlap with previous match 16540474 - 34674266 (one more conformation containing 6 trails coming please don't 
2 CONC delete)
2 CONT
2 CONT === Recensements/Censuses ===:[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671a.htm 1671 Acadian Census], age 6 years.≤ref>The original census can be found here. [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census 
2 CONC microfilmC-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 3-14. Also: [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671a.htm Scan of original]; [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671cens.htm Tim Hebert transcripti
2 CONC on]≤/ref>
2 CONT :Pierre THIBEAUDEAU, laboureur, 40 ans
2 CONT :Jeanne TERRIAU sa femme, 27 ans:6 enfants : Marie 10 ans (ZC), Marie 8 à 9 ans , Marie 7 ans,''' Anne Marie 6 ans''', Catherine 4 ans, Pierre 1 an.
2 CONT :Terres labourables: 7 arpents; 12 bêtes à cornes, 11 brebis.
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1678cens.htm 1678 Census] at Port Royal.≤ref>Hebert, Tim. “Recensement 1678, Port-Royal, Acadie.” Edited by Clarence d'Entremont. Acadian-Cajun Genealogy & History. Rootsweb.com. [https://freepages.r
2 CONC ootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm. 1678]≤/ref>:On Folio 20: one of five girls age 12 to 1 in household of Pierre THIBAUDEAU & Jeanne TERRIOT. There are also three boys. She would be the girl age 4 years (sic).
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1686cens.htm 1686 Acadian Census at Port-Royal. age 17 years [sic]. Listed in entry of parents, with a sisteralso named Anne Marie, age 4 years and 3 sisters name Marie.≤ref>The original census can b
2 CONC e found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Image 15-61≤/ref>:Pierre TIBAUDEAU 55, Jeanne TER
2 CONC RIOT: 43; children: Marie 25, Marie 23, Marie 21, Catherine 19, Anne-Marie 16, Pierre 16, Jeanne 14, Jean 13, Antoine 12, Pierre 10, Michel 8, Cecille 6, Anne-Marie 4, Claude 2; 1 gun, 10 arpents, 14 cattle, 5 sheep, 7 hogs.
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1693cens.htm 1693 Acadian Census], at Port-Royal, Acadie. age 24 years [sic]. Living with husband, 30, and 5 children, ages 10 to 1.≤ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana
2 CONC .ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 AcadianCensus microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-]≤/ref>:Pierre TIBAUDEAU 59, Jeanne TERRIOT 50, Anthoine 17, Pierre 15, Mich
2 CONC el 13, Cecille 11, Marie 10, Claude 8, Catherine Josephe 7, Charles 4; 20 cattle, 30 sheep, 12 pigs, 30 arpents, 2 guns
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1698cens.htm 1698 Acadian Census], at Riviere St. Jean.≤ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 Acadian Censusmicrofilm C-2572 of 
2 CONC the National Archives of Canada “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 107-109]≤/ref>:Pierre TIBAUDEAU 65; Jeanne TERRIOT (wife) 57; Jean 24; Antoine  22; Pierre 21; Michelle 19; Claude 13; Catherine 11; Charles 7;  20 cattle, 
2 CONC 20 sheep, 8 hogs, 32 arpents, 20 fruit trees, 4 guns,
