2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Michel Thibodeau, son of Pierre Thibodeau and Jeanne Thériot, was born around 1680.≤ref>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hbert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Généalogique 
2 CONC Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p.1509, 1517-1519. ≤/ref>≤ref>Per the history on nosorigines.qc.ca, he would have been born in 1679 as he had a brother b
2 CONC orn in 1678 and a sister in 1680. [http://www.nosorigines.org/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogy=Michel_Thibodeau&pid=1003466&lng=en&partID=1003467 Michel Thibodeau] at nosorigines.org≤/ref>  Between 1686 and 1701, he was enumerated 
2 CONC with his parents and siblings in the censuses of Port Royal. The family was doing well with a large number of animals and land holdings.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freep
2 CONC ages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the Nationa
2 CONC l Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal: Pierre TIBAUDEAU 55, Jeanne TERRIOT: 43; children: Marie 25, Marie 23, Marie 21, Catherine 19, Anne-Marie 16, Pierre 16, Jeanne 14, J
2 CONC ean 13, Antoine 12, Pierre 10, Michel 8, Cecille 6, Anne-Marie 4, Claude 2; 1 gun, 10 arpents, 14 cattle, 5 sheep, 7 hogs. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http:/
2 CONC /freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the N
2 CONC ational Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote>Pierre TIBAUDEAU 59, Jeanne TERRIOT 50, Anthoine 17, Pierre 15, Michel 13, Cecille 11, Marie 10, Claude 8, Catherine Josephe 7, Charles 4; 20 
2 CONC cattle, 30 sheep, 12 pigs, 30 arpents, 2 guns≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Trans
2 CONC cribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-166≤
2 CONC blockquote>Pierre TIBAUDEAU 65; Jeanne TERRIOT (wife) 57; Jean 24; Antoine 22; Pierre 21; Michelle 19;Claude 13; Catherine 11; Charles 7; 20 cattle, 20 sheep, 8 hogs, 32 arpents, 20 fruit trees,  4 guns≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim 
2 CONC Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 CensusTranscribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca
2 CONC /view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 167-173.≤blockquote>Piere THIBAUDEAU 66; Jeanne TERRIOT (wife) 57; Anthoine 26; Pi
2 CONC ere 22; Michel 20; Claude 15; Charles 11; Marie 17; Catherine 14; 30 cattle, 28 sheep, 30 arpents, 3 guns.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsw
2 CONC eb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Census Transcription]. The originalcensus can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives
2 CONC  of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote>Pierre TIBAUDEAU 71, Jeanne THIRIOT [Terriot] (wife) 50; Jean TIBAUDEAU 27, Anthoine 23, Pierre 21, Michel 19, Claude 16, Charles 13, Cecile 19, Catherine 1
2 CONC 4; 7 guns, 30 cattle, 25 sheep, 12 hogs, 19 arpents.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT When Michel Tibaudeau was about 24 years of age, he married Agnès Dugat age 18, daughter of Claude Dugat and Françoise Bourgeois, at Port-Royal in 1704. ≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-
2 CONC Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image119) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/119?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>''Nova Scotia Archives'', "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapo
2 CONC lis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26 page 273; online database with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1198 Michel Tibaudeau and Agnes Dugat marriage 13 November 1704],  accessed 15 December 
2 CONC 2019 ≤blockquote>Registration Date	13 November 1704≤br/>
2 CONT Groom	Michel Tibaudeau≤br/>
2 CONT Father	Pierre Tibaudeau≤br/>
2 CONT Mother	Jeanne Theriot≤br/>
2 CONT Bride	Agnes Dugat≤br/>
2 CONT Father	Claude Dugat≤br/>Mother	Françoise Bourgeois≤/blockquote>≤/ref> Three years later, the Port-Royal census shows that Michel and Agnès had 2 girls and owned 3arpents of land, 9 head of cattle, 6 sheep, 5 hogs and 1 gun.≤ref>Ti
2 CONC mHebert; Transcription of the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana
2 CONC .ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>Michel THIBEAUDEAU and his wife, 2 girls less than 12; 3 ar
2 CONC pents, 9 cattle, 6 sheep. 5 hogs. 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  The growing family was enumerated again in Port-Royal in 1714.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb
2 CONC .com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. Theoriginal census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives o
2 CONC f Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote>Michel THIBODEAU and wife, sons 4, daughters2.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Between 1705 and 1728, they had fifteen children: Marguerite, Agnès, Michel, Pierre, Joseph, Charles, Marie-Madeleine, Marie-Josèphe, Élisabeth, François, Benjamin, Jean-Baptiste, Amand-Grégoire, Claire, Anne.
2 CONT Michel passed away on 27 November 1734 and was interred the next day in Annapolis Royal (formerly Port-Royal).≤ref>''Nova Scotia Archives'',"An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-
2 CONC 1755," register RG 1 volume 26a page 129; online database with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2037 Michel Thibaudot burial 28 November 1734] accessed 15 December 2019≤blockquote>Witnesses:	Antoine 
2 CONC Thibaudot brother of the deceased, Claude Thibaudot brother of the deceased, Agnes Dugas his wife, Pierre Thibaudaut son of the deceased, Charles Thibaudaut son of the deceased, Joseph Thibaudaut son of the deceased≤/blockquote>≤/
2 CONC ref>
2 CONT
