2 CONT
2 CONT Blais Brousseaux was born in 1756 while in exile from Acadia. He died in Opelousas, LA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT "Blaise, younger son of Cosme Brasseur di Brasseux and Elisabeth Thibodeau followed his family to Maryland in 1755. He arrived in Louisiana in 1767 with his widowed mother and siblings and followed them to St. Gabriel d'Iberville 
2 CONC on the river about New Orleans. Probably after his mother died, he and four of his sisters moved to the Opelousas District, where he married Marie-Anne, called Anne, daugther of fellow Acadian Amand Prejean, in the mid 1770s. They
2 CONC  setteld in the Bellevue area of what became St. Landry Parish, south of Opelousas. Their daughters married into the LANDRY, PRATHER, RICHARD, SMITH and WOOD families. Blaise's succession record was filed at the Opelousas courthou
2 CONC se, St. Landry Parish, in January 1822; he would have been 70 years old that year. Only two of his sons created families of their own. They settled probably on the upper Atchafalaya River near the boundary between St. Landry and P
2 CONC ointe Coupee parishes. Typical of Acadians who lived in that area, most of Blaise's descendants married Creoles."
2 CONT {excerpt from Brasseau Genealogy from Acadians in Gray by Stephen A. Cormier}
