2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication. Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive chang
2 CONC es. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT '''Françoise Savoie''', daughter of [[Savoie-9|François Savoie]] and[[Lejeune-11|Catherine Lejeune]], was born c.1653≤ref name=1671Cen>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," on his website, 
2 CONC ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,'' [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acad
2 CONC ian Census microfilm C-2572of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>  She was counted twice: once with her parents, and then with her husband in the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port
2 CONC -Royal: 
2 CONT :Francois SAVOYE, 50, 
2 CONT :wife, Catherine LeJEUNE 38; 
2 CONT :children: '''Francoise 18,''' 
2 CONT :Germain 17, 
2 CONT :Marie 14, 
2 CONT :Jeanne 13, 
2 CONT :Catherine 9, 
2 CONT :Francoise 8, 
2 CONT :Barabe 6, 
2 CONT :Andree 4, 
2 CONT :Marie 2; 
2 CONT :cattle 4.	
2 CONT and
2 CONT :Jehan CORPORON, 25, 
2 CONT :wife '''Francoise SAVOIE 18'''; 
2 CONT :one daughter of 6 weeks; 
2 CONT :cattle 1, sheep 1.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>probably in Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France. Her parents married in 1651 and had nine children;≤ref>Stephen A. White, ''Dictionnaire Gnéalogique des Familles Acadiennes,'' 1636-1714  (Monc
2 CONC ton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999) p. 1456       :  SAVOIE: Né en France vers 1621, François Savoie est arrivé en Acadie avant 1651, date où il s'est marié à Catherine Lejeune. Neuf enfants sont issus de leur ma
2 CONC riage, dont Germain, né vers 1654, qui épousa vers 1678 Marie Breau, fille de Vincent Breau et de Marie Bourque.≤!-- N/A:  Germain Savoie, l'aîné des douze enfants de ceux-ci, vit le jour vers 1682. Le 13 janvier 1709, à Port-Roya
2 CONC l, il prit pour femme Geneviève Babineau, fille de Nicolas Babineau et de Marie -Marguerite Granger. Jean Savoie, l'aîné des dix enfants de ces derniers, naquit à Port-Royal, le 14 février 1710. Le 22 août 1735, au même endroit, J
2 CONC ean épousa Anne Landry, fille de Charles Landry et de Catherine Broussard. Peu après leur mariage, Jean et Anne s'établirent àChipoudy. En 1755 ils se sont évadés des Anglais. On les retrouve par la suite à la rivière Miramichi. -
2 CONC ->
2 CONT ≤/ref> she was their first.
2 CONT She married [[Corporon-71|Jean Corporon]] in Port-Royal in c.1670,≤refname=1671Cen />estimated by the age of their first listed child, a unnamed girl, 6 weeks old at the time of the 1671 Port-Royal Census. By 1686, still in Port-R
2 CONC oyal, they had seven more children;≤ref>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," from his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,'' [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.
2 CONC htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1
2 CONC 752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>1686 Census at Port Royal: :Jean Coporon 39, 
2 CONT :'''Francoise Savoye 35'''
2 CONT : children: Marie 16, 
2 CONT :Magdelaine 14, 
2 CONT :Jeanne 12, 
2 CONT :Jean 10, 
2 CONT :Marie 8, 
2 CONT :Isabelle 6, 
2 CONT :Cicille 4, 
2 CONT :Marguerite 1; 
2 CONT :2 cattle, 2 sheep, 1 hog≤/blockquote>
2 CONT ≤/ref>by 1693 two children were gone with nine remaining at home.≤ref>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," from his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,''  [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~a
2 CONC cadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada
2 CONC ] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> 
2 CONT :Jean CORPORON 44, 
2 CONT :'''Francoise SAVOYE 41''', 
2 CONT :Jacques 18, 
2 CONT :Jean 15, 
2 CONT :Elisabeth 11, 
2 CONT :Cecille 6, 
2 CONT :Marguerite 8, 
2 CONT :Martin 6, 
2 CONT :Francois 5, 
2 CONT :Charles 2,
2 CONT : Jean CORPORON 1; 
2 CONT :6 cattle, 4 sheep, 6 pigs, 6 arpents, 1 gun≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT In 1698 they were still living in Port-Royal, and had nine children remaining at home; Charles was not counted.≤ref> Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," from his website, ''Acadian-Cajun 
2 CONC Genealogy,'' [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~/acadiancajun/genealogy1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census micro
2 CONC film C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-166≤blockquote>
2 CONT : Note:  fr 1698 Port Royal Census
2 CONT : Jean CORPORON 50; 
2 CONT :'''Francoise SAVOYE (wife) 46'''; 
2 CONT :Jean 21; 
2 CONT :Elisabeth 17, 
2 CONT :Cecile 15; 
2 CONT :Margueritte 13 
2 CONT :Martin 11; 
2 CONT :Francois 9; 
2 CONT :Jean 7; 
2 CONT :Marie 4; 
2 CONT :Ambroise 2; 
2 CONT :4 cows, sheep, 1 servant.≤/blockquote>
2 CONT ≤/ref>They were counted there again in 1700 with nine children; Charles andAmbroise were missing.≤ref> Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," from his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,'' [
2 CONC http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of
2 CONC  the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 167-173.≤blockquote> 
2 CONT :Jean CORPORON 51; 
2 CONT :'''Francoise SAVOIE (wife) 48'''; 
2 CONT :Jaques 25; 
2 CONT :Jean 22; 
2 CONT :Martin 13; 
2 CONT :Francois 12; 
2 CONT :Jean 8; 
2 CONT :Elisabet 18; 
2 CONT :Cecille 16; 
2 CONT :Marguerite 15; 
2 CONT :Marie 7; 
2 CONT :5 cattle, 6 sheep, 6 arpents, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT ≤!-- -->
2 CONT Francoise Savoie, Madame Corporon, was buried on  27 December 1711 at St Jean Baptiste Parish, in Port Royal, aged about 60 years. The date of death is not mentioned in the register.≤ref>''Nova Scotia Archives'', "An Acadian Paris
2 CONC h Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste,Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26 page 355; onlinedatabase with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1493 Françoise Savoye burial (reg
2 CONC istered in 1711)],  accessed 6 Nov 2019≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 200) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869
2 CONC /200?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT
