2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jeanne Savoie, fourth child of Francois Savoie and Catherine Le Jeune, born in 1657 at Port-Royal, Acadia, and married Etienne Pellerin at the age of 18. Etienne Pellerin died at Port-Royal 17 nov 1722 at 76. Jeanne Savoie died 3 
2 CONC nov 1722 at Port-Royal at age 78. This couple became the ancestors of an extraordinarily numerous posterity in Canada and the U.S., particularly around Louisianna. There is a detailed article on the Pellerin in the Apr-May-June 19
2 CONC 81 issue of Memoires. They had five sons and five daughters: Madeleine 1676, Marie 1678, Pierre 1681, Anne 1683, Marguerite 1694, Charles 1696. Pierre died in infancy. But that still leaves four unaccounted for. All of the daughte
2 CONC rs married to Calve dit LaForge, Gaudent, Brun and Doucent. The sons married at Port-Royal: Jean-Baptiste II to Marie Martin in 1710, Bernard II to Marie-Marguerite in 1713, Alexander II to Jeanne Gaudet in 1713, Charles II to Mad
2 CONC eleine Robichaud in 1725, dau of Prudent and Henriette Petitpas.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
