2 CONT [[Category: Beaubassin, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spellings and attempts to add unsourced parents. Please 
2 CONC contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT :Andrée Savoie , daughter of François Savoie and Catherine LeJeune, was born about '''1667''', in Port-Royal, Acadie. She was age 4 years on the census of '''1671''' taken at Port-Royal.≤ref name="S66">1671 Port Royal Census. The 
2 CONC original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Image 6, p. 5.:Tim Hebert; T
2 CONC ranscription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie.::Francois SAVOYE, 50, wife, Catherine LeJeune 38; children: Francoise18, Germain 17, Marie 14, Jeanne 13, Catherine 9, Francoise 8, Barabe6, '''Andree 4''', Marie 2; 
2 CONC cattle 4.≤/ref>
2 CONT :Her parents were married about '''1651''', (based on birth of first child) in Port Royal≤ref name="S25">Young, John Austin. ''The Lejeunes of Acadia and the Youngs of Southwest Louisiana.'' Publication:  John Austin Young, Grand 
2 CONC Pere Farm≤/ref>
2 CONT :The '''1671''' Port Royal Census listed her parents (age 50 and 38) and their children: [[Savoie-10|Francoise Savoie]], 18; [[Savoie-15|Germain Savoie]], 16; [[Savoie-14|Marie Savoie]], 14; [[Savoie-11|Jeanne Savoie]], 13; [[Savo
2 CONC ie-17|Catherine Savoie]], 9; [[Savoie-19|FrancoiseSavoie]], 8; [[Savoie-20|Barabe Savoie]], 6; [[Savoie-1|Andree Savoie]], 4; [[Savoie-16|Marie Savoie]], 2; and 4 cattle.≤ref name="S66"/>
2 CONT :On the [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1686cens.htm '''1686''' Port Royal Census], she was age 21 and the wife of Jean Prijean. They have onechild Marie, age 2, so married at least by 1683-1684≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 
2 CONC 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recense
2 CONC ments 1671 – 1752”, Image 32, p. 31:Text: Jean PRIJEAN 35, Andree SAVOYE 21; child: Marie 2; 2 guns, 1 arpent, 1 hog.≤/ref> Her husband is listed as Jean Brigeau. ≤ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana
2 CONC .ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Image63, p. 61:Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Ac
2 CONC adie. Jean :BRIGEAU 42, Andree (wife) 26, Marie 9, Anne 6, Pierre 3,Jean Baptiste 1; 6 cattle, 8 sheep, 5 pigs, 14 arpents, 1 gun≤/ref>
2 CONT :The [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1698cens.htm '''1698''' Port Royal Census] lists Jean Prijean, age 47, Andree Savoye, age 31 and their first six children. ≤ref>Acadian-Cajun Genealogy &History website; Note:The original census 
2 CONC can be found on microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada. :Text: Jean PREJAN 47; Andree SAVOIE (wife) 31; Marie 14; Anne 11, Pierre 9; Jean 7; Francois 3; Madeleine 1; 17 cattle, 19 sheep, 5 hogs, 8arpents, 60 fruit tre
2 CONC es.≤/ref>
2 CONT :When the [http://www.acadian-home.org/census1700.html '''1700''' Acadian census] at Port Royal, Acadia was taken, she was age 33 and the again the wife of "Jean BRIGEAU", 49. There are 4 children where were the other 2 children J
2 CONC oseph and Madeleine?≤ref>:The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”
2 CONC , Image 171, p. 151-152.: Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal,Acadie.:Text: Jean "BRIGEAU" 49; Andree (wife) 33; Pierre 10; Jean-Baptiste 8; Marie 16; Anne 14; 7 cattle 6 sheep, 14 arpents, 1 gun.:T
2 CONC im Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocih
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT :The census of '''1701''' gives names and ages. Andree Savoye and JeanPrejan are ages 52 & 35 and the number of children is seven.≤ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?
2 CONC r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. T:Jean PREJAN 52, Andree SA
2 CONC VOYE (wife) 35; Pierre 12, Jean 10, Francois8, Joseph 5, Marie 17 Anne 14, Magdeleine 3; 1 gun 16 cattle, 10 sheep, 12 hogs, 3 arpents.≤/ref>
2 CONT :The census of '''1703''' doesn't name anyone but the heads of household, but the number of children is 7. Jean is back to being called Jean"Prijan". No ages were given.≤ref>The original census can be found at[http://heritage.cana
2 CONC diana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 212-220.:Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703 Acadian Census, at Port-Roy
2 CONC al, Acadie. 
2 CONT :Jean PRIJAN, his wife, 4 boys, 3 girls, 1 arms bearer.≤/ref>
2 CONT :'''1714''' Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. This is the last census we know of that Andree is found on. The two eldest daughters Marie and Anne were married by 1714. The 8 sons are Pierre L'Aine, Jean Baptiste, François, Jo
2 CONC seph, Nicolas, Charles, Pierre le Cadet and Honoré. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie
2 CONC  Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239
2 CONT :LE BRETON and wife, 8 sons, 2 daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''Marriage''':Andrée Savoie married [[Prejean-106|Jean Prejean]] in '''1683''', atPort Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada.≤ref> Title: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes; Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: 
2 CONC 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes,1999; pp. 1351 & 1457
2 CONT :No place given for marriage. No parents given for groom.:Text: Jean PREJEAN dit Le Breton married around 1683 to Andrée SAVOIE, daughter of François & Catherine LEJEUNE; twelve children listed.≤/ref>
2 CONT :'''Children''' according to Stephen White there were twelve children born to this marriage. Honoré died at sea. The census of 1714 lists 10 children: 8 sons, 2 daughters, eldest daughters Marie and Anne were married by 1714.
2 CONT #Marie PREJEAN ca 1684-
2 CONT #Anne PREJEAN ca 1687-/1755
2 CONT #Pierre L'Aine PREJEAN ca 1690-
2 CONT #Jean Baptiste PREJEAN ca 1692-/1760
2 CONT #Francois PREJEAN ca 1695-
2 CONT #Marie Madeleine PREJEAN ca 1697-
2 CONT # Joseph PREJEAN ca 1700-1756/
2 CONT #Marie Josephe PREJEAN 1702-
2 CONT # Nicolas PREJEAN 1704-1765
2 CONT # Charles PREJEAN 1706-/1763
2 CONT # Pierre le Cadet PREJEAN 1708-1768
2 CONT # Honore PREJEAN 1711-1758
2 CONT
2 CONT === DNA ===
2 CONT :'''Ethnic Origins.''' Some have speculated that Andree's mother Catherine Lejeune was Amerindian. The [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/MothersofAcadia/default.aspx Mothers of Acadia maternal DNA project] posts its ongoing Ma
2 CONC ternal DNA results [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults '''here''']. To date, the haplogroup of both sisters is consistently reported as U6a7a, indicating European origins. 
2 CONT :Another group known as [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/AcadianAmerindian/default.aspxAMERINDIAN Ancestry Out of Acadia DNA PROJECT], posts its results [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/AcadianAmerindian/default.aspx?sec
2 CONC tion=mtresults here]. They too report that Catherine and Edmee have European haplogroups.
2 CONT
