2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''*NOTE: There are different theories as to the parents of Vincent, but no records have been found to support either. Parents shown here are speculative.  If you have solid evidence of parents, please contact a curator to add par
2 CONC ents.  Thank you!'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *Sources:'''
2 CONT **1671 Acadie Census - shown to be 40 years old which estimates birth c.1631
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography  According to Stephen White[1], Vincent Breau was born around 1631 and his origins are unknown. Another theory is that he was part of the Brault family who were on Governor d'Aulnay's seigneury in La Chausée France.[2]  
2 CONC Around 1661, we find Vincent in Acadia, when he married Marie Bourg, daughter of Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry. Between around 1662 and 1685, the couple had 12 children: Marie (dit Vincelotte), Antoine, Marguerite, Pierre, s
2 CONC on unknown, Anne, François, Jean, Marie, Jeanne, René, and Elisabeth.  At the time of the first Acadian Census in 1671[3], the family was living in Port-Royal, Acadia (Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada). Forty year old Vincent 
2 CONC and 26 year old Marie were living with their four children. Four arpents[4] of their land was cultivated and they had 9 cattle and 7 sheep. Their homestead was situated on the north bank of the Dauphin (Annapolis River) to the eas
2 CONC t of the Belleisle Marsh.[1][5]  Sadly, Vincent died in his 50s sometime before 1686, leaving his widow to care for the children aged 2 months to 22 years.  Timeline  c1631 Birth, in France  1632 Treaty Saint-Germain-en-Laye cedes
2 CONC  Acadia to France; Razilly brings ~300 elite men[6]  1636 D'Aulnay brings the first French families to settle permanently[2][7]  1654 British capture Port-Royal; French settlement ceases[8]  c1661 Marriage to Marie Bourg, in Acadi
2 CONC a  c1662 Birth of daughter, Marie (dit Vincelotte)  c1666 Birth of son, Antoine  c1668 Birth of daughter Marguerite  1667-70 Treaty of Breda cedes Acadia to the French; settlement resumes[9]  c1670 Birth of son Pierre  1671 Reside
2 CONC nce, Port-Royal  c1671 Birth of son unidentified  c1673 Birth of daughter Anne  c1674 Birth of son François  c1678 Birth of son Jean  1678 Residence, Port-Royal  c1680 Birth of daughter Marie  c1684 Birth of daughter Jeanne  c1685
2 CONC  Birth of son René  c1685 Birth of daughter Elisabeth  b1686 Death  Sources  "A Breau Genealogy" Compiled by Clarence T. Breaux and Robert Brault, Second Edition 2004, pg. 1  1671 Acadian Census at Port Royal: Vincent BROT, 40, wi
2 CONC fe Marie BOURG 26; Children: Marie 9, Antoine 5, Marguerite 3, Pierre 1; cattle 9, sheep 7.  1678 Acadian Census at Port Royal:Vincelot Beraud Marie Bourg 3 acres 5 cattle 4 boys: age 12- born 1666; 9-1669; 7-1671; 4-1674; and 2 g
2 CONC irls: 11- 1667; 8-1670.  1686 Acadian Census at Port Royal: Note, the family appears twice in the census  Marie BOURC/BOURG, widow of Vincent BREAU, 50; children: Antoine 22, Marguerite 18, Pierre 16, Anne 14, Francois 12. Jean 11
2 CONC , Marie 9, Jeanne 6, Rene 3, Susanne 2 months; 3 arpents, 6 cattle, 4 sheep, 6 hogs.  Marie BOURC/BOURG (widow of Vincent BROT/BREAU) 41; children: Antoine 20, Marguerite 18, Pierre 16, Anne 17, Francoise 11, Jeanne 9, Marie 7, je
2 CONC anne 5, Rene 3, Isabelle 5 months; 4 arpents, 10 cattle, 5 sheep, 5 hogs.  White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes. Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Uni
2 CONC versité De Moncton, 1999, Print, p270. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note  Note:  Vincent * BROT (rec. 1671) / BRAULT (index). · Pionnier, en Acadie. · Immigration: Vers 1652 Acadie. · Acadie, rec. de 1671: Vincent BROT (40 ans), et sa femme Marie BOURG (*), et 4 enfants: Antoine (5 ans), Pierre (1
2 CONC  an), et 2 filles. Le couple 9 bêtes à cornes, et 7 brebis. · A Port-Royal, rec. de 1686: Marie BOURC (50 ans, veuve de Vincent BREAU), 50 ans. 10 Enfants: Antoine 22, Marguerite 18, Pierre 16, Anne 14, Francois 12. Jean 11, Marie
2 CONC  9, Jeanne 6, René 3, Susanne 2 mois; 3 arpents de terre cultivées, 6 bêtes à cornes, 4 moutons, 2 porcs.) Sources: · personne: http://www.gov.ns.ca/nsarm/cap/acadian/default.asp · naissance: GenCircles, by Linda Harrison. · baptê
2 CONC me: Saint-Jean-de-Sauves (Saint-Clément). · décès: (avant rec.début-1686 = Suzanne: 2 mois@@1686). · mariage: v 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Vincent BRAULT and Marie BOURG
2 CONT
2 CONT [86123] BRAULT, Vincent (..), ploughman (laboureur), born about 1631 (rec. 1671), died between 1684-11 and 1686-01
2 CONT
2 CONT * married about 1661, from Port-Royal ? (Acadie)
2 CONT
2 CONT BOURG, Marie (Antoine & Antoinette LANDRY [46444]), born about 1645 (rec. 1671, rec. 1686, rec. 1693, rec. 1698) or 1644 (rec. 1699), buried 1730-09-19 Port-Royal (Acadie)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Antoine, married about 1687 Marguerite BABIN
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Élisabeth, married Port-Royal (Acadie) 1710-11-24 Marcel SAULNIER
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) François, married before census 1703 Marie COMEAU
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Jean, married about 1700 Anne CHIASSON dit LAVALLÉE
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Jeanne, married Port-Royal (Acadie) 1714-05-23 Jean LEBERT dit JOLICOEUR
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Marie1, married about 1678 Germain SAVOIE
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) Marie2, buried 1742-12-20 Saint-François-de-la-Rivière-du-Sud (Qc), married before census 1714 Abraham GAUDET
2 CONT
2 CONT 8) Pierre, born about 1670 (rec. 1671, rec. 1686), 1671 (rec. 1693) or 1672 (rec. 1699) Port-Royal (Acadie), died 1758-04-25 Braintree (Massachusetts), USA, married about 1694 Marie Josèphe BOURGEOIS, married about 1705 Anne LEBLA
2 CONC NC
