2 CONT Bibliographie : Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes (White); Dictionnaire des Acadiens d'Archange Godbout; Acadian Church Records; http://www.umoncton.ca/etudeacadiennes/centre/cea.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/086/086123.php
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT On page 20 of "A Breaux Family History" Gerald P. Breaux wrote: "Vincent Brault was born in 1631 in France and was from LaChaussee, region of Loudun, department of Vienne.  He arrived in Acadia in the year 1652, as a single man ap
2 CONC proximately 21 years old.  Vincent was destined to become the 'Adam' of the entire Acadian line of descent bearing his name and it's later derivatives.  All family branches - regardless of name spelling - converge upon this one ma
2 CONC n, since he was the only male member of the family to settle in Acadia and produce descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT At about age 30, Vincent Brault married a 16-year old native Acadian girl, Marie Bourg, and raised a family of 11 children, consisting of 5 boys and 6 girls....Marie was the eldest daughter of Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry, 
2 CONC who were among the earliest settlers, arriving in Acadia as newly-weds in 1636.  They also originated from the same place in France as Vincent Brault.... Thus, it appears that these early settlers were closely related and associat
2 CONC ed even before their arrival in Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Vincent Brault and Marie Bourg was raised in Port Royal, Acadia.  The spelling of the name was apparently modified to Brot - perhaps to signify a new beginning in a new land.This new land presented an environment tha
2 CONC t was distinctly different from Vincent's homeland in France."  -- Norma (Aubey) Lewis
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Vincent Breaux Immigrated from France to Quebec, Canada in 1647, this according to "Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500's-1900's"
2 CONT
2 CONT Vincent Breaux Married Marie Brough in 1661, this according to the "US and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900's"
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Event: Name Variations Vincelotte, Vincelate, Brault, Beault, Breaux, Brot, Barault, Beraut, Berault
2 CONT --------------------
