2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Vincent BRAULT and Marie BOURG
2 CONT
2 CONT [86123] BRAULT, Vincent (..), ploughman (laboureur), born about 1631 (rec. 1671), died between 1684-11 and 1686-01
2 CONT
2 CONT * married about 1661, from Port-Royal ? (Acadie)
2 CONT
2 CONT BOURG, Marie (Antoine & Antoinette LANDRY [46444]), born about 1645 (rec. 1671, rec. 1686, rec. 1693, rec. 1698) or 1644 (rec. 1699), buried 1730-09-19 Port-Royal (Acadie)
2 CONT
2 CONT       1) Antoine, married about 1687 Marguerite BABIN
2 CONT
2 CONT       2) Élisabeth, married Port-Royal (Acadie) 1710-11-24 Marcel SAULNIER
2 CONT
2 CONT       3) François, married before census 1703 Marie COMEAU
2 CONT
2 CONT       4) Jean, married about 1700 Anne CHIASSON dit LAVALLÉE
2 CONT
2 CONT       5) Jeanne, married Port-Royal (Acadie) 1714-05-23 Jean LEBERT dit JOLICOEUR
2 CONT
2 CONT       6) Marie1, married about 1678 Germain SAVOIE
2 CONT
2 CONT       7) Marie2, buried 1742-12-20 Saint-François-de-la-Rivière-du-Sud (Qc), married before census 1714 Abraham GAUDET
2 CONT
2 CONT       8) Pierre, born about 1670 (rec. 1671, rec. 1686), 1671 (rec. 1693) or 1672 (rec. 1699) Port-Royal (Acadie), died 1758-04-25 Braintree (Massachusetts), USA, married about 1694 Marie Josèphe BOURGEOIS, married about 1705 Anne
2 CONC  LEBLANC
2 CONT
2 CONT       9) René, married Port-Royal (Acadie) 1715-12-18 Marie HÉBERT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes (White); Dictionnaire des Acadiens d'Archange Godbout; Acadian Church Records; http://www.umoncton.ca/etudeacadiennes/centre/cea.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/086/086123.php
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Marie Bourg was the oldest daughter of Antoine Bourg & Antoinette (Landry) Bourg.  Marie was a nativeof Acadia whose parents were among the earliest settlers of Acadia when they arrived as newlyweds in 1636. She spent over half of
2 CONC  her 86 years as a widow, managing to finish raising her large family with the help of her sons. (Norma Lewis)
2 CONT --------------------
