2 CONC ritten in French) pgs 133 - 140 4. Brault name in Carole Brow letter (on the Web) 6/97 5. Place of death given by given by the Breaux Du Monde newsletter & society. 6. The 1671 Acadian Census Arsenault. 7. Marriage record from Loi
2 CONC selle Marriage Index (film#543,747) shows parents of both bride & groom, as well as date. 8. #14 --"A Breau Genealogy" by Clarence T. Breaux& Robert Brault "The 1671 census of Port Royal shows Pierre with his parents. He is also s
2 CONC hown with them in the 1678 census and with his widowed mother in the 1686 census. Shortly after his marriage he moved to the Grand Pre' area and settled at Riviere aux Canards. Following the death of his first wife he married agai
2 CONC n and is shown in the 1714 census at that location with this second wife, threesons and three daughters. In 1755 he and Anne were deported to Massachusetts. On 25 April 1757 he is listed as Pierre Braux, 87, with wife Ann, 77, liv
2 CONC ing in Braintree MA. In 1760 he is shown as Peter Brow with wife Hannah as sent to Boston."
2 CONT
