2 CONT == Research ==*Karen Theriot Reader, Geneanet.org, citing: "The Passenger List of the Ship SAINT-JEHAN and the Acadian Origins," in FRENCH CANADIAN AND ACADIAN GENEALOGICAL REVIEW; 1600-1700; vol. 1, no. 1 (spring 1968); p. 55; ::
2 CONC Pierre BRAU had his marriage contract at Les Mines drawn up in 1693 by a notary of Port-Royal, and seven years later the inventory of marriage co-ownership (Reference: Rameau, UNE COLONIE FEODALE; 1889, vol. II; pp. 318-1319 [sic]
2 CONC ). [Originals could still have been destroyed in1710.] Note: The [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/stjehan.htm scan of the passenger list] has only "Pierre Brault" as a passenger.
