2 CONT
2 CONT In 1761, John is identified with his family in Miramichi by Pierre DuCalvet. He was appointed "Dianne" and had a family of seven boys and five girls. We only know the name of nine children, five boys and four girls. It endoyait ch
2 CONC ildren in Miramichi in the absence of the missionary.
2 CONT
2 CONT The arbitrators decided that the land of Amand and Joseph should be divided into equal sizes and that they should settle their accounts in the presence of Otho Robichaud, they should follow the advice. This document is in the pres
2 CONC bytery of Burnt Church, was later translated into English by William em Ferguson then be registered at Newcastle. Amand, Joseph François Savoie and made their marks, while Michel Allain and Father Bourg signed the document.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Savoie died before 1791. Her children, unable to agree on the division of property, had recourse to the missionary Mathurin Bourg June 18, 1791 to resolve the dispute. Then it was agreed on the appointment of three arbitrator
2 CONC s to settle the dispute: Father Mathurin Bourg, and Florent Otho Robichaud. Under the agreement, the arbitrators' decision would be final and respected all of a penalty of $ 25 British Pounds. Mgr Donat Robichaud, Greffe de Newcas
2 CONC tle, vol. 9, P. 197, no 92; enregistré le 18 septembre 1811.
2 CONT
