2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography =='''Amant Gregoire Savoye''' was born  30 March 1727. He was the son of[[Savoie-64|Germain Savoie]] and [[Babineau-31|Geneviève Babineau]].He was baptized the next day at Annopolis Royal, Acadia. His godparents were 
2 CONC René La Noue, son of Pierre La Noue and Magdelaine Blanchard,daughter of Antoine Blanchard.≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Amant Gregoire Savoye baptism RG 1 volume 
2 CONC 26 page 368 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1589≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada,Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-.)-1870 C-1870 (image 212) http://heritage.canadiana
2 CONC .ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/212?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT Amant Savoye, son of Germain Savoye and Genevieve Babinot married Jeanne Victoire Blanchard, dauhgter of Guillaume Blanchard and Jeanne Dupuis 3 February 1749 at Annopolis Royal, Acadia. There was a dispensation for 3-4 consanguin
2 CONC ity. Witnesses were Pierre Lanoue, Charles Bourg, François Miraut, François Bourg, Baptiste Raimon and Michel Bourgeois.≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Amant Savoye 
2 CONC and Jeanne Victoire Blanchard marriage RG 1 volume 26a page 378 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=3073≤/ref>
2 CONT We last see Amand on the 12 August 1763 Census - SC: Aman SAVOY, listed with his wife Victoire BLANCHARD, and two sons.≤ref>Acadian Exiles in the Colonies - Janet Jehn - Covington, KY: Author, 1977 - pp. 226 & 235≤/ref>
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />BIRTH-BAPTISM-MARRIAGE-CENSUS: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes - Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714 - Stephen A. White - 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Ce
2 CONC ntre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999 - p. 1462
2 CONT * BIRTH-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-IMMIGRATION: Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS; 1625-1810; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, 6 vols.; p. 797 (Port Royal)
2 CONT * Les Savoie, une grande famille acadienne au nouveau-brunswick. Fidele Theriault.
2 CONT
