2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Josèphe Richard was born in 1691 in Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France. Her parents were [[Richard-70|Alexandre Richard]] and [[Petitpas-3|Isabelle Petitpas]]. She married François Savoye, son of Germain Savoye and Marie Br
2 CONC au on November 23, 1707 at Port Royal.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had 13 children:
2 CONT # [[Savoie-161|Marie-Josèphe Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-162|Francois Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-153|Brigitte Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-638|Marguerite Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-152|Jean Baptiste Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-154|Honore Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-40|Jeanne Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-155|Anne Marie Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-156|Madeleine Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-134|Jean-Charles Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-636|Simon Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-159|Joseph Savoie]]
2 CONT # [[Savoie-158|Pierre Savoie]] She died in 1734 in Acadie 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===In records 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1693cens.htm 1693 Acadian Census], at Port-Royal, Acadie, age 22 years.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 Acadian Census micr
2 CONC ofilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-] </ref>			:Alexandre RICHARD 25, Isabel PETITPAS, Jean Baptiste 6, '''Marie Josephe 2'''; 8 cattle, 10 sheep, 8 pigs, 18 arpents, 1 gun 
2 CONC :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1698cens.htm 1698 Acadian Census], at Riviere St. Jean. It isn't clear if she is the "Marie", both "Marie" and "Marie-Josephe" are listed on the census 0f 1700 but neither are listed in 1701.<ref>The
2 CONC  original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/107?r=0&s=3 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 107-109] </ref>			:
2 CONC Alexandre RICHARD 30; Elisabeth PETITPAS (wife) 30; Marie 10; Marguerite 6; Jeanne 4; Pierre 2; 12 cattle, 20 sheep, 10 hogs, 16 arpents, 1gun, :[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Acadian Cens
2 CONC us], Port-Royal.<ref>The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Ima
2 CONC ges 151-173] </ref>:Alexandre RICHARD, 32; Elisabeth PETITPAS (wife) 35; Jean-Baptiste 13; Pierre 3; Jean 1; '''Marie-Josephe 9'''; Marie 8; Marguerite 7; Jeanne 5; Angelique 2; 12 cattle, 14 sheep, 20 arpents, 2 guns. :[http://fr
2 CONC eepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Acadian Census], Port-Royal].<ref>The original census can be foundat [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 
2 CONC of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.]</ref>:Alexandre RICHARD 38, Isabel PETITPAS (wife) 30; Pierre 5, Jean-Baptiste 1; servant: Ame Petitpas 13; 1 gun, 10 cattle, 15 sheep, 7 hogs
2 CONC , 4arpents.
2 CONT
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1707cens.htm 1707 Acadian Census]:Alexandre RICHARD and his wife, 4 boys less than 14, 2 girls 12 or older, 2 younger girls; 6 arpents, 10 cattle, 14 sheep, 10 hogs, 2 guns
2 CONT
2 CONT :[http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1714cens.htm 1714 Acadian Census] :Alexandre RICHARD and wife, 4 sons.
2 CONT
