2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Baptiste Savoie''' was born 9 MAR 1714/15 in Port Royal, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 27 DEC 1787 in St Cuthbert, Quebec, Canada . He was buried 28 DEC 1787 in age 73, St Cuthbert, Quebec, Canada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie Hache on 11 AUG 1734 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada . 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Francois Savoie and Marie Josephe Richard . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wc-rootsweb-com.translate.goog/trees/109046/I00315/jeanbaptiste-savoie/registry?_x_tr_sl=fr&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=sc
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean Baptiste /Savoie/ and Marie /Hache/ are:
2 CONT # Marie Josephe Savoie was born AFT 1734.
2 CONT # Marguerite Savoie was born ABT 1736, and died BEF 4 OCT 1765.
2 CONT # Madeleine Savoie was born ABT 1738, and died 7 MAY 1809 in Louiseville, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Rosalie Savoie was born 30 OCT 1741 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 27 OCT 1789 in Quebec City, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Marie Anne Savoie was born ABT 1744 in Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 3 MAR 1790 in Riviere du Loup (Louiseville), Maskinonge, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Madeleine Savoie was born 9 APR 1745 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada .
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste Savoie was born 20 JUN 1748 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 1 NOV 1811 in Louiseville, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Pierre Savoie was born ABT 1752 in St Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec, Canada , and died 29 MAY 1830 in age 94, St Barthelemy, Berthier, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Marie Francoise Savoie was born ABT 1753 in Chipoudy, Acadia, Canada , and died 7 FEB 1832 in St Jacques de l’Achigan, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Female Savoy was born BET 1754 AND 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Baptiste Savoye''' was born 9 Mar 1715. He was a twin to Honore. He was the son of [[Savoie-65|François Savoie]] and [[Richard-174|Marie-Josèphe Richard]]. He was baptized the day of his birth at PortRoyal. His godparents 
2 CONC were Jean Savoye and Angelique Richard.<ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Jean Baptist Savoye baptism 9 March 1715 RG 1 volume 26 page 133 https://novascotia.ca/archive
2 CONC s/acadian/archives.asp?ID=552</ref>
