2 CONT {{One Name Study|name=Savoie|category=Louisiana, Savoie Name Study}} 
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Charles was born 30 May 1721<ref>Edmund West, comp.. Family Data Collection - Births [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2001. Family Data Collection - Births<br/>
2 CONT '''Text:'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;'''Name: Charles Savoie'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Father: Francois Xavier Savoie<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Mother: Josephe Marie Richard<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;'''Birth Date: 30 May 1721'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;City: Port Royal<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;County: Acadia<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;State: Ns<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Country: Canada</ref> in Port Royal, Acadia. He was the 10th child of [[Savoie-65|François Savoie]] and [[Richard-174|Marie-Josèphe Richard]]<ref>Mawhorter, Bill. http://savoiegenealogy.blogspot.com/. 6 Jan 2009. Accessed 27
2 CONC  Aug 2017.<br/>
2 CONT '''Text:'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;'''Third Generation'''<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;28. Francois-Xavier SAVOIE (Germain-2, Francois-1) was born about 1684 in Port-Royal, Acadia. He lived in Chipoudy, Acadia on 11 Aug 1734. This is when son Jean-Baptiste was married. In the Port-Royal census of 1686, Francoi
2 CONC s is age 2; in 1693 age 9; in 1698 age 14; in 1700 age 16; and in 1701 age 18.<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;Francois-Xavier SAVOIE and Marie-Josephe RICHARD were married on 23Nov 1707 in Port-Royal, Acadia (St-Jean Baptiste). Marie-Josephe RICHARD (daughter of Alexandre RICHARD and Isabelle (Elizabeth) PETITPAS) was born in 1691 i
2 CONC n Port-Royal, Acadia. Francois-Xavier SAVOIE and Marie-Josephe RICHARD had the following children:<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+119 i.Marie-Josephe SAVOIE (born on 25 Apr 1709).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+120 ii. Francois-Xavier SAVOIE (born on 30 Nov 1710).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+121 iii. Brigitte-Marguerite SAVOIE (born on 12 Apr 1712).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+122 iv. Marguerite SAVOIE (born on 20 Aug 1713).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+123 v. Jean-Baptiste SAVOIE (born on 9 Mar 1715).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+124 vi. Honore SAVOIE (born on 9 Mar 1715).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+125 vii. Marie-Jeanne SAVOIE (born on 28 Sep 1716).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+126 viii. Anne-Marie SAVOIE (born on 2 Jun 1718).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+127 ix. Madeleine SAVOIE (born on 5 Dec 1719).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;'''+128 x. Charles dit Jean-Charles SAVOIE (born on 30 May 1721).'''<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+129 xi. Simon SAVOIE\SAINT-SAUVEUR (born on 17 Aug 1723).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+130 xii. Pierre SAVOIE (born in 1725).<br/>
2 CONT &emsp;&ensp;+131 xiii. Joseph SAVOIE (born on 8 Jun 1727).</ref> and a first generation Louisianian. He was married three times and fathered 11 children before his death at the age of 59{{citation needed}}.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriages ===
2 CONT Charles married his third wife [[Arceneau-6|Judith Arcenault (Arceneaux)]]<ref>Edmund West, comp.. Family Data Collection - Individual Records [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2000. Birth year: 1721
2 CONC ; Birth city: Port Royal; Birth state: Ns.<br/>
2 CONT '''Text:'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;'''Name: Charles Savoie'''<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Spouse: SavoieJudith<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Parents: Richard Francois Marie<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Birth Place: Richmond, Port Royal, Ns<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;Birth Date: 30 May 1721<br/>
2 CONT &ensp;'''Marriage Date: 7 Jan 1761'''</ref> on 7 Jan 1761 while in Restigouche. Judith's sister [[Arseneau-8|Marie Arceneau]] and husband [[DesRoches-22|Julien DesRoches]] were recently deceased and Judith was raising their now si
2 CONC x year old son [[DesRoches-44|Basile DesRoches]].<ref>Cormier, Steven A. Acadians in Gray. http://www.acadiansingray.com. Copyright (c) 2000-17  Steven A. Cormier. [http://www.acadiansingray.com/Acadians%20of%20LA-Intro-1.htm#THE_
2 CONC ACADIANS_OF_LOUISIANA Book Six: The Acadian Immigrants of Louisiana]. Accessed 27 Aug 2017.<br/>
2 CONT '''Text:''':Julien DesRoches and his wife Marie Arseneau died on the eve of Île St.-Jean's fall, so their children were raised by relatives.  One of the younger ones, Basile, was only three years old when the British came in 1758.
2 CONC   He was raised by his maternal aunt Judith Arseneau, only 19 years older than Basile and still unmarried when she took him into her care.  She married Charles dit Jean-Charles, son of fellow AcadiansFrançois Savoie and Marie-Josè
2 CONC phe Richard of Annapolis Royal and widower of _____ and Marie-Madeleine Richard, at Restigouche in January 1761, after the British attacked the French stronghold the previous summer.  They evidently were not among the 300 Acadians
2 CONC  the British had packed off to prisoner-of-war compounds in Nova Scotia after the attack, but sometime in the early 1760s they either surrendered to, or werecaptured, by British forces and joined their fellow Acadians in Nova Scot
2 CONC ia.  In August 1763, British officials counted Basile, along with the Savoies, at Halifax, probably in the prison compound on Georges Island.</ref>   
2 CONT
