2 CONT == Biography ==:Pierre Savoie, son of Francois Savoie and Marie Josephe Richard, was born about 1734. <ref>Source: [[#DGFA]]   p. 1461 No place given for birth</ref> <ref>Title: Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes, [
2 CONC http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac/wf/wf/pdf/cor-dict.pdf "Ajouts et corrections"]; Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: University of Moncton, Centre d'études acadiennes; Online; Appeared in Nov 1999 & Sep 2003;
2 CONC  for p. 1461:Text: Pierre was born around 1734 [when his mother would have been about age 43]. </ref> Pierre died 13 May 1811 in St-Luc, Quebec, Canada and was buried there 15 May 1811.<ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] p. 1461:Text: Pierre d
2 CONC ied/was buried (Register of St-Luc, Quebec) on 13/15 May 1811, age around 77 years.</ref>
2 CONT :Francois Savoie married (1) Anne Felicite Lord, daughter of Jean Lordand Marie Madeleine Comeau about 1756 in Acadie. <ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] p.  1461</ref> :Pierre was a witness to the marriage of his nephew Joseph COMEAU (sonof 
2 CONC Brigitte) in 1759 (Quebec Register); also witness for his niece Marie-E'lisabeth THIBODEAU (daughter of Anne-Marie in 1762 (Quebec Register).<ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] p.  1461</ref> :He married (2) Anne Melanson, daughter of Claude M
2 CONC elanson & Marguerite Babineau, 27 Jul 1761 in Charlesbourg, Quebec, Canada. <ref>Source: [[#DGFA]]  pp. 1165 & 1461</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==* Source: <span id='DGFA'>DGFA</span> Title: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes; Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999. Copy in possess
2 CONC ion of  [[Girouard-4019|Girouard-4019]].
2 CONT
