1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Charles Babineau
2 CONT * Birth:	Oct 10 1722 - Acadie
2 CONT * Death:	Jan 1 1775 - Becancour, Qc
2 CONT * Parents:	Rene dit Reynaud Babineau dit Deslauriers, Marie Madeleine Savoie
2 CONT * Wife:	Cecile Comeau 
2 CONT * Children:	Charles Justinien Babineau Deslauriers, François Xavier François Babineau, Antoine Dominique Babineau, Jean Baptiste Babineau, Marguerite Doucet, Marie Angelique Babineau, Genevieve Babineau, Augustin Babineau
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Babineau-142
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Delorier was born 10 Oct 1722. He was the son of Rene Babineau and Marie Savoie. He was baptized at birth by Marie Dugas and ceremonies took place18 Oct 1722 at Annapolis Royal. His godparents were Charles Melanson and Mar
2 CONC ie Joseph Savoye.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Cecile Comeau, daughter of François and Marie Madeleine Lord, about 1750 in Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to historian André-Carl Vachon, Charles and Cécile were deported to Georgia and made their way back to Acadie. They were aboard the ship La Flore which left Isle Saint-Jean on 9 August 1756 and arrived at the port of Que
2 CONC bec on 25 August 1756. On that day, Charles was hospitalized at Hotel Dieu hospital in Quebec. [3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 additional children not recorded are Geneviève Babineau, born in April 1756 in RIVIERE MORAMCOU DANS L'ACADIE, baptized on 29 July 1756 in Notre-Dame cathedral of Quebec city; Augustin Babineau, born 24 March 1766 in St-Charles 
2 CONC (Bellechasse), QC.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Babineau_Charles&pid=180461
