2 NOTE Guillaume Couillard was knighted in December 1654 , under the administration of the governor of New France Jean de Lauzon for “  his fine actions in the country of Canada  ”. However, his letters of nobility were revoked, which of
3 CONC ficially made Pierre Boucher de Boucherville the first Canadian settler to be ennobled; also first to be ennobled directly by Louis XIV in France, in 1661.
3 CONT In 1668 , the letters of nobility were renewed in favor of two of his sons, Louis Couillard de L'Espinay and Charles-Thomas Couillard des Islets and Beaumont, as well as their descendants.
3 CONT
