1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mathilde Marie COOK Posey was born during the American Civil War, 1861-1865 the daughter of British child immigrant from London, England; Frederick Henry Cook, Sr. and his wife Tamelie Roselie CAVELIER Cook. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father: being the son of British immigrants Henry 'Harry' Cook, Sr. and Ann Bradwin WRIGHT Cook. Their family immigrated to New York in 1833/4 when Frederick, Mathilde's father was only 5 years old. He grew up in New York City
2 CONC  before he later migrated to New Orleans, LA in 1852.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother: being of the Cavelier family; longtime citizens of New Orleans well before the Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and the daughter of Charles Louis Henri Cavelier, Sr. and Tamelie Adelaide MASCEY Cavelier.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Mathilde was young, the Cook family moved around a good bit with her father's industrial employ as they lived in Louisiana, Illinois, Canada, and New York before finally returning to New Orleans, LA where Mathilde married Edw
2 CONC ard Lloyd Posey, Sr. on 20 Dec 1884. The young couple raised their children in New Orleans, LA. Her husband was a well respected businessman, practitioner of the Law, and elected Senator in the Louisiana State Legislature, 1888.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once widowed, she lived for 15 years in Houston, TX with her daughter Rosalind Marie POSEY Pincoffs and family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathilde and Edward Lloyd's children are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Gilbert Posey (died age 6) 2. Ethel Marie POSEY Webre b.1887 3. Edward Lloyd Posey, Jr. b.1888 4. Mathilde Ethel POSEY Wogan (1893-1984) 5. Helena Marie POSEY Kernaghan b.1894 6. Rosalind Marie POSEY Pincoffs (1896-1972) Inscri
2 CONC ption: MATHILDE MARIE COOK BELOVED WIFE OF E. LLOYD POSEY, SR. MAY 26, 1864 - JAN. 23, 1942 (Dual stone engraving with her son Edward Lloyd Posey, Jr.)
