1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Walter Henry Cook was born the son of Frederick Henry Cook, Sr. and Tamelie Roselie CAVELIER Cook.  His father being a British child immigrant born in London, UK and later a successful inventor and businessman.  Hi
2 CONC s mother being born into a well respected, established, and early New Orleans family that migrating from Rouen, Normandy, France during the early years of the city.
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon after Walter's birth, the Cook family was on the move with his father’s busy employ which took their family to New York, Illinois, and Canada before returning to Louisiana in the late 1880’s.  Back home in his place of birth 
2 CONC Walter met and later married Marie Leoine ALDIGE Cook on 23 Jan 1893 in New Orleans, LA.  Soon Marie was with child and her daughter Leonie Gladys Cook was born into this world on 31 Mar 1894.  Most sadly Walter and the newborn ch
2 CONC ild would lose Marie likely due to complications from the pregnancy on  15 May 1894.  Marie Leonie ALDIGE Cook is laid to rest here in St. Louis Cemetery #3.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the year 1899 Walter Henry Cook would lose his own proud father, and also enter into a 2nd marriage with Louise Marie JOUBERT DE VILLEMAREST Cook on 06 Jun 1899 in New Orleans, LA. She being the daughter of Joseph Eugene "Leon"
2 CONC  Joubert de Villemarest and Claire Angele PESCHIER Joubert de Villemarest, and she being born 07 Mar 1878 in Orleans Parish, LA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The newly married couple would care for their growing family throughout their lives here in the Gulf Coast Region.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter and Marie's daughter: 1. Leoine Gladys COOK Martin b.1894 - married Joseph Denegre Martin
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter and Louise’s known children are: 2. Mabel COOK Flower b. 1900 - married Clarence Flower 3. Harold J. Cook (1901-1984) 4. Emily Marie COOK b. 1902 5. Edmond P. Cook b. 1905 Inscription: Dual Stone
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Walter H. Cook NEE Marie Leonie Aldige Died May 15 1894 Aged 20 Years
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter H. Cook 1870-1935
