1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Funeral Held for John J. Smith Of Grand Coteau 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Monday for John J. Smith, 73, prominent resident of the second ward, who died at 7 a.m. Sunday at his home in Grand Coteau.  He had been ill for several months.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body rested at Lafond and Son funeral home until 10 a.m. Monday.  Services were read at a low mass at Sacred Heart Catholic church in Grand Coteau.  Interment was in the adjacent cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith was a native of Grand Coteau and for 35 years had operated a flower nursery there.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, the former Blanche Mizzi of Grand Coteau; three sons, Kenneth of Opelousas, Charles of Grand Coteau, and J. T. of Harvey; two daughters, Mrs. E. R. Sellers of Opelousas and Miss Mercedes Smith of Grand 
2 CONC Coteau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also surviving are five sisters, Mrs. James Fox, Miss Marie Smith and Mrs. Henry Richard, all of Grand Coteau, Sister Estelle of Alton, Ill., and Mrs. Willie Devalcourt of Sunset; and six grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAILY WORLD Opelousas, Louisiana, Tuesday, March 29, 1955  Front Page and continued on page 32.  Photo on obituary also. [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=103560900  Edith Garland Dupré] Library, UL Lafayette.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Plant Now  Drive over and see Our large selections Of Camellias, Azalea, Evergreen And Fruit trees.
2 CONT  Smith's Nursery 
2 CONT
