2 CONT Walter Smith,Sr. Expires at 68
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter C. Smith, Sr., 68, of Opelousas, died at 4:05 p.m. yesterday in Houston, Tex., where he had gone for medical treatment.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was returned here and is resting at Lafond and Son Funeral home.  Services will be read at a low mass at 9 a. m. tomorrow at the Sacred Heart Catholic church in Grand Coteau.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=77614166  Father Burleigh,] pastor, will officiate at the mass.  Father Patrick Reagan of Washington will read the funeral service.  Interment will be in the adjacent cemetery
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith was a native of Grand Coteau and life long resident of St. Landry.  He owned and operated a farm on the Washington highway where he resided.  He had been in ill health for six years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors are his wife, the former Beatrice Smith of this city: two sons, Dick of Opelousas, and Walter, Jr. of Loreauville; and one daughter, Mrs. Donald Taylor of Houston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also surviving are three brothers, John of Grand Coteau, F. C. "Cook" Smith of Opelousas, and Alex of New Orleans; five sisters, Mrs. Alectar Richard, Mrs. Zita Fox, Miss Marie Smith all of Grand Coteau, Mrs. Willie Devalcourt of 
2 CONC Sunset, and Sister Estelle of Alton, Ill.; and five grandchildren.
2 CONT ------------
