2 CONT "Mothers of Acadia" (filed L-14-16) shows the following:  Martine Gauthier(#1984), spouse of Denise Gaudet (#1983), was the grandmother of all the Acadian Gaudets of America.  Born in France, she married in Port-Royal in 1645, 2 o
2 CONC r 3 years after her arrival on the Ship Aulnay.  (Denis Gaudet had come to Acadia in 1632, with his father Jean (#2005) who was 96 in 1671 and who had remarried to Nicole Coleson (#2006) from the Scottish group that ahd settled at
2 CONC  Port-Royal (Scottish Port) in 1629.
2 CONT "The Grand Families" from the internet (copy filed L-14-16) shows him born to unknown mother about 1625.
2 CONT See #2005 for more on the Gaudet Genealogy.
