2 CONT April 1997, p160), and died 1687 in Acadia (Source:
2 CONT phall@primenet.com). She married Francois Gauterot 1646 in Port
2 CONT Royal, Acadia (Source: Acadian Descendants, Vol I, by Janet
2 CONT Jehn). Children of Edmee LeJeune and Francois Gauterot are
2 CONT listed under Francois
1 NOTE Married about 1665 Pierre Vincent (born 1631) at Acadia, Canada; sources; Drouin pg 1345; "Généalogie de l'ancienne Acadie" [S-Z] pg 9. shows this family with 4 children.
2 CONT The 1671 census of Acadia shows her age 25; census filed with censuses.
2 CONT Another 1671 census of Acadia shows: PIERRE VINCENT, age 40; his spouse ANNE GAUDET, age 27; 4 children: Huguette, age 7; Thomas, age 6; Michel,age 3; Pierre, age 2.
2 CONT Family group sheet from Ancestry.com (copy filed L-14-8).
2 CONT <http://www.genealogie.com/dgaa/index.html> Add'l info (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http:www.geocities.com/Heartland/Pointe/6106/genealogy-gaudet.html>
2 CONT "Mothers of Acadia" (filed L-14-16) shows the following:  Anne Gaudet (#1985), daughter of Denis (#1983) and
2 CONT Martine Gauthier (#1985), married Pierre Vincent.  Her daughter, Huguette in Port-Royal 1684, became the wife of Jean de Bastarache, grandmother of all the Bastarache who came from the Basque Country (High Pyrenees).
2 CONT See #2005 for more on the Gaudet Genealogy.
2 CONT Durocher/Ferguson Genealogy on internet (copy filed L-14-8).
2 CONT Hebert Genealogy from the internet (copy filed L-14-8) shows this family with 6 children.
2 CONT <http://jason.gaudet.com/gaudet/gaudet_gen2a.htm>. (copy filed L-14-8).
2 CONT <http://geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga7.html> (copy filed L-14-8).
2 CONT "Généalogie de L'ancienne Acadie" [G-K] pg 1 & [S-Z] pg 9.
2 CONT "Histoire et Généalogie des Acadiens"-Arsenault Vol I, pg 407.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Their daughter Huguette married Jean Bastarache, the following pertains to him:
2 CONT It was acquired from <http://www.acadian-home.org/ancestorsacadian.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT JEAN  BASTARACHE aka BASQUE
2 CONT
2 CONT The very fact that Jean Bastarache was enumerated at Port-Royal in 1703 as Joannis LeBasque clearly attests to his place of origin. He was born abt 1658 and came to Acadia before 1685, at which time he married Huguette Vincent, da
2 CONC ughter of Pierre Vincent and Anne Gaudet. Jean Bastarache died at Port-Royal September 5, 1733. The youngest of his five children was named Pierre. He was born at Port-Royal on July 18, 1702 and married there on January 19, 1724 t
2 CONC o Marguerite Forest, daughter of René Forest and Françoise Dugas. Pierre Bastarache died at Port-Royal on May 7, 1751.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
