1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Beaubassin, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spelling, attempts to add unsourced parents or is an his
2 CONC torically important person (matriarch of Daigre family. Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Marie Gaudet is the ancestral matriarch of the Acadian Daigre/Daigle family.
2 CONT Marie was born around 1650 to parents Denis Gaudet and Martine Gauthier. ≤ref name=DGFA>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Généalogique
2 CONC  Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.:Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p668-669; 446-7.≤/ref>
2 CONT Around 1666 Marie married Olivier Daigre. Between about 1667 and 1681,she gave birth to 10 children: Jean, Jacques, Bernard, Unknown girl, Louis, Olivier, Jean, Marie, Anne, and Pierre.≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT Marie and Olivier were enumerated in 1671 at Port-Royal with their three young sons.  They owned 6 head of cattle and 6 sheep, but no cultivable land was listed.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Ro
2 CONC yal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microf
2 CONC ilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Olivier DAIGRE 28, wife, Marie GAUDET 20; Children: Jean 4, Jacques, 2, Bernard 1; cattle 6, sheep 6.
2 CONT ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT In the 1678 census their homestead was near Port-Royal was at St-Christophe, at the Ste-Marie Brook≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entrem
2 CONC ont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port-Royal: Ollvier Daigre Marie Godet 6 boys the oldest 12 years1666. 2 girls 2 years 1676 St Cristoffe 
2 CONC at the Ste Marie Brook 4 acres 6 cattle≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, possibly the same as son Olivier's 1707locale on the [http://goo.gl/maps/4SYTo south bank of the river across from Bridgetown.]  
2 CONT Olivier died in his late thirties or early forties after 1681 when hislast child was born and before 1686. Marie remarried around 1685 withJean Fardel. They appeared in the 1685 census of Port-Royal with seven Daigle children in t
2 CONC he household.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http:
2 CONC //heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal: Jean FARDEL 46, Marie GODE
2 CONC T 36; children: Bernard 16, Louis 13, Olivier 12, Jean 10, Marie 9, Anne7, Pierre 5; 1 gun, 5 arpents, 13 cattle, 9 sheep,8 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Marie died on May 2 1734 at Annapolis Royal (formerly Port-Royal), andwas buried the next day. She was about 88 years of age.≤ref>''Nova Scotia Archives'', "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapo
2 CONC lis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26a page 121; online database with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2002 Burial of Marie Godet 3 May 1734], accessed 25 Nov 2019≤br/>
2 CONT ≤blockquote>
2 CONT Priest:	De St. Poncy de La Vernède ≤br/>
2 CONT Registration Date:	3 May 1734 ≤br/>
2 CONT Event: Burial ≤br/>
2 CONT Name: Marie Godet ≤br/>died: 2 May 1734 , about eighty-eight years old, widow of the late Jean Fredelle ≤br/>Witnesses:	Jean Le Prince, Jacques Forest, Marie Daigle, Jeanne Blanchard≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT '''DNA'''. Marie Gaudet's mother was Martine Gauthier. The Mothers of Acadia Maternal DNA project is conducting ongoing research to verify their origins. In 2010, [http://www.acadian-home.org/Founding-Mothers-of-Acadia.html Stephe
2 CONC n White reported] that Martine Gauthier had a J1b1haplogroup. I don't know the details re how many of her descendants were tested to support this report. Lucie Leblanc Constantino describesone maternal tree [http://www.acadian-hom
2 CONC e.org/origins-mtdna.html here]. Ongoing test results are also reported [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. As ofMay 2014,  2 of 2 descendants have reported a J haplogroup, in
2 CONC dicating European origins.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
