2 CONT 14. PIERRE aka the elder3 GAUDET (DENIS2, JEAN1) was born Abt. 1652. He married ANNE BLANCHARD Abt. 1672, daughter of JEAN BLANCHARD and RADEGONE LAMBERT. She was born Abt. 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ANNE BLANCHARD (Widow of François Guérin):
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of PIERRE GAUDET and ANNE BLANCHARD are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 75. i. BERNARD4 GAUDET, b. Abt. 1673; d. 17 March 1750/51, Port-Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. PIERRE GAUDET, b. Abt. 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. CLAUDE GAUDET, b. Abt. 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. ABRAHAM GAUDET, b. Abt. 1679.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. MADELEINE (TWIN) GAUDET, b. Abt. 1682.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. MARIE (TWIN) GAUDET, b. Abt. 1682.
2 CONT
2 CONT 76. vii. JEANNE GAUDET, b. Abt. 1684; d. Bef. 28 April 1732.
2 CONT
2 CONT 77. viii. AUGUSTIN GAUDET, b. Abt. 1686.
2 CONT
2 CONT ix. JEAN GAUDET, b. Abt. 1690.
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------
2 CONT <http://www.geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga25.html> (copy filed L-14-4) shows the following:
2 CONT Pierre Gaudet aka the elder settled on land west of his younger brother, Pierre le young.  In the census of the Port Royal river valley for the year 1686, Pierre Godet the elder was 35 years old, his wife Anne Blanchard was 41 yrs
2 CONC  old, their children were: Gerard (stepson), aged 20 years; Bernard, aged 13; Pierre, aged 11; Claude, aged 9; Abraham, aged 7; Marie, aged 4; Madeleine, aged 4; and Jeanne, aged 2.  Pierre the elder had 4 arpents of cultivated la
2 CONC nd.  In the 1693 census of the Port Royal river valley, Pierre Godet the elder gives his age as 41 years old, his wife Anne Blanchard was 48 years old; their children were: Bernard, aged 19 years; Pierre, aged 17 years: Claudd, ag
2 CONC ed 15; Abraham, 13; Magdaleine and Marie (twins), 11; Jeanne, 9; Augustine, 7; and Jean, aged 3 years.  Pierre the elder had 26 arpents of cultivated land, 10 cattle, 12 sheep, 10 pigs and 3 shotguns.  Pierre the elder left the Po
2 CONC rt Royal river valley in 1696, leaving his farm to his eldest son, Bernard "le Vieux" (the old), who married Jeanne Terriot.  In 1698, the farm had an orchard of 50 trees.  Bernard became the chief of the branch of Gaudets who per
2 CONC petuated in this place at the same time with the descendants of his uncle Pierre Gaudet aka the young, his neighbor.  Pierre the elder settled at Beaubassin, where he expanded the most vast marsh land on the east coast of North Am
2 CONC erica.  He built his home on the hill beside the Tintamarra (today Tantramar) river.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
