2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Double In Law Marriages]]
2 CONT [[Category:Beaubassin, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT ==Attention!=='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of confusion about brothers. Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive ch
2 CONC anges. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT :'''[[Gaudet-11|Pierre 'the younger' Gaudet]] and [[Gaudet-17|Pierre 'the elder' Gaudet]] are both listed on the 1671 Census.''' They were brothers and both married women named Blanchard. Each had a son named Jean or Jean Baptiste
2 CONC . Anne born about 1645 married the elder Pierre and Marie born about 1656, married the younger Pierre. 
2 CONT :There is '''confusion''' about '''which''' Pierre Gaudet '''died''' in '''1741'''. There is a record which states a Pierre Gaudet died on 8Dec. 1741, age 89 which would give a birth year of about 1652, consistent with the older b
2 CONC rother, however their birth dates are only about 2 years apart and age at death in a record is very unreliable.  Stephen White assigns this date to the younger Pierre.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==Pierre (Lejeune) Gaudet, son of Denis Gaudet and Martine Gauthier, wasborn about 1654 in Port-Royal. He married about 1675 in Port Royal toMarie Blanchard, daughter of Jean Blanchard and Radegonde Lambert.≤ref name=
2 CONC "DGFA">Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLESACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; p. 668≤/ref>
2 CONT He is found living with his parents at age 17 in Port Royal in 1671: at Port Royal: [[Gaudet-16|Denis Gaudet]], 46,  wife, [[Gauthier-61|Martine Gauthier]] 62; Children (the first 2 married):  [[Gaudet-18|Anne]] 25,  [[Gaudet-13|M
2 CONC arie]] 21,  [[Gaudet-17|Pierre]] 20,  [[Gaudet-11|Pierre]] 17,  [[Gaudet-15|Marie]] 14;  cattle 9, sheep 13.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadianc
2 CONC ajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acad
2 CONC ie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤/ref>
2 CONT Just a few years later, he is married and living with his wife and twosons, age 3 and 5 months≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=pierre+le+jeune&n=gaudet&oc=
2 CONC 1 Karen Theriot Reader-Pierre Le Jeune Gaudet] citing Clarence J. d'Entremont, "Recensement de Port-Royal," in MEMOIRESDE LA SOCIETE GENEALOGIQUE CANADIENNE -FRANCAISE; vol. 22, no. 4; p. 231; sent by PERSI in Jun 1999. On Folio 1
2 CONC 9: Pierre GODET & Marie BLANCHARD, listed just after widowed father Onis [sic] GODET, with two boys ages 3 and 5 months.   His older brother is on the verso of Folio 19, with Anne BLANCHARD and three sons age 6, 4, and 2.≤/ref>, g
2 CONC iving him a marriage date of about 1675≤ref name="DGFA" />. Over 22 years theyhad 10 children:≤ref name="DGFA" />
2 CONT #Pierre-Will Gaudet b1676		      m  Madeleine Pellerin
2 CONT #Antoine Gaudet b 1678		      m   Marie Louise Bourg
2 CONT #Germain b1680
2 CONT #Guillaume Gaudet	b1683		   m   Marie Boudrot
2 CONT #Denis b1685                                m    Anne Doucet
2 CONT # Marguerite Gaudet	b1688	      m  Bernard Pellerin
2 CONT # Jean-Dit-Varouel Gaudet b1690   m Madeleine Brun
2 CONT #Bernard Gaudet	b1691			     m Marguerite Pellerin, Marie Doucet
2 CONT #Marie Gaudet	b1694		           m  Jean-Baptiste Prejean
2 CONT # Jeanne Gaudet b1698		            m Alexandre Pellerin
2 CONT The family had expanded to 5 boys by 1686≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original c
2 CONC ensus can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>vierre GODET, 
2 CONC the younger, 32; Marie BLANCHARD 30; Children: Pierre 10, Antoine 7, Germain 5, Guillaume 3, Denis 2 months; 2 guns, 3 arpents, 10 cattle, 18 sheep, 10 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>. Ten years later the family was almost complete when 
2 CONC Marie was pregnant with their last child in 1698≤ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The ori
2 CONC ginal census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671  1752”, Images 110-150≤blockquote>Pierre
2 CONC  GODET, the younger, 46; Marie BLANCHARD (wife) 44; Pierre 22; Antoine 20; Germain 18; Guillaume16; Denis 14; Marguerite 12; Jean 9; Bernard 7; Marie 4; 25 cattle, 35 sheep, 15 hogs, 26 arpents, 72 fruit trees, 2 guns,≤/blockquote
2 CONC >≤/ref> as the last baby is now present in 1700.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Census Transcribed]. The ori
2 CONC ginal census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 –1752”, Images 151-173.≤blockquote> Pier
2 CONC re GODET 46; Marie BLANCHARD(wife) 44; Pierre 23; Anthoine 20; Germain 18; Guillaume 16; Denis 14; Jean 10; BERNARD 5; Marie 12; Marie-Anne 3; Jeanne 2; 23 cattle, 27 sheep, 25 arpents, 3 guns.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT His land holdings became significant, with 12 arpents and quite a few animals in 1707≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.
2 CONC htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 –
2 CONC  1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>Pierre GODET, the younger, and his wife; 12 arpents, 22 cattle, 12 sheep, 22 hogs, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>.  He was only one oftwo grown Godets in Port Royal by 1714≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcripti
2 CONC on of the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac
2 CONC _reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote> Pierre GODET and wife, 3 sons, 2 daughters.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, his older brot
2 CONC her and several others were living in Beaubassin by then.
2 CONT He died having received the sacraments on December 8, 1741 and was buried at Beaubassin, Acadie ≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered: The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755. RG 1, vol. 26a, p. 212. [https://no
2 CONC vascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2520Burial Record]≤blockquote>Pierre GAUDET died 8 Dec 1741 about 89 years old, buried 9 Dec 1741. Witnesses: Guillaume BLANCHARD; Denis ST. CENE (St. Seine); Richard LE BRETON; Pierre 
2 CONC GAUDET; Charles PREJEAN. Priest was C. de la GOUDALIE.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref name="DGFA" />
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:* BIRTH-NAME-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-RESIDENCES: Bona Arsenault, H ISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS; 1625-1810; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, 6vols.; p. 555 (Port Royal) . Pierre GAUDET dit le Jeune, born 1654 [4years after 
2 CONC his brother Pierre l'Aine or Elder], sons of Denis & Martine GAUTHIER. This Pierre married around 1675 to Marie BLANCHARD [sister to the Anne BLANCHARD that married brother Pierre. BEWARE of name confusion.]. This couple had eleve
2 CONC n children.*http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Pierre_Gaudet&pid=72533&lng=fr&partID=72534
