1 NOTE {geni:about_me} !BIRTH-CHRISTENING-PARENTS-MARRIAGES-CENSUS-DEATH: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQU E DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 199 9, 2 vols.; p. 1499; own c
2 CONC opy. Francoise THE'RIOT, daughter of Claude & Agnes AUCOIN, born (B elle-Ile-en-Mer Declaration) at St-Joseph of Riviere-aux-Canard, born 27 Mar 1772, baptized ( Grand Pré Register) 26 Apr 1722. Sponsors: Jean THE'RIOT & Anne THE'
2 CONC RIOT. She was on list o f passengers from Penryn-Falmouth to France in 1763, age 28 years (sic), a widow. She marrie d 1st (B-I-M Declaration) around 1740 to Michel RICHARD, son of Michel & Marie-Josephe BOURGE OIS. She married 2n
2 CONC d (BIM Decl) at Falmouth in 1758 to Charles TRAHAN, son of Guillaume & Jac queline BENOIT (widower of Anne-Marie HE'BERT). She died (Role of 1772) at Morlaix on 1 Aug 1 773.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BIRTH-CHRISTENING: Diocese of Baton Rouge, CATHOLIC CHURCH RECORDS; 1707-1748; vol. 1a, Bato n Rouge, LA, Diocese, 1999; p. 183; own copy; Acadian records from Grand Pré, carried into ex ile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA
2 CONC . Francoise TERRIOT, daughter of Charles [sic, shou ld be Claude?] & Agnes AUCOIN, born 27 Mar 1722, baptized 26 Apr 1822. Sponsors: Jean TERRIO T and Anne TERRIOT (SGA-2, 32).
2 CONT
2 CONT !BIRTH-CHRISTENING: Eglise catholique, Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand Pré, Acadia); REGISTRE S PAROISSIAUX; 1702-1755; microfilm of original [sic] in possession of Public Archives of Can ada, Ottawa, vol. 12-1 (MG9, B8); p. 146; S
2 CONC alt Lake City Family History Library, film #048409 . Francoise TE'RIOT, legitimate daughter of Claude [sic] & Agnes AUCOIN, born 27 Mar 1722, ba ptized 26 Apr 1722. Sponsors: Jean TERIOT & Anne TERIOT. Recorded by Fr. Felix PAIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NAME-MARRIAGES: Arsenault, H&G, p. 1297, name spelled THE'RIAU.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BIRTH-PARENTS-MARRIAGES: Linda Dube', THERIAULT GENEALOGY; 1601-1993; Madawaska, ME, author , 1993; p. 219; own copy; in 2 vols., continuously pages; covers mainly the Canadian branches . Francoise THERIAULT, born 1724 [sic] at R
2 CONC iv Canards, daughter of Claude & Agnes AUCOIN, mar ried 1st in 1745 at Riv aux Canards [Grand Pré, Acadia] to Michel RICHARD; married 2nd in 175 8 at Falmouth, England to Charles TRAHAN.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MARRIAGES-RESIDENCES: Janet Jehn, ACADIAN EXILES IN THE COLONIES; 1755-1785; Covington, KY , Author, 1977; p. 27; own copy. Francoise TERRIOT, daughter of Claude & Agnes AUCOIN, marrie d Michel RICHARD, son of Michel de Beaupre' 
2 CONC & Marie BOURGEOIS; five children born 1741-1754 . They were sent to Virginia; Michel died en route to England. Francoise married 2nd in Engla nd to Charles TRAHAN; he died at Falmouth in 1761. She was in England in 1767 with child
2 CONC ren.
