1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **"Acadian Immigrants to Bayou des Écores, New Feliciana, 1785-86" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***Deported from Île St.-Jean to St.-Malo, France, aboard one of the Five Ships 25 Nov 1758, arrived St.-Malo 23 Jan 1759, age 38
2 CONT ***At Ploubalay 1762, age 41
2 CONT ***At St.-Malo 1772, age 51
2 CONT ***Sailed to la Luisiana on ''La Ville d'Archangel'', age 64
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana Dec 1785
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES (1) ploughman 23 Jan 1759arrived France on one of"Five Ships"  3 Dec 1785arrived LA on "La Villed'Archange" 1772 Census of Acadians in France shows Joseph AUCOIN - 51; laborer of St. Malo Anne Hebert - 33; sews, spins & cuts
2 CONC  Joseph Yves AUCOIN - 11 Pierre Alexis AUCOIN - 10 Jean Charles AUCOIN - 6 Francois Malo AUCOIN - 2 Gabriel Guillaume AUCOIN - 1 Anne Marie AUCOIN - 8 Sailed aboard La Ville d'Arcangel, a 600-ton frigate chartered by the Spanish g
2 CONC overnment to carry Acadian exiles from France to Louisiana. Traveled to Louisiana with his wife and six children. Departed St. Malo, France, on August 12, 1785. The ship ran out of provisions several days before reaching Balize, a
2 CONC n outpost at the mouth of the Mississippi River. Upon arrival at Balize, thirty-eight of the Acadian passengers were very ill. Spanish authorities consequently rushed medical supplies, provisions,and fresh water to the vessel. La 
2 CONC Ville d'Arcangel arrived at NewOrleans on December 3, 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aboard this ship, among others was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph AUCOIN - 64  Anne HEBERT, wife - 48  Francois AUCOIN, son - 15  Anne AUCOIN, daughter - 21  Gabriel AUCOIN, son - 13  Marie Magdelaine AUCOIN, daughter - 11  Francoise AUCOIN, daughter - 8  Jacinte AUCOIN, son - infant (b. 
2 CONC Apr. 5. 1785)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
