1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Aucoin-57
2 CONT **Drouin Institute (Archived birth and baptismal record)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT parents: Pierre Aucoin, Catherine Comeau.
2 CONT It is appropriate here to correct an error that the genealogy books have continually reproduced. Marie-Josette Aucoin was always said daughter of Rene Aucoin and Madeleine Bourg, which is false. In the will of these, drafted by th
2 CONC e Royal Notary Louis de Courville, their daughter is named Mary High Corner (Marie Aucoin) woman in Seconds noces Gregoire Maillet. She was widowed as the first wife of Victor Leblanc. So, we must eliminate from the outset this Ma
2 CONC rie Aucoin. The indirect evidence that Marie-Josette Aucoin is the daughter of Pierre Aucoin and Catherine Comeau is given to us by the marriage of her daughter Marguerite Jeanson with Joseph Comeau on August 30, 1768 in Windsor, 
2 CONC Nova Scotia, where it is said that they have an exemption from 3rd (Joseph) to 4th (Marguerite) degrees of kinship (see table).[3]  [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Aucoin-57 WikiTree]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/KCM5-T5B
2 CONT Brief Life History of Marie Josephe'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Marie Josephe Aucoin was born in July 1720, in Saint-Charles-des-Mines, Grand-Pré, Kings, Nova Scotia, Canada, her father, Pierre Aucoin, was 31 and her mother, Catherine COMEAU, was 23. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Guillaume Jamson Jeanson about 1741, in Grand-Pré, Kings, Nova Scotia, Canada. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 3 daughters.
2 CONT Marie Françoise Jeanson 1744–1826
2 CONT Marguerite Jeanson 1748–1840
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Johnson 1752–1825
2 CONT Michel Johnson 1761–1834
2 CONT Jean Neponnoene Apul Janson 1767–
2 CONT Paul Johnson 1767–1852
2 CONT Eusebe Michel Jamson 1768–
2 CONT Elisabeth Jeanson 1770–1849
2 CONT [Note spellings on last names very erratic due to Franch to English translations]
