2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Jean Bourg was born around 1684 in Port-Royal, Acadie.≤ref>White, Stephen A. Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert, ''Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes'' (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre d'études acadiennes, Université de Mo
2 CONC ncton, 1999) p. 224 & 240; #10: ≤blockquote>He was on the 1752 census at Louisbourg, age 69 years. He was buried (Port Lajoie Register) on 22 Feb 1757, age 74 years.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> He passed away in February 1757 at about 74 y
2 CONC ears of age, and was buried on 22 February of that year in the cemetery of Port-la-Joye, (sud-ouest de la Croix). ≤ref>Archives Nationales d'outre-mer État civil, Ile Saint-Jean (Port La Joye) Parish Records 1721-1758, Year, p. 3 
2 CONC [http://anom.archivesnationales.culture.gouv.fr/caomec2/osd.php?territoire=CANADA&commune=ILE%20SAINT-JEAN%20(PORT-LA-JOYE)&annee=1757 Burial ofJean Bourg 22 February 1757 ]≤/ref>
2 CONT === Residence ===
2 CONT
2 CONT :CENSUS: 1686, Port Royal, Acadia, age 3 [after 6 daughters]
2 CONT
2 CONT :CENSUS: 1693, age 9 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT :CENSUS: 1698, age 14 [or 16] years, resident, unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT :CENSUS: 1700, age 16 years.
2 CONT :CENSUS: 1752, age 69 Isle Saint-Jean≤ref>"The Island Register", hosted by Dave Hunter; [http://www.islandregister.com/1752.html The 1752 LaRoque Census of Isle St. Jean (Prince Edward Island)] updated 1/22/98,accessed  March 2020
2 CONC . [http://www.islandregister.com/1752_page2.html#port%20la%20joye p. 2 Rivière de l'ouest]≤/ref>
