2 TITL Canada, Find A Grave Index, 1600s-Current
1 NOTE Alternate spellings include THERIAULT, THERIOT,TERRIAU.
1 NOTE According to Geneviève Massignon, at least 509 families could
2 CONT be traced to Jehan Terriau in the early 1960s. In the 1671 Port
2 CONT Royal census he is given the age 70. The Terriau's were linked
2 CONT by marriage to the Dupuis before leaving France. Marguerite
2 CONT Terriot, wife of Armand Granger of Rivière-aux-Canards, was
2 CONT exiled to Belle-Île-en-Mer in 1765 where she died in 1807.
2 CONT Jean Theriot was born 1601 in Martaize, Loudun, Vienne, France
2 CONT (Source: w-boudre.ged phall@primenet.com), and died 1685 in
2 CONT Port Royal, Acadia (Source: phall@primenet.com). He married
2 CONT Perrine Bourg Abt 1635 in Loudun, France (Source: Acadian
2 CONT Descendants, Vol I, by Janet Jehn). He arrived Acadia about
2 CONT 1637 and lived in Port Royal. He died before 1686 Port Royal
2 CONT census. Also spelled Terriau or Teriot THE NAME(S) THERIAULT...
2 CONT At the time, it was common practice to modify ones family name.
2 CONT And so records indicate today's 'Theriault' name came from
2 CONT 'Terriot'-'Theriot'-'Theriau'-'Therriault' and finally to
2 CONT 'Theriault'.
2 CONT It would appear that JEHAN TERRIOT, the grand daddy of all
2 CONT 'Theriault's' in North America, was recruited as a labourer in
2 CONT New France, by Charles de Menou, Sieur D'Aulnay and Charnisay
2 CONT and Gouvernor of Acadia from 1604-1650. While JEHAN TERRIOT'S
2 CONT birth certificate is not available, the first Acadia Census of
2 CONT 1671 indicates that he lived in Port Royal and was, at the
2 CONT time, 70 years old. It is therefore safe to assume, that JEHAN
2 CONT was born 'ABT 1601'. The 1671 Port Royal Acadian Census,
2 CONT indicates that JEHAN and his family owned six cattles and one
2 CONT sheep, at the time the census was taken. Historians have not
2 CONT been able to locate records of JEHAN, Perrine and Claude (their
2 CONT oldest son)'s 'boarding pass' registering their Sea voyage from
2 CONT France to Acadia, New France however it is estimated they
2 CONT arrived in the late 1630's or early 1640's. Historical
2 CONT documents confirm that JEHAN was in fact a recruit of Charles
2 CONT de Menou in 1635. We also know that Charles de Menou of
2 CONT D'Aulnay, conducted two significant 'recruitment voyages', one
2 CONT in 1642 and another in 1644. On both occasions, he transported
2 CONT a number of families from his home parish (La Chaussee) in
2 CONT France, to Acadia, New France. During this period of time,
2 CONT JEHAN worked as a labourer, residing in the village of
2 CONT Martaize, located just a few kilometers from La Chaussee. Given
2 CONT these two facts (working for Charles de Menou and residing in
2 CONT his close proximity), is it possible that JEHAN accepted a 36
2 CONT month work contract and travelled from Port de la Rochelle
2 CONT (France) to Port Royal (Acadia), and that he and his family
2 CONT (wife Perrine and oldest son, Claude) were one of the twenty
2 CONT french families, on the 1644 voyage? While historians are
2 CONT unable to confirm JEHAN'S actual date of death, the Acadia
2 CONT Census of 1681 records 'Perrine Brault is the WIDOW of JEHAN
2 CONT TERRIOT'. By 1681, many of the 'Therriot Family' had moved to
2 CONT Beaubassin, Grand-Pre, Riviere-aux Canards and Cobequid.
2 CONT Historical records indicate, that by the early 1730's, some of
2 CONT the 'Terriot Families' had travelled up the St. John River and
2 CONT re-located in areas known today as the Province of New
2 CONT Brunswick. In early 1730, some of the Theriault families
2 CONT travelled up the St. John River and located in what is today
2 CONT known as the Province of New Brunswick.
2 CONT Children of Jean Theriot and Perrine Bourg are: Bonaventure
2 CONT Theriot, born 1636 in Port Royal, Acadia; died May 04, 1731 in
2 CONT Grand Pre, Acadia. Claude Theriot, born 1637 in France; died
2 CONT September 17, 1725 in Port Royal, Acadia. Jean Theriot, born
2 CONT 1639 in Port Royal, Acadia (Source: p-hall.ged); died Bef 1686
2 CONT (Source: p-hall.ged). Jeanne Theriot, born 1644 in Port Royal,
2 CONT Acadia; died December 08, 1726 in Port Royal, Acadia. Germain
2 CONT Theriot, born 1646 in Port Royal, Acadia (Source: Acadian
2 CONT Descendants, Vol I, by Janet Jehn); died 1676 in Port Royal,
2 CONT Acadia (Source: p-hall.ged). He married Marie Renee Brault 1667
2 CONT in Acadia (Source: w-boudre.ged). Jeanne Catherine Theriot,
2 CONT born 1650 in Port Royal, Acadia; died July 21, 1713 in Port
2 CONT Royal, Acadia. Pierre Theriot, born 1655 in Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT (Source: Acadian Descendants, Vol I, by Janet Jehn); died March
2 CONT 22, 1724/25 in Grand Pre, Acadia (Source: p-hall.ged). He
2 CONT married Cecile Landry 1683 (Source: Acadian Descendants, Vol I,
2 CONT by Janet Jehn).
