2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Discussion =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [[Project:Acadians|Acadian Project]] because of frequent duplication, variant name spelling, attempts to add unsourced parents or is an historically important person (
2 CONC matriarch of the Acadian Thériot family), and is in the Top 100 highly viewed Acadian profiles.  Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate
2 CONC  information.
2 CONT '''Last Name'''. Ambiguity still exists among researchers as to Perrine's last name due to lack of evidence other than the 1671 census.≤ref>[http://www.terriau.org/archive/sources.htm Name]≤/ref> Brault and Bourg are proposed alte
2 CONC rnatives to Rau≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?iz=36&n=rau&oc=0&p=perrine&type=fiche Perrine Rau] citing *Adrien Bergeron, LE GRAND ARRANGEMENT DES ACADIENS AU QUEBEC; 1600-1889; vol. 8, Syr-Vig; p. 49
2 CONC ; Gail Burk's copy. Name spelled Perrine RUAU, born 1611. But on p. 43, says that Jean TERRIAU married Perrine BOURG [sic] (Reference: Coll. de manuscrits: I/83). *Genevieve MASSIGNON's "Les Parlers Francais d'Acadie," p. 49. Name
2 CONC  isspelled RUAU*Janet B. Jehn, CORRECTIONS & ADDITIONS TO ARSENAULT'S HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS; 1630-1830; by author, 863 Wayman Branch Road, Covington, KY 41015, 1988; p. 10 (reference to p. 595 of Arsenault). ≤blockqu
2 CONC ote>Should be Perrine RUAU "as closely as can be determined from handwritten census, and not BOURG. (1671 census of Acadia)." Also on p. 15-16 (in reference to p. 804 in Arsenault): "Perrine BOURG should read RUAU, according to ha
2 CONC ndwritten original of 1671 census [of Acadia]."≤/blockquote>≤/ref>. Massignon determines Brault as most likely≤ref>[https://www.acadian.org/theriault.html See Point #2 Massignon]≤blockquote>Translated from Bona Arsenault  "More th
2 CONC an half of the records from 1626 to 1650 concern the names of families which we find among the families listed in the 1671 Census of Acadia: Babin, Belliveau, Bertrand, Bour, Brault (in the feminine Braude), Brun..." She continues
2 CONC  "Thenames of Blanchard, Bourg, Brault, Giroire, Godet, Guerin, Poirier, Terriot were among the tenants of the mother of Charles d'Aulnay."  It should also be noted that the 'Ruau' family does exist today in the Loire region of Fr
2 CONC ance as does the 'Reau' family but not in the area where the 'Terriot's' are said to have come from. As far as we know, the only instance in which this name shows up in any of the Acadian records and history is in the first Acadia
2 CONC n census. For these reasons, we believe that Perrine's maiden name was misunderstood and incorrectly recorded in the Census of 1671. And, since no definitive evidence is available to resolve this ambiguity, we have chosen to side 
2 CONC with the 'Brault' advocates simply because the Acadian Census of 1671 gives her lastname as Reau or Rau whose pronunciation is phonetically closer to Brault than to Bourg. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.g
2 CONC eneanet.org/katheriot?iz=36&n=rau&oc=0&p=perrine&type=fiche Perrine's Name] ≤blockquote>NAME: Her name is sometimes given by researchers as RAU, or REAU, RUAU, BREAU, even BEAU, but the only existing record giving her name is the 
2 CONC first census of Port Royal, Acadia in 1671.There are two versions of this document, in two different handwritings, both apparently done near the same time. One is found in France, the other is in the Canadian archives. [There is a
2 CONC lso another Acadian woman in 1671 named Perrine BOURG married to René LANDRY.]
2 CONT ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT ''Until more documentation is found, her last name will be Rau as found on the only original document in existence.''
2 CONT Given Perrine's ambiguous identity, it follows that her parents are not known. [[Brault-17 | René Brault]] and [[Renaulme-1 | Marie Renulme]] have been suggested as being Perrine's parents, but DNA evidence would suggest Perrine d
2 CONC oes not share the same mother as Marie's daughter[[Brault-6 | Renée]]≤ref>[[Space:Roland_Arsenault_-_notes_de_recherche#Are__Perrine_Rau_and_Ren.C3.A9e_Brault_sisters.3F|Notes on mtDNA results]]≤/ref> Also, René would have been ar
2 CONC ound 8 years old when Perrine was born.
2 CONT ''No parents may be added without documentation and discussion with the Project.''
2 CONT '''DNA'''.  Perrinne Rau's maternal DNA is H4a ≤ref>[http://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults FTDNA Mothers of Acadia project results]≤/ref> Ongoing test results are also reported [https:/
2 CONC /www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. As of May 2014, 8 descendants have consistently reported a  haplogroup H, indicating European origins. Maternal family trees linked to mtDNA are f
2 CONC ound at WikiTree (see connection upper right corner of this profile page), as well as on Lucie LeBlanc Constantino`s [http://www.acadian-home.org/origins-mtdna.html origins page].
2 CONT '''FIrst Spouse Pierre Brouillard'''. Some trees maintain that PerrineRau/Reau was the first wife of Pierre Brouillard. They were married in 1628 in Chalons France, when she was around 17 years old. They separated after the birth 
2 CONC of their first child [[Brouillard-114|Louis]], born 1635 in Chambon France. Perrine went to Acadia while Pierre stayed in France. Pierre remarried (Marguerite Pognon) as did Perrine (Jean Terriau/Theriot). Source to track down: Fa
2 CONC mily records of Lee Marie Brouillard (2011 Edmonton Canada) who cites Maritime Archives - Ministry of the Colonies Records, Paris France.   ''These towns are many km apart (about 600 each way) so this would be an unlikely relation
2 CONC ship in 1627.''
