2 CONC  p. 5 2, household of Bonaventure TERRIOT, Jeanne BOUDROT, on 1 a rpent, with 7 cattle, 1 gun. There are 3 girls, ages 10 , 5 and 3 [could this be months?]. The editor names them a s Marie, born 1666/1668; Anne, born1673/1674, and
2 CONC  unnamed , born 1675. A footnote says: "It was their daughter Mari e TERRIOT who was to marry Claude GAUTROT. The Marie TERRIO T who will marry Pierre LeBlanc was the daughter of Claud e TERRIOT & Marie GAUTROT." !CENSUS: 1686, Po
2 CONC rt Royal, Acadia, age 43 years, name spell ed TE'RIO, with wife 42 and 2 daughters. They had 1 gun , 4 arpents of land, 5 horned animals, 6 sheep, and 2 p igs. !CENSUS: 1693, Port Royal, Acadia. Age 49 years (sic), wit h 14 arpent
