2 CONC un, 3 girls: 10, 1668; 5, 1673; 3, 1675.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  By 1686, the oldest daughter and newly married Marie had left the household. Only Anne and Marguerite were living with their parents. The young unnamed girl who was ment
2 CONC ioned inthe previous census was absent and had probably died as an infant.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal,Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Cen
