2 CONT ----:Germain Thériot was born about 1646 Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France. His parents were [[Thériot-99|Jean Thériot]] and [[Rau-71|Perrine Rau]]. He married [[Brun-11|Andrée Brun]] in 1668. ≤ref name="DGFA"> Stephen A. White,
2 CONC  DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999,2 vols.; pp. 1484 & 1488≤/ref>  Together they had 3 children:
2 CONT # [[Thériot-145|Germain Thériot]]
2 CONT # [[Thériot-147|Pierre Thériot]]
2 CONT # [[Thériot-148|Catherine Thériot]]
2 CONT :When the census of Port-Royal was taken in 1671, Germain Terriau was a farmer, age 25 and his wife Andree Brun was age 25. There was one child Germain, age 2, 5 cattle, 2 sheep and 2 arpents of land.≤ref>1671 Acadian Census, at P
2 CONC ort-Royal, Acadie The original census can be foundat [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 3-
2 CONC 14.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm Transcription of census]≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :He died in 1676 in Port-Royal, Acadie. ≤ref name="DGFA"/>
