2 CONT Catherine Theriot, daughter of Jean Theriot and Perrine Rau, emigrantsfrom France, was born about 1650 in Port-Royal, Acadie. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]]≤/ref>She was age 21 on the 1671 census of Port-Royal.≤ref>Source: [[#S66]]≤/ref>
2 CONT Catherine and Pierre Guilbeau married about 1668 in Port-Royal. There are 7 known children born to Catherine and Pierre. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] pp. 780 & 1484, GUILBEAU #1, No place given for marriage, no parents given for groom.:
2 CONC Text: He married around 1668 to Catherine THÉRIOT, daughter of Jean & Perrine RAU; seven children listed.≤/ref>
2 CONT Caterine Teriot, widow of Guillebaud died in Port-Royal in July 1713, aged more than 60 years and was buried 21 July 1713 upriver in the cemetery of St Laurent chapel.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholiq
