2 CONT • Biography: 4 5 October 1687: Claude Thériot est signataire d'une attestation en faveur de l'oeuvre du govereneur d'Aulnay; la famille Thériot est donc arrivée en Acadie avant 1650, l'année de la mort de d'Aulnay (ANF, Col, C11D,
2 CONC  vol II, fol 85). 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Biography: August 1695 (old time): Claude Thériot et son frère Bonaventure prêtent le serment d'allégeance au roi d'Angleterre àPort-Royal; ils font leurs marques (Mass. Arch. volII, fol 540). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Biography: 4 5 October on 1687: Claude Thériot is signatory of a certificate in favour of the work of the govereneur of Aulnay; the Thériot family therefore arrived in Acadie before 1650, the year of the death of d' Aulnay (ANF,
2 CONC  Collar, C11D, flight II, crazy 85). 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Biography: August 1695 (old time): Claude Thériot and his brother Bonaventure take the oath of loyalty to the ÀPort-royal king of England; they make their marks (Mass. VolII, crazy Arch 540). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 5 October 1687: Claude Theriot has signed a certificate for the work of governor Aulnay; Theriot family is arriving in Acadia before 1650, the year of the death of d'Aulnay ANF, Col, C11D, vol II, fol 85).
2 CONT
2 CONT August 1695 (old time): Claude Theriot and his brother Bonaventure take the oath of allegiance to the King of England at Port-Royal, they make their mark (Mass. Arch. VolII, fol 540).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Était à Port-Royal en 1704. Au recencement de 1671, en Acadie avec sa femme et 4 enfants: Germain, 9; Marie, 6; Marguerite, 4; et Jehan, 1. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT While CLAUDE'S birth certificate is not available, the first Census of Acadia in 1671, records him to be 34 years of age at the time. It is therefore safe to assume that Claude was born ABT 1637". This same census indicates that C
2 CONC LAUDE owned six cattle and one sheep. The Port Royal Acadian census of 1678-79 indicates that CLAUDE TERRIOT and Marie Gautrot owned 3 acres of  land, and 5 cattles. At the time, they had 3 boys age 16 (born in 1662), age 9 (born 
2 CONC in 1669), age 1 (born in 1677) and four girls; age 14 (born in 1664), age 12 (born in 1666), age 8 (born in 1670) and age 4 (born in 1674). The children are not named in the Census.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT MARRIAGE: 1660, Port Royal, NS
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:   Madeleine TERRIOT
2 CONT
