2 CONT By 1707, all the children had left the home. Claude, 70 years of age and Marie, then 62, were listed in the census as living alone, without any land holdings or farm animals.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1707 Acadian Censu
2 CONC s at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian
2 CONC  Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Claude TERRIOT and his wife. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  Their situation was the same in 1714.≤ref
2 CONC >Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canad
2 CONC iana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Claude TERRIOT and his wife. ≤/blockquo
2 CONC te>≤/ref>
2 CONT Claude  passed away and  was buried at Annapolis Royal (formerly Port Royal) on September 17 1725 at 87 years of age.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-
2 CONC 1870 (image 84) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/84?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755Claude Teriau burial RG 1 volume 26 page 222  
2 CONC https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1055≤/ref>  Marie died 7 years later at the age of about 87.
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:* Paternal relationship is confirmed to Thériot-99 by a triangulated group consisting of [[Nash-3461|John Nash]] GEDmatch  A710955, [[Landry-1199|Robert Joseph Landry]] GEDmatch  M695728 and [[Lajiness-24| Kevin Lajiness]
2 CONC ] GEDmatch M658673 sharing a 10.8 cM segment on chromosome1 from 232938635 - 236793313 (10.394 cM), 232938635 - 236788800 Overlap with previous match* [http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Theriault_Claude
2 CONC &pid=973372&lng=fr Nos Origines]
