2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:MtDNA Haplogroup H4a1]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication and variant name spelling and is among the Top 100 most highly viewed A
2 CONC cadian profiles. Please contact the Acadian Project before makingany substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Claude was born around 1637.≤ref name=DGFA>White, Stephen A. Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert, ''Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes'' (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre d'études acadiennes, Université de Moncton, 1999) p.1
2 CONC 484-1486≤/ref> His age was given as 34 in the1671 Port Royal Census.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census 
2 CONC Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.
2 CONC ≤blockquote>*(listed in his father's household) Jean TERRIAU, 70, wife, Perrine RAU 60; Children (married): Claude 34, Jean 32, Bonaventure 30, Germain 25, Jeanne 27, Catherine 21; (not married): Pierre 16; cattle 6, sheep1.*(list
2 CONC ed in his own home) Claude TERRIAU 34, wife, Marie GAUTEROT 24; Children: Germain 9, Marie 6, Marguerite 4, Jehan 1; cattle 13, sheep 3, 6 arpents of cultivated land.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  He was the eldestchild of [[Thériot-99|Jean
2 CONC  Thériot]] and [[Rau-71|Perrine Rau]]. His location of birth is uncertain. The Theriot family arrived in Acadiebefore 1650, prior to the death of Acadian Governor d'Aulnay in that year.  Claude, although 13 years old at the time o
2 CONC f his death, attested to d'Aulnay's accomplishments in a letter dated 5 October 1687. ≤refname=DGFA/>
2 CONT Around 1661≤ref>Year before the birth of first child, Germain≤/ref> Claude married [[Gautrot-20|Marie Gautrot]], daughter of [[Gautrot-42|François]] and [[Lejeune-21|Edmée Lejeune]], at Port Royal quite possibly, according to the 
2 CONC declarations of their descendants at Belle-Isle-en-Mer. ≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=claude&n=theriot  ClaudeTheriot] citing Acadians in France, The vo
2 CONC l. II - Milton P. and NormaGaudet Rieder - Metairie, LA: Authors, 1972 - vol. II: Belle Isle en Mer Register & La Rochette Papers - Family History Library - Family History Library, 35 North West Temple, Salt Lake City UT 84150 - E
2 CONC UROPE 944 W2r v.2 - p. 50 ≤Blockquote>In the Belle-Ile-en-Mer Declaration ofPierre DOUCET, he said of his great-great-grandfather Claude THERIOT:"who came from France, married at Port Royal to Marie Gautrot and bothof them died at
2 CONC  the said place."≤/blockquote> ≤/ref> ≤ref name=DGFA/>Between about 1662 and 1693, the couple had 14 children: [[Thériot-144|Germain]], [[Therriot-3 |Marie (b.1665)]], [[Thériot-121|Marguerite(b. 1667)]], [[Thériot-146|Jean]], [[T
2 CONC heriot-238|Anne]], [[Thériot-641|Jeanne]], [[Thériot-166|Claude]], [[Thériot-149|Marie]], [[Theriault-302|Madeleine]], [[Theriot-25|Pierre]], [[Terriot-24|Elisabeth]],[[Terriot-27 |Joseph]], [[Theriot-17|Marie]] (b. c1691), and [[
2 CONC Thériot-72|Marguerite]] (b.c1693). ≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT In 1678, there were 3 boys and 4 girls in the family home at Port-Royal as shown in the census. Claude and Marie owned 5 head of cattle and 3 arpents of land.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlat
2 CONC ions for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J.d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port Royal : Claude Terriot & Marie Gautrot, 3 
2 CONC acres 5 cattle. 3 boys (16 1662 Germain 1662); (9 1669 Jean 1670); (1 1678 Claude 1678). 4 girls (14 1664; Marie 1665); 12 1668 Marguerite 1667); (8 1670 Anne 1673); (4 1674 Jeanne 1675)≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT In 1686, forty-nine-year old Claude and forty-year-old Marie owned 13 arpents of land, 8 head of cattle, 6 sheep and 1 gun. Seven children between the ages of 1 and 18 were counted in the household.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription o
2 CONC f the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_
2 CONC c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Censusmicrofilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal :  Claude TERRIOT 49, Marie GOTRO his wife 40; children: Jean 18. Claude 
2 CONC 8, Pierre 2, Anne 14, Jeanne 12, Marie 7, Magdelaine 5, Elisabet 1; 1 gun, 13 arpents. 8 cattle, 6 sheep. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  Their land holdings as well as their family continued to grow as shown in the subsequent censuses betwe
2 CONC en 1693 and 1703.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [ht
2 CONC tp://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> at Port Royal:  Claude TERRIOT 55, Ma
2 CONC rie GOUTROT 48, Jeanne 18, Claude 15, Marie 12, Madeleine 12, Pierre 9, Elisabeth 7, Joseph 6, Marie 2; 12 cattle, 15 sheep, 7 pigs, 15 arpents, 1 gun  ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  ≤ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Censu
2 CONC s at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Ce
2 CONC nsus microfilm C-2572 of the NationalArchives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-150≤blockquote> at at Port Royal: Claude TERRIOT 60; Marie GOTROT 53 (wife) 53; Marie 18; Claude 17; Magdelaine 15; Pierre 13; 
2 CONC Joseph 10;Margueritte 8; 12 cattle, 20 sheep,12 hogs, 18 arpents, 50 fruit trees, 1 gun, ≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadianca
2 CONC jun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadi
2 CONC e Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 151-173.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Claude TERRIOT 62; Marie GOUTROT (wife) 55; Claude 22; Pierre 16; Joseph 13; Marie 19; Madelaine 17; Elisabeth 14; Marie 9; Marguerite 7; 10 cattle, 13 sheep,
2 CONC  15 arpents 1gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Census Transcription]. The original cens
2 CONC us can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote> at Port Royal
2 CONC : Claude TERRIOT 66, Marie GOUTROT (wife) 55; Abraham 18, Claude 13, Anthoine 10, Marguerite 17, Agnes 9, Francoise 6; 1 gun, 15 cattle, 20 sheep, 14 hogs, 12 arpents. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703
2 CONC  Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1703cens.htm 1703 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r
2 CONC =0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives ofCanada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 212-220.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Claude TERRIOT, his wife, 2 boys, 2 girls, 1 arms bearer. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT By 1707, all the children had left the home. Claude, 70 years of age and Marie, then 62, were listed in the census as living alone, without any land holdings or farm animals.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1707 Acadian Censu
2 CONC s at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian
2 CONC  Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Claude TERRIOT and his wife. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  Their situation was the same in 1714.≤ref
2 CONC >Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canad
