2 CONT
2 CONT 1693 Census      (Conflicting information) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHAUX 26, Marie TIBEADEAU 29, Angelique 6, Augustin & Pierre (twins) 3, Anthoine 1; 10 cattle, 18 sheep, 7 pigs, 6 arpents, 1 gun  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1698 Census
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHO 30; Marie TIBAUDEAU (wife) 33; Angelique 10; Charles and Rene, twins, 8; Augustine 6; Jean 4; Alexandre 2; Joseph 1; 9 cattle, 9 sheep, 6 hogs, 10 arpents, 1 gun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1700 Census
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHAUX 34; Marie THIBAUDEAU (wife) 35; Charles and Rene (twins) 10; Anthoine 8; Augustin 7; Jean 6; Allexandre 5; Joseph 3; Francois 2; Angelique 13; 12 cattle, 14 sheep, 16 arpents, 1 gun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1701 Census
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHO 30, Marie TIBAUDEAU (wife) 30; Rene and Charles (twins) 10, Jean 8, Alexandre 7, Joseph 4, Francoise 2, Jacques 1, Isabel 14; 1 gun, 6 cattle, 9 sheep, 8 hogs, 6 arpents. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1703
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHEAU, his wife, 1 girl, 1 arms bearer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1707
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles ROBICHEAU and his wife, 8 boys less than 14; 3 arpents, 14 cattle, 9 sheep, 11 hogs, 1 gun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...................................................
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepage.ntlworld.com/pitretrail/myline/paternal/CRobichaud.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Robichaud dit Cadet was born Abt. 1667 at Port Royal, Acadia, and died Bef. 18 May 1737 in Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT First wife Marie Thibodeau was born Abt. 1664 at Port Royal, Acadia, and died Abt. 1701 in Acadia.  They were married Aft. 1686 at Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1- Angelique Robichaud  b: Abt. 1687  Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 2- Charles Robichaud  b: Abt. 1690  Port Royal, Acadia; d: 25 October 1702  Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 3- Rene Robichaud  b: Abt. 1690  Port Royal, Acadia           
2 CONT
2 CONT 4- Antoine Robichaud  b: Abt. 1692  Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 5- Augustin Robichaud  b: Abt. 1693  Acadia; d: 28 March 1759  hospital, St. Malo, Ille et Villaine, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Augustin Robichaud:
2 CONT
2 CONT - 23 January 1759: Augustin disembarked at St. Malo from one of the ‘Five Ships’.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6- Jean Robichaud b: Abt. 1694  Port Royal, Acadia; d: Bef. 6 November 1758      
2 CONT             +Marie Leger  b: Abt. 1699  Port Royal, Acadia; m: 23 November 1717  Port Royal, Acadia; d: Abt. 13 December 1758  in a shipwreck on way to France
2 CONT
2 CONT 7- Alexandre Robichaud  b: Abt. 1695  Port Royal, Acadia                                      
2 CONT             +<nowiki>------</nowiki> Bourg  b: Abt. 1705  Grand Pre, Acadia; m: Abt. 1726  Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 8- Joseph Robichaud  b: Abt. 1697  Port Royal, Acadia; d: Bef. 1 July 1760 
2 CONT             +Madeleine Dupuis  b: Abt. 1707  Acadia; m: 24 May 1725  Grand Pre, Acadia; d: Bef. 1 July 1760
2 CONT
2 CONT 9- Francois Robichaud  b: Abt. 1698  Port Royal, Acadia; d: 2 May 1759  La Gonais, Ploubalay, Cotes du Nord   
2 CONT             +Agathe Turpin  b: Abt. 1708; m: Abt. 1728  Acadia; d: Aft. 1759
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Francois Robichaud:
2 CONT
2 CONT - 23 January 1759: Francois Robichaux, wife Agathe Turpin, and children Mathurin, Jean Pierre, Joseph & Genevieve disembarked at St. Malo from one of the ‘Five Ships’.  The family lived in Ploubalay 1759-1760, Plouer 1760-1763, an
2 CONC d St. Servan 1763-1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10- Jacques Robichaud  b: Abt. 1700  Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT Second wife Marie Bourg was born Abt. 1673 at Port Royal, Acadia, and died Aft. 1718.  They were married 18 June 1703 at Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1- Joseph Robichaud  b: Abt. 1704  Acadia; d: 12 March 1759  St. Servan, Bretagne           
2 CONT             +Claire Leblanc  b: 1 June 1710  Grand Pre, Acadia; m: 30 April 1726  Grand Pre, Acadia; d: Aft. 1759
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Joseph Robichaud: - 23 January 1759: Joseph Robichaux, wife Claire Leblanc, and children Michel, Isidore, Jean Baptiste, Charles, Marie Josephe, Anne Theodose, Francoise, & Marguerite Pelagie disembarked at St. Malo from
2 CONC  one of the ‘Five Ships’.  The family lived in St. Servan 1759-1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2- Marie Madeleine Robichaud  b: 25 September 1705  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 29 September 1705 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); d: 27 March 1707  Port Royal, Acadia     
2 CONT
2 CONT 3- Pierre Robichaud  b: 25 April 1707  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 26 April 1707 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); d: Aft. 1752                             
2 CONT             +Susanne Brassaud  b: Abt. 1707  Acadia; m: Abt. 1730  Acadia; d: Aft. 1752
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Pierre Robichaud: - 1752 Ile St. Jean census: Pierre Robichud dit Cadet, ploughman, native of l'Acadie, aged 45 years, he had been 21 months in the country. Married to Suzanne Brasseau, native of l'Acadie, aged 45 years.
2 CONC   They have eight children, three sons and five daughters: Pierre, aged 15 years, Olivier, aged 10 years, Phirmain Foelix, aged 19 months, Suzanne, aged 19 years, Marie Rose, aged 16 years, Marie Anne, aged 14 years, Anastazie, ag
2 CONC ed 8 years, Marie Joseph la Blanche, aged 3 years.  In live stock they have one ox, one bull, two cows, two heifers, four pigs, and four fowls.  The land upon which they are settled is situated as in the preceding cases. It was gi
2 CONC ven to them verbally by Monsieur de Bonneventure. On it, they have made a clearing for the sowing of six bushels of wheat in the coming spring.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4- Charles Robichaud  b: 10 March 1709  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 11 March 1709 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5- Marie Robichaud  b: Abt. 1712  Acadia                                       
2 CONT             +Pierre Arosteguy    m: 18 May 1737  Grand Pre, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 6- Claire Robichaud  b: 4 March 1713  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 18 April 1713 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); d: 22 October 1786  St. Martinville, LA           
2 CONT             +Jean Baptiste Hebert  b: 20 April 1711  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 20 April 1711 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); m: Abt. 1735  Acadia; d: Bef. 9 April 1766
2 CONT
2 CONT 7- Cecile Robichaud  b: 5 April 1715  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 7 April 1715 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); d: 12 June 1756  Port La Joie, Ile St. Jean       
2 CONT             +Pierre Boudrot  b: Abt. 1715; m: Abt. 1740  Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT 8- Marguerite Robichaud  b: 14 April 1718  Port Royal, Acadia; d: 12 March 1796  Becancour, Quebec   
2 CONT             +Claude Hebert  b: 18 February 1719  Port Royal, Acadia (baptism: 19 February 1719 St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal); m: Abt. 1748  Acadia; d: 6 January 1799  Becancour, Quebec
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Charles Robichaud: - 1693 Acadian census: (Port Royal): Charles Robichaux 26, Marie Tibeaudeau 29, Angelique 6, Augustin & Pierre, twins, 3, Anthoine 1; 10 cattle, 18 sheep, 7 hogs, 16 arpents, 1 gun.  - 1698 census: (Po
2 CONC rt Royal): Charles Robicho 30, Marie Tibaudeau 33, Angelique 10, Charles & Rene, twins, 8, Augustine 6, Jean 4, Alexandre 2, Joseph 1; 9 cattle, 9 sheep, 6 hogs, 10 arpents, 1 gun.  - 1700 census: Charles Robichaux 34, Marie Thiba
2 CONC udeau 35, Angelique 13, Charles & Rene, twins, 10, Anthoine 8, Augustin 7, Jean 6, Allexandre 5, Joseph 3, Francois 2; 12 cattle, 14 sheep, 16 arpents, 1 gun.  - 1701 census: Charles Robicho 30, Marie Tibaudeau 30, Isabel 14, Rene
2 CONC  & Charles, twins, 10, Jean 8, Alexandre 7, Joseph 4, Francoise 2, Jacques 1; 1 gun, 6 cattle, 9 sheep, 8 hogs, 6 arpents.  - 1707 census: Charles Robicheau, wife, 8 boys less than 14; 3 arpents, 14 cattle, 9  sheep, 11 hogs, 1 gu
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
