2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''Charles Robichaud''' was born about 1667. He was the son of [[Robichaud-81|Étienne Robichaud]] and [[Boudrot-28|Françoise Boudrot]].  He used the name Cadet at least once at the burial of his son Charles.≤ref>Nov
2 CONC a Scotia Archives, "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26 page 338; online database with images,[https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp
2 CONC ?ID=1382 Son's burial ]
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT He married first Marie Thibodeau, daughter of Pierre and Jeanne Theriot about 1686 at Port Royal.≤ref>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes. Moncton, N.-B.: Cent
2 CONC re D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print. P. 1404≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Children
2 CONT # Angelique ROBICHAUD ca 1687-1700/
2 CONT # Charles ROBICHAUD ca 1690-1702
2 CONT # Rene ROBICHAUD ca 1690-1700/
2 CONT # Antoine ROBICHAUD ca 1692-1699/
2 CONT # Augustin ROBICHAUD ca 1693-1759
2 CONT # Jean (dit Cadet) ROBICHAUD ca 1694-/1758
2 CONT # Alexandre ROBICHAUD ca 1695-
2 CONT # Joseph (dit Cadet) ROBICHAUD ca 1697-/1760
2 CONT # Francois ROBICHAUD ca 1698-1759
2 CONT # Jacques ROBICHAUD ca 1700-
2 CONT Charles ROBICHAUX signed by mark the oath of allegiance at Port Royal in Aug 1695.≤ref>Mary Brown LaRocca, "The Robichaux Family of Acadia, Massachusetts, and Main," in THE NEW ENGLAND HISTORICAL AND GENEALOGICAL REGISTER; vol. CX
2 CONC LIII, no. 569 (Jan 1989); p. 5.≤/ref>
2 CONT Charles Robucho, son of the late Etienne Robucho and Françoise Boudrot married second, Marie Bourg, daughter of the late Jean Bourg and Marguerite Martin 18 June 1703 at Port Royal. Marie signed.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, F
2 CONC onds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 113-114) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/113?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jea
2 CONC n-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal,1702-1755 Charles Robucho and Marie Bourg marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 265 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1183≤/ref> 
2 CONT
