2 CONT
2 CONT == Census ==Charles does not appear in the 1671 census because his father refused to answer the census.
2 CONT CENSUS: 1678, Port Royal, Acadia: Estienne Robichau, Francoise Boudrot, 1 acre, 19 cattle, 4 boys: 12, 1666; 9, 1669; 4, 1674; 1, 1677; 2 girls: 15, 1663; 6, 1672.
2 CONT CENSUS: 1686, Port Royal, Acadia, age 19 years. He is the oldest son at home, and his father is dead.
2 CONT CENSUS: 1693, Port Royal, Acadia: Charles ROBICHAUX 26, Marie TIBEADEAU 29, Angelique 6, Augustin & Pierre (twins) 3, Anthoine 1; 10 cattle,18 sheep, 7 pigs, 6 arpents, 1 gun
2 CONT CENSUS: 1698, Port Royal, Acadia: Charles ROBICHO 30; Marie TIBAUDEAU (wife) 33; Angelique 10; Charles and Rene, twins, 8; Augustine 6; Jean4; Alexandre 2; Joseph 1; 9 cattle, 9 sheep, 6 hogs, 10 arpents, 1 gun. 
2 CONT CENSUS: 1700, Port Royal, Acadia: Charles ROBICHAUX [Robichaud] 34; Marie THIBAUDEAU (wife) 35; Charles and Rene (twins) 10; Anthoine 8; Augustin 7; Jean 6; Allexandre 5; Joseph 3; François 2; Angelique 13; 12cattle, 14 sheep, 16 
2 CONC arpents, 1 gun.
2 CONT CENSUS: 1701, Port Royal, Acadia: Charles ROBICHO 30, Marie TIBAUDEAU (wife) 30; Rene and Charles (twins) 10, Jean 8, Alexandre 7, Joseph 4,Francoise 2, Jacques 1, Isabel 14; 1 gun, 6 cattle, 9 sheep, 8 hogs, 6 arpents.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away before 18 May 1737
