2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Claude Boudrot (1663-1738) was born in Port Royal, (Acadia), (Annapolis Royal), Nova Scotia.  He married Anne Marie Catherine Thibodeau in Port Royal, 1682.  His occupation was “laborer/ploughman, general, civil and criminal lieut
2 CONC enant of Acadie”.   Excerpt from a History of Acadia: “Claude, born in c1663, married Anne-Marie, daughter of Pierre Thibodeaux, at Port-Royal in c1682 and moved to Rivière-des-Habitants in the Minas Basin.  He remarried to Cather
2 CONC ine, daughter of Jean Meunier, probably at Minas in c1700, and remarried again--his third marriage--to Madeleine, another daughter of Jean Corporon, and widow of Bernard Doucet at Port-Royal in August 1735.  Claude fathered 21 chi
2 CONC ldren by his first two wives, including nine sons who married into the Hébert, Préjean, Comeau, Aucoin, Doiron, Thibodeau, Gautrot, and Doucet families.  His daughters married into the Hébert, Aucoin, LeBlanc, Daigre, and Doiron f
2 CONC amilies.  Claude died at Grand-Pré in March 1740, in his late 70s.”  He was buried at Grand-Pré (Acadie/Acadia).
2 CONT
