2 CONT Claude Boudrot was born around 1663, possibly in Port-Royal.≤ref>Based on his age in the 1671 census.≤/ref>  He was mentioned for the firsttime in the Port-Royal census of 1671.≤ref name=census1671>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the
2 CONC  1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c257
2 CONC 2/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>Michel BOUDROT, 71, wife Michelle AUCOIN 53; Children (3 married): Francoise 29, Jeanne 25, M
2 CONC arguerite 20; (these not married): Charles 22, Marie 18, Jehan 16, Abraham 14, Michel 12, Olivier 10, Claude 8, Francois 5; cattle 5, sheep 12.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  He was listed as 8 years old at the time, livingwith his parents a
2 CONC nd ten siblings. Claude was enumerated in Port-Royal again with his family in 1678,  at the age of 16.≤ref name=census1678>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. C
2 CONC larence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>Michel Broudrot and Michelle Aucoin; 12 acres; 10 cattle; 3 guns; 5 boys: 22, 1656; 20, 1
2 CONC 658; 18, 1660; 16, 1662; 12, 1666. Michel Boudrot at the brook of brother Joseph Tirat at the southeast at Maitre Abraham to the River Au Seigneur 2 Leagues≤/blockquote> ≤/ref>
2 CONT Claude was married three times, and fathered twenty one children.≤ref name=DGFA>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ''Dictionnaire Généalogique desFamilles Acadiennes''] 
2 CONC (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p.185,190-192≤/ref>≤br/>
2 CONT The first marriage was to Anne-Marie Thibodeau around 1682, resulting in eight children. The newly married Claude age 23 years, and Anne-Marie 20, appeared in the 1686 Acadian census, living in Les Mines, Acadie. No children, land
2 CONC  or animals were listed.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be foun
2 CONC d at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671  1752”, Images 15-60.≤/ref>  Seven years later, in the 1693 cens
2 CONC us,five children are listed and they own cattle, sheep, pigs, cultivatedland and one gun.≤ref name=census1693>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun
2 CONC /genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of theNational Archives of Canada] “Acadie Re
2 CONC censements 1671 – 1752”,Images 62-108≤blockquote>	Claude BOUDROT 30, Anne Marie TIBAUDEAU 24, Claude 10, Michel 8, Jacques 6, Francoise 3, Madeleine 1; 6 cattle, 3 sheep, 4 pigs, 8 arpents, 1 gun≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤br/>
2 CONT When Anne-Marie died, Claude married Catherine Meunier around 1700, resulting in thirteen children.≤br/>
2 CONT Claude was widowed from Catherine Meunier and about 72  years old whenhe married Madeleine, 63 years old, in 1735.≤ref name=marriage>''NovaScotia Archives'', "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Anna
2 CONC polis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26a page 138; online database with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2086&Language=French marriage of Claude Boudrot and Madelene Corporon  7 aout  1735],
2 CONC  accessed 30 October 2019≤/ref>≤br/>
2 CONT Claude passed away five years later. He was interred on March 7, 1740 in the parish of St-Charles aux Mines, Grand-Pré. "Claude Boudrot, age ca 80, bur. 7 March 1740 in the cemetery of the parish of St Charlesaux Mines, wit. Pierr
2 CONC e Doucet (s) ≤ref>(s) means they signed the document≤/ref>; Joseph Terriot (s); Francois Boudrot; Michel Boudrot (SGA-3,4b)"  ≤ref>Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Church Records: Acadian Records, 1707-1748, Volume 1a Revised. Cath
2 CONC olic Diocese of Baton Rouge,1999. p. 30 ≤blockquote>Note: The Book, Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Church Records, Acadian Records, 1707-1748, Vol 1-A which contains records abstracted from Acadian Records brought with Acadian Se
2 CONC ttlers to St Gabriel Parish, Louisiana when they arrived from Acadie and France. Although they are currently in deteriorating conditon, thanks to years of work by dedicated volunteers, they are here saved for our day!≤/blockquote>
2 CONC ≤/ref>≤ref name=Burial>Nova Scotia Church Records. Library and Archives Canada. Héritage/Canadiana online database with images. Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869, Image 856 [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c
2 CONC 1870/856?r=0&s=1 Claude Boudrot Burial7 March 1740]≤/ref>≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographie ==Claude est né vers 1663≤ref name=DGFA/>, possiblement à Port-Royal. Il est mentionné pour la première fois à l'âge de huit ans dans lerecensement de Port-Royal de 1671, ≤ref name=census1671/> et à nouveau en alors 
2 CONC qu'il était âgé de 16 ans et vivait toujours avec ses parents et frères et soeurs à Port-Royal.≤ref name=census1678/>
2 CONT Claude s'est marié trois fois et a eu vingt-et-un enfants.≤ref name=DGFA/>≤br/>À l'âge d"environ 19 ans, vers 1682, il  épousa en premières nocesAnne-Marie Thibodeau qui avait 16 ans à l'époque. Ils ont eu huit enfants.≤br/>Il épo
2 CONC usa en seconde noces Catherine Meunier vers 1700 qui lui a donné treize enfants.  En 1686 le jeune couple vivait aux Mines, en Acadie. En 1693, Claude, Anne-Marie et leurs cinq enfants vivaient aux Mines et possédaient six bêtes à
2 CONC  cornes, trois brebis, quatre cochons, huit arpents de terre en valeur et un fusil. ≤ref name=census1693/>≤br/>Après le décès de celle-ci, alors qu'il était âgé d'environ 72 ans, il a épousé Madeleine Corporon 63 ans,  en 1735.≤re
2 CONC f name=marriage/>
2 CONT Claude est décédé en 1740 à une date non précisée et a été inhumé le  7 mars 1740 à Grand-Pré, Nouvelle-Écosse. ≤ref name=Burial/>
2 CONT '''Liste des enfants connus d'Anne Marie Thibodeau et de Claude Boudrot:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #Claude BOUDROT b: ~ 1683, Port Royal, Acadie
2 CONT #Michel BOUDROT b: ~ 1685, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT #Joseph BOUDROT b: ~ 1687, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT #Marie Anne BOUDROT b: ~1690, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT #Marie (Madeleine) BOUDROT b:~ 1692, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT #Anne BOUDROT b: ~1694, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT #Elisabeth BOUDROT b: ~ 1696, Acadie
2 CONT #Marguerite BOUDROT b: ~ 1698, Grand Pré, Acadie
2 CONT '''Liste des enfants connus de Catherine Meunier et de Claude Boudrot:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #Catherine Boudreau	1702
2 CONT #Cécile Boudreau	1703 - 04 Déc 1725
2 CONT #Étienne Boudreau	1704
2 CONT #Marie Boudreau	1705 - 8 Fév 1759
2 CONT #Paul Boudreau	16 Oct 1707	
2 CONT #François Boudreau	18 Juil 1709
2 CONT #Jean Boudreau	1710
2 CONT #Pierre Boudreau	1712 - 2 Juin 1759
2 CONT #Françoise Boudreau	1715 - 28 Mars 1751
2 CONT #Marie Josephte Boudreau	4 Jan 1718
2 CONT #Claire Boudreau	27 Déc 1719 - 1 Nov 1741
2 CONT #Anne Boudreau	22 Nov 1721 - Août 1756
2 CONT #Charles Boudreau	23 Oct 1725	
