2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography ==Claude Boudrot was the son of Claude Boudrot and Anne-Marie Thibodeau.He was born about 1683 in Acadia (Nova Scotia Canada). It is not known if he was born in the Acadian village of Port Royal or Grand Pre as his par
2 CONC ents were living in Port Royal in 1671 and 1678 but by 1686 they had moved to Grand Pré.
2 CONT About 1706 Claude married Catherine Hebert, daughter of Jean and Marie-Anne Doucet. Possibly they married at Grand Pré as their children were baptized there beginning in 1708. 
2 CONT Between 1708 and 1734, the couple had 10 children: Claude, Anne-Marie,Marguerite, Joseph, Isabelle, Pierre, Jean, Francoise, Olivier, and Charles.  All but one (Olivier) have baptismal records in Grand Pré. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude died after his daughter Elisabeth's marriage as he was present for that event on Oct 1, 1742.  No further information available at this time([[Bourque-573|Bourque-573]] 14:04, 9 March 2020 (UTC)).
2 CONT He did not move to Louisiana, as he died before the general immigration of deported Acadians.{{citation needed}}
2 CONT The surname Boudrot was later changed to Boudreaux in Louisiana. Both the Boudreaux and Thibodeaux families are common Acadian/Cajun surnames in the parishes west of New Orleans, Louisiana, and some family members immigrated there
2 CONC  after the British took over Acadian lands in the 1700s.  See the story of the Boudreaux in Louisiana at the [http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-BOUDREAUX.htm Acadians in Gray website]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
