2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Acadian Villages 1630s to 1755
2 CONT http://www.acadian-home.org/Pre-Deport-Villages.html
2 CONT Rivière des Habitants (New Minas)
2 CONT The first settlers in this village were young couples from Port-Royal, newly married and without children who
2 CONT were looking to start life in a new place through maintaining strong ties with their families in Port-Royal.
2 CONT Located on the banks of the Rivière St.Antoine or La Rivière Grand-Habitant (Cornwallis River), on the
2 CONT opposite side of the river from Côte des Boudreau (Starr's {pomt), the village was sometimes known as la
2 CONT Rivière des Habitants. Based on the census of 1714, Acadian families living here were the Dupuis, Sire/Cyr
2 CONT Hébert, LeBlanc, Landry, Benoit, Boucher and Darois.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT :Michel BOUDROT, born around 1685, son of Claude & Anne-Marie THIBODEAU. He married 1st around 1708 to Cécile LE BLANC, daughter of Jacques& Catherine HÉBERT; eleven children. He married 2nd (Port Royal Register) 16 Apr 1732 Anne 
2 CONC PRÉJEAN, daughter of Jean & Andrée SAVOIE (widow of Francois PITRE); no children. ≤ref> Title: [https://archive.org/stream/gnalogiedesf00gaud#page/60/mode/2up/search/thibodeau|Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes]; Au
2 CONC thor: Stephen A. White;Publication: 2 vols; Moncton, NB: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; pp. 90 & 207.≤/ref>
2 CONT :Michel passed away between Sep 1755-1756.≤ref> Title: Dictionnaire gnéalogique des familles acadiennes, "Ajouts et corrections"; Author:Stephen A. White; Publication: University of Moncton, Centre d'études acadiennes; Online for 
2 CONC pp. 190 & 207:Among those transported to Bristol, England, and died between then and the smallpox epidemic of Sep 1756.:Text: Died (according to P[aul]. Delaney) between Sep 1755 and the end of Sep 1756.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :Children
