2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT :Joseph Boudrot was born in about 1687 to [[Boudrot-15|Claude Boudrot]] and [[Thibodeau-31|Anne Marie Thibodeau]].≤ref name= "DGFA">White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_fam
2 CONC illes_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p.190.≤/ref> He wed [[Comeau-326|Francoise Comeau]] on 27 July 1712 in Grand
2 CONC  Pre.≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/561?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Church Record Volume 1a revised: The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia 1707-1748; John J. Pastorek,
2 CONC  Editor; Catholic Diocese of Baton Rouge:Baton Rouge, 1999. p.32.Text:::Joseph Boudrot (Claude Boudrot and decd. Anne Tibeaudo) m. 27 July 1712 Francoise Commeaux (Jean Commeaux and Catherine Babin) wit. ClaudeBoudrot (s); Joseph 
2 CONC Dugas (s); sig. {+} Joseph Boudrot; {+} FrancoiseCommeaux (SGA-1,12)≤/ref>
2 CONT :He died sometime before 17 May 1763, ≤ref name= "DGFA" /> This is thedate that the Acadians exiled to England sailed for St-Malo and whilehis wife was listed on the passenger list of La Dorothee, he was not.≤ref>[http://froux.pag
2 CONC esperso-orange.fr/divers/dorothee.html Roll des familles acadiennes embarquées sur la frégate du Roy La Dorothée, Capitaine Lavenant], accessed 30 September 2017.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :Son of Claude Boudrot and Anna Marie Thibodeaux Boudrot.
2 CONT :Surname Boudrot was later changed to Boudreaux in Louisiana. 
2 CONT :May have up to 20 siblings
2 CONT :Died before May 17, 1763. Records are probably in French.:Among those transported to Bristol, England; died between then and the smallpox epidemic of Sep 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT * Title: Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes, "Ajouts et corrections" Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: University of Moncton, Centre d'études acadiennes; Note: Appeared in Nov 1999 & Sep 2003. :Repository: Name
2 CONC : Internet; [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac/wf/wf/pdf/cor-dict.pdf "Ajouts et corrections"] for pp. 190 & 211:: Note: Among those transported to Bristol, England, and died betweenthen and the smallpox epidemic 
2 CONC of Sep 1756.
2 CONT :: Text: Died (according to P. Delaney) between Sep 1755 and the end of Sep 1756.
2 CONT *Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel 
2 CONC Church of Iberville, LA. pp. 32 & 50
2 CONT :: Text: Witnesses: Claude BOUDROT [signed]; Joseph DUGAS [signed]; groom and bride made X (SGA-1, 12) .
2 CONT
2 CONT * Note: Décès avant May 17, 1763-(S. White) See corrections above
2 CONT ::Translation: Died before May 17, 1763.
