2 CONT She had 10 children.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Marguerite Boudreaux (Boudrot) (1695-1767) was born in Ste. Charles des-Mines, Grand-Pre, Acadia, the daughter of Claude Boudreau (Boudrot) and Anne Marie Catherine Thibodeau.  She accompanied her husband, Francoise Leblanc, and c
2 CONC hildren into exile to Massachusetts.  Six years after her husband’s death, she arrived in St. Pierre and Miquelon, alone per the manifest. Her death was reported as May 15, 1767, in both Port Royal, N. S. and Memramcook, Westmorla
2 CONC nd, N. B. 
2 CONT --------------------
