2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography =='''Claude Landry''' was born in 1663. He was the son of [[Landry-70|René Landry]] and [[Bernard-67|Marie Bernard]]. He was married 3 times.His 3rd marriage was to Jeanne Bellemare, widow of Mathieu Brasseaux and dau
2 CONC ghter of Andre Celestin and Perrine Basil 15 May 1741 at Saint Charles des Mines, Grand-Pré, Acadia. ≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, 
2 CONC Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 740):  http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/740?r=0&s=4≤/ref>
2 CONT CLAUDE LANDRY, n. vers 1663; m. (1) MARIE-CATHERINE THIBODEAU, vers 1684; m. (2) MARIE BABIN, vers 1725, Grand-Pré, St-Charles des Mines, Acadie; m. (3) JEANNE CÉLESTIN DIT BELLEMÈRE, 15 mai 1741, Grand-Pré, St-Charles des Mines, 
2 CONC Acadie.≤ref>[http://www.claude.dupras.com/les_landry.htm C.Dupras les Landry]≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Génalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes,
2 CONC  Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p924.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Messages
2 CONT :Re: Jean Landry m.Claire Olive LeBlanc
2 CONT :Posted by: Marilyn 	Date: April 29, 2002 at 10:02:48:In Reply to: Jean Landry m.Claire Olive LeBlanc by Lilly Mounts 	of 2122::In my tree I have Alexis Landry, born Aug. 25, 1721, son of Jean Landry, born est 1694, and Claire LeB
2 CONC lanc. They were married 1716 in Acadia. Alexis was one of fifteen children. The parents of Jean Landry were Claude Landry, born est 1663, and Catherine Thibodeau, born est 1667. They were married in Port Royal in 1684. Claude Land
2 CONC ry remarried twice after Catherine Thibodeau died (around 1725). Hope this is what youare looking for. I have no info on Claire Olive LeBlanc.
