2 CONT == Biography ==Jean Baptiste Landry was born about 1686. He was the son of [[Landry-74|Claude Landry]] and [[Thibodeau-176|Marie-Catherine Thibodeau]].  Since the family lived in Les Mines in 1686 when the census was taken, and he
2 CONC  was born after that census and still found in the same place in 1693, he is thought to have been born in Les Mines.≤ref>White, StephenA. English Supplement to the Dictionnaire Généalogique Des FamillesAcadiennes ,Part I 1636 to 1
2 CONC 714; Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 2000, Print. P. 924≤/ref>
2 CONT He married Marguerite Comeau, daughter of Jean Comeau and Catherine Babin 17 Oct 1718 at Saint Charles des Mines.≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/594?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Ch
2 CONC urch Records: Acadian Records 1707-1748 (Baton Rouge, LA, Diocese of Baton Rouge, 1999), Personal Collection, Marriage of Marguerite Comeaux (Jean ≤u>Comeaux and Catherine Babin≤/u>) m. ≤u>17 Oct.≤/u> 1718 Jean Baptiste Landry (Cl
2 CONC aude Landry and Catherine ≤u>Thibodeau≤/u>) wit. Jean Commaux (s); Claude Babyn (s); Pierre Doucet (s); J. Mouton (s); Claude Landry (s); Claude Babin. Note: part of page259 is missing, underlined text is from 1895 transcription. 
2 CONC (SGA-2, 258-259)."≤/ref>
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT :: Date:  1686:: Place:  Mines, Grand Pre, Nova Scotia≤ref>Source: [[#S337]]  Page: Source number: 757.000; Source type: Electronic Database; Number of Pages: 1; Submitter Code: JTW≤/ref>
2 CONT
