2 CONT [[Category:Acadians]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Biography =='''Rene Landry''' was born about 1688. He was the son of [[Landry-74|Claude Landry]] and [[Thibodeau-176|Marie-Catherine Thibodeau]]. He married Marie Magdeleine Melanson, daughter of Pierre Melanson and Marie Blanc
2 CONC hard. 8 Nov 1712 at Saint Charles des Mines. ≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 
2 CONC 564):  http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/564?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Other than René's funeral, the only other record found for his familywas the funeral of his son Joseph Landry, dead 21 May 1795, funeral on the 22nd in L'Acadie (in what is now Québec province), aged 53, listed as son of René Land
2 CONC ry and Madeleine Melançon≤ref>[https://www.genealogiequebec.com/Membership/LAFRANCE/acte/394926 funeral Joseph Landry IGD]≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT René Landry died on 19 Feb 1769, funeral on the 21st in Montréal (ND)≤ref>[https://www.genealogiequebec.com/Membership/LAFRANCE/acte/363305 funeral IGD]≤/ref>, listed as around 81 years old, native of Acadie,buried in the cemetery
2 CONC  near the church, only priests were named as present and signed the record.
