1 NOTE René Landry (b.1688) of Charles-des-Mines (Canning area):
2 CONT This René Landry resided at "la rivière des Habitants." He married Marie-Madeleine Melanson at Saint-Charles-des-Mines, on 8th November, 1712. Of nine children, five were boys: Honoré (b.1714 [#11121]), Anselme (b.1717 [#11122]), 
2 CONC Jean Baptiste (b.1720 [#11123]), Joseph (b.1735 [#11124]), Prosper18 (b.1736 [#11125]), & Michel (b.1739 [#11126]).
2 CONT There was an René Landry who was among the 483 men whom Col. John Winslow <../Hist/BiosNS/1700-63/Winslow.htm> confined on the 10th September, 1755, at Grand Pré. He is listed to be from the village of "Antoine" and was the owner 
2 CONC of 5 bullocks, 6 cows, 10 young cattle, 20 sheep, 12 hogs, and 2 horses; one son, one daughter listed.19
2 CONT
2 CONT another source says that Rene who married Madeleine Melanson had 10 children
