2 CONT [[Category:Pisiguit, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT :Anne Marie was born around 1691 in Acadia, to parents Pierre Thibodeau and Anne-Marie Bourg. ≤ref>Title: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes; Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: C
2 CONC entre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p. 1511:No place of birth given.≤/ref>The location of her birth is in question as Pierre resided in Port Royal in 1686 but is found in Les Mines (Minas Basin) in 1693 with wife Anne Marie and 2 yea
2 CONC r old daughter Anne Marie.  The family settled at [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/pisiguit.htm Pisiguit Nova Scotia] in the Minas Basin.  On November 6 1713 Anne Marie married Jean Baptiste Comeau, son of Jean the elder and Francois
2 CONC e Hebert. Anne Marie died at L'Assomption de Pisiguit, Nova Scotia.≤ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748;Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles a
2 CONC ux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried intoexile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. pp. 50-51 & 188-189:Text: (SGA-1, 44).≤/ref>≤ref>https://www.genealogie.umontreal.ca/Membership/en/PRDH/union/6662≤/ref> She was said to
2 CONC  be deceased when her daughter Rosalie married on 22 January 1743.
2 CONT : CENSUS: 1693, Les Mines, Acadia, age 2 years, living with parents Pierre THIBAUDEAU & Anne BOURG. Brother Philippes is 3 months old.
2 CONT
