2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==Pierre Tibodeau was born about 1696. He was the son of [[Thibodeau-33|Pierre Thibodeau]] and [[Bourg-40|Anne-Marie Bourg]]. ≤ref name=White>IDictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes; Author: Stephen A. Whit
2 CONC e; Publication: 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p.  1511. No place or date of birth given.
2 CONT :: Text: Drowned; buried (Port Lajoie Register) on 22 Nov 1723.≤/ref>
2 CONT He married Marie Joseph Boudrot, daughter of Charles Boudrot and MarieCorporon 2 Oct 1719 at Saint Charles des Mines.≤ref>[http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/602?r=0&s=5 Marriage] found inthe Catholic Church R
2 CONC ecords, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registersof St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. p
2 CONC p. 33 & 191-192. Text: (SGA-2, 254).≤/ref>
2 CONT Unfortunately Pierre died quite young, at just 26 or 27 years old whenhe drowned.  His burial was Nov 22, 1723 at Port Lajoie, Isle Saint Jean ≤ref name=White />≤ref>Archives Nationales d'outre-mer État civil, Ile Saint-Jean (Port
2 CONC  La Joye) Parish Records 1721-1758, 1723 p. 5 [http://anom.archivesnationales.culture.gouv.fr/caomec2/osd.php?territoire=CANADA&commune=ILE%20SAINT-JEAN%20(PORT-LA-JOYE)&annee=1723 Burial]≤/ref>
2 CONT
