2 CONT Category:Great Upheaval Category:Beaubassin, Acadie Category:Grand-Pré, Acadie
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT :'''Pierre Cormier and Cécile Thibodeau are the ancestors of all the Cormiers  in southeastern New Brunswick'''<ref name=37families>White, Stephen A. ''La généalogie des trente-sept familles hôtesses des Retrouvailles 94,'' online
2 CONC  articles, Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne, vol. 25, nos 2 et 3 (1994), [https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac/wf/wf/pdf/37fam-cormier.pdf CORMIER], page 1-2 </ref>
2 CONT :Cecile Thibodeau, daughter of Jean Thibodeau and Marguerite Hebert was born 5 Nov 1712 in Grand Pré, Acadia and was christened there the next day. Sponsors: Jean MELANSON & Cécile MELANSON.<ref>Paroisse de St. Charles des Mines, 
2 CONC Grand Pré, Acadie, Baptèmes, vol. 12-1 [images10-334, pages 1-311] Image 76, [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/76?r=0&s=5 entry for Cecille Tibeaudo], 6 November 1712 ; digital images, Héritage, Genealogy co
2 CONC llection, Library and Archives Canada, reel C-1869, "Parish Registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869," roll 1, accessed 3 Nov 2019. ''This register is a transcript written around 1895 of the original registers currently held at the Baton R
2 CONC ougeDiocese Archives in Louisiana, USA.''</ref> :Pierre dit Palette CORMIER, son of Pierre CORMIER, deceased, & Catherine LEBLANC, married 17 [difficult to decipher date, taken from 1895 transcription] July 1730 to Cecille TIBAUDO
2 CONC , daughter of Jean TIBAUDOT & deceased Marguerite HÉBERT. Witnesses: Manuel HÉBERT; Jean LEBLANC; Pierre CORMIER; Jean TIBEAUDEAUD (signed); bride and groom made marks (SGA-2, 221).<ref>Paroisse de St. Charles des Mines, Grand Pré
2 CONC , Acadie, Mariages, vol. 12-3, p. 646 [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/646?r=0&s=5 entry for Pierre Cormier & Catherine Tibaudot], 17 July 1730; digital images, Héritage, Genealogy collection, Library and A
2 CONC rchives Canada, reel C-1869, "Parish Registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869," roll 1, accessed 3 Nov 2019. ''This register is a transcript written around 1895 of the original registers currently held at the Baton Rouge Diocese Archives i
2 CONC n Louisiana, USA.''</ref><ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carri
2 CONC ed into exileto St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. Personal Copy; pp. 52 & 189</ref> :The family was counted in the 1750-1751 census at Ouescoque (Vechkok).<ref name=census1750>Acadian & French Canadian Ancestral Home"; 2005 – P
2 CONC resent, hosted by Lucie LeBlanc Consentino; [http://www.acadian-home.org/census1751.html 1750/1751 Census] [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1732cens.htm 1752 Census Transcribed].<blockquote>Pierre CORMIER, hi
2 CONC s wife and 10 children.</blockquote></ref> :Pierre passed away before 1752 since Cécile was listed as a widow inthe 1752 census at Le Lac, with 5 children.<ref>Acadian & French Canadian Ancestral Home"; 2005 – Present, hosted by L
2 CONC ucie LeBlanc Consentino; [http://www.acadian-home.org/census1752.html 1752 Census] The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the Natio
2 CONC nal Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 277-308.<blockquote> The widow CORMIER, 2 boys, 3 girls.</blockquote></ref> She was only 40 years of age. :Cécile and many of her children would stick together in t
2 CONC heir perilous exile to the French territories (New Brunswick and Quebec). Many ofthe children would eventually settle in Cormier's Cove, New Brunswick. 
2 CONT
2 CONT : '''Children'''<ref name=37families/># Jean-Baptiste, n Beaubassin 2 mars 1733; m Kamouraska 5 juil 1762 Madeleine LANDRY (Alexis & Marguerite Aucoin); d St-Basile 14 fév 1822.#Pierre dit Pierrot à Nannette, n Beaubassin 3 août 1
2 CONC 734; m v 1755 Anne dite Nannette GAUDET (Augustin & Agnès Chiasson); d Memramcook 24mars 1818.
2 CONT #Marie, n v 1736.#François, n v 1740; m St-Pierre-du-Sud 3 août 1761 Anastasie MELANSON (Paul & Marie Thériault) veuve de Claude Brun; d Memramcook 7 janv1825.# Joseph, n v 1740; m (1) v 1759 Marguerite SAULNIER (Jacques & Anne Hé
2 CONC bert); m (2) PointeCoupée (Louisiane) 25 avril 1771 Anne MICHEL (Jacques & Jeanne Breau) veuve de Michel Brun et de Victor Comeau; s Opelousas 5 août 1795.#Michel, n Beaubassin 19 janv 1741; m (1) v 1769 Anne SAULNIER (Jacques & A
2 CONC nne Hébert) veuve de Basile Babin; m (2) v 1775 Catherine STELLY(Johann Georg & Christine Edelmeyer); m (3) St Martinville (Louisiane) 10 fév 1789  Madeleine BREAU (Charles & Claire Trahan); s Opelousas30 déc 1790.
2 CONT #Marie-Josèphe, n Beaubassin 27 sept 1742.
2 CONT #Charles, n Beaubassin 26 juin 1744.#Marie-Cécile, m St-Thomas de Montmagny 18 fév 1765 Pierre-FrançoisCHOUINARD (Eustache & Marie-Madeleine Bérubé).#Jacques, m Ekoupahag (Kingsclear) 24 janv 1770 Marie-Osite POTHIER (Jean & Marie
2 CONC -Josèphe Hébert). #Amand, m Rivière St-Jean 5 sept 1774 Marie-Josèphe ROY (Joseph & Marie-Agnès D'Amours de Chauffours); d v 1786.  :She died (according to P. GAUDET) in 1787 or 1788, age 80 years (sic), on the trip between Ste-An
2 CONC ne of Pays Bas and Memramcook.
2 CONT
