2 CONT == Biography =='''Joseph Tibaudeau''' was born 1 Mar 1727. He was the son of [[Thibodeau-1286|Antoine Thibodeau]] and [[Prejean-18|Marie Prejean]]. He was baptized the next day at Port Royal. His godparents were Alexis Doucet, son
2 CONC  of Jacques Doucet and Françoise Martin, daughter of Etienne Martin.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 110) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/vie
2 CONC w/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/110?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Joseph Tibaudeau baptism RG 1 volume 26 page 260 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/arch
2 CONC ives.asp?ID=1170≤/ref>
2 CONT He married Marie Landry, daughter of Charles and Marie Josephe Girouard about 1759. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Children
2 CONT # Jean THIBODEAU ca 1760-
2 CONT # Joseph THIBODEAU ca 1763-
2 CONT 12 August 1763 Census - SC: Joseph Thibodeau, listed with his wife Marie Landry, and two children: Jean Thibodeau, age 3; and Joseph Thibodeau, age 5 days.≤ref>Exiles in the Colonies - Janet Jehn - Covington, KY: Author, 1977 - p.
2 CONC  236≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away before 1774.
