2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Acadian [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Benjamin Thibodeau''' was born on September 20, 1721 in Acadia. He was baptized in Port Royal the next day, his sponsors being Paul Savoie and Anne Thibodeau.<ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Sai
2 CONC nt-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 47) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/47?r=0&s=5</ref><ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 B
2 CONC enjamin Thibaudault baptism RG 1 volume 26 page 180 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=876</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elisabeth Thibodeau in Acadia about 1746. Witnesses: de GOUTIN; Claude THIBODEAU; PONTIF (who have signed with the groom). (Also in Tanguay, vol. VI, pp. 290-29 1.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd at Port-Royal on 21 Jun 1752 to Marguerite Lanoue, daughter of Charles & Marie Landry. Witnesses were Jean Tibodeau, Fabien Tibodeau, Charles Lanoue and Joseph Lanoue.<ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers 
2 CONC of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Benjamin Tibodeau and Marguerite Lanoue marriage https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=3375</ref> Two children. Benjamin lived at Petitcoudiac.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Residence ==
2 CONT : Census:   :: Date:  1763:: Place:  Southampton, , Hampshire, England  Benjamin was on the 1763list of passengers from Southampton to France "ancien prisonnier de guerre de Bristol"; also on 1763 list of arrivals at St-Malo, age 
2 CONC 34 years (sic) , cousin of Joseph HENRY : Census:   :: Date:  1772 :: Place:  St. Malo, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family of Origin ==
2 CONT : Husband:  @I673@ : Wife:  @I706@ : Child:  [[Thibodeau-422|Marguerite Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-423|Agnes Anne Thibodeau]] : Child:  @I5823@ : Child:  [[Thibodeau-439|Pierre Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-424|Joseph T
2 CONC hibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-425|Charles Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-426|Marie Madeleine Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-427|Marie Josephe Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-428|Elisabeth Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibode
2 CONC au-429|Francois Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-430|Benjamin Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-431|Jean Baptiste Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-432|Amand Gregoire Thibodeau]] : Child:  [[Thibodeau-433|Claire Thibodeau]] : Chi
2 CONC ld:  [[Thibodeau-434|Anne Thibodeau]]: Marriage:  13 NOV 1704, Port Royal, Acadia<ref>Source: [[#S14]]  Page:  pp. 1509 & 1517. Text:  Witnesses: de GOUTIN; Claude THIBODEAU; PONTIF (who have signed with the groom). (Also in Tangu
2 CONC ay, vol. VI, pp. 290-29 1.)</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT  * See also:* BIRTH-CHRISTENING-PARENTS-MARRIAGES-CENSUS: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714 ; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999 , 2 vols.; p. 1518; #(36)* BIRTH-P
2 CONC ARENTS-MARRIAGES-CHILD: Web page of Univ. of Moncto n, Centred'etudes acadiennes, by Stephen White, on the 3 7 Acadian families hosting the 1994 World Congress; orig. published by La Societe historique acadienne, CAHIERS; vol . 25
2 CONC , no. 2&3 (Apr-Sep 1994), at <http://www.umoncton.ca/et udeacadiennes/centre/white/sha.html>* BIRTH-MARRIAGES-CHILDREN-RESIDENCES: Arsenault, H&G, p. 80 8 (Port Royal). Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DE S ACADIENS; 1600-18
2 CONC 00; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, vols . 2-6; p. 1576
