2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography =='''Guillaume Bourgeois''' was born about 1674. He was the son of [[Bourgeois-15|Germain Bourgeois]] [[Belliveau-45|Marguerite Belliveau]]. He married first Marguerite Mius, daughter of Abraham and Marguerite deSaint
2 CONC -Etienne de La Tour about 1700 in Acadia. There was 1 known child: Marie Josephe BOURGEOIS ca 1702-/1760
2 CONT He married second  Catherine Tibeaudeau, daughter of the late Pierre Tibeaudeau and Jeanne Teriot on February 17th, 1705 in Port Royal.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Roy
2 CONC al, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 119) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/119?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Guillaume Bourgeois and C
2 CONC atherine Tibeaudeau marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 274 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1200&Language=≤/ref>≤ref>Gaudet, P. (1906). Généalogie des familles acadiennes : avec documents : rapport concernant les a
2 CONC rchivescanadiennes pour l'année 1905 https://archive.org/stream/gnalogiedesf00gaud≤/ref>≤ref>Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes - Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714 - Stephe
2 CONC n A. White - 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999 - p. 1509 -≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Marie Marguerite BOURGEOIS 1708-/1748
2 CONT # Catherine Josephe BOURGEOIS 1711-/1762
2 CONT # Michel BOURGEOIS 1713-
2 CONT # Sylvain BOURGEOIS 1715-1751
2 CONT # Guillaume BOURGEOIS 1717-1794
2 CONT # Marie Agnes BOURGEOIS 1719-1755
2 CONT # Amand BOURGEOIS 1721-
2 CONT # Anne BOURGEOIS 1723-1781
2 CONT # Theotiste BOURGEOIS 1726-/1763
2 CONT # Marie Josephe BOURGEOIS 1729- 
2 CONT # Madeleine Victoire BOURGEOIS 1734-
2 CONT Guillaume Bourgeois died 7 August 1747, about sixty-two years old, married to Catherine Tibodeau and was buried the next day at Port Royal. Witnesses were Claude Bourgeois and Gregoire Bourgeois.≤ref>An AcadianParish Remembered Th
2 CONC e Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Guillaume Bourgeois burial RG 1 volume 26a page 339 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2945≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* BIRTH-PARENTS-MARRIAGES-CHILDREN-DEATH-BURIAL: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; pp. 259-260
2 CONT * BIRTH-MARRIAGES-CHILDREN: Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DESACADIENS; 1600-1800; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, vols. 2-6; p. 458(Port Royal)
