2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Simon LeBlanc m. Marguerite Guilbeau did arrive in New Orleanswith the February 1765 group led by Joseph Broussard ditBeausoliel.  Hisdaughter, Marie-Angelique, bn. 1/1/1765 was baptised in NewOrleans2/20/1765. Her sister, Marie-L
2 CONC ouise, bn.1/30/1762 was baptizedin NO on2/22/1765. Their mother Catherine-Louise Thibodeaux [Simon's 1stwife]died11/15/1765 in Attakapas.  Simon was on the list of those whosubmitted a"card money" claim.Stanley LeBlancThe informat
2 CONC ion available reSimon[-Joseph] indicates that he is the son of Rene LeBlanc andAnneTheriot. His four sisters married four sons of Joseph BroussardditBeausoliel. One of them, Rose, widow of Raphael Broussard,became theFirst Acadian
2 CONC  Nun in Louisiana. His youngest brother Rene [PetitRene]m. Marguerite Trahan. His eldest brother Etienne m. ElisabethBoudrot -my 5th Great-Grandparents. All except Etieen arrived in Feb.1765 - theevidence indicates that Etienne ar
2 CONC rived in May 1765.Information posted by email by Stanley LeBlanc
