1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **Baptism:  "Canada, Nova Scotia Births and Baptisms, 1702-1896", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:V5ML-QPV : 7 February 2020), Marie Corporon in entry for Pierre Trahant, 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT **"Acadians Aboard English ship Britannia, 1769" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***At Baie des Espagnols, Île Royale, Apr 1752, age 5
2 CONT ***Sailed to Halifax, Colony of Nova Scotia, probably 1754
2 CONT ***Resettled at Lunenburg/Mirliguèche, Colony of Nova Scotia, after 9 Oct 1754
2 CONT ***Imprisoned on Georges Island, Halifax, Sep 1755
2 CONT ***Exiled to Province of North Carolina, Dec 1755, aboard sloop Providence,  age 36
2 CONT ***Moved to Province of Maryland, c1760
2 CONT ***In report of Acadians at Port Tobacco, Province of Maryland, Jul 1763
2 CONT ***Departed Port Tobacco, Province of Maryland, 5 Jan 1769, aboard English schooner Britannia 
2 CONT ***Lost in the Gulf of Mexico & held by Spanish at La Bahia, Spanish Texas
2 CONT ***Arrived Natchitoches Post, la Luisiana, 24 Oct 1769, overland from Spanish Texas, age 18
2 CONT ***Settled below Bayou Plaquemine, St.-Gabriel District, la Luisiana with other Acadian exiles from the Britannia, Apr 1770
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1777, listed as Pierre Trahant, age 27
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1785, listed as Pre Trahan
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1788, Bellevue, listed as Pre. Trahan
2 CONT ***On Opelousas militia list, Jul 1789, fusilier, called Pierre Trahan
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1796, Faquetaic District, called Pierre Trahan
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana on 24 Oct 1769, age 18
2 CONT ----
