1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pierre LeBlanc, sergeant in the American Revolutionary War, served for only fifteen days, at £ 2 8 s. per month. Commonly known as Pierre à Charles, he was born at Pisiguit about 1751 to Charles LeBlanc and Marie B
2 CONC arrieau. He married Marie Saulnier, daughter of Charles Saulnier and Marie-Josèphe Savoie, about 1779, and settled at Memramcook, N.B. The date of Pierre à Charles’s death is unknown. See LeBlanc-1 i, and for his twelve children, 
2 CONC LeBlanc-2. http://stephenwhite.acadian-home.org/american-revolution.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Pisiguit, Acadie]] [[Category:Company of Frenchmen]] 
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography == Pierre was born in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pisiguit Pisiguit] about 1751.   He married Marie Saulnier about 1779. She was the daughter of [[Saulnier-33|Charles Saulnier]] and [[Savoie-236|Marie-Josèphe Savoi
2 CONC e]]. <ref>WHITE, Stephen A. « La généalogie des trente-sept familles hôtesses des "Retrouvailles 94" », Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne, vol. 25, nos 2 et 3 (1994).https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac
2 CONC /wf/wf/pdf/37fam-leb.pdf. 1. CHARLES LEBLANC (à François à Jacques), m MARIE BARRIEAU. Enfants:2. i. Pierre, n Pisiguit v 1751; m v 1779 Marie SAULNIER (Charles & Marie-Josèphe Savoie). </ref>
2 CONT * Pierre LeBlanc and 18 other young Acadians from Memramcook participated in the American Revolutionary War as soldiers during [https://www.pc.gc.ca/en/lhn-nhs/nb/beausejour/culture/histoire-history/siege-1776 The Siege of Fort Cu
2 CONC mberland]. They were known as [http://stephenwhite.acadian-home.org/american-revolution.html The Company of Frenchmen]. The attack on this fort was the first part of a plan to make Nova Scotia the 14th American Colony.
2 CONT * The profiles of the 18 other Acadians who were part of this group can be seen [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Category:Company_of_Frenchmenhere].
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT * http://www.genealogie-acadienne.net/?action=indiDetails&I=343
2 CONT * http://stephenwhite.acadian-home.org/american-revolution.html
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Fort_Cumberland* https://societehistoriqueacadienne.files.wordpress.com/2018/04/0701_total.pdf
