1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT {{Unsourced}}
2 CONT == Biography == '''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the Acadian Project becauseof conflicts, frequent attempts to duplicate or add parents or other family members without adequate sourcing. Please post below this notice if 
2 CONC you have anything meaningful to contribute. 
2 CONT :The mother of Edmee and Catherine is unnamed.  Mitochondrial DNA tests of her descendants shows that she was of European descent. Many trees list the mother as of native origins, but this has been disproven inthe Mothers of Acadi
2 CONC a mtDNA project.
2 CONT :The name "Collineau de Montaguerre", with a few variants as it got copied from one genealogy to another, was apparently, initially, a code name for a female brick wall in New France genealogies. This is supported by the fact that
2 CONC  most Collineau de Montaguerre individuals are setas earliest ancestors, female, and paired off with Unknown spouses.
2 CONT :Connection of Edmee and Catherine (sisters) ≤ref>Stephen A. White, "ACloser Look at Some of the Records", Centre d’études acadiennes, Université de Moncton.'' http://www.acadian-home.org/SAW-CloserLookRecords.html '' ≤/ref>::"It 
2 CONC had long been known that a number of dispensations found in the marriages between the descendants of Edmée Lejeune and those of Catherine Lejeune proved that the two women were sisters, and it was thought that with the far more ex
2 CONC tensive documentation that had become available since Father Godbout’s death there might be found some additional previously unknown or unnoticed dispensations that would support his suppositions. It was also realized, however, th
2 CONC at if marriages between Lejeune descendants were traced where dispensations ought to have been granted according to Father Godbout’s presumptions, but were not, then those presumptions would be cast into doubt and thereby rebutted
2 CONC ::"It must be remembered that there are no records that actually statethat any of the early Lejeunes in Acadia were siblings. The only thing that had been observed to connect them was their common name, which gave rise to a presum
2 CONC ption that they were related. The presumption insofar as it respected Edmée and Catherine Lejeune was '''long ago replaced by a certainty because of dispensations found in certain marriagerecords in the Port-Royal registers'''."
2 CONT
2 CONT === DNA ===
2 CONT The [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/MothersofAcadia/default.aspxMothers of Acadia maternal DNA project] posts its ongoing Maternal DNA results [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresu
2 CONC lts '''here''']. '''To date, the haplogroup of both sisters is consistently reported as U6a7a, indicating European origins.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT == Acknowledgements ==
2 CONT ::[[Reader-22 | Karen Theriot Reader]] Rootsweb.com.
