1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Sources:'''
2 CONT **1671 Acadie Census - shown to be 47 years old which estimates birth c.1624.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * AKAN: Aimée 
2 CONT * Nickname: dit Briard 
2 CONT * Census: 1671; 1693 Port-Royal
2 CONT
2 CONT *Edmee is listed as a Metis woman, having been born in a Metis village, as well as having the title of "Sauvagesse". 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Edmee is believed to be the daughter of Pierre Lejeune b. 1595 in France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Regarding DNA==
2 CONT DNA Haplogroup U6A7a1. This is from the Iberian Peninsula area, although a mutation of it, this particular cluster evolved in Acadia 500 years ago. This indicates some degree of blood from there. There are multiple reasons this co
2 CONC uld be but none can be proven absolutely. She was born in a Metis village and raised as such, indicating she is Metis. The possible reasons for her mtDNA having the haplogroup:
2 CONT *  Her mother's side may have a Basque woman on it at some point.
2 CONT *  Her mother's side may have a Basque man whose mtDNA crossed over, as it does happen, albeit rarely. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes:'''   mtDNA does not often cross over from the paternal line, though it can and does happen, albeit rarely. Basque women did not go on voyages with the men and the Basque never attempted to settle the area with families, 
2 CONC thus causing the problems of how either is possible. It is likely we will never know exactly how this occured, and people will have their own theories. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her records all come with the title "Sauvagesse"  It's the feminine form of Sauvage, a French description of the native peoples, that translates in English as "savage." 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Edmee's parents are unknown, though all that is known is thus:'''
2 CONT * She was born in a Metis settlement, and given the title of "Sauvagesse".  
2 CONT * She has Portuguese ancestry from her mother's side. 
2 CONT * Her mother likely was Metis herself, or else mostly Mi'kmaq with some Basque blood in her. 
2 CONT * Her father is believed to have been Pierre Lejeune, a frenchman who is rumoured to have come with his family, including Edmee, though all records suggest he came alone and list Edmee as having been born in a Metis village in Aca
2 CONC dia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born 1624 at Micmac Village near Port Royal, Acadie, NS, Canada. Mother Micmac Indienne (I03533), Father Pierre Lejeune (I03326). Siblings Catherine Jeanne Lejeune, Pierre Lejeune. Marriage of Francois Gautrot and Edmee Legune 163
2 CONC 5 at Martaize, Loudun, Vienne, France. Children: Marie Francois Louise Gaudrot, Claude Gautrot, Charles Gautrot, Anne Gautreaux. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~treeleavesbycole/NWEB1/ppl/b/5/b5869d89caa390f65ae.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !1st husband - POTET 
2 CONT 2nd husband - Gautreaux
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse with her husband's first wife, Marie. Both wives had a daughter named Marie. Also read all the notes in Discussions. This woman was not Amerindian, nor was she the daughter of Pierre Lejeune. Please do not attach he
2 CONC r as a child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Edmee's WikiTree profile for more complete information and discussion: https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lejeune-21
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmée Lejeune was born about 1624 in France. She was most likely the sister of Catherine Lejeune (m. Francois Savoie) since Edmee's and Catherine's descendants share the haplogroup U6a71a, although it's also possible they could ha
2 CONC ve had the same grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT The names of Edmee's parents are unknown. It is a frequent assumption that Catherine and Edmee Lejeune's mother was of Amerindian descent, however the mtDNA haplogroup U6a71a is of European descent which disproves this theory. See
2 CONC  the ongoing mtDNA test results of Acadian mothers here: https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia?iframe=mtresults
2 CONT
2 CONT It is often assumed that Pierre Lejeune dit Briard is the brother of Catherine and Edmee, but considering the lack of dispensation for kindred in the 1760 marriage between a granddaughter of Pierre & a grandson of Catherine Lejeun
2 CONC e, we can conclude Pierre is not the brother of either Catherine or Edmee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmee Lejeune married François Gautrot about 1644 in Port Royal. François was previously married to a woman named Marie and he had 2 children with her. Edmee and François had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Marie (c1645-1732) m. c1661 Claude Theriot
2 CONT 2) Jean (c1648-___)
2 CONT 3) Renee (c1652-1737) m. c1671 Jean Labat dit Le Marquis
2 CONT 4) Marguerite (c1654-1727) m. c1670 Jacques dit Jacob Girouard
2 CONT 5) Francois (c1657-bef.1683) m. c1677 Marie Brun
2 CONT 6) Claude (c1659-1733) m. c1684 Marie Theriot
2 CONT 7) Charles (c1661-c1724) m. c1684 Francois Rimbault
2 CONT 8) Jeanne (c1665-1749) m. c1682 Pierre Lanoue
2 CONT 9) Germain (c1668-___)
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmee's death is not recorded but she died sometime between the 1693 and 1698 Port Royal census.
2 CONT
2 CONT mtDNA for Edmee Lejeune
2 CONT HVR1: 16172C 16219G 16278T
2 CONT Reason This Information Is Correct:
2 CONT acadian-home.org, go to mtDNA section
2 CONT or DNA Haplogroup U6A7a1
