2 CONT Edmée Aimée Lejeune
2 CONT Birth: 1624, Canada
2 CONT Death: 1698, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmee was baptized in about 1624. She married Francois Gaudreau in 1644, in Port Royal, Acadia. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Marie (1645-1732) md Claude Theriault
2 CONT 2) Renee (1652-1737) md Jean Labatte
2 CONT 3) Marguerite (1654-1727) md Jacques-Jacob Girouard
2 CONT 4) Francois (1657-) md Marie-Sebastienne brun
2 CONT 5) Claude (1659-1733) md Marie-Elizabeth Theriault
2 CONT 6) Charles (1661-) md Francois Raimbault
2 CONT 7) Jeanne (1665-1749) md Pierre Lanoue
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmée is the sister of Catherine Lejeune.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links:
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT François Gaudreau (1613 - 1693)*
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse with her husband's first wife, Marie. Both wives had a daughter named Marie. Also read all the notes in Discussions. This woman was not Amerindian, nor was she the daughter of Pierre Lejeune. Please do not attach he
2 CONC r as a child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Edmee's WikiTree profile for more complete information and discussion: https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lejeune-21
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmée Lejeune was born about 1624 in France. She was most likely the sister of Catherine Lejeune (m. Francois Savoie) since Edmee's and Catherine's descendants share the haplogroup U6a71a, although it's also possible they could ha
2 CONC ve had the same grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT The names of Edmee's parents are unknown. It is a frequent assumption that Catherine and Edmee Lejeune's mother was of Amerindian descent, however the mtDNA haplogroup U6a71a is of European descent which disproves this theory. See
2 CONC  the ongoing mtDNA test results of Acadian mothers here: https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia?iframe=mtresults
2 CONT
2 CONT It is often assumed that Pierre Lejeune dit Briard is the brother of Catherine and Edmee, but considering the lack of dispensation for kindred in the 1760 marriage between a granddaughter of Pierre & a grandson of Catherine Lejeun
2 CONC e, we can conclude Pierre is not the brother of either Catherine or Edmee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmee Lejeune married François Gautrot about 1644 in Port Royal. François was previously married to a woman named Marie and he had 2 children with her. Edmee and François had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Marie (c1645-1732) m. c1661 Claude Theriot
2 CONT 2) Jean (c1648-___)
2 CONT 3) Renee (c1652-1737) m. c1671 Jean Labat dit Le Marquis
2 CONT 4) Marguerite (c1654-1727) m. c1670 Jacques dit Jacob Girouard
2 CONT 5) Francois (c1657-bef.1683) m. c1677 Marie Brun
2 CONT 6) Claude (c1659-1733) m. c1684 Marie Theriot
2 CONT 7) Charles (c1661-c1724) m. c1684 Francois Rimbault
2 CONT 8) Jeanne (c1665-1749) m. c1682 Pierre Lanoue
2 CONT 9) Germain (c1668-___)
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmee's death is not recorded but she died sometime between the 1693 and 1698 Port Royal census. 
2 CONT
