2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jean arrived in Acadie in 1668.
2 CONT 1671 Census of Acadie - Jehan was age 25, his wife, Francoise Savois was age 18. Their six week old baby girl had not yet been named. They had one cow and one sheep and no cultivated land.
2 CONT 1686 Census of Port Royal - Jean Corporon was shown as 39, wife Francois Savoye was age 35. They had the following children-Marie age 16, Madelaine age 14, Jeanne age 12, Jean 10, Marie 8, Isabelle 6, Cicille 4, Marguerite 1. They
2 CONC  had 2 cattle, 2 sheep and 1 hog.
2 CONT 1693 Census of Port Royal-Jean age 44, Francoise age 41. Their children-Jacques 18, Jean 15, Elisabet 11, Cecille 6, Marguerite 8, Martin 6, Francois 5, Charles 2, Jean 1. They had 6 cattle, 4 sheep, 6 hogs, 6 arpents and one gun.
2 CONC  Daughter Madgeleine was married to Bernard Doucet. Daughter Jeanne was married to Antoine Hebert. Daughter Marie was married to Charles Boudrot (census of the Mines).
2 CONT 1698 Census of Port Royal-Jean age 50, Francoise Savoye was age 46. Children were Jean 21, Elisabeth 17, Cecile 15, Marguerite 13, Martin 11, Francois 9, Jean 7, Marie 4, Ambroise 2.  They had 4 cows, 7 sheep and one servant. Daug
2 CONC hter Jean was married to Antoine Hebert. Daughter Magdne was married to Bernard Doucet.
2 CONT 1700 Census of Port Royal-Jean age 51, Francoise Savoie age 48. Children were Jaques age 25, Jean age 22, Martin age 13, Francois 12, Jean 8, Elisabet 18, Cecille 16, Marguerite 15, Marine 7. They had 5 cattle, 6 sheep, 6 arpents 
2 CONC and one gun. Daughters Madeleine and Jeanne were married to Bernard Doucet and Antoine Hebert, respectively.
2 CONT 1701 Census - Jean and wife Francoise were missing from census.
2 CONT 1703 Census - showed a Jean Corporon, his wife, 1 girl and 1 arms bearer (could be Jean Jr.)
2 CONT 1707 Census - showed a Corporon and his wife, 3 boys 14 or older, 1 younger boy, 2 girls 12 or older and 1 younger girl.
2 CONT Jacques may not belong to this family. He is missing from the 1686 and 1698 census but appears in the 1693 and 1700 census. According to census Charles dies circa 1695 and Ambroise ca 1699 as they are missing from the 1698 and 170
2 CONC 0 census reports and they would have been young children during those two reports.
