2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT '''Marie Magdeleine Corporon''' was born in Acadie around 1672. She was most likely the first-born child of Jean Corporon and Françoise Savoie, counted on the census as "daughter, six weeks old" with her parents in Port-Royal in 1
2 CONC 671.≤ref name=1671Cen />(If a Jacques were born before her he seems likely to have died young.No records for him have surfaced, and another son possibly named [Jean] Jacques was born a few years later.)  Her parents' marriage date
2 CONC  has been estimated by this listing of an only child, almost certainly Magdeleine, who was 6 weeks old at the time of the 1671 Port Royal Census.≤ref name=1671Cen>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Roya
2 CONC l, Acadie," from his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy'' [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm
2 CONC .lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>
2 CONT : Jehan CORPORON, 25, 
2 CONT :wife Francoise SAVOIE 18; 
2 CONT :Child: one daughter of 6 weeks; 
2 CONT :cattle 1, sheep 1.≤/blockquote>
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT The family was counted again in Port-Royal in 1686. She was about sixteen at the time of the 1686 Port Royal Census; there is some confusionwith the first two daughters' names.≤ref>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Ce
2 CONC nsus, at Port-Royal, Acadie," online at his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,'' at [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritag
2 CONC e.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the NationalArchives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>
2 CONT : Jean CORBERON             39
2 CONT : Francois SAVOYE            35
2 CONT : Marie                                16
2 CONT : Magdelaine                     14
2 CONT : Jeanne                              12
2 CONT : Jean                                   10
2 CONT : Marie                                  8
2 CONT : Isabelle                              6
2 CONT : Cecille                                4
2 CONT : Marguerite                        1≤/blockquote>
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT Madeleine married [[Doucet-94|Bernard Doucet]] around 1690 (the date apparently estimated from the information regarding a child on the census of 1693)≤ref>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.
2 CONC ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ''Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes''] (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p. 411≤/ref> and they were living in Port Royal with one child in 1693. If they
2 CONC  had a daughter c.1689, she evidently was overlooked, or had died before 1693.≤ref>Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," online at his website, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy,'' [http://freepage
2 CONC s.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 ofthe National Ar
2 CONC chives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote>
2 CONT :Bernard DOUCET 28, 
2 CONT :Madeleine CORPORON 22, 
2 CONT :Jean 1; 
2 CONT :4 cattle, 6 sheep, 5 pigs, 1 gun ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT They were counted in Port-Royal again in 1698.≤ref> Tim Hebert, "Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie," from hiswebsite, ''Acadian-Cajun Genealogy''; [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealog
2 CONC y/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensemen
2 CONC ts 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-166≤blockquote> 
2 CONT :Bernard DOUCET 30; 
2 CONT :Madeleine, CORPORON (wife) 25; 
2 CONT :Jean-Marie 7; 
2 CONT :Marie 4; :3 cattle, 4 sheep, 2 hogs, 2 arpents, 5 1/2 arpents.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT After Bernard Doucet died in 1709, Madeleine married François Le Clair dit la Verdure, soldier, son of François Le Clair, wine merchant living in Tionville in Lorraine and Marie Savoye on 24 November 1710 at Port Royal.≤ref>Librar
2 CONC y and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 151) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/151?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>François Le Clair and Magdelaine 
2 CONC Corporon, marriage 24 November 1710, in ''An Acadian Parish Remembered'', "The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755," RG 1 vol. 26, p. 300; online at 1710 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?I
2 CONC D=1269≤/ref>
2 CONT When the widowed Madeleine was about 63 years of age, she married Claude Boudrot in 1735. ≤ref>''Nova Scotia Archives'', "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 
2 CONC 1 volume 26a page 138; online database with images, [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2086 marriage of Claude Boudrot and Madelene Corporon  7 Aug  1735], accessed 30 October 2019≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine died in 1753 in Grand Pre, Nova Scotia. {{citation needed}}
2 CONT
