2 CONT == Biography =='''Marguerite Pellerin''' was born around 1699. She was the daughter of [[Pellerin-2|Étienne Pellerin]] and [[Savoie-11|Jeanne Savoie]]. She was age 1 on the 1700 census of Port Royal.
2 CONT She married Bernard Godet, son of  Pierre Godet and Marie Blanchard 7 February 1716 at Port Royal. The bride and groom both signed and Pierre Godet and Nicolas Daigle also signed.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroi
2 CONC sse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 173) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/173?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered TheRegisters of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis
2 CONC  Royal, 1702-1755 Bernard Godet and Marguerite Pellerin marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 317 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1321≤/ref>
2 CONT *Five children: Joseph Gaudet, Germain Gaudet, Marguerite Gaudet,AmandGregoire Gaudet, Pierre Gaudet
2 CONT She passed away 1 February 1724 aged about 25 years, and was buried the next day at Port Royal, Acadia. ≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Marguerite Pellerin burial RG
2 CONC  1 volume 26 page 365 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1575≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada,Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-.)-1870 C-1870 (image 210) http://heritage
2 CONC .canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/210?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
