2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography =='''Joseph Christome  Prejean''' was born about 1700 in Port Royal, Acadia. He was the son of [[Prejean-7|Jean Prejean]] and [[Savoie-1|Andre Savoie]]. He was age 5 months on the 1701 census of Port Royal.
2 CONT Joseph Prijan married Marie Louise Como, daughter of Abraham Como and Marguerite Pitre, 28 September 1723 at Port Royal.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870
2 CONC  C-1870 (image 183) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/183?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755Joseph Prijan and Marie Louis Como marria
2 CONC ge RG 1 volume 26 page 334 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1372≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Children:
2 CONT # Amand PREJEAN ca 1724-1787
2 CONT # Marguerite PREJEAN ca 1725-1777
2 CONT # Anne PREJEAN ca 1729-
2 CONT # Joseph PREJEAN 1731-/1771
2 CONT # Charles PREJEAN 1735-1805
2 CONT # Amable dit Pierre-Cadien PREJEAN 1738-1810
2 CONT # Abraham PREJEAN 1741-ca 1785
2 CONT # Basile PREJEAN ca 1745-1823
2 CONT # female PREJEAN ca 1747-
2 CONT CENSUS: 1701, Port Royal, Acadia: Jean PREJAN 52, Andree SAVOYE (wife)35; Pierre 12, Jean 10, Francois 8, '''Joseph 5 (sic for months)''', Marie 17 Anne 14, Magdeleine 3; 1 gun 16 cattle, 10 sheep, 12 hogs, 3 arpents.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away after 30 August 1756.
