2 CONT Marguerite LeBreton aka Duguay Born about 1715 in Bayonne, Gascogne, France Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown] [sibling(s) unknown] Wife of Irené Duguay — married about 7 Oct 1733 in Ste-Famille, Pabos, Chandler, Ga
2 CONC spé, Qc., Canada [uncertain] DESCENDANTS descendants Mother of Marie-Anne Duguay, Geneviève Duguay, Anne Duguay, Catherine Thérèse Duguay, Pierre Duguay, Jacques Duguay, François Duguay, Jean Marie Duguay, Marie-Josephe Duguay, Pi
2 CONC erre René Duguay, Marquerite Duguay and Irene Duguay Died 7 Oct 1773 in Paspébiac, Gaspe, Quebec Profile managers: Lawerence Duguay private message [send private message], Dawn Ellis private message [send private message], Almon P
2 CONC ope private message [send private message], Antoinia Breau private message [send private message], Theresa Salari private message [send private message], and Louise Reville private message [send private message] Profile last modif
2 CONC ied 23 Oct 2019 | Created 27 Jan 2015 This page has been accessed 2,066 times. Biography PRDH does not give a birth date for Marguerite, but does indicate that she was from Bayonne, Gascogne, France. They say she and René Duguay m
2 CONC arried before 1729 in France. They had nine children. [1] Elle a eu 10 enfants Duguay (Anne, Geneviève, Jacques, François, Jean-Marie, Catherine-Thérèse, Marie-Josèphe, Pierre-René, Marguerite, René).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage ou union de fait Marguerite à 19 ans & Rene à 19 ans 1729 in France Source: Mariage avant 1729 en France de parents inconnus. S. White ne fait aucune allusion non plus, que Marguerite Breton soit d'origine Acadienne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Flag of France Marguerite LeBreton migrated from France to New France. Flag of New France Sources ↑ IGD, (http://www.genealogie.umontreal.ca/Membership/en/PRDH/Individu/160245), Individual Detail for Marguerite Breton, # 160245, I
2 CONC nstitut généalogique Drouin, La Prairie, Québec. See also:
2 CONT
