2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Beaubassin, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==:Gabriel dit Pierre Chiasson, son of Guyon & Jeanne Bernard, was born about 1667. ≤ref name=White>ITitle: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714; Author: Stephen A. White; Publi
2 CONC cation: 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p. 1457≤/ref>
2 CONT He is found working in Beaubassin as a domestique de Michel Le Neuf deLa Valliere≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census,at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1
2 CONC 686 Census Transcribed]. The original census canbe found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, 
2 CONC Images 15-60.≤blockquote>CHIGNOUCTOU/BEAUBASSIN, Acadia, age 20 years, as Gabriel, domesticof Michel LE NEUF de La Valliere. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Gabriel married around 1688 to Marie SAVOIE, daughter of Francois & Catherine LEJEUNE of Port-Royal.  ≤ref name=White />.  They settled in Beaubassin≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, atPort-Royal, Acadie [
2 CONC http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can befound at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of 
2 CONC the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote>  Gabriel CHIASON 26, Marie SAVOYE his wife 25, Michel 4, Pierre 2; 4cattle, 6 sheep, 3 hogs, 3 arpents, 1 gun. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>T
2 CONC im Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadian
2 CONC a.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> Beaubassin: Gabriel CHIASSON 40 [sic]; Marie SAVOYE (wife) 
2 CONC 33; Michel 14; Jean 8; Francois 3; Marie 6; 3 cattle, 1 hog, 3 arpents, 1 gun. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/geneal
2 CONC ogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada]“Acadie Recense
2 CONC ments 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote> Beaubassin: Gabriel CHIASSON, widower; Children: Marie Joseph, Francois, Abraham, Francoise, Margueritte, Judith.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT He died 10 APR 1741 in Beaubassin, Acadia and was buried there the next day.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada Fonds des Archives départementales de la Charente-Maritime [La Rochelle, France] : C-1207 Registres de Beaubassin - reel_
2 CONC c1207 MG 6 A 2 (Image 79) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1207/79?r=0&s=6 Burial]≤blockquote>Age 75 years old. Witnesses: Jean Baptiste CHIASSON, son of the deceased; Jacques QUESSY; Abraham ARSENAUD.≤/blockquot
2 CONC e>≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:* Milton P. and Norma Gaudet Rieder, Acadian Church Records, vol. II (Metairie, LA: Authors, 1976). Repository: Family History Library;  Salt Lake City  UT 84150* [http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?pid=87
2 CONC 834 Genealogy Gabriel-Pierre Chiasson]
2 CONT
