2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Antoine arrived in Acadia in 1636. Possibly on same ship as Jerome Guerin?
2 CONT "Vraisemblement originaire de Martaize dans la region de Loudon department
2 CONT de la vienne en France. Arrive de France en Acadie vers 1636. Il etait sans
2 CONT doute le beau gendre de Rene Landry." This quote may be from Bona Arseneau,
2 CONT but since I did not do the original note I am not sure. Marriage Source:
2 CONT Corrections to Bona Arsenault.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine was born in France in 1609 and traveled to Port Royal, Acadie in 1636.
2 CONT He married Antonette, his first year in Port Royal. They sought sanctuary on
2 CONT Isle-St.-Jean in 1755 but were eventually deported to France.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Antoine Bourg, born in 1609, was probaby a native o Martaize in theregion of Loudun, department of Vienne, France. He came to Acadia about1636. The year h arrived he married Antoinette Landry who had come toAcadia with her brother
2 CONC , Rene Landry. Antoine and Antoinette settled inthe area of Port Royal. Re: Martin, Lucien and Melba: "Remember Us" Page 69-70 Arsenault, Bona: Histoire et Genealogie desAcadiens, vol. 2, pp.448-50, 452, 612, 717, 804; vol. 6, p. 
