2 CONT Background Notes
2 CONT He arrived in Acadia in 1636 and was undoubtedly the brother-in-law of
2 CONT Rene Landry (Arsenault, Vol 2, page 448; see also Massignon, Genevieve,
2 CONT Les Parlers francais d'Acadie, Vol 1, page 49). In the 1678 census of
2 CONT Port Royal, he and his wife had three acres, six cattle, one gun, and a
2 CONT boy, age 10 born in 1660 and a girl born in 1667 andage 11.
2 CONT
