2 CONC  by Phobe Chauvin Morrison, p. 67. Published by Terrebonne Genealogical Society, Houma, LA. Book located in Dallas Public Library.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Antoine Bourg was born 1609 in Martaize, France in the region of Loudun,
2 CONT department de la Vienne. He arrived in Acadia in 1636 and established
2 CONT his home at Port Royal where he married Antoniette Landry that same
2 CONT year. Antoine was the progenitor of the Bourg line in Acadia. Some of
2 CONT his children established their homes at Cobequid. Many of his
2 CONT descendants were to flee Colbequid prior to the expulsion in order to
2 CONT escape the English and sought sanctuary on Isle-St. Jean which was a
2 CONT French Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Background
2 CONT "Antoine Bourg, born in France in 1609, married Antoinette Landry, and came to Acadie in 1632 with the Commander de Razilly. He was the ancestor of the Acadian families of Bourg or Bourque, and grandfather of Alexander Bourg, sieu
2 CONC r de Bellchumeur, royal notary of Mines District." -"Notes to Accompany The Plan of the River of Annapoilis Royal", prepared by Mr. Placide Gauet, Genealogist to the Public Archives of Canada. Acadian Genealogy Exchange, Vol. XX #
2 CONC 1, Jan., 1991, pg. 25 "Antoine Boure arrived in Acadie about 1636, as a colonist recruited from the Seigneury of Aulnay. In the 1671 census of Port Royal he is listed as a plowman with four arpents of cleared land. Anoine and Anto
2 CONC inette were both still living at the time of the 1686 census." -
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Notes by Mr. Placide Gauet
2 CONT "Antoine Bourg, born in France in 1609, married Antoinette Landry, and came to Acadie in 1632 with the Commander de Razilly. He was the ancestor of the Acadian families of Bourg or Bourque, and grandfather of Alexander Bourg, sieu
2 CONC r de Bellchumeur, royal notary of Mines District." -" Notes to Accompany The Plan of the River of Annapoilis Royal", prepared by Mr. Placide Gauet, Genealogist to the Public Archives of Canada. Acadian Genealogy Exchange, Vol. XX 
2 CONC #1, Jan., 1991, pg. 25 "Antoine Boure arrived in Acadie about 1636, as a colonist recruited from the Seigneury of Aulnay. In the 1671 census of Port Royal he is listed as a plowman with four arpents of cleared land. Anoine and Ant
2 CONC oinette were both still living at the time of the 1686 census." -
