1 NOTE His father, unknown, born in 1583 in Of, Loudun, Vienne France; his mother, unknown, born abt 1585 in France; they were married abt 1607 in Touraine, Poitou, France; show another child other than Antoine, Perrine Bourg, born in 16
2 CONC 22 in Loudun, Vienne, France, she died in 1686 in Acadie, Canada; source: <http://home.attbi.com/~sodapop68/webtree/pafg53.htm> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT Married 1636 Antoinette Landry and 9 children; sources: Individual record of self (filed L-13-30); A short bio of Antoine Bourg acquired from the internet (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT The 1671 census of Acadia shows:  ANTOINE BOURC (sic) age 62, his spouse ANTHOINETTE LANDRY, age 53; 11 children, (4 married, Marie, age 26; Francois, age 27; Jehan, age 24; Bernard, age 22); others, Martin, age 21; Jeanne, age 18
2 CONC ; Renee, age 16; Huguette, age 14; Jeanne, age 12; Habrahan, age 9; Marguerite, age 4.
2 CONT "Mothers of Acadia" (copy filed L-14-16) shows the following: Antoinette Landry (#3487), 65 years old, wife of Antoine Bourg (#3433), raised a family of 11 children.
2 CONT Bourg Village, on the north river and close to the fort at Port-Royal, face Belleview Village on the south river.  Antoine Belliveau, head of the family, married Andree Guyon. <http://www.geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga15.html
2 CONC > (copy filed L-13-30) states married 1642 at Port Royal, Acadia, Canada to Antoinette Landry with a family of 12 children.
2 CONT A short bio of Antoine Bourg acquired from the internet (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT 1686 Census lists Antoine, age 95 and Antoinette, age 80; source: A short bio of Antoine Bourg acquired from the internet (copy filed L-13-30).
