2 CONT
2 CONT The following is the translated version: <http://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=fr&u=http://www.smartnet.ca/users/roberochon/bour.htm&prev=/search%3Fq%3D%2522jean%2Bclaude%2Blandry%2522%26start%3D40%26hl%3Den%26lr%3D%26ie
2 CONC %3DUTF-8%26sa%3DN>:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANTOINE Borough-bourque
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Bour or Borough 1st, was born in France in 1609, according to the census of 1671 and in 1591, according to that of 1686. Some believe that it is originating in Martaizé, small commune located in the province of Poitou, tod
2 CONC ay in the department of Vienna.
2 CONT
2 CONT We know that Antoine came to Acadie at the beginning of the year 1640, or perhaps even between 1632 and 1636. About 1642, he marries at Port-Royal, Antoinette Landry, born in 1620, daughter of the ancestors, Jean-Claude Landry and
2 CONC  Marie Sallée, and sister of Rene Landry married to Perrine Bourg, the sister of Antoine Bourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Acadie, the household of Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry fixes itself on northern bank of the river of Port-Royal and gives his name to the village of the Borough. This village is located at a short distance, in the North-W
2 CONC est of the Fort old man of the Capital.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Village, of the Borough had a splendid sight on the human regrouping of the Fort. There Mélanson, Boudrot , Vigneau, Bergeron and others are established, because "people of the Fort" came from a little everywhere, being French
2 CONC  soldiers or, and especially, craftsmen of all the utility trades.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the thirteen children of the Antoine/Antoinette couple, three have a descent to us, in this genealogical description.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first child, who is in fact, the second of the couple, Jean Bour, born in 1647. Jean marries in Cobequid, about 1667, Marguerite Martin. She was born about 1639, sister of Marie Martin, married to Pierre Morin , said Boucher a
2 CONC nd daughter of the ancestor Pierre Martin and Catherine Vigneau, came from Saint-Germain de Bourgueil. On the census of 1686, Jean Bour is 40 years old and Marguerite Martin is 42 years old, at Port-Royal. Their daughter Magdelein
2 CONC e Bour is 8 years old and she continues the bond of descent by marrying Pierre Leblanc, in 1694, son of the ancestor Daniel Leblanc and Francoise Gaudet .
2 CONT The second child, a girl, the sixth of the couple, named Jeanne Bour, born in 1653. She marries about 1669, at Port-Royal, Pierre Comeau, known as Esturgeon, born in 1653, also in Port-Royal, elder son of the ancestors of Comeau, 
2 CONC Pierre and Pink Bayols. On the census of 1686, Pierre Comeau and Jeanne Bour are 32 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Then, the third child who concerns us, the eighth of the couple Antoine/Antoinette, Hughette Bour, born in 1657. She marries about 1676, at Port-Royal, Sebastien Brun, son of the Brun ancestors, Vincent and Marie Brault.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first nominal census, in Acadie, in 1671, shows us Bour; Antoine Bour, the father with his sons Michel, Bernard, François and Jean Bour, forming as many households. On the acadian census of 1686, Antoine Bour is 95 years old a
2 CONC nd Antoinette Landry is 80 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Bourc, is only one simple typographical error. The etymology-even of the name Bour, in Dict. of former French, also means "fraud:
2 CONT catch "; it comes from the Latin-popular word "will burra".
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Bour, can also come from Flemish "boer" which decides "bour" while meaning "country".
2 CONT
2 CONT The word Bourg means "large village, which comes from the Germanic word" borc "which means castle-extremely.
2 CONT
2 CONT The graphic variations are: Bour - Flock - Bouhours - Borough - Dubourg - Bourk - Bourgues - Bourcq - Bourque.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus thanks to the ancestor Antoine Bourg, the name of Borough and Bourque took root in America.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.acadian-home.org/ancestorsacadian.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANTOINE  BOURQUE
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Bourque, is the father of the Bourque family in Acadia. He was born in France about 1609. There is no actual proof of birth place but it is assumed that he was born in Martaizé, in the province of Poitou (today, Vienna). I
2 CONC n any event, it is known that Antoine came to Acadia at the beginning of the years of 1640, or perhaps sooner. About 1642, he married Antoinette Landry and they had at least 11 children together.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.kencrouse.com/stories/alfred3.htm>:
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Bourg, born 1609 in Martaize, Loudin region, Vienne, France. He married Antoinette Landry 1641 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoinette Landry, born 1618 in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Francois Bourg, born 1644; married (1) Marguerite Boudrot 1664 in Port Royal, Acadia; married (2) Marguerite Robichaud 1680 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Marie Bourg, born 1645; married Vincent Breault 1661 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Jehan Bourg, born 1647 in Port Royal, Acadia; died Abt. 1695 in Cobequid, Acadia; married Marguerite Martin 1667 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Bernard Bourg, born 1649 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Francoise Brun 1670 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Martin Bourg, born 1650 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Marie Potier Abt. 1675 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Jeanne (Marie) Bourg, born 1653 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Jean Antoine Belliveau 1671 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. Renee Magdeleine Bourg, born 1655 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Charles Boudrot 1674 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. Huguette Bourg, born 1657 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Sabastien Brun 1676 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ix. Jeanne Bourg, born 1659 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Pierre Paul Esturgeon Comeau 1677 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT x. Abraham Bourg, born 1662; married Marie Brun 1679 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT xi. Michel Bourg, born 1665 in Port Royal, Acadia; died Bef. 1671 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT xii. Marguerite Bourg, born 1667 in Port Royal, Acadia; married Louis Allain 1690.
