2 CONT From Stephen White:
2 CONT Antoine Bourque is the father of the Bourque family in Acadia. He was born in France about 1609. There is no actual proof of his birthplace, but it is assumed that he was born in Martaize, in the province of Poitou (today Vienna).
2 CONC  In any event, it is known that Antoine came to Arcadia at the beginning of the year 1640, or perhaps sooner. About 1642 he married Antoine Landry and they had at least 11 children together.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.geocities.com/bourque_ca/history.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT BOURQUE FAMILY HISTORY
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Bourg was the first of our ancestors, in the Bourg, Bourq, Bourque, Burke direct male line, to arrive in the new world. France had begun to have colonies that lasted over the winter months in Acadia and Quebec in the early
2 CONC  1600's. Antoine and his wife, Antoinette Landry, were one of the first agrictulural colonial families to settle in the new world after Acadia was confirmed French in 1632. Records show that they probably came from the estates of 
2 CONC Charles D'Aulnay or from the estates of D'Aulnay's mother, near or in Martaize, department de la Vienne, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine and his wife, Antoinette, Antoine's sister Perrine Bourg and her second husband, Rene Landry,Antoinette's brother,(brother and sister married sister and brother), settled in Port Royal, D'Aulnay's headquarters, a community
2 CONC  situated in a sheltered bay off the Bay of Fundy. We can trace our family genealogy from these two families to the descendants of Pierre Bourg (1740) and Cecile Dugas (c.1813). The mojority of Pierre and Cecile's descendants live
2 CONC  in four small Cape Breton communities, French Cove, Sampsonville, River Bourgeois, and Isle Madame (Arichat).
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.cafa.org/BourqueGenealogy.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of Antoine Bourg:
2 CONT Genealogy of Antoine Bourg: This genealogy information has been updated with Stephen Whites recent publication "Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes."
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST GENERATION
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Antoine Bourg- was born 1609 in Martaize, France. Arrived in Acadie with Commander Isaac de Razilly in 1632. In 1636 Antoine moved to Port Royal to establish his farm. Antoine married Antoinette Landry in 1642 and according to 
2 CONC the Port Royal census of 1671, they had 11 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT
2 CONT I Francois b 1643 Port Royal; m 1665 PR Marguarite Boudrot d/o Michel Boudrot/Michelle Aucoin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii Marie b 1645 PR; m ca 1659-1661 PR Vincent Brault d 19 Apr 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT iii Jean b 1646 PR; m 1667 Marguerite Martin d/oPierre Martin/Catherine Vigneau d 1698 Cobequid
2 CONT
2 CONT iv Bernard b 1648 PR; m 1670 Francoise Brun d/o Vincent Brun/Renee Breau; d 1725 Cobequid.
2 CONT
2 CONT v Martin b 1650 PR; m 1670 Marie Potet d/o___otet/Marie Gauterot. Resided at Cobeequid.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi Jeanne b 1653 PR, m 1673 Jean Antoine Belliveau s/o Antoine Belliveau/Marie Guyon; (2) Cecil Melanson-2 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii Renee b 1655 PR; 1672 (1) Charles Boudrot s/o Michel Boudrot/Michelle Aucoin; (2) Marie Corporon.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii Huguette b 1657 PR; m 1675 Sebastien Brun s/o Vincent Brun/Renee Brot at PR; d 1708 France.
2 CONT
2 CONT ix Jeanne b 1659 PR; m 1677 Pierre Comeau s/o Pierre Comeau/Rose Bayol PR; d aft 1708; 19 children
2 CONT
2 CONT x Abraham b 1662 PR; m ca 1683 Marie Brun d/o Vincent Brun/Renee Breau
2 CONT
2 CONT xi Marguerite b 1667 PR; m 1690 Louis Allain PR; d PR 13 Sept 1727
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Some sources have two additional children: Michel b 1665 and Madeleine       b 1666. If any members can offer information that validates these additions, please forward that information to us.
2 CONT
2 CONT STEPHEN WHITE CHANGES: As a result of Stephen Whites recently released information, at least one of the ancestral lines published in our reunion genealogy book is under question. In fact we have 31 different members with the ances
2 CONC tral line under question. This particular line is Antoine, then Martin, then Francois Louis and on down to the member. According to Stephen Whites information, there is no such person as Francois Louis. There is a Francois, son of
2 CONC  Martin, married to Madeleine Hebert. Then there is a Louis, son of Jean, married to Cecile Michel. Therefore, if we are to assume that Cecile Michel is the right wife, then we have to go with Louis, who is the son of Jean. So the
2 CONC  ancestral line should be: Antoine-Jean-Louis instead of Antoine-Martin-Francois-Louis.
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------
