2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Antoine BOURC, 62, wife Antoinette LANDRY 53; Children (4 married): Marie 26, Francois 27, Jehan 24, Bernard 22; (not married) Martin 21, Jeanne 18, Renee 16, Huguette 14, Jeanne 12, Abraham 9, Marguerite 4; cattle 12, sheep 8. 16
2 CONC 71 Acadian Census Port Royal
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The spelling of the name "Bourg" also appears as "Bourc". This is the spelling used by Elfer Miller in his research.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Background
2 CONT Antoine was born in France in 1609 and traveled to Port Royal, Acadie in 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Antonette, his first year in Port Royal. They sought sanctuary on Isle-St.-Jean in 1755 but were eventually deported to France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He arrived in Acadia in 1636 and was undoubtedly the brother-in-law of Rene Landry (Arsenault, Vol 2, page 448; see also Massignon,Genevieve, Les Parlers francais d'Acadie, Vol 1, page 49). In the 1678 census of Port Royal, he and
2 CONC  his wife had three acres, six cattle, one gun, and a boy, age 10 born in 1660 and a girl born in 1667 and age 11.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Arrived in Port Royal, Acadia in 1636. Marriage also listed as 1643.
2 CONT
