2 CONT '''Do not confuse Jeanne with her younger sister, [[Bourg-21|Marie Jeanne]], who was born around 1659 and married [[Comeau-36|Pierre Comeau]].'''
2 CONT Jeanne was born about 1653 in Acadia to  [[Bourg-126|Antoine Bourg]] and [[Landry-17|Antoinette Landry]].≤ref name=DGFA221 >White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. ''Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadienn
2 CONC es Première partie, 1636 à 1714.'' Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p.221.≤/ref> 
2 CONT She married [[Belliveau-18|Jean-Antoine Belliveau]] around 1673.≤ref name=DGFA221 />≤ref name=DGFA96-98 >White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant,and Hector-J Hébert. ''Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes Première partie, 
2 CONC 1636 à 1714.'' Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p.96-98.≤/ref>
2 CONT Jeanne Bourg died sometime after the 1700 Census of Port Royal≤ref name=DGFA221 />≤ref name=DGFA96-98 />≤ref name=1700C /> and before 1703-1704 when her husband marries the widowed [[Melanson-30|Cécile Melanson]] and has their fir
