2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/086/086028.php
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Renée Madeleine Bourg Bourg
2 CONT BIRTH	1655
2 CONT Port Royal, Annapolis County, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT DEATH	1686 (aged 30–31)
2 CONT Quebec, Canada
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Garrison Graveyard
2 CONT Annapolis Royal, Annapolis County, Nova Scotia, Canada 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	145112608 · View Source
2 CONT MEMORIAL
2 CONT PHOTOS 1
2 CONT FLOWERS 5
2 CONT Renée is the daughter of Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry. She was born about 1655 per Steven A. White and the Port Royal census of 1671, where she was 16 years old. She married Charles Boudrot in about 1672 and they are the pa
2 CONC rents of the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Marie (1675-) md Jean-Charles Trahan
2 CONT 2) Charles (1676-) md Marie Rivet
2 CONT 3) Anne (abt 1678-)
2 CONT 4) René (1680-
2 CONT 5) Marguerite (abt 1682-) md Jean Babin
2 CONT 6) Claude/twin (abt 1683-)
2 CONT 7) Jean-Baptite/twin (abt 1683-) md (1) Cecile Corporon and (2) Louise Saulnier
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 1686 census of Port Royal, Charles is a widower. Her burial record has not been found but Stephen A. White lists her death as before 1686, in accordance with Charles' status on the the census. There is a note on t
2 CONC he Généalogie du Québec et d'Amérique Française site which says "décédé (Décl BIM) Ste-Famille de Pgt avant Rc 1686 (S. White)" which makes it look like he is saying she died in Ste-Famille, but the part he is verifying is the dat
2 CONC e. I have changed her burial from Ste-Famille to Port Royal, as that's where her children were born and where her husband was still living in 1686.
2 CONT ∼
2 CONT Died at Ste. Famille de Pisquit, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT
