2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spelling.   Please contact the Acadian Project before mak
2 CONC ing any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree thebest site for accurate information.
2 CONT :Renée Bourque or Bourg, daughter of [[Bourg-126|Antoine Bourg]] and [[Landry-17|Antoinette Landry]], was born about 1655 in Port Royal, Acadie. 
2 CONT :She was enumerated in the 1671 census of Port-Royal at the age of 16,with her parents and her ten siblings.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadianc
2 CONC ajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadi
2 CONC e Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14. ≤blockquote>  at Port Royal: Antoine BOURC, 62, wifeAntoinette LANDRY 53; Children (4 married): Marie 26, Francois 27, Jehan 24, Bernard 22; (not married) Martin 21, Jeanne 18, Renee 16, Hu
2 CONC guette 14, Jeanne 12, Abraham 9, Marguerite 4; cattle 12, sheep 8.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :Renée and Charles Boudrot, son of  Michel Boudrot and Michelle Aucoin, were married about 1672 in Port-Royal.≤ref>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert,  [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ‘’Dictionnaire Gén
2 CONC éalogique des Familles Acadiennes’’] (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D’études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton,1999) p. 186, 222 ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :They had  eight children:≤br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT # BOUDROT b: Abt 1673 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Charles BOUDROT b: Abt 1674 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Marie BOUDROT b: Abt 1675 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Anne Elizabeth BOUDROT b: Abt 1677 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Rene BOUDROT b: Abt 1678 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Marguerite BOUDROT b: Abt 1682 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Claude BOUDROT b: Abt 1683 in Port Royal
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste BOUDROT b: Abt 1683 in Port Royal
2 CONT :The 1678 census of Port-Royal shows the household of Charles and Rene with their four children, two boys and two girls.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev.
2 CONC  Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm1678 Census]≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Charles Boudrot and Renée Bourg; 9 cattle; 1 gun; 2 boys: 5, 1673; 4, 16
2 CONC 74; 2 girls; 3, 1675; 1, 1677. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :“She does not appear on the 1686 census with her husband and 6 children. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Ce
2 CONC nsus Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Image
2 CONC s 15-60.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Charles BOUDROT 40 (widower); children: Marie 11, Charles 10, Anne 8, Rene 6, Marguerite 4, twins Claude and Jean-Baptiste 3, 1 gun, 2 arpents, 9 cattle, 12 sheep. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  She must 
2 CONC have died between the birth of the twins in 1683 and 1686.”≤ref> KarenTheriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?iz=36&n=bourg&oc=0&p=renee&type=fiche Renée Bourg] at Geneanet, ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:* http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogy=Jean-Baptiste_Boudreau&pid=18496&lng=en&partID=18497
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
