2 CONT == Biography ==:Huguette was born around 1657 in Port Royal, Acadia.≤ref name=White>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. ''Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'' Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'tudes Aca
2 CONC diennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p222. She diedbetween 1687 and the census of 1693.≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/ge
2 CONC nealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Rece
2 CONC nsements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>Antoine BOURC, 62, wife Antoinette LANDRY 53; Children (4 married): Marie26, Francois 27, Jehan 24, Bernard 22; (not married) Martin 21, Jeanne 18, Renee 16, Huguette 14, Jeanne 12, Ab
2 CONC raham 9, Marguerite 4; cattle 12, sheep 8.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :She was married 1675 in Port Royal, Acadia.≤ref> Milton P. and Norma Gaudet Rieder, THE ACADIANS IN FRANCE; 1755-1795; vol. II, Metairie, LA, Authors, 1972; p. 34; EUROPE 944 W2r v.2; contains the Belle Isle en Mer Registers, and
2 CONC  the La Rochette Papers. Her grandson Claude PITREnamed her Henriette BOURG, wife of Sebastien LEBRUN. ≤/ref>. By 1678 she had two children.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this cens
2 CONC us were done by Rev. ClarenceJ. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>
2 CONT Vincent Brun Widower
2 CONT Bastien Brun & Huguette Bourg
2 CONT 1 boy                          1   16771 girl                         2   1676    Jeanne                  1677
2 CONT 6 acres   8 cattle≤≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :Their family had grown with a new baby every two years≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. 
2 CONC The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote
2 CONC >Bastien BRUN 32, Hugette BOURG 28; children: Jeanne 9, Claude 7, Abraham 6, Vincent 5, Jean 4, Antoine 1; 1 gun. 12 cattle 12 sheep, 10 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT : She died in Acadia before the census of 1693.
