1 NOTE Married abt 1676, Sebastien Brun, (born 1654/1656; son of Vincent & Marie Renee Brode/Brault) at Port-Royal, Acadia, Canada; sources: <http://www.odyssee.net/lutrin/Bourg/01.html> (copy filed L-13-30; <http://members.tripod.com/~C
2 CONC yberBart/bourque.htm> (copy filed L-13-30); <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/bour.htm> (copy filed L-13-30 also in her father's internal textfile); "Genealogie de l'ancienne Acadie", BO pg 14 and BR-BU pg 9 shows family with 7 chi
2 CONC ldren;
2 CONT <http://home.attbi.com/~sodapop68/webtree/pafg52.htm> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT A short bio of Antoine Bourg acquired from the internet (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT <http://www.genealogie.com/dgaa/dgaa-b4.html> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~bobmartell/Landry/Landry3.htm>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Jean Claude Landry
2 CONT Generation No. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT 14.  HUGETTE3 BOURQUE (ANTOINETTE (TWIN)2 LANDRY, JEAN CLAUDE1) was born Abt. 1657 in St. Jean Baptiste, Port Royal, Acadia, and died Bet. 1687 - 1693.  She married SEBASTIEN BRUN Abt. 1675 in Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, s
2 CONC on of VINCENT BRUN and MARIE BREAU.  He was born Abt. 1655 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada, and died 15 Aug 1728 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of HUGETTE BOURQUE and SEBASTIEN BRUN are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 73.              i.    JEANNE4 BRUN, b. Abt. 1676.
2 CONT ii.    CLAUDE BRUN, b. Abt. 1678, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; d. 12 Mar 1760, Riviere-Oulle; m. CECILE DUGAS, 27 Nov 1709, Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada; b. Abt. 1692, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT 74.            iii.    ABRAHAM BRUN, b. 1680, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; d. 09 Jul 1713, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT iv.    VINCENT BRUN, b. 1682, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; d. 10 Apr 1708, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT 75.             v.    JEAN BAPTISTE BRUN, b. 1684, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; d. 01 Jun 1751, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT vi.    ANTOINE BRUN, b. Abt. 1685, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; m. MARIE FRANCOISE COMEAU, 29 Oct 1709, Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT 76.           vii.    MARIE BRUN, b. Abt. 1687, Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/BrunV.htm> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT This is a short bio of Sebastien Brun's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT VINCENT  BRUN
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bruns as their associates of the first hour Brault must be put at the row of older and more deserving families of Acadia.  Both, if not to doubt come from the French parish of La Chaussee, province of Poitou.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lebrun acadiens are none other than the Bruns, only graphic acadien authentication.  What arrived, it is not known too much for some reason, it is that with the fourth generation of Brun, they take the nickname of Lebrun, that
2 CONC  the descendants preserve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown parents, Vincent Brun was born about 1616, in Poitou.  The first marriage of the ancestor takes place in France, between 1638 and 1640, with Vincende Braude and the second marriage, in 1646, with Renee Braude, presumed to 
2 CONC be the sister of Vincende and surely also sister of the ancestor Henri Brault married to Claude DeChevrainville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vincent has a girl from his first marriage and four children from his second, three girls and a son.  It is the son who binds us to the ancestor, in this genealogy.  The Brun family arrives in Acadia about 1648.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son, Sebastien Brun was born a twin in 1654, he marries about 1676, in Royal Port, in Acadia, Hughette Bourg, born in 1657, daughter of the ancestor Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry.  Sebastien has seven children with Hughe
2 CONC tte, of which Abraham, born in 1680, which marries about 1701, at Port-Royal, Marie-Anne Pellerin, born in 1683, daughter of the ancestor Étienne Pellerin and Jeanne Savoye.  On the acadian census of 1686, Bastien Brun is 32 years
2 CONC  old and Hughette Bourg is 28 years old, at Port-Royal.
2 CONT
2 CONT In their turn, Abraham Brun and Anne Pellerin have at least five children, of which the junior born in 1712, Joseph Brun, married at Port-Royal, January 31, 1752, the widow of Pierre Doucet, Francoise Comeau, born in 1713, daughte
2 CONC r of Abraham Comeau and Marguerite Pitre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Brun and Francoise Comeau have only two children, the young person, is baptized like his father, Joseph, who marriesy on February 5, 1781, at Port-Royal, Marie-Anne Dupuis, daughter of Olivier Dupuis and Marie-Anne Boudrot.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the other hand, Joseph and Marie-Anne have eight children, and it is the penultimate one which supplements the bond with the Bruns.  Marie-Rosalie or Marie-Rose Brun becomes the wife on January 11, 1885, of Louis Clouet, son of
2 CONC  Joseph Clouet and Marie Bergevin, also known as Langevin, of Beauport, a bond which continues to my father, Roger Rochon.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor Vincent Brun is listed in 1686, to be 70 years old, at Port-Royal.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
