2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because she is historically important as matriarch of Acadian Allain family. Thanks for helping make Wi
2 CONC kiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Marguerite Bourg is the ancestral matriarch of the Acadian Allain family. 
2 CONT Marguerite was born around 1667 in Acadia, being 4 years old on the 1671 census. Her parents were Antoine Bourg and Antoinette Landry.≤ref name=DGFA>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. ''Dictionnaire Généalogi
2 CONC que Des Familles Acadiennes.'' Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p13-14; 221-222.≤/ref>
2 CONT Around 1690, Marguerite married Louis Allain. Between about 1691 and 1693, the couple had two children: Pierre and Marie, a relatively smallfamily for those times.≤ref name=DGFA/> The family was listed in the Acadian Census at Por
2 CONC t Royal between 1698 and 1714. In 1714, they liveat Cappe near Port Royal.
2 CONT Marguerite Bourk, wife of Louis Alain died on September 13, 1727, aged55 years in Port Royal (renamed ''Annapolis Royal, Acadia or Nova Scotia'' by that time). She was buried the next day. Witnesses were Claude Landry and Claude M
2 CONC elançon.≤ref name=DGFA/>≤ref>Nova Scotia Archives, "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste,Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755," register RG 1 volume 26 page 272 [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.a
2 CONC sp?ID=1604 Burial]≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 214) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/214?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Residences'''*[http://www.acadian-home.org/census1693.html 1698 Acadian census] at Port-Royal: Louis ALLAIN 44; Marguerite BOURG (wife) 31; Pierre 7; Marie 5; 10 cattle, 12 sheep, 8 hogs, 5 1/2 arpents, 31 fruit trees, 4 guns 1
2 CONC  servant.
2 CONT *[http://www.acadian-home.org/census1701.html 1701 Acadian census] at Port-Royal: Louis ALLAIN 46, Marguerite BOURG (wife) 30; Louis ALLAIN 10, Marie 6; employees: Abraham BRUN, Isaac BERGERAT; 2 guns, 20 cattle, 30 sheep, 20 hogs
2 CONC , 3 arpents.
2 CONT *[http://www.acadian-home.org/census1703.html 1703 Acadian census] at Port-Royal:Louis ALLAIN, his wife, 2 boys, 2 arms bearers. 
2 CONT *[http://www.acadian-home.org/census1707.html 1707 Acadian census] at Port-Royal: Louis ALLAIN and his wife, 1 boy 14 or older, 1 girl 12 orolder, 3 arpents; 25 cattle, 27 sheep, 14 hogs, 2 guns. 
2 CONT *[http://www.acadian-home.org/census1714.html 1714 Acadian census] at Port-Royal (Cappe): Louis ALLAIN and his wife, 1 son, 1 daughter.
2 CONT '''DNA'''. Marguerite's mother was Antoinette Landry. The Mothers of Acadia Maternal DNA project is conducting ongoing research to verify their origins. In 2010, [http://www.acadian-home.org/Founding-Mothers-of-Acadia.html Stephen
2 CONC  White reported Antoinette Landry had an H haplogroup].  Lucie Leblanc Constantino reported one result [http://www.acadian-home.org/origins-mtdna.html here]. Ongoing test results are also reported [https://www.familytreedna.com/pu
2 CONC blic/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. All of the descendants have reported an Hhaplogroup, indicating European origins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT
