2 TITL Histoire et généalogie des Acadiens (Bona Arsenault)
1 NOTE Married abt 1690 to Louis Allain at Port Royal. Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada; children: Marie and Pierre; sources: <http://www/familyorigins.com/users/s/t/g/Bob--Stgelais/FAMO1-0001/d184.html> (copy filed L-13-30).; and <http://
2 CONC www/familyorigins.com/users/s/t/g/Bob--Stgelais/FAMO1-0001/d185.html> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT <http://home.attbi.com/~sodapop68/webtree/pafg52.htm> (copy filed L-13-30);
2 CONT "Genealogie de l'ancienne Acadie" shows family with 2 children: Louis, born 1691 and Marie, born 1695 and married to Jean Nicolas Gauthier.
2 CONT 1698 Census of Acadia shows the following: Louis ALLAIN 44; Maguerite BOURG (wife) 31, Pierre 7, Marie 5; 10 cattle, 12 sheep, 8 hogs, 5 1/2 arpents, 31 fruit trees, 4 guns, 1 servant.
2 CONT <http://www.genealogie.com/dgaa/dgaa-b4.html> (copy filed L-13-30).
2 CONT "Genealogie de l'ancienne Acadie, BO" pg 14.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~bobmartell/Landry/Landry3.htm>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Jean Claude Landry
2 CONT Generation No. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT 17.  MARGUERITE3 BOURQUE (ANTOINETTE (TWIN)2 LANDRY, JEAN CLAUDE1) was born 1667 in Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, and died 13 Sep 1727 in Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia.  She married LOUIS ALLAIN Abt. 1690 in Port Royal,
2 CONC  Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada.  He was born 1654 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada, and died 15 Jun 1737 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of MARGUERITE BOURQUE and LOUIS ALLAIN are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.    PIERRE4 ALLAIN, b. Abt. 1691; d. 04 Oct 1744; m. MARGUERITE LEBLANC, Abt. 1717; b. 1699, St. Charles des Mines; d. 18 Apr 1778, Miquelon.
2 CONT ii.    MARIE ALLAIN, b. Abt. 1693; m. JOSEPH NICHOLAS aka BELLAIRE GAUTIER, 04 Mar 1714/15, Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.acadian-home.org/ancestorsacadian.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT LOUIS  ALLAIN
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Allain, entrepreneur and blacksmith arrived in Acadia abt 1686. He married Marguerite Bourque , daughter of Antoine Bourque and Antoinette Landry. Their only son, Pierre Allain moved to Grand-Pré following his marriage to Ma
2 CONC rguerite Leblanc, daughter of Antoine and Marie Bourgeois. The Allain families of New Brunswick descend from Louis Allain, eldest son of Pierre, who married Anne Leger, daughter of Jacques Leger and Anne Amirault, June 24, 1748 at
2 CONC  Beaubassin.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
