2 CONT [[Category:Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT [[Category:Les Mines, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==:Anne LeBlanc was born around 1681, likely in Port-Royal since her parents Jacques LeBlanc and Catherine Hebert were settled there.  
2 CONT :Anne was counted in the Port-Royal census of 1686 at the age of 5 with her 7 siblings. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686ce
2 CONC ns.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 
2 CONC – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Jacques Leblanc, 35, Catherine Hébert, 23, Jean, 12, Marguerite, 11, Jacques, 9, Marie, 6 years old, Anne, 5 years old, Catherine, 3 years old, Pierre, 2 years old, René, 1 month old. 3 rifles, 6 
2 CONC arpans in plowing, 25 bestes with horns, 30 sheep, 15 pigs. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  By 1693 Jacques and Catherine had moved to Minas, by then a village just a little smaller than Port Royal.  Anne was 11 years old at the time. ≤ref>(
2 CONC Note: according to Stephen White, Anne was listed inthis census but her name does not appear in the transcription nor theoriginal census. ) Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepa
2 CONC ges.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National
2 CONC  Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> Jacques LEBLANC 42, Caterine HEBERT 32, Jean 19, Jacques 17, Marie 15, Antoine 13, Caterine 11, Genevieve 9, Madeleine 7, Francois 5, Pierre 3, Igna
2 CONC ce 1; 12 cattle, 6 sheep, 6 pigs, 11 arpents, 1 gun≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref name=Theriot>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=marie+anne&n=le+blanc Marie Anne LeBlan
2 CONC c] at Geneanet.≤blockquote> [On one version does not appear with rest of family? But there is an Antoine, age 13. Stephen WHITE says this is Pierre, 13 years (sic)]≤/blockquote>≤/ref> All of their 11 children are born and ten stil
2 CONC l living at home, with Ignace just a toddler.  
2 CONT :Around 1705 she married Pierre Breau, widower of Marie-Josephe Bourgeois. Pierre was the son of Vincent Breau and Marie Bourg. 
2 CONT :Pierre and Anne lived in Minas in 1707.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcriptionof the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original c
2 CONC ensus can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>Pierre BRAU
2 CONC LT, his wife, 3 boys less than 14, 1 girl 12 or older, 3 younger girls; 2 arpents, 10 cattle,6 sheep, 30 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  
2 CONT :By 1714 they had settled at Rivière-aux-Canards with their children.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census 
2 CONC Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 23
2 CONC 9-261.≤blockquote>Pierre BREAU and wife, 3 sons, 5 daughters.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  
2 CONT
2 CONT :Children:≤ref name ="DGFA"/>	
2 CONT #Joseph c1706
2 CONT #Catherine 1708
2 CONT #Anne 1710
2 CONT #Isabelle  1712
2 CONT #Pierre c1715
2 CONT #Paul  1717 
2 CONT #Brigitte 1719
2 CONT #Amand c1721
2 CONT #Agathe c1723
2 CONT :Pierre and Anne  were deported to Massachusetts with their family. Hedied at Braintree, MA in the Boston area according to Bona Arsenault.≤ref name=Theriot/>  Anne was on the 1757 census at Braintree, MA, age77 years.≤ref name="D
2 CONC GFA"/>
