1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LHN9-1XQ
2 CONT Brief Life History of Paul'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Paul Brault was born on 3 July 1717, in Rivière-aux-Canards, Acadia, New France, his father, Pierre Breaux, was 48 and his mother, Anne LeBlanc, was 35. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie Josephe Landry in 1742, in Grand-Pré, Kings, Nova Scotia, Canada. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 4 daughters. 
2 CONT Joseph Brault 1743–1787
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Brault 1745–1832
2 CONT Marie Anne Brault Brooks 1747–1791
2 CONT Marie Breau 1751–1797
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Breau 1755–1776
2 CONT Elizabeth Brault 1757–1836
2 CONT Pierre Breault 1759–1824
2 CONT Daughter Breaux 1760–1767
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Paul and his family were reportedly exiled to Ipswich, Massachusetts in 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 15 June 1783, in Saint-Jacques, Montcalm, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 65, and was buried in Saint-Jacques, Montcalm, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/154421246/paul-brault
2 CONT extract from "A Breau Genealogy", p. 11:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul and his family lived at Grand Pre, from whence they were deported to Massachussetts in 1755 [on 20 Dec, on the schooner Race Horse, or on 12 Dec on the Swallow]. They arrived at Ipswich MA 9 Feb 1756 along with the families o
2 CONC f John Landry and Francis Landry. They had come from Boston to Marblehead, apparently by water, and then had been transported to Ipswich by ox team. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul's family was listed as consisting of Paul, his wife Mary Joseph, and 6 children: Joseph 14, John 12, Nanne 8, Mary 6, John Battis 2 1/2, and baby Elizabeth 2 months. The 20 Jul 1760 list of Acadians at Ipswich showed Paul Bre
2 CONC au 43, wife Mary 41, Joseph 17, John 15, nanny 13, Molly 10, Elizabeth 8, Jno. Batits 6 and Peter 1. The 14 Aug 1763 list of Acadians in Massachusetts showed Paul Broux with wife erroneously recorded as Margueritte, four sons and 
2 CONC four daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They left Ipswich shortly after 18 Aug 1766 and established themselves at St. Jacques de l'Achigan, Montcalm, Quebec, in 1767 and had two of thier children, who had been born in Massachusetts, baptized at L'Assomption, Quebec. Pau
2 CONC l and Marie Joseph apparently had eight children.
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------
2 CONT
