2 CONT [[Category: Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT :Anne Landry, daughter of Charles (dit Charlot) Landry and Catherine Joseph Broussard, was born in Port Royal 29 Nov 1718. She was baptized the same day by Justinen Durand. Her godparents were Guillaume Blanchard and Anne Babin, w
2 CONC ife of Claude Brossard.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 21) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/21?r=0&s=5≤/ref> ≤ref>
2 CONC Nova Scotia Archives: An Acadian Parish Remembered: The Registers of St Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal 1702-1755, RG 1, Vol. 26, p. 161 [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=745 Baptismal Registration]≤/ref> 
2 CONT :Anne Landry and Jean (dit Djanee) Savoie, son of Germain Savoye & Genevieve Babinau were married in Port-Royal in 1735.  ≤ref>Title: An Acadian Parish Remembered; Author: Public Archives of Nova Scotia; Note: The Registers of St.
2 CONC  Jean-Baptiste [parish church], Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755. Includes digitized images of original register entries;  RG 1, vol. 26a, p. 140 [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2091 Marriage Registration]:Text: 
2 CONC Jean SAVOYE, about twenty-six years old, son of Germain SAVOYE & Genevieve BABINAU, married 22 Aug 1735 at parish of St. Jean Baptiste at Annapolis Royal to Anne LANDRY, about seventeen years old, daughter of Charles Landry & Cate
2 CONC rine BROSSARD, both deceased. Witnesses: Pierre SAVOYE, brother of the groom; François LANDRY, brother of the bride; Paul BLANCHARD; Joseph DUPUY; Dominique ROBICHAUX (who signed); Jean Baptiste JEANSON. Priest was De St. Poncy De
2 CONC  Lavernède.
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT :She died before 6 September 1803.≤ref>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ''Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes''] (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadien
2 CONC nes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p. 939≤/ref>
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
