2 CONT [[Category:Chipoudy, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT '''Pierre Paul Savoye''' was born 19 Nov 1739. He was the son of [[Savoie-550|Jean Savoie]] and [[Landry-819|Anne Landry]]. He was baptized 22 May 1740 at Beaubassin. His godparents were Paul Savoy and Marie Dupuy.≤ref>Library and
2 CONC  Archives Canada Fonds des Archives départementales de la Charente-Maritime [La Rochelle, France] : C-1207 Registres deBeaubassin - reel_c1207 MG 6 A 2 (Image 67) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1207/67?r=0&s=6≤
2 CONC /ref>
2 CONT He married [[Bujold-150|Anne Marie Bujold]], daughter of [[Bugeaud-22|Paul Bujold]] and [[Poirier-337|Marie Poirier]] around 1775.
2 CONT Pierre Paul passed away on 30 January 1806 in Négouac.≤ref>Néguac, Nouveau-Brunswick, Registre de la paroisse Saint-Bernard, catholique, Baptêmes et Mariages 1796-1848, Sépultures 1796-1846 ( F.M. 9, A 11, vol 9), Image 1206, [htt
2 CONC p://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c3018/1206?r=0&s=2 entry for Pierre Savoie] Burial 1 February 1806, digital images, Héritage, Genealogy collection, Library and Archives Canada, reel C-3018, Parish Registers: New Bru
2 CONC nswick : C-3018 accessed February 2020. ≤/ref> ≤ref>Stephen A. White, "La généalogie des trente-sept familles hôtesses des Retrouvailles 94," online articles, ''Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne,'' vol. 25, nos 2 et 3
2 CONC (1994), [https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-ceaac/wf/wf/pdf/37fam-savoie.pdf  SAVOIE], page 1 ≤blockquote>ii. Pierre-Paul dit Aufils, n Chipoudy 19 nov 1739; m v 1775 Anne-Marie BUJOLD (Paul &Marie Poirier); d Négouac 3
2 CONC 0 janv 1806.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
