1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/L4BB-JB9
2 CONT Brief Life History of Marie Josephe'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Josephe Savoie was born about 1754, in New Brunswick, Canada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Michel Allain on 4 May 1786, in Miramichi, Northumberland, New Brunswick, British North America. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 6 daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 13 January 1823, in Neguac, Northumberland, New Brunswick, Canada, at the age of 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Date and age given by Placide Gaudet in an article of the Acadian Monitor, apr 18, 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Rene Joyer wrote in his notes of the 1806 mission that is Michael Allain who "usually houses the missionary who is very well treated. The wife of a resident named Josephte is unmatched for its convenience for priests. "AAQ 
2 CONC NB VI-9
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT P. 246 Les Savoie - Fidèle Thériault
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT P. 246 Les Savoie - Fidèle Thériault
