1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Isle Saint-Jean, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT Jean-Baptiste was born about 1750.  He married Madeleine Haché in 1773. <ref>"Canada Marriages, 1661-1949," database,FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F2PS-L5D : 10 February 2018), Jean Arseneau and Magdeleine 
2 CONC Hache, 10 Sep 1773; citing Sainte Anne De Restigouche Catholic, Carleton, Bonaventure, Quebec, reference ; FHL microfilm 1,319,997. </ref><ref>Actes d’état civil et registres d’église du Québec (Collection Drouin), 1621 à 1967. On
2 CONC line publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2008. Gabriel Drouin, comp. Drouin Collection. Montreal, Quebec, Canada: Institut Généalogique Drouin. Institut Généalogique Drouin; Montreal, Quebec, Canada; Drouin 
2 CONC Collection; Auteur: Gabriel Drouin, comp. Search: C Carleton 1773-1862. Accessed on ancestry.ca, January 2020.* View {{Ancestry Image|1091|d13p_30761236|ca}} on ancestry.ca,  (requires subscription).* View free [https://www.ancest
2 CONC ry.ca/sharing/18933055?h=6291c2 Ancestry Sharing Image]. <blockquote>On 10 September 1773, marriage between Jean Arseneau, son of Abraham Arseneau and Josete Savoye, residents of Île St-Jean,  andMagdeleine Haché, daughter of Jacq
2 CONC ues Haché and Josette Boudraut residents of Miscou. Witnesses: Jacques Haché, father of the bride; Cyprien Haché; Simon Joseph LeBlanc; Joseph Boudraut.</blockquote> 
2 CONT </ref>He died about 1810. <ref>First-hand information as remembered by [[Arsenault-464 | Fred Arsenault]], Tuesday, August 26, 2014. ''Replace this citation if there is another source.'' </ref> Info taken from the St-Philippe & St
2 CONC -James Parish books in Egmont Bay,PEI:  <blockquote>Jean-Baptiste was living on his 117 acres land, lot number 15,  he gave half of his land to his son Marcellin, who in return would take careof him and his wife. </blockquote>
2 CONT
