1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-Hache-Gallant/6000000119547718942?through=6000000004121718443
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marie Hache''' was born ABT 1713, and died 26 SEP 1790 in Riviere du Loup (Louiseville), Quebec, Canada . She was buried 27 SEP 1790 in age 77, Riviere du Loup (Louiseville), Quebec, Canada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Jean Baptiste Savoie on 11 AUG 1734 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wc-rootsweb-com.translate.goog/trees/109046/I00315/jeanbaptiste-savoie/registry?_x_tr_sl=fr&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=sc
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean Baptiste /Savoie/ and Marie /Hache/ are:
2 CONT # Marie Josephe Savoie was born AFT 1734.
2 CONT # Marguerite Savoie was born ABT 1736, and died BEF 4 OCT 1765.
2 CONT # Madeleine Savoie was born ABT 1738, and died 7 MAY 1809 in Louiseville, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Rosalie Savoie was born 30 OCT 1741 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 27 OCT 1789 in Quebec City, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Marie Anne Savoie was born ABT 1744 in Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 3 MAR 1790 in Riviere du Loup (Louiseville), Maskinonge, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Madeleine Savoie was born 9 APR 1745 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada .
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste Savoie was born 20 JUN 1748 in Beaubassin, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada , and died 1 NOV 1811 in Louiseville, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Pierre Savoie was born ABT 1752 in St Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec, Canada , and died 29 MAY 1830 in age 94, St Barthelemy, Berthier, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Marie Francoise Savoie was born ABT 1753 in Chipoudy, Acadia, Canada , and died 7 FEB 1832 in St Jacques de l’Achigan, Quebec, Canada .
2 CONT # Female Savoy was born BET 1754 AND 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Haché dite Gallant was born about 1713 in Beaubassin.[1]. She was the firstborn child of Michel Hache-Gallant and Madeleine LeBlanc.[2]. She married Jean-Baptiste Savoie 11 Aug 1734 at Beaubassin.[3]. She died at Louisville 
2 CONC 26 Sep 1790 and was buried the next day per the register at Louisville.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 1: The name Marie Hache Galand is used by PRDH.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 2: The name Larché is cited by S.A.W. for Marie's grandfather, Michel Haché (Larché) dit Gallant and his father, Pierre Larché.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographie
2 CONT
2 CONT Michel Haché dit Gallant pourrait être le fils naturel de Pierre Larcher, originaire de la paroisse de Saint-Pierre de la ville de Montdidier, en Picardie. Dès 1682, on le retrouve à Beaubassin où il est établi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épouse Anne Cormier vers 1690. Elle est la fille de Thomas Cormier et de Marie-Madeleine Girouard. Ils auront un enfant prénommé Michel, né en 1691, qui se mariera à Grand Pré, le 12 octobre 1711, avec Madeleine Leblanc, fille 
2 CONC de Jacques Leblanc et de Catherine Hébert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Près de 30 ans plus tard, soit en 1720, Michel (le père), son épouse Anne et leurs enfants seront la première famille à s'établir à l'île Saint-Jean (Ile du Prince-Edouard).
2 CONT
2 CONT L'ancêtre des Haché dit Gallant périra noyé dans la rivière du Nord, le 10 avril 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: La Société historique acadienne.
2 CONT
