1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain William Ernest Moran, called Naneece, and his family resided at 1002 Lameuse Street.  He made his livelihood as a carpenter and the captain of the pleasure boat, Iona Louise, which he had operated since 190
2 CONC 5.  Captain Moran took tourist primarily for the Midwest to Ship Island and up theTchoutacabouffa River for $1.00 per day.  He was well known at the Biloxi Yacht Club.
