2 CONT First married 14 May 1657 Jacques Fournier (bap. 1619, bur. 25 Oct 1699 at Church of St Thomas, son of Michel & Michelle Croier) at Immaculee
2 CONT Married  21 Aug 1683 to Francois Renou aka Lachapelle at Boucherville, Chambly, Qc.; source: <http://winwalker.familytreeguide.com/familygroup.php?familyID=F01036&tree=T1>.
2 CONT Conception de Trois Rivieres, St Maurice, Quebec, Canada; marriage annuled 1659 (no children), sources: Jette pg 437; Tanguay Vol I pg 250; Tanguay Vol III pg 199; Tanguay Vol I pg 239 shows family with no children; "Our French Ca
2 CONC nadian Forefathers" (copy filed 60-2).
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://www.leveillee.net/ancestry/registreTR1657tr.htm>.In the year of our Lord 1657, May 14, I, Paul Ragueneau, priest of the Society of Jesus, after having announced the three bans of marriage 
2 CONC according to custom during the celebration of masses in the Blessed Virgin Chapel in Trois-Rivières, questioned and received their mutual consent by word and presence, I united in marriage Jacques Fournyer, son of Michel Fournyer 
2 CONC and of the deceased Michelle Croier, Parisians (from Paris): and Marguerite Crevier, daughter of Christopher Crevier and Jeanne Évart, inhabitants of the the said village of Trois-Rivières. The witnesses were Mr. Godefroy and Mr. 
2 CONC de Saint-Quentin.
2 CONT -----------------------------------
2 CONT Remarried 6 Aug and Oct 1683 Francois Renou (bap. 1644. son of Christopher & Marie Serle) at Repentigny and 21 Aug 1683 at Boucherville; sources: Tanguay Vol I pg 250 & 515 & Vol III pg 199 shows a date if 21 Aug 1683 at Bouchervi
2 CONC lle; family (3 children) is listed in Jette pg 979; Tanguay Vol I pg 515 shows family with 3 children; "Our French Canadian Forefathers" (copy filed 60-2).
2 CONT Remarried (ct. 10 Oct 1699, Normandin) to Robert Groton (aka Groston, bur. 7 Jun 1707 at Montreal) at Cap de la Madeleine; sources: family (8 children) is listed in Jette pg 532; Tanguay Vol I pg 285 shows family with 7 children; 
2 CONC Tanguay Vol III pg 199.
2 CONT Internet -- <http://www.kersur.net/~fleuette/anc/remi.htm> -- Fleuette Family Association.  This reference also applies to her spouse.  "Our French Canadian Forefathers" (copy filed 60-2) states that she never married Pierre Groto
2 CONC n.
2 CONT Additional information acquired from the net (copy filed 21-3).
2 CONT "The Grand Families" from the internet (copy filed 21-6).
