1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Notes'''
2 CONT * Location info: [https://www.geni.com/projects/Maine-province-France/24701 Maine, France] (birth,marriage), [https://www.geni.com/projects/Trois-Rivi%C3%A8res-Qu%C3%A9bec-Canada/24574 Trois-Rivières] (death); a habité le [https:/
2 CONC /www.geni.com/projects/Perche-France/24550 Perche, France]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/projects/Pioneers-of-Canada-Quebec/17839 Pionnière de la Nouvelle-France]. Arrive au Québec le 4 juin 1634 à bord du [https://www.geni.com/projects/Passagers-du-Navire-de-Nesl%C3%A9-1634/24863 « Navire de N
2 CONC eslé »] avec son marie et cinq enfants, Madeleine, Pierre, Nicolas, Marie et Marguerite.
2 CONT * Elle est morte avec son mari dans l'incendie de leur maison familiale.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''More Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the aunt of Jeanne Dodier, who is married with Adrien Jolliet.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also known under the name of Nicole LEMÈRE and under the name by Nicole Lemaine also. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the daughter of Nicolas Lemaire and Marie Castrie, also known as the Gastrie. She was born March 10, 1595 in Mamers, Le Mans, Sarthe, France. She married Gaspard Boucher, son of Jacques Boucher and Françoise Paigne on 12 De
2 CONC cember 1619 in Mamers. She died between 19 June 1652 and 1666 census in Trois-Rivières, Mauricie, Quebec, Canada.Died between 19-6 - 1652 and 1666 Trois-Rivières census. She was burned in a fire with her husband, Gaspard, in their
2 CONC  family home.
2 CONT
