1 OCCU Quand elle est morte, elle était faible d'esprit depyuis un an.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A daughter of Catherine and Etienne Charest, she was born in 1674, however, their parents were not married on any Record of Source, till 1680. Written, published family Genealogists have stated that Etienne and Cat
2 CONC herine did not perform the wedding ceremony until 1680, that they always had the intention of being married, while they were starting to produce their children in 1674. This is publicly published knowledge by written sources of do
2 CONC cumentation.
2 CONT
2 CONT The place she died, in 1725, the County was not called Monteregie, at that time(1725) it was Boucherville, Longueuil, Quebec, Canada. Today, 2024 it is Boucherville, Monteregie, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT Her birth surname, most modern research says Clarette. Earlier research was Charet/Charest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early published family genealogists that have written of this family state that this Francoise Clare was six(6) years of age in 1680, and was present at the Marriage Ceremony of her parents Catherine and Etienne Charest. Oscar Doa
2 CONC ne Lambert's book quotes her as being at the ceremony with numerous witnesses.
2 CONT
2 CONT I going to go with some of Boucher and others research, and the surname, Charest, with possibly dropping the s out, if sources show up.(April 2025)(S.R.S)
2 CONT Note: these are going to be mostly Canadian records of Sources, highly most probably. Her mother, who gave birth to her in 1674(Record of Source), is showing on sourced Record as being born in 1655, being married with sourced Reco
2 CONC rd in 1680, to Etienne, as they had the intention of being married when she became pregnant. This fact is shown on written, published family sources of documented Records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several researchers studies of the surname have concluded that the surname Clarette is the very most likely surname. Her mother being Catherine Bissot Clarette, and her father is Etienne Clarette.
2 CONT Francoise Clare married Jean Boucher de Monbrun(Boucher) on 24 of November in 1692 at Pointe-de-Levy, Canada, Nouvelle-France.
