2 CONT ***************************
2 CONT
2 CONT ? Joe De Valcourt 28?671900 Co. D. 2nd ?? APo#5? %P.M. NY. NY Post Marked June 1 4 P.M. 1945 A.P.O.5
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209387  Mrs. H. S. De Valcourt] Many; Louisiana 1 St Johanniskirchen Germany? May 31, 1945 [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209387  Dear Louise,] It 
2 CONC has been quite some time since I've written you, so will try to do so to-day. It is now eleven o'clock it has been raining since last nite about 7 o'clock somewhat chilly over here yet. We had some pretty cold weather in the first
2 CONC  part of May.  Snowed for 4 days + nights it was pretty tough then. We were up in the mountains of Czechoslovakia at that time very high altitude in most parts of Czech. We had our last battle on the morning of May 7 in Czech.  Of
2 CONC  course you know I wasn't sorry at all when we were notified to cease firing.  There was no celebration seemed as if the boys just took it as another happening and went on about their work.. We had plenty to do as we alone our Com
2 CONC pany of about 250 had about 10 thousand prisoners to take care of.  It really was a job getting the transportation and food.  There were also many civilians who were trying to keep ahead of the Russian Armies?, We had to stop them
2 CONC  + send them back.  Mostly women + children carrying all their belongings on their backs.  You couldn't help but feel sorry for the babies + Kids but often seeing some of the Concentration  camps + the horrors that were committed 
2 CONC their in one wouldn't have any pity on them. We were in one camp where there were about 120 Polish Russians and French women whom they had been using as forced laborers they were all starved.  We saved maybe 50 or sixty of them al
2 CONC l the others died, we took all of them to the hospital they were nothing but skin + bones. Weighing about 30 or 40 lbs., where they should have been weighing about 110 to 140; these 120 were all that was left of 1800 of them which
2 CONC  had left Selisia about 6 weeks before, they were marched all the way which was over a thousand miles the way they had to go. There were a lot of them dead out in the woods about 5 miles away.  The military government made some of
2 CONC  the civilians pick them up put them in coffins and lined them up by the grave yard about 25 to 50 a day.  Then we rounded up every civilian in town made them line up and go by and look at them then they had a funeral, this lasted
2 CONC  about a week.  Will be able to tell you a lot more when I get back. I had a letter from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209338   Stephen] a few days ago, said he was still well and doing ok. I'm sure your
2 CONC  boy must be growing right along bet [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209338   Steve] would be glad to see him.  He thinks he might be back sometimes in the next few months, I think we will be coming back s
2 CONC oon ourselves for a 30 day furlough + additional training then to Pacific. I mailed you a rifle for [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209338  Stephen] you should get it in a couple of months.  I mentioned to
2 CONC  him I was going to if I got a chance. Will say bye, Hope this finds you + Jr. doing the best. Yours Bess? Joe
2 CONT
2 CONT *************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember visiting Uncle Joe with mom (Louise) and dad (Steve de Valcourt) a short time before he passed away.  Uncle Joe was pretty much in a comatose state at this time, Aunt Hattie and dad wanted to make sure that Uncle Joe kn
2 CONC ew that his brother was here to see him.  Dad kept telling him that Steve was here, after a little while Joe managed to mention sweet potatoes or bring me some sweet potatoes?  We knew then that Joe was aware that his brother Step
2 CONC hen was there.  Dad always tried to share any extra produce that he had with the family.  That night we spent the night at Aunt Phil's house and all I can remember is that the Grand Father Clock kept me awake that night.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=111275728 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 17 2018, 9:20:29 UTC''
