1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DEVALCOURT, Silveste Woodrow (William & Estelle SMITH) b. 31 Dec. 1912 (GC Ch.: v.4, p.212)
2 CONT -------
2 CONT  Source: Southwest Louisiana Records (1750 – 1900) Book by [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=88080739  Rev. Donald J. Hébert ]
2 CONT
2 CONT **********************
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvester "Woodrow" Wilson de Valcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 13 DEC 1937
2 CONT
2 CONT  Woodrow DeValcourt 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at St. Genevieve Catholic Church today at a 3 p.m. Mass for Mr. Woodrow W. DeValcourt, 61, who died from results of a tractor accident Saturday at  6:30 p.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment was in Calvary Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his widow, Mrs. Leola Gaudet DeValcourt of Lafayette; one daughter of Lafayette; one granddaughter; five brothers, Steven DeValcourt of Lafayette, William and John DeValcourt, both of New Orleans, and Joseph and 
2 CONC Theo DeValcourt, both of Port Arthur; and four sisters, Mrs. Carrie Elmer, Mrs. Ethel Daily, Mrs. Hazel McManus, and Mrs. Philomena Bourg, all of Port Arthur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. DeValcourt, a native of Sunset and resident of Lafayette all of his life, was the son of William DeValcourt of Sunset and Stella Smith of Grand Coteau.  He was a self-employed real estate broker and land developer for twenty-f
2 CONC ive years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. DeValcourt was a member of the Young Mens Business Club, the Krewe of Zues, and the Elks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin and Castille Funeral Home was in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Advertiser, Lafayette, La., Mon., June 19, 1978 Lafayette Parish Public Library, Down Town location.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Woodrow's age does not appear to be correct on this obituary.
2 CONT
2 CONT *******
2 CONT
2 CONT  Tractor Crushes Local Man 
2 CONT
2 CONT A 61 year old man was crushed to death by an overturned tractor off of Maryview Farm Road at about 8 p.m. yesterday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Woodrow W. Devalcourt of 101 Moreland Drive was pronounced dead at the scene by Lafayette Parish [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=144463367  Coroner Henry Voorhies].
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=173821779  Sheriff Carlo Listi] said Devalcourt was operating a bushog with a tractor when the vehicle apparently hit a mound of dirt and overturned, pinning him beneath it. 
2 CONC  A neighbor told the Advertiser the tractor apparently went off a six foot dirt embankment.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sheriff's department rescue unit was dispatched to the scene and removed the tractor.  An Acadian Ambulance unit which had been dispatched to the scene took Mrs. Devalcourt to Lafayette General Hospital where she was treated f
2 CONC or mild shock and returned home in fair condition.
2 CONT
2 CONT The neighbor said Devalcourt had been working alone, shredding and cutting grass on property which was being developed as a subdivision.  He was discovered pinned under the vehicle by family members who went to take him refreshmen
2 CONC ts, the neighbor stated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin and Castille Funeral Home of Lafayette is in charge of funeral arrangements.
2 CONT -------
2 CONT The Sunday Advertiser Lafayette, La. Sunday, June 18, 1978 Front page, Column 8 Page 6, Column 4
