1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DEVALCOURT, Mary Ethel (William & Estelle SMITH) b. 7 May 1903 (GC Ch.: v.4, p.102)
2 CONT -------
2 CONT  Source: Southwest Louisiana Records (1750 – 1900) Book by [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=88080739  Rev. Donald J. Hébert ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ************************
2 CONT
2 CONT She was christened on 21 Jun 1903 in Grand Coteau, St Landry, LA.
2 CONT
2 CONT  MRS. R. R. DAILEY  3829 6TH STREET PORT ARTHUR, TEX. 77640
2 CONT
2 CONT Mar 25, 1982
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209338  Stephen] + [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75209387  Louise],
2 CONT
2 CONT I was cleaning out some dresser drawers a few days ago, and found this article on the Jack de Valcourt Family, which I thought I had sent back to [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=110499390  Estelle], Its been
2 CONC  such a long time ago. but I'm sure you would want it. And hope you will forgive me for keeping it so long. I spent two weeks with Ralph + Mary Helen in New Orleans, in the beginning of this month. Ralph will retire March 31st. Th
2 CONC ey have property on Bull Shoals Lake in Missouri, and will move up there when their house is built, they are really excited about it all and looking forward to Retirement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hope you + family are all well- Love and Best Wishes from all of us- Love Ethel 
2 CONT
2 CONT Post Marked: BEAUMONT TX 777 29 MAR 1982
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The above article was about the Jack deValcourt Family.
2 CONT  Jack deValcourt Family  First time in twelve years the John deValcourt family was all together the summer of 1965.  They are shown on the front steps of their home at 501 Julia street in New Iberia.  Children of Family Choose Ent
2 CONC ry Into Religious Life. SOUTHWEST LOUISIANA REGISTER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  PROMINENT SUNSET COUPLE MARRIED _______
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph Dailey and Miss Mary Devalcourt are Wedded At Nupital Mass _______ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Special to the Clarion-Progress SUNSET, La., Aug. 26,-- Ralph R. Dailey, son of Hon. J. E. Dailey, for many years a member of the St. Landry police jury from the second ward and Miss Ethel Mary Devalcourt, daughter of W. M. Devalc
2 CONC ourt, were married in Grand Coteau at 6:30 o'clock Thursday morning at nuptial Mass.  The ceremony was performed by [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=59647415  Rev. Father Baehr] in the presence of a large num
2 CONC ber of friends and relatives of the contracting parties.  Appropriate music and singing was furnished for the occasion by the Sacred Heart Choir.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=smith&GSfn=theo&GSiman=1&GScid=68777&GRid=125145364&  Mr. Theo Smith] acted as best man while Miss Louise Dailey, sister of the groom, was bridesmaid.  The bride was dressed i
2 CONC n lovely blue satin, trimmed in blue overlace. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following a wedding breakfast, at which intimate friends and close relatives were invited.  Mr. and Mrs. Dailey departed on the Southern Pacific for Galveston, and other points in Texas on their honeymoon.  They will be at their h
2 CONC ome in Port Arthur after September 15th.
2 CONT
2 CONT PAGE TWO THE DAILY CLARION-PROGRESS Saturday, August 26, 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=103560900  Edith Garland Dupre'] Library UL Lafayette
