2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{French_Roots_Project}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT '''DNA'''. The unknown spouse of Jean Gaudet, married around 1622 had two daughters: Francoise and Marie. The Mothers of Acadia Maternal DNAproject is conducting ongoing research to verify their origins. In 2010, [http://www.acadi
2 CONC an-home.org/Founding-Mothers-of-Acadia.html Stephen White reported] Francoise and Marie Gaudet had a J1b2 haplogroup. Idon't know the details re how many of her descendants were tested to support this report. Ongoing test results 
2 CONC are also reported [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. As of May 2014, 10 descendants of Francoise and 9 descendants of Marie have consistently reported a J haplogroup, indica
2 CONC ting European origins.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research notes ===
2 CONT Stephen White note un extrait écrit par Archange Godbout [http://www.sgcf.com/content/memoire/memoires_detail.php?vol=11 publié en 1960] par la [http://www.sgcf.com Société généalogique canadienne-française] qui démontre qu'un '''
2 CONC Jean Gaudet, âgé de 59 ans en 1727, doncné vers 1668, qui s'est marié avec une Marie Daussy, ne peut pas être le même Jean Gaudet qui se trouve déja en Acadie et marié depuis plusieurs années à Nicole Colleson en 1668.'''≤ref>DGFA
2 CONC , p667≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation to English:≤br>Stephen White notes written by Archange Godbout extract published in 1960 by French-Canadian Genealogical Society which shows that '''Jean Gaudet, 59 years old in 1727, therefore born about 1668, who is 
2 CONC marriedwith Marie Daussy, can not be the same Jean Gaudet that this is already in Canada for several years and married to Nicole Colleson''' in 1668.
2 CONT
2 CONT === See last note by Stephen White (LeBlanc) re Nicole Colleson===
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Génalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes,
