2 CONT
2 CONT 7. ↑ 1671 Census Transcription at Port Royal: Jean GAUDET 96, wife, Nicole COLLESON 64; Child: Jean 18; cattle 6, sheep 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. ↑ CENSUS: 1678 Port Royal, Acadia, Nicolle Colleron (sic) is listed as widow of GODET
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. ↑ George MacBeath, “RAZILLY, ISAAC DE,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, University of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003–, accessed May 10, 2019, [http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/razilly_isaac_de_1E.html Razilly
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. ↑ William I. Roberts, 3rd, “SEDGWICK, ROBERT,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, University of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003–, accessed May 10, 2019, [http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/sedgwick_robert_1E.html Sedgwick
2 CONT
2 CONT See Also:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1686 Acadian Census at Port Royal: Nicole COLLESON 80. Jean GODET her son 45, Jeanne HENRY his wife 30; children: Francoise 13, Jean 12, and three other children by his first wife; 1 gun, 4 arpents, 4 cattle, 4 sheep, 3 hogs. 1686
2 CONC  Census Transcription
2 CONT
2 CONT Undocumented Genealogy.com Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Jennifer Payne, family tree which requires account:  http://www.gencircles.com/users/harrison-md/2/data/385 (http://www.geocities.com/Heartland/Pointe/3829/acadian_history.html this link defunct) Gaudet was origin
2 CONC ally from the village of Martaize, Vienne, France and he arrived in Acadia in 1636 with his second wife, Nicole Coleson, and his two children from his first marriage, Francoise who later married Daniel LEBLANC, and Denis who would
2 CONC  marry Martine Gauthier. Jean and Nicole Coleson had two children after arriving in Acadia: Marie-Anne who married Etienne HEBERT and Jean who married Jeanne Henry
2 CONT
