2 CONT When I answered your message re the wife of Jean Gaudet, I recalledthe following quotation, but could not put my hands on it. Here it is from ACADIAN GENEALOGICAL EXCHANGE, VOL XXV, #2&3, April & July1996,published by Janet Jehn, 
2 CONC p 38:
2 CONT "MARIE DAUSSEY, WIFE OF JEAN GAUDET (translated from MÉMOIRES DE LASOCIÉTÉ GÉNÉALOGIQUE CANADIENNE-FRANÇAIS, VOL XL, 1989, P 299) In his monumental work titled Le Grand arrangement des Acadiens auQuebec, Father Adrien Bergeron pre
2 CONC sented acertain Marie Daussey as being thefirst wife of Jean Gaudet who arrived in Acadia about 1640.From a telephone conversation in the Fall of 1982, Father Bergeron told me that he hadfound this information in an issue of NOVA 
2 CONC FRANCIA, Spring of1927, in whichissue a correspondent who signed "Dr. L----"spoke of said Jean Gaudet, of Abbeville, Picardy, 59 years in 1727, that there was a maritimeregister by virtue of that of Colbert, son of Jean and of Mar
2 CONC ie Daussey, marriedto Jacqueline Harquebout. Master of a ship by becoming an admiral ofAbbeville the 18th Feb., 1700. This anonymous doctor responded thus to aquestion from the genealogist Placide Gaudet, who in an earlier issue o
2 CONC f the review inquired regarding the origin of this family. One does not need a long exzplanation to realize that this French Gaudet family could not inany way attach itself to the Acadian Gaudet family; moreover, Placide Gaudetdid
2 CONC  not retain these erroneous explanations in hislater genealogical work.Father Bergeron also, after more ample verification of the documentation,admitted without delay that he was evidently misled on this point. We dare tosay that 
2 CONC at the moment of thebirth in France in about 1688 of JeanGaudet, Jr., mast of the ship, the old Jean Gaudet, Acadian, well settled at PortRoyal, was not married to Marie Daussey but rather to Nicole Coleson, whoaccording to the ag
2 CONC e she declared at the census of 1671 in Acadia, was in her sixties....... The name of the first wife of Jean Gaudet, ancestor of all the Gaudetsof America, remains unknown to this day."
2 CONT Elaine
2 CONT
2 CONT [v08t0745.ftw]
2 CONT There is much controversy concerning this man. According to FrenchScholars he M. Marie DAUS SY ca. 1598 in Fr., 2nd m. NicoleCOLESON/COLLESON CA.1628 in Fr. Additionally there are records that marryhim to a Leonore Femme ?MERCIER.
2 CONC  To addto the muddle Steve White liststhe COLLESON M. as 1652. His is further exacerbated by a Date of DEATHfo Jean dit Jehan of 1636. Local sources are Rod Wilscam, Jeanette Dinwoodie and Ed Barrieau.I will not add my name to the
2 CONC  debate butwill simply report the facts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Gaudet (Godet) was listed as a censitaire on the fief at Martaizhe village of Martaizsh of Martaizouze boisseaus froment mesure de Loudun et trois derniers de cens a rente feodalle deue par Jean Gendre, Jean Godet, Renoubert 
2 CONC les heritiers Pierre Bourg de sauseau et les heritiers Francois Godet par raison d'une piece du terre et signer estant en terre et signer estant en terre est du Rondonay le tout contenant ensemble et tenant deux septiers six boiss
2 CONC eaus..." (A "fresche" is an old Frenchword for rent due to the seigneur from his or her fief)
2 CONT Jean Gaudet and his son Denis, came together from France about the year1636. They settled first on the north bank of the Port-Royal river,opposite la Pronged to the Gaudet family in 1710.
2 CONT Extract from the census of Port Royal, Acadia, dated November 1671: Laboureur- Jehan Gaudet aagen Labour trois arpens en deux places, Leurs bestes a cornes six pi
2 CONT Jean Gaudet had two brothers, Aubin and Fran
2 CONT Not sure if the rest of Jehan's children came with him to Acadia when hecame with his son, Dennis. - Ronald Joseph Arthur Gaudet
2 CONT On November 12, 1999, Susan (DuBois) Pacheco posted a message on theGaudet Family Genealogy Forum that the first wife of Jean may have been awoman named Marguerite Martin. Susan's E-mail address isspacheco@middlesexbank.com - Rona
2 CONC ld Joseph Arthur Gaudet
2 CONT
2 CONT [11221a.ged]
2 CONT Jean Gaudet was born Abt. 1575 in Martaize, Vienne, France1, and died1672 in Port Royal, Acadia2. He married (2) Nicole Colleson 1628 inFrance3, daughter of Nicolas Colleson and Genevieve Petit.
2 CONT Notes for Jean Gaudet: ACADIAN DESCENDANTS, Vol I, pg 18. Arrived in Port Royal, Acadia, in 1636from Martaise, France. Settled at Port Royal. JEAN GAUDET married twice. Godbout states that he had fourchildren:Francoise, Denis, Mar
2 CONC ie and Jean, the first three of whom becameancestors of ours. He reasoned that Francoise and Denis were born ofJean's first wife (name unknown); that Marie and Jean wereborn of NicoleCOLLESON, his second wife; that the first three
2 CONC  were born in France; andthat Jean came to Acadia after 1633 with his second wife. GODBOUTconsidered that COLLESON was a French name rather than traceable to theScotch settlers who accompanied Sir William ALEXANDER, as has beensug
2 CONC gested.
2 CONT ARSENAULT states that Jean GAUDET probably came to Acadia after 1636,having married Nicole COLLESON "en deuxieme noces" about 1628. Jean islisted in the 1671 census as a 96-year-old farmer (laboureur)living inPort Royal with his 6
2 CONC 4-year-old wife Nicole COLLESON. Still living withthem was their 18-year-old son Jean. They had six head of cattle, threesheep, and three acres of land under cultivation.
2 CONT MASSIGNON identified GAUDET as a name found in Martaize among tenants ofd'AULNAY's seigniory. She also noted that in 1671 Jean GAUDET had 22grand- children and 10 great-grandchildren, thus becoming the ancestor ofone tenth of the 
2 CONC Acadian population.
2 CONT AGE, Apr/Jul 96, Page 38 - Marie Daussey was NOT the first wife of Jean
2 CONT Children of Jean Gaudet are: Denis Gaudet, born 1625 in France; died October 11, 1709 in Port Royal,Acadia. Francoise Gaudet, born 1626 in Martaize, France; died 1698 in Port Royal,Acadia. Child of Jean Gaudet and Nicole Colleson 
2 CONC is: MarieAnne Gaudet, born 1633 in Martaize, France; died July 30, 1710 inPort Royal, Acadia. Jean Gaudet, born 1643 in Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT all of above from Internet: "Someday" Steve and Natalie Flemings Homepage
2 CONT and translated from the webpages of Robert Rachon :Liste des Petronymes" : JEHAN GAUDET Jehan Gaudet was born in France, towards 1575. Surely in the seignioryof Aulnay, the parish of Mortaiz,̌ in Mortagne Perche. The acadianancest
2 CONC or arrived to America, little after 1634. He is the oldest livingat Port Royal. With the census of 1671, Jean (Jehan) Gaudet (Cup), theworthy senior of the colony is then96 years old. He thus has, in France29 or 30 years, at the t
2 CONC ime of the foundation of Port-Royal, and since heis then in the strength of the age, he had to form part of the firstforwarding of Poutrincourt. It is one of these rare French who remains inAcadie, after the capture of Port-Royal 
2 CONC by the Kirth brothers. He marriedby twice, in France, that is to say towards 1598, with Marie Daussy andtowards 1628, with Nicole Colson, born towards 1600. Two girls of thethree children, who belong certainly to the first Gaudet/
2 CONC Daussy marriage,concern us in this genealogical description, by creating links to mymother Pierrette Boisvert. The first, Francoise Gaudet, born in 1623,married before 1644, with Jehan Mercier, in first wedding. Her husbanddecease
2 CONC d, she remariě towards 1650, with that which becomes theancestor of Leblanc, Daniel, born into 1626, unknown parents, probably ofPoitou. With the acadian census of 1686, with Port-Royal, Daniel Leblancand his wife, Francoise Gaude
2 CONC t, are 60 years old. Daniel Leblanc is oneof notable with Port-Royal and, when on May 24 1690, Sir William Phipps,which has just seized the place, requires on behalf of the inhabitants ofPort-Royal and among those of the river of 
2 CONC the same name, to choose sixof them to form the Council, in orderto keep peace among them and tomanage justice there, Daniel Leblanc is one of those on which the choicerests. He dies with the St. Lawrence vault between the years 1
2 CONC 693-1698.Their son, Pierre Leblanc, born in 1664, took to wife in 1684,Marie-Élisabeth Terriot, then in 1689, Madeleine Borough, girl of JeanBorough and Marguerite Martin. The second girl of the coupleGaudet/Daussy, Marie Gaudet, 
2 CONC born towards 1626, becomes the wife into1650 of the ancestor Étienne Hb̌ert, whose two their children weave otherlinks of descents which interest us in this genealogy. The first,Marguerite Hb̌ert, born in 1652, wife the ancestor J
2 CONC acques-NicolasLePrince. Second Étienne Hb̌ert, born in 1654, took to wife in 1678,Jeanne Comeau, born in 1662, girl of Pierre-Étienne Comeau and RoseBayols. The father Archange Godbout described Jehan Gaudet as beingAbraham of Aca
2 CONC die, so much many is his descent. According to the censusof 1671, Jehan Gaudet was born towards 1575. Weare unaware of the dateof his death, like that of his wife, Nicole Coleson (Colson), who is 60years old, with the census of 16
2 CONC 86, with Port-Royal.
2 CONT following from internet: Notes for Jean Gaudet: He arrived in Acadie in 1636 a widower, leaving his brothers Aubin andFrancois behind; he settled at Port Royal. In the 1671 census of Port Royal, Acadia is shown Jean Gaudet age 86 
2 CONC andNicolle Colleson age 64. Property showed that he owned 6 cattle and 3sheep.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean (Jehan) Gaudet is considered to be the patriarch of the Gaudet family because he was the oldest & first Gaudet known to have come to Acadia.
2 CONT According to Massignon, in 1671 Jean Gaudet had 22 grand-children and 10 great-granchildren thus become the ancestor of one-tenth of the Acadian population.
2 CONT Jean (Jehan) Gaudet settled in Acadia about 1636.
2 CONT According to Albert Dauzat from his Etymology Dictionary of Family names of France, Gaudet is known to derive from Gaudon, ancient Germanbaptismal name of Waldo, from Waldon, governor. The spelling "Godet,"means "a manufacturer of
2 CONC  godets"(pots, bowls or glass). Two dictionaries describe the godet as a small drinking bowl with no stem or handle, of which the brim is lobed (rounded divisions). In botany, a godet refers to the she
2 CONT
