2 CONT The 1671 census of Acadia shows: DANIEL LEBLANC, age 45; his spouse FRANCOISE GAUDET, age 48; 7 children: (1 married: Francoise, age 18); others: Jacques, age 20; Estienne, age 15; Rene, age 14; Andre, age 12; Antoine, age 9; Pier
2 CONC re, age 7.
2 CONT <http://acadian-home.org/ancestorsacadian.html> (copy filed L-14-6) contains a brief bio of Daniel Leblanc which quotes many source citations.
2 CONT Listed on 1678 census of Port Royal, Acadia, Canada with Daniel Leblanc and 3 sons.
2 CONT LDS Ancestral file, individual record of self (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http://jason.gaudet.com/gaudet/gaudet_gen1.htm> (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http://geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga12.html> (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT "Mothers of Acadia" (copy filed L-14-16) shows the following: Francoise Gaudet, daughter of Jean (#2005), born in France in 1624, wed Daniel Leblanc in Port-Royal about 1650.  She would count three Acadian Bishops (as of 1945 but 
2 CONC more now) among her descendants and Rene Leblanc, Notary of Grand-Pre her grandson, the son of Rene and Anne Bourgeois.  NOTE: The marriage location is different than previously posted in this record.
2 CONT "The Grand Families" from the internet (copy filed L-14-16) shows her born to unknown mother about 1623.
2 CONT Gaudet Descendents from the internet (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http:www.geocities.com/Heartland/Pointe/6106/genealogy-gaudet.html>. Durocher/Ferguson Genealogy on internet (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT See #2005 for more on the Gaudet Genealogy.
2 CONT Francoise was a widow when she married Daniel.  She had been maried to Jehan Mercier.  She was the daughter of Jean Gaudet and Marie Gaudet.  She died between the Port-Royal census of 1698 and 1700.
2 CONT Durocher/Ferguson Genealogy on internet (copy filed L-14-16) shows her married about 1650 in Port Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT Hebert Genealogy from the internet (copy filed L-14-16) shows a marriage in 1644 to a Mr. Mercier; family of one child, Marie.  Married in 1650 to Daniel Leblanc at Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; family of 7 children.
2 CONT LDS Ancestral File, Descendancy Chart of #2005 (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/gaudet.htm> (copy filed L-14-16 also in her father's internal textfile).
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.baileypages.net/JensCorner/Surnames/gaudet.htm>:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Francoise3 Gaudet (Jean2, Jehan1) was born Abt. 1623 in Martaize, Vienne, France, and died Abt. 1698 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada. She married (1) Mercier in France. She married (2) Daniel LeBlanc Abt. 1650 in Port Royal, Acad
2 CONC ia, Canada, son of Rene LeBlanc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Francoise Gaudet and Daniel LeBlanc are:
2 CONT + 9 i. Jacques4 Leblanc, born Abt. 1651 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died in St Charles des Mines, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 10 ii. Marie-Francoise Leblanc, born Abt. 1653 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 11 iii. Etienne Leblanc, born Abt. 1656 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 12 iv. Andre Leblanc, born Abt. 1657 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 03 May  1743 in St Charles des Mines, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 13 v. Rene Leblanc, born Abt. 1657 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 04 Jan 1733/34 in St Charles des Mines, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 14 vi. Antoine Leblanc, born Abt. 1662 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 20 Jul 1730 in St Charles des Mines, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 15 vii. Pierre Leblanc, born Abt. 1664 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 03 Nov 1717 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/LeblancD.htm> (copy filed L-+14-16); a translated version follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL LEBLANC
2 CONT
2 CONT The most numerous family acadienne has only an alone stump, Daniel Leblanc, that was born in France about 1626, native of Martaizé, parish of the Aulnay seigneurie, in Loudunais, High poitou, current department of the Coming, Fran
2 CONC ce.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor Daniel Leblanc arrives in Acadie, about 1645.  He marries about 1650, the widow of a certain Jehan Haberdasher, Françoise Gaudet, born in 1623, daughter of Jehan Gaudet, tax-based of the Aulnaie seigneurie, at Mortaiz
2 CONC é, in 1634, and Marie Daussy.  Jehan Gaudet and Marie arrived in Acadie and establish to Lay Royal, about 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Lay Royal, to the census of 1671, one counts 68 families, of which the one of Daniel Leblanc, 45 years, and his woman Françoise Gaudet, 48 years, inventoried in the category of the laboureurs.  The census gives us the names of 
2 CONC the seven children of Daniel and Françoise.  Of the six sons, of which five that were founded their own homes.  The youngerer Pierre Leblanc, born in 1664, we link to the ancestor Leblanc, in this genealogical description.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre Leblanc married first with Marie Elisabeth Terriot, about 1684, then in second marriage about 1689, to Madeleine Town (Bourque), born in 1678, at Cobequid, daughter of Jean Town and Marguerite Martin.  Four boys and two gir
2 CONC ls perpetuated the family link to Leblanc.  Pierre Leblanc is buried at Lay Royal, November 5 1717.  NOTE:  A group sheet sheet of Pierre and Marie Terriot was acquired from <http://www.terriau.org/archive/d3.htm> and follows:
2 CONT 10. Marie Terriot 1-[15] 2,41 (Claude2, Jehan1) was born about 1665 at Port Royal, , , Acadia 41 and died before 1694 at Port Royal, , , Acadia, before age 29.45.,46
2 CONT Marie married Pierre LeBlanc -[948] [MRIN:357], son of Daniel LeBlanc -[973] and Marie Francoise Gaudet -[974], about 1684 in Port Royal, , , Acadia.41 Pierre was born in 1664 in Port Royal, , , Acadia, died in 1717 in Port Royal,
2 CONC  , , Acadia, at age 53, and was buried on 5 Nov 1717 in Port Royal, , , Acadia.
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT 64 M    i. Pierre LeBlanc 1-[975] 2 was born about 1685 in Port Royal, , , Acadia and died after 1700, after age 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT To the census acadien of 1686, Daniel Leblanc and his spouse Françoise Gaudet, are 60 years old, at Lay Royal.  Daniel Leblanc saught to conquer the esteem and the recognition of its compatriots.  When May 24 1690, Sir William Phi
2 CONC pps, that has just seized this place, demands from the Harbor inhabitants of Royal and of those of the river of the same name to choose six of them to form a Counsel in order to keep the peace among them and of there to manage jus
2 CONC tice, Daniel Leblanc is the one on that the choice falls.
2 CONT
2 CONT In France, the White adjective is the nickname of a big number of persons.  Even, it some generates others as Blanchet, Blanchon, Blanchot, etc.  United with the simple, white item gives Leblanc, very common in the North of the co
2 CONC untry, patronyme more old and the most important one of the France of the ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor Daniel Leblanc deceases between the years 1693 and 1698.  The history, sometimes cruel, did not only keep the day of his death to Lay Royal.  Françoise Gaudet, widow a second time, dies with his son Pierre, between th
2 CONC e years 1698 and 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT Erroneous ancestry of Daniel Leblanc, that is some does a noble family Leblanc one without kinship
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  Rene LEBLANC
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  Alphonse LEBLANC
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  Platform Isabeau
2 CONT
2 CONT [diagnosis] impossible, confusion with the family Leblanc one while one does not know even from which comes Daniel Leblanc and that this patronyme is rather common
2 CONT
2 CONT Source (origin) : [High poitou] p. 95-96, maybe native of Martaizé, but confirmed no (the patronyme would exist to this place), according to Geneviève Massignon
2 CONT
2 CONT reference: : http://www.genealogie.com/dgaa/dgaa-ll.ht
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.acadian-home.org/ancestorsacadian.html>:
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL  LEBLANC
2 CONT
2 CONT The largest Acadian family began with one man, Daniel LeBlanc, who was born in France about 1626. Arriving in Acadia before 1650, sometime that year, he married Françoise Gaudet, widow of an unknown Mercier, daugher of Jean Gaudet
2 CONC  and his first wife whose name is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of their six sons, five had large families. Among them, they had 35 sons among whom 31 married. Thus, the LeBlanc family grew very rapidly which explains its predominance among Acadian families.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Stephen White:
2 CONT
2 CONT The place of origin and the ancestors of Daniel LeBlanc are unknown. Some have wanted to believe that Daniel descended from a noble family of Dauphiné, based on research by d'Entremont (J. Alfred LeBlanc - the Origins of the LeBla
2 CONC nc Family, "Footprints of the Exiled: A LeBlanc Family Newsletter", vol I, 1986, p. 7), but the family proposed (to René to Alphonse to Pierre) is a Blanc or deBlanc family, rather than LeBlanc (see MM. de La Chenaye-Desbois & Bad
2 CONC ier, "Dictionnaire de la noblesse, 3e édition, Paris, 1863, vol. III, p. 314-317).
2 CONT
2 CONT The jointly-owned land mentioned below, leads researchers to believe that there existed a bond of some kind between Antoine Gougeon and his son-in-law Guillaume Blanchard on one side of the family and with Daniel LeBlanc on the ot
2 CONC her. The nature of the connection is yet unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel LeBlanc settled on the north banks of the Port-Royal River (today clled Annopolis River), to the northeast of the marsh lands of Bélisle, about nine miles further up than fort at Port-Royal, and a half mille further down th
2 CONC an Saint-Laurent chapel, where he died between the years of 1693-1698 (Placide Gaudet "Arbre généalogique de Mgr Edouard LeBlanc, évêque de Saint-Jean, N.B. (First Acadian Bishop), BRH vol XVIII, 1912, p. 357).
2 CONT
2 CONT October 5, 1687: State of executed works in Acadia by Sir d'Aulnay; among those who made their mark: Daniel LeBlanc. Therefore, Daniel came to Acadia before the death of d'Aulnay in 1650 (ANF, Col, C11D, vo II, fol 85).
2 CONT
2 CONT May 24, 1690: Daniel LeBlanc is one of six members of the Council demanded by Phipps and responsible for maintain the peace and to render justice (BRH vol SVIII, p. 357).
2 CONT
2 CONT August 1695: Daniel LeBlanc promises fidelity to the king of England at Port-Royal; if made his mark (Massachusetts Archive, Vol II, fol 540).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1734: Schedule of the Seignorial Rents payable yearly by the Inhabitants of Annapolis Royal...
2 CONT
2 CONT The names of the Several Plantations: 1. Paradis Terrestre 2. Do La Grave or Point LeChesne
2 CONT
2 CONT The first Grantees: 1. Daniel LeBlanc & Guillaume Blanchard 2. Daniel LeBlanc and Antoine Goujon pay one Den per Arpent (per acre)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Present Possessors: 1. John Prince and Pierre Godet 2. Guillaume Blanchard, Joseph LeBlanc and his brethren.
2 CONT
2 CONT (GB, PRO, CO 217, vol VII, fol 90)
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/l/e/b/Trish-Leblanc-NF/GENE5-0001.html>.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. DANIEL LEBLANC (RENÉ1) was born 1626 in France, and died 1693 in Port Royal, Acadia. He married FRANÇOISE GAUDET 1650 in Port Royal, Acadia, daughter of JEAN GAUDET and MARIE DAUSSY. She was born 1623 in France, and died 1698 i
2 CONC n Grand Pré, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for DANIEL LEBLANC:
2 CONT 1671 Acadian Census (Port Royal) - Daniel LeBLANC, 45, wife Francoise GAUDET 48; Children (1 married): Francoise 18; (not married) Jacques 20, Etienne 15, Rene 14, Andre 12, Antoine 9, Pierre 7; cattle 17, sheep 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About DANIEL LEBLANC and FRANÇOISE GAUDET:
2 CONT Marriage: 1650, Port Royal, Acadia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of DANIEL LEBLANC and FRANÇOISE GAUDET are:
2 CONT i.   JACQUES3 LEBLANC, b. 1651, Port Royal, Acadia; d. Bef. 1743, Grand Pré, Acadia.
2 CONT ii.   MARIE FRANÇOISE LEBLANC, b. 1653, Port Royal, Acadia; d. 1680.
2 CONT iii.   ETIENNE LEBLANC, b. 1656, Port Royal, Acadia; d. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ETIENNE LEBLANC:
2 CONT Etienne left home at an early age and went to sea. He was never heard from again.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.   RENÉ LEBLANC, b. 1657, Port Royal, Acadia; d. January 03, 1733/34, Grand Pré, Acadia.
2 CONT v.   ANDRÉ LEBLANC, b. 1659, Port Royal, Acadia; d. May 05, 1743, Grand Pré, Acadia.
2 CONT vi.   ANTOINE LEBLANC, b. 1662, Port Royal, Acadia; d. July 20, 1730, St. Charles des Mines, Acadia.
2 CONT vii.   PIERRE LEBLANC, b. 1664; d. 1717, Port Royal, Acadia.
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------
