2 CONT :Around 1633, Marie Gaudet was born to parents Jean Gaudet and an unknown mother. ≤ref name=DGFA >White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes. Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D
2 CONC 'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print. P.667;800-801≤/ref>. Shortly after Marie married Étienne Hébert, her father remarried (to Nicole Colleson) and her youngest sibling was born about the time of her third child
2 CONC .
2 CONT :Around 1650, Marie married [[Hébert-1269|Etienne Hébert]], brother of [[Hebert-54|Antoine]].≤ref name=DGFA /> Between 1651 and 1670 Mariegave birth to 10 children: Marie, Maguerite, Emmanuel, Etienne, Jean,Françoise, Catherine, M
2 CONC artine, Michel, and Antoine.≤ref name=DGFA />According to depositions from their descendants, Marie came to Francewith her husband.≤ref name=origins >White, Stephen A.  Origins of thePioneers of Acadia, According to the Deposition
2 CONC s made by Their Descendants at Belle-Ile-en-Mer in 1767 [http://acadian-home.org/acadian-origins.html English Translation], Publication: University of Moncton, Centre d'études acadiennes; Online≤/ref> 
2 CONT :'''Children of Marie Gaudet and Étienne Hebert''' are as follows≤refname=DGFA />:#[[Hebert-121|Marie Hebert]], bn. Abt. 1651, Port Royal, Acadia, d. Bet. 1677 - 1678, Port-Royal, Acadie
2 CONT #[[Hebert-118|Marguerite HEBERT]], bn. Abt 1652 in Port-Royal, Acadie#[[Hebert-130|Emmanuel Hebert]], bn. Abt. 1653, Port-Royal, Acadie. d.30 Nov 1744, Grand Pré, Canada#[[Hebert-127|Etienne Hebert]], bn. Abt. 1654, Port Royal, Ac
2 CONC adia, N.S., CA, d. 02 Nov 1713, St. Chas. de Mines, Ac.
2 CONT #[[Hebert-147|Jean HEBERT]], bn. Abt 1659 in Port-Royal, Acadie#[[Hebert-142|Françoise Hebert]], bn. Abt. 1661,  bur. 17 Feb 1713, Port Royal, Acadia at approx. 50 years old#[[Hebert-101|Catherine Hebert]], bn. Abt. 1662, Port-Roy
2 CONC al, d. 3 Aug 1727, Louisbourg, Cape Breton
2 CONT #[[Hébert-663|Martine HEBERT]], bn. Abt 1665 in Port-Royal, Acadie
2 CONT #[[Hebert-110|Michel HEBERT]], bn. Abt 1666 in Port-Royal, Acadie
2 CONT #[[Hébert-1266|Antoine HEBERT]], bn. Abt 1670 in Port-Royal, Acadie
2 CONT :When Etienne died between 1669 and 1671,≤ref name=DGFA />≤ref>Libraryand Archives Canada. [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572 ''Acadie Recensement 1671-1752.'' Transcript.] Dépôt des papiers publics des colon
2 CONC ies; état civil et recensements : Série G 1 :Recensements et documents divers : C-2572. MG 1, G1, volume 466, part1. 1671 Port Royal Census, pages 1-13  (images 2-14). [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/4?r=0
2 CONC &s=4 1671 Census for Marie Gaudet], page 3-4 (image 4-5)≤blockquote>Marie GAUDET, Widow of Etienne HEBERT, 38, Children (married): Marie 20, Marguerite 19; (not married): Emmanuel 17, Etienne 17, Jean 13, Francoise 10, Catherine 9
2 CONC , Martine 6, Michel 5, Antoine 1; cattle 4, sheep 5. Living next door to daughter Marie, 20 and son-in-law Michel De FOREST.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>Marie married Dominique Gareau, Royal Sargeant, around 1676.≤ref name=Gareau >White, St
2 CONC ephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. Dictionnaire Généalogique Des Familles Acadiennes. Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print. P.665-666.≤/ref> They had one child Marie around 16
2 CONC 77.≤ref name=Gareau />≤ref>Library and Archives Canada. 1678 Port Royal Census.  [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c9157 MG 1, Série E, carton 277, partie 1.] France. Archives des Colonies: série E. Dossiers perso
2 CONC nnels. Transcript on microfilm C-9157. Page 23-27 (images 929-933). [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c9157/931?r=0&s=3 1678 Census Entry for Dominiq Garrau & Marie Godet], page 25 (image 931).≤blockquote>Dominiq'
2 CONC  Garrau & Marie Godet, 2 sons age 13 & 11, 3 daughtersaged 18, 13, & 2.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''Children of Marie Gaudet and Dominique Gareau''' are:#[[Gareau-1|Marie Garaut]], bn. Abt. 1677, Port Royal, Acadia, d. Aft.1755, Virginia. ≤ref name=Gareau />
2 CONT :She was widowed again between 1686≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census 
2 CONC can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Dominique GARAULT 6
2 CONC 0, Marie GODET; childrenof Marie (and Emanuel HEBERT): Michel 20, Antoine 16; and Elarie Garault 9; 3 arpents, 4 sheep, 3 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>and 1698≤ref> TimHebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Ac
2 CONC adie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-25
2 CONC 72 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-150≤blockquote> Marie GODET widow 60.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada. [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c257
2 CONC 2/151?r=0&s=2 ''Numéro 18. "Recensement des habitans de Port-Royal leurs familles, terre en valeur, Bestiaux, Arbres fruitiers et fusils pour l'année 1698,"''] pages 106 to 133. 15 images. Microfilm reel F-768, MIKAN no. 2319372. 
2 CONC [http://collectionscanada.gc.ca/pam_archives/index.php?fuseaction=genitem.displayEcopies&lang=eng&rec_nbr=2319372&title=%5bNum%C3%A9ro%2018.%20%20%22Recensement%20des%20habitans%20de%20Port-Royal%20leurs%20familles,%20terre%20...%
2 CONC 5d.&ecopy=e002014424 1698 Census for Marie Godet, widow], on item 5.≤blockquote>Marie GODET, widow 60[sic].≤/blockquote>≤/ref>.  Curiously her burial record says she was widow of Hebert, and does not specify that she was widow of 
2 CONC Gareau.
2 CONT :Marie Godet, wife of Hebert was buried at Port Royal on July 30 1710 aged about 80 years.≤ref>Eglise catholique. Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia). The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755. 
2 CONC Nova Scotia Archives. RG 1 volume 26 page 354 [https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1481 Burial]≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870
2 CONC  C-1870 (image 199) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/199?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT :'''DNA'''. The Mothers of Acadia Maternal DNA project is conducting ongoing research to verify their origins. As of 2015, [http://www.acadian-home.org/Founding-Mothers-of-Acadia.html Stephen White reported] Marie Gaudet had a J1b
2 CONC 2 haplogroup. Ongoing test results are also reported [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. As of 14 Sep 2019, 16 descendants have consistently reported a J haplogroup with 6 of
2 CONC  those doing full testing to J1b2 , while  15 descendants of her sister [[Gaudet-14|Francoise Gaudet]] have reported a J haplogroup with 7 of those doing full testing to J1b2. J haplogroups indicate European origins.
2 CONT == Sources ==
