1 NOTE A short bio of Jehan Gaudet acquired from the internet (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT Married abt 1650 Etienne Hebert (born 1630 at france; died 1670 at Port Royalat Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; sources: Drouin pg 652; family record acquired from the internet (copy filed L-14-16), shows a family of 10 children; "Gén
2 CONC éalogie de L'ancienne Acadie" [G-K] pg 13-14 shows this marriage with a family of 11 children, also that Etienne died bef 1671 and that Marie remarried Dominique Garault (born 1626) and "Généalogy de L'ancienne Acadie" [G-K] pg 1 
2 CONC shows them with family of 3 children; her marriage as listed above must be in error, she was born in  France and came to Acadia abt 1632/36; <http://www.rivette.ourfamily.com/d0013/f85.html>.
2 CONT The 1671 census of Acadia shows the following:  MARIE GAUDET widow of Estienne Hebert age 38, 10 children, (2 married -- Marie age 20, Marguerite, age 19); others, Emmanuel, age 17; Estienne, age 17; Jehan, age 13; Francois, age 1
2 CONC 0; Catherine, age 9; Martine, age 6; Michel, age 5; Anthoine, age 1.
2 CONT "Mothers of Acadia" (copy filed L-14-16) shows the following:  Marie Gaudet (#3028), daughter of Jean (#2005), had married Etienne Hebert in Port-Royal, in 1650.  When P. Molin visited her, she was a 38 year old widow who was prep
2 CONC aring to care for her 10 orphaned children.  One of her daughters, Marguerite Hebert, would marry Jacques Prince at Port-Royal, 1678 and would be the grandmother of all Prince Acadians, including the first Bishop Prince at Saint-H
2 CONC yacinthe.
2 CONT "The Grand Families" from the internet (copy filed L-14-16) shows her born to Nicole Coleson about 1633.
2 CONT Additional information acquired from the net (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT See #2005 for more on the Gaudet Genealogy.
2 CONT <http://geocities.com/ronald_gaudet2001/wga12.html> (copy filed L-14-16).
2 CONT <http:www.geocities.com/Heartland/Pointe/6106/genealogy-gaudet.html>
2 CONT <http://jason.gaudet.com/gaudet/gaudet_gen1.htm> (copy filed L-14-16) shows her born abt 1626 in France and married abt 1641 to Etienne Herbert.
2 CONT <http://home.attbi.com/~sodapop68/webtree/pafg54.htm> (copy filed L-14-16) shows her family with 10 children.
2 CONT <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/HerbertE.htm> (copy filed L-14-16 also in her internal textfile below).
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/HebertE.htm> (copy filed L-14-16); a translated version follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT ESTIENNE  HÉBERT
2 CONT
2 CONT Two Hébert brothers arrived at Port-Royal, in Acadia, between the years 1645 and 1650.  The elder one, Antoine Hébert was born between 1614 and 1621.  He arrives with his wife Genevieve LeFrance.  The junior, Estienne Hébert was b
2 CONC orn about 1630.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are unaware of the name of their parents, nor the place of their exact origin.  Perhaps originating in Tourraine or Loudunois, the Roadway, in Martaizé.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is not any bond of the pioneer to the pioneers, Louis Hébert.  Present description, relates mainly to the ancestor Estienne Hébert, who creates our bonds of descent, in this genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estienne Hébert, ploughman and farmer, married at Port-Royal, in 1650, Marie Gaudet, born between 1626 and 1633, daughter of the ancestor Jehan Gaudet and Nicole Colleson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Étienne Hébert and Marie Gaudet have ten children, five sons and five daughters, between 1651 and 1669, at Port-Royal, in Acadia.  A daughter and a son have descent which concerns us, in this genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite Hébert was born in 1652, at Port-Royal and becomes the wife in 1678, of the ancestor Jacques-Nicolas LePrince, born in 1646, originating in St-Malo of Brittany.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son, Étienne Hébert, born a twin with Emmanuel, in 1654, married in 1678, at Port-Royal, Jeanne Comeau, born in 1662, sister of Pierre Comeau, also known as Esturgeon and daughter of the ancestors Pierre-Estienne Comeau and Ro
2 CONC se Bayol.  Étienne Hébert and Jeanne Comeau have eight children, six girls and two boys, of which Jean-Baptiste Hébert, born in 1692.  Jean-Baptiste marries at Grand-Pre, about 1711, Jeanne-Anne Boudrot, then, after the death of t
2 CONC his one, he marries on January 9, 1719, Élisabeth Granger, daughter of Pierre Granger and Élisabeth Guillebourg.  In the fourth generation, Honore Hébert, born in 1738, in Pisiguit, marries on November 4, 1771, Madeleine Prince.  
2 CONC In the fifth generation, Jean-Chrysostome Hébert, born in 1779, marries on April 20, 1807, at Nicolet, Marie-Anne Héon, born in 1787, in Bécancour.  Their daughter, Marie-Zoe Hébert, marries on January 11, 1836, Moïse Boisvert, a 
2 CONC bond that continues to my mother, Pierrette Boisvert.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor Estienne Hébert dies in 1670.  The grandmother, Marie Gaudet marries in a second wedding to Dominique Garault.
2 CONT
2 CONT The significance of the name Hébert, derived in Normandy from Herbert, itself derived from the Germanic name Hari-Berht, is of Hari = armed, people and of Berht = shining, famous.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Rochon
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.baileypages.net/JensCorner/Surnames/gaudet.htm>:
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Marie Anne3 Gaudet (Jean2, Jehan1) was born Abt. 1633 in Martaize, Loudun, France, and died 30 Jul 1710 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada. She married (1) Etienne Hebert Abt. 1650 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada, son of Hebert. She m
2 CONC arried (2) Dominique Garant Abt. 1670 in Port Royal, Acadie, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Marie Gaudet and Etienne Hebert are:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 21 i. Marie4 Hebert, born Abt. 1651 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died Abt. 1679 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT + 22 ii. Marguerite Hebert, born Abt. 1652 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died in Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT + 23 iii. Emmanuel Hebert, born Abt. 1654 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 01 Dec 1744 in Canada.
2 CONT + 24 iv. Etienne Hebert, born Abt. 1654 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 01 Nov 1713 in St. Chas Mines, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT + 25 v. Jean Hebert, born Abt. 1658 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died in Pisiquit,  Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT + 26 vi. Francoise Hebert, born Abt. 1661 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died 17 Feb 1712/13.
2 CONT + 27 vii. Catherine Hebert, born Abt. 1662.
2 CONT + 28 viii. Martine Hebert, born Abt. 1665 in Port Royal, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada; died Abt. 1759 in Pisiquit, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada.
2 CONT + 29 ix. Michel Hebert, born Abt. 1666 in Port Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada; died 20 Jan 1735/36 in Grand Pre, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT + 30 x. Antoine Hebert, born Abt. 1670 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada; died Aft. 1740 in Port Royal, Acadia, Canada.
2 CONT 31 xi. Marie Hebert, born Abt. 1670.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://www.landrystuff.com/hebert.htm>.
2 CONT
2 CONT HEBERT
2 CONT
2 CONT Today in Louisiana, the surname HEBERT is the most populist French name in the state. Like many other French names in Louisiana, the Heberts can trace their ancestory back to Acadia and France.
2 CONT
2 CONT The progenitor of the Heberts in Louisiana was Jacques Hebert. He was born 1600 at LaHaye Descartes, Parish of Balesne, Touraine, France. He married Marie Juneau. They had at least three sons;
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine
2 CONT Jacques
2 CONT Etienne
2 CONT Antoine was born in 1621 at the same location as his parents. He married in 1639, in France, Genevieve LaFrance, also from France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine, Jacques, and Etienne arrived in Acadia in July, 1640, from a new recruitment conducted by Charles de Menou, and under the guidance of Germain Doucet, Lord of LaVerdure, Captain of the Arms of Pentagoet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Census of Port Royal in 1671 listed;
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine 50
2 CONT Genevieve 58
2 CONT Jehan 22
2 CONT Jehan 18
2 CONT Catherine 15
2 CONT Antoine listed his occupation as a cooper.
2 CONT
2 CONT Etienne was born in 1625 also at LaHaye Descartes. He married in 1650 at Port Royal a Marie Gaudet, the daughter of Jean Gaudet and Nicole Coleson. Their children included
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie 1651
2 CONT Marguerite 1652
2 CONT Emmanuel and Etienne 1654
2 CONT Jean 1658
2 CONT Francoise 1661
2 CONT Catherine 1662
2 CONT Martine 1665
2 CONT Michel 1666
2 CONT Antoine 1670
2 CONT Etienne died in 1670 at Port Royal.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
