2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT BIO: Pierre died before 1686, at the age of 55. He married Anne Gaudet in about 1663, in Port-Royal, Acadie. They are believed to be the parents of the following:1) Huguette (1664-1717) md Jean Bastarache2) Michel (1668-) md (a) A
2 CONC nne-Marie Doiron and (b) Marie-Josephe Richard3) Pierre (1669-1732) md Marie-Jeanne Trahan4) Clement (1674-) md Madeleine Levron ::  https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/156815791/pierre-vincent#add-to-vc
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spellings and attempts to add unsourced parents. Please 
2 CONC contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT ----:Pierre Vincent was born about 1631, location unknown at this time. His parents are unproven.  These parents were on the profile  [[Vincent-2244|Michel Vincent]] and [[Unknown-266816|Jeanne Unknown]] but have been removed sinc
2 CONC e there is no documented proof of the parents of Pierre. 
2 CONT :He married [[Gaudet-18|Anne Gaudet]], daughter of Denis Gaudet and Martine Gauthier,  around 1663 in Port-Royal, according to the depositions of their descendants at Belle-Isle-en-Mer.≤ref name="DGFA"/> Together they had 6 known 
2 CONC children between around 1664 and 1674:
2 CONT
2 CONT # [[Vincent-391|Huguette Vincent]]
2 CONT # [[Vincent-943|Thomas Vincent]]
2 CONT # [[Vincent-667|Michel Vincent]]
2 CONT # [[Vincent-2651|Magdeleine Vincent]]
2 CONT # [[Vincent-3245|Pierre Vincent]]
2 CONT # [[Vincent-309|Clement Vincent]]
2 CONT :In 1671 Pierre, a ploughman age 40,  and Anne age 27,  were enumerated in the first Acadian census in Port-Royal. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~a
2 CONC cadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada]
2 CONC  “Acadie Recensements 1671  1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>at Port Royal: Pierre VINCENT, ploughman 40, wife Anne GAUDET 27; Children: Huguette 7, Thomas 6, Michel 3, Pierre 2; cattle 18, sheep 9. He works 16 arpents of land.≤/bloc
2 CONC kquote> Also: [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671a.htm Scan of original]; [http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671cens.htm Tim Hebert transcription]≤/ref>  They owned 18 head of cattle, 9 sheep and 16 arpents of land. There were 3 boys a
2 CONC nd 1 girl in the household. 
2 CONT :Anne passed away before 1678 since Pierre was  listed without a wife in the 1678 census, but with four boys and two girls: Thomas Michel, Pierre, Unnamed, Huguette and unnamed.  He owned 15 head of cattle, and8 "acres" of land.≤r
2 CONC ef>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 167
2 CONC 8 Census]≤blockquote>Folio 20, at Port Royal: Pierre Vincent, 15 cattle, 8 acres, 4 boys: age 13- born 1665; 11-1667, 9-1669, 7-1671; 2 girls: age 15- born 1663, 10-1668.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :He died before 1687 in Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France ≤ref name="DGFA">Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ''Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes''] (M
2 CONC oncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p.p. 1575-1576.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :Vincent first ancestor known in America.{{Citation Needed}}
2 CONT :Father Léopold Lanctôt omi says in a book whose title is: [https://archive.org/details/famillesacadienn02lanc FAMILIES ACADIENNES] (Volume II), the following:≤ref>The online archived copy contains one reviewwhich is not in agreem
2 CONC ent on the reliability of this publication. Caution is advised. See citation under Sources.≤/ref>
2 CONT ::"Pierre Vincent, was born in France in 1631. He came to Canada in 1654, with Emmanuel Le Borgne, Sieur du Coudray, merchant of La Rochelle, just supply the colony, where he has business interests. The Châteaufort, armed in war, 
2 CONC made available by Le Borgne by his associate, theDuke of Vendome, from La Rochelle 25 March 1654. It carries on board some new settlers, and Pierre Vincent Michel Richard, laborers, and Pierre Thibodeau, miller. It is also loaded 
2 CONC with supplies, weapons and ammunition, whose value amounts to 75,000 pounds ($ 15,000). the ship of 300 tons arrived in Port-Royal in mid-May 1654. "
2 CONT ::"A few days after his arrival, Pierre Vincent attends the capture ofPort Royal by Sedgwick ..........."
2 CONT :When Father Lanctôt writes about Pierre Thibodeau, he said and I quote:
2 CONT
2 CONT ::"...... Emmanuel Le Borgne of Belleisle, lord of Port Royal ......"
2 CONT
2 CONT ::"...... The Châteaufort, captained by Guilbeau ......."
2 CONT ::"Two months after the arrival of Peter" (Thibodeau) "in Acadia, July31, 1654, although one is right in peacetime, a British fleet commanded by Major Robert Sedgwick, appeared before Port Royal . it is composed of three warships 
2 CONC and a ketch (sailboat with two masts), carrying 500 soldiers of fort Sedgwick arrives the Saint John river, which he took over and where he made prisoner Charles Saint-Étienne de La Tour, governor of Acadia. After two weeks of stu
2 CONC bborn resistance, despite its small garrison of 120 men, Germain Doucet, said La Verdure, commander of Port Royal, to capitulate. the French garrison and its commander . and Le Borgne, are returned to France aboard Châteauford Aft
2 CONC er the departure of the French garrison, the English also leave Port Royal, leaving no garrison: people govern themselves through a Council chairedby a trustee, Guillaume Trahan. (His daughter Jeanne married Pierre (II) Vincent).≤
2 CONC ref>"Familles acadiennes", Lanctot, Leopold; Ste-Julie, Qc : Editions du Libre-Echange, 1994; Collection inlibrary; printdisabled; bostonpubliclibrary; americana; Digitizing sponsor Boston Public Library; Language French; Volume v
2 CONC .2≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:*Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=pierre&n=vincent Pierre Vincent] at Geneanet*Roger Vincent, "Histoire et généalogie des Vincent", PDF accessed at htt
2 CONC p://sergevincent.com/Genealogie/Histoire%20et%20Genealogie%20Vincent.pdf*Nos origines [http://nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?pid=52366  Pierre Vincent]
2 CONT
