2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication. Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantivechang
2 CONC es. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Huguette Agathe Vincent was born around 1664 to parents Pierre Vincentand Anne Gaudet in Port Royal, Acadia. .≤ref name=DGFA/>  She was counted in the first Acadian census in 1671 at the age of 7, in Port-Royal, ≤ref>Tim Hebert; T
2 CONC ranscription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/o
2 CONC ocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Pierre VINCENT, 40, wife Anne GAUDET 27; Children: Huguette
2 CONC  7, Thomas 6, Michel 3, Pierre 2; cattle 18, sheep 9.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>and again in 1678 at the age of 15. There were 4 boys in the household, and she was the eldest of the 2 girls.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census 
2 CONC noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port Royal: Pierre Vin
2 CONC cent, 15 cattle, 8 acres, 4 boys: age 13- born 1665; 11-1667, 9-1669, 7-1671; 2 girls: age 15- born 1663, 10-1668.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Around 1684 Huguette married Jean Bastarache from the Basque region inFrance.≤ref name=DGFA>White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Généalog
2 CONC ique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p 81, 1575≤/ref> They likely married in Port Royal (Annapolis Royal,Nova Scotia, Canada) as her parents had been liv
2 CONC ing there since 1671.
2 CONT The couple settled in Port Royal. Between around 1685 and 1702, Hugette gave birth to 5 children: Marie-Anne, François-Marie, Anne, Jean and Pierre.≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT In the 1686 census of Port-Royal, they were listed with their young daughter Marie Anne 7 months old. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/ge
2 CONC nealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. Theoriginal census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recen
2 CONC sements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal :  Jean de BASTARACHE 25, Huguette VINCENT 22; child: Marianne 7 months
2 CONT ≤/blockquote>≤/ref> No land or possessions were mentioned.
2 CONT Between 1693 and 1707, the censuses show that Jean and Huguette seemedto be doing well with a growing family and an increasing number of animals and cultivable land.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Por
2 CONC t-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census mi
2 CONC crofilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Jean BASTARACHE 35, Agat VINCENT hiswife 29, Marie Anne 9, Francoise-Marie 6; 5 cattle 6 sheep, 4 hogs,
2 CONC  4arpents, 1 gun. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 AcadianCensus, at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census
2 CONC  can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-150≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : J
2 CONC ean BASTARACHE 35; Huguette VINCENT (wife) 30; Marie 12; Francois 10; Anne 6; Jean 2; 12 cattle, 8 sheep, 9 hogs, 5 arpents, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie
2 CONC  [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 
2 CONC of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 151-173.≤blockquote>Jean PASTATCH [Jean (Joannis) dit Le Basque Bastarache] 42; Agathe VINCENT [Huguette Agathe Vincent] (wife)36; François 4, Marie-Ann
2 CONC e 15, Françoise-Marie 13; 7 cattle, 6 sheep, 5 arpents, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcriptionof the 1701 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 
2 CONC 1701 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 175
2 CONC 2”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Joannes BASTARACHE45, Huguette VINCENT (wife) 40;Francois 12, Jean 6, Marie Bastarache 17, Anne 8; 1 gun, 8 cattle, 10 sheep, 6 hogs, 2 arpents.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Tra
2 CONC nscription of the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oo
2 CONC cihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Joannes BASTARACHE and his wife, 1 hoy 14 or older, 2 
2 CONC younger boys, 1 girl 12 or older; 2-1/2 arpents, 8 cattle, 20 sheep,4 hogs, 3 guns.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> 
2 CONT By 1707, the family homestead was located east of the fort (Anne) [https://goo.gl/maps/jJlSZ on the south side of the Dauphin] (Annapolis) River.≤ref name=homestead>1707 homestead location of Jean Bastarache. In Au Coeur de l'Acad
2 CONC ie Acadian Settlement on the Annapolis River 1707 Map Parks Canada≤/ref>
2 CONT In 1714, Jean was around 56 years of age and Huguette was about 50. There were 2 sons still living with them. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcriptionof the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadianc
2 CONC ajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Ac
2 CONC adie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote> at Port-Royal : LeBASQUE and his wife, 2 sons≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT Huguette passed away in October 1717, aged about 50 years and was buried 28 October 1717 at Port Royal, Acadia.≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered: The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755, RG 1 Vol. 26 p.360, 
2 CONC Huguette Vincent burial https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1542≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 206) http://heri
2 CONC tage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/206?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT '''DNA'''. Huguette Vincent's mother was Anne Gaudet, whose mother wasMartine Gauthier. The Mothers of Acadia Maternal DNA project is conducting ongoing research to verify their origins. In 2010, [http://www.acadian-home.org/Found
2 CONC ing-Mothers-of-Acadia.html Stephen White reported] that Martine Gauthier had a J1b1 haplogroup. I don't know the details re how many of her descendants were tested to support this report. Lucie Leblanc Constantino describes one ma
2 CONC ternal tree [http://www.acadian-home.org/origins-mtdna.html here]. Ongoing test results are also reported [https://www.familytreedna.com/public/mothersofacadia/default.aspx?section=mtresults here]. As of May 2014,  2 of 2 descenda
2 CONC nts have reported a J haplogroup, indicating European origins.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Timeline'''
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''c1664''' birth 
2 CONT * :''1667-70 Treaty of Breda cedes Acadia to the French; settlement resumes≤ref>[http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/morillon_du_bourg_1E.html Incollaboration, “MORILLON DU BOURG,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, Universit
2 CONC y of Toronto/Université Laval, 2003–, accessed November 20, 2013]≤/ref>''
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''1671''' residence, in Port Royal
2 CONT :'''1678''' residence, in Port Royal
2 CONT :'''c1684''' marriage to Jean Bastarache, in Port Royal
2 CONT :'''c1685''' birth, daughter Marie-Anne
2 CONT :'''1686''' residence, in Port Royal
2 CONT :'''c1687''' birth, son François-Marie
2 CONT :''1687 War of the League of Augsburg (King William’s War) starts between England and France≤ref name=Griffiths2005>Griffiths, Naomi E.S.,From migrant to Acadian : a North-American border people, 1604-1755, Montreal (Québec), McGi
2 CONC ll-Queen's University Press, 2005, p147-151 (King William’s War); p 267-268 (oaths of allegiance)≤/ref>'':''1690 Phipps captures and sacks Port-Royal, coerces inhabitants' oaths of allegiance to English Crown, sets up local Peacek
2 CONC eeping Council and leaves within 12 days.≤ref name=biophips>[http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/phips_william_1E.html C.P.Stacey, “PHIPS, SIR WILLIAM,” in Dictionary of Canadian Biography, vol. 1, University of Toronto/Université Lava
2 CONC l, 2003, accessed November 20, 2013]≤/ref>≤ref name=biowikiphips>Wikipedia contributors, "William Phips," Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=William_Phips&oldid=931316163 (accessed January
