2 CONT :Michel lost his mother when he was only about 11 years old as she wasnot counted in the 1678 census at Port-Royal.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clar
2 CONC ence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>Folio 20, at Port Royal: Pierre Vincent, 15 cattle,8 acres, 4 boys: age 13- born 1665; 11-16
2 CONC 67, 9-1669, 7-1671; 2 girls:age 15- born 1663, 10-1668.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> Michel was one of fourboys and there were also two girls, all between the ages of 7 and 15.
2 CONT :In 1686, at age 18, Michel was living with his brother Thomas, age 20. They were both single.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/
2 CONC 1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements
2 CONC  1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Thomas VINCENT 20, Michel VINCENT his brother 18. Germain DOUCET 45, Marie LANDRY 35, Bertrand 19, Laurens 16, Jacques 15, Claude 12, Marie 8, jeanne 6. Alexis 4, Pierre 1; 5 arpents, 9 catt
2 CONC le, 10 sheep.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :Michel was married twice, and he fathered 19 children.
2 CONT :His first marriage was to Marie Josèphe Richard, daughter of Michel Richard and Madeleine Blanchard, around 1689 in Port-Royal according to the deposition of their descendants at Belle-Isle-en-Mer.≤ref name=DGFA/> Between about 1
2 CONC 690 and 1709, they had 8 children, all born in Pisiguit, Acadia.
2 CONT : '''Children''' Michel Vincent & Marie Josèphe Richard≤ref name=Theriot>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=michel&n=vincent Michel Vincent]≤/ref>
2 CONT # Marie c1690 
2 CONT # Agnès c1692
2 CONT # Anne c1693
2 CONT # Marguerite c1695
2 CONT # Elisabeth Isabelle c1697-1704
2 CONT # Claire c1706
2 CONT # Pierre (dit Pierre à Michel) c1708
2 CONT # Antoine c1709
2 CONT :By 1693, Michel and Marie Josèphe had settled at Les Mines. They owned 3 arpents of land, 6 head of cattle, 5 sheep, 3 hogs and 1 gun. They had 2 young girls. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Roy
2 CONC al, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfi
2 CONC lm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> at Mines: Michel VINCENT 25, Marie RICHARD his wife 18, Marie 3, Agnes 1; 6 cattle, 5 sheep, 3 hogs, 3 arpents, 1 gun.≤/blo
2 CONC ckquote>≤/ref>   They were counted again in the censuses at Les Mines between 1701 and 1707.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/17
2 CONC 01cens.htm 1701 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements
2 CONC  1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote>at Rivière-de-l'Ascension, Les Mines : Michel VINCENT,his wife, 5 girls, 12 cattle. 16 sheep, 3 hogs, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703 Acadian Census, a
2 CONC t Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1703cens.htm 1703 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Ce
2 CONC nsus microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 212-220.≤blockquote> at Les Mines: Michel VINCENT, his wife, 5 girls, 1 arms bearer.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcript
2 CONC ion of the 1707 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1707cens.htm 1707 Census Transcription]. The original censuscan be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac
2 CONC _reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archivesof Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 221-237.≤blockquote>at Mines: Michel VINCENT, his wife, 2 girls 12 or older, 4 younger girls; 1 arp
2 CONC ent, 10 cattle, 8 sheep, 4 hogs≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :After Marie Josèphe passed away in October 1709, Michel, about 42 years of age, married Anne Marie Doiron, age 19, daughter of Jean Doironand Marie Anne Canol, around 1710 in Pisiguit.≤ref name=DGFA/>  Together they had 11 childr
2 CONC en, born between about 1711 and 1735.
2 CONT
2 CONT :'''Children''' Michel Vincent & Anne Marie Doiron≤ref name=Theriot/>
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste c1711 in Pisiguit
2 CONT # Anne Marie c1713 in Pisiguit
2 CONT # Madeleine Aug 1714 in Pisiguit
2 CONT # Elisabeth c1718 in Acadia
2 CONT # Marguerite 1 Oct 1720 in Pisiguit
2 CONT # Joseph 11 Jul 1722 in Acadia 
2 CONT # Charles 5 Mar 1725 in Riviere aux Canards, Acadia 
2 CONT # Anne Euphrosine 4 May 1726 in Acadia
2 CONT # Michel  25 Jul 1729 in  Acadia
2 CONT # Marie Josephe c1733 in Pisiguit
2 CONT # Jeanne c1735 in Pisiguit
2 CONT :By 1714, Michel was back in Pisiguit with his second wife Anne Marie.There were 3 sons and 5 daughters living with them.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.c
2 CONC om/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of
2 CONC  Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote> at Riviere Pisiguit: Michel VINCENT and his wife, 3 sons, 5 daughters.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT :Michel passed away after 1735  (birth of last child). Stephen White does not give a date or location for his death.≤ref name=DGFA/> 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT == Acknowledgments ==*Thanks to [[Arsenault-64 | Roland Arsenault]] for starting this profile.
