2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==:John (Jean) FARDEL (FREDELLE), born around 1643, married around 1685 to Marie GAUDET, daughter of Denis & Martine GAUTHIER; no children traced. It seems likely that he was English; as John FARDEL he took the pledge
2 CONC  of allegiance to the English king at Port Royal in 1695 (old style) (MASS.ARCH., vol.II, fol.540).  Even being English, he raised Marie Gaudet's children as his own over a number of years until they disappeared from the records.
2 CONT * [[1686 Acadian Census]] at Port-Royal: '''Jean FARDEL 46''', Marie GODET 36; children: Bernard 16, Louis 13, Olivier 12, Jean 10, Marie 9,Anne 7, Pierre 5; 1 gun, 5 arpents, 13 cattle, 9 sheep,8 hogs. '''[Note Marie Gaudet is re
2 CONC -married.]'''≤ref>Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; p. 613; own copy. #1:≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT *CENSUS: 1693, age 50 years.
2 CONT *CENSUS: 1698, Port Royal, Acadia, age 60 years (sic), living with wife Marie GODET age 50, and Jean [DAIGLE], age 22. They have 12 cattle, 15 sheep, 10 hogs, on 6 arpents, with 15 fruit trees; 1 gun, 1 servant. [Who? This census 
2 CONC lists 8 unnamed servants among the 575 persons named at Port Royal.]
2 CONT
2 CONT *CENSUS: 1700, age 57 years.
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
