2 CONT
2 CONT Olivier Daigre, born in France in c1643, reached Acadia by c1666, the year he married Marie, daughter of Denis Gaudet and Martine Gauthier.  Between 1667 and 1681, Olivier and Marie had 10 children, seven sons and three daughters.
2 CONC   Olivier died at Port-Royal before c1686, in his early 40s, and Marie remarried to a Fardel or Fredelle.  Two of Olivier's daughters married into the Sibilau, Gouzil, Poitevin dit Parisien, and Tennier or Thénière families.  One 
2 CONC of them, Marie, had "natural" daughters with Gabriel Moulaison dit Recontre and Louis Blin.  Olivier's youngest daughter and her family perished aboard the British transport Violet in a North Atlantic storm during the deportation 
2 CONC of the island Acadians to France in late 1758.  Only two of Olivier's sons created families of their own, at Port-Royal, Minas, and in the French Maritimes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
