2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of potential confusion between brothers of same name (see note below). Please contact the Acadi
2 CONC an Project before making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT IMPORTANT NOTE: This family had two sons named Jean-one born about 1667 and the other born about 1676.
2 CONT Jean was born about 1667 in Port Royale to his parents Olivier Daigre and Marie Gaudet. ≤ref>Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DESFAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 
2 CONC 2 vols.; p. 446; own copy.≤/ref>He is found on the first Acadian census as Jehan, age 4.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671c
2 CONC ens.htm 1671Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 
2 CONC – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>Olivier DAIGRE 28, wife, Marie GAUDET 20; Children: Jean 4 (see Jehan in the original), Jacques, 2, Bernard 1; cattle 6, sheep 6.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>. This birth year is consistent with the 1678 acco
2 CONC unting in which birth years are compared≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont,Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com
2 CONC /~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>Ollivier Daigre & Marie Godet
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 boys the oldest             12   1666    Jean           1667
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 girls                        2   1676    Marie                  1677
2 CONT
2 CONT St Christoffe at the Ste Marie Brook
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 acres   6 cattle≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Clarence J. d'Entremont, "Recensement de Port-Royal," in MEMOIRESDE LA SOCIETE GENEALOGIQUE CANADIENNE-FRANCAISE; vol. 22, no. 4; p. 229; sent by PERSI in Jun 1999. Folio 18: There are six
2 CONC  boys (this oldest age 12 years) and two girls in the household of Olivier DAIGRE & Marie GODET.≤/ref>
2 CONT In 1686 when Jean would have been about 20, his younger siblings were living with their mother and her new husband Jean Fardel≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.roots
2 CONC web.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives
2 CONC  of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Jean FARDEL 46, Marie GODET 36; children: Bernard 16, Louis 13, Olivier 12, Jean 10, Marie 9, Anne 7, Pierre 5; 1 gun, 5 arpents, 13 cattle. 13 sheep, 8 hogs.
2 CONC ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>and in 1693 his brother Bernard, newly married is in Minas.  Bernard has moved and Olivier (his brother) has resurfaced in 1701 and they are both present with their families in 1703 and 1707.  Bernard went to Pi
2 CONC siguit and then Port Lajoie, his sister Anne was in St. Pierre Du Nord in 1752.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes ==No marriage or death information has been provided (by White, his corrections, or by Reader).  No Jean Daigre in the 1752 LaRoque census (only his sister Anne aged 80 is found).  No records for him in Drouin/Qu
2 CONC ebec.
2 CONT
