2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Bernard was born around 1670[1], probably in Port-Royal, Acadia (Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada) since his parents Olivier Daigre and Marie Gaudet had settled there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard was counted in his family's household in Port-Royal in the censuses of 1671 (age 1)[2], and 1678 (age 7)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1686, at Port Royal, Bernard, aged 16, was living with his stepfather, Jean FARDEL, aged 46, and his mother, Marie Godet [sic], aged 36, and his six siblings: Louis, aged 13, Olivier, aged 12, Jean, aged 10, Marie, aged 9, Anne
2 CONC , aged 7, and Pierre, aged 5. The family owned 1 gun and was living on 5 arpents of cultivable land with 13 cattle, 9 sheep and 8 hogs.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard (20) married Marie Claire Bourg (19) (born about 1671 in Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France; daughter of Bernard Bourg and Françoise Brun) in 1691 in Pisiguit, Acadie. Their known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Daigre (abt. 1692–bef. 1763) .
2 CONT Pierre (Daigle) Daigre (abt. 1696–1759) .
2 CONT Joseph Daigre (abt. 1696–1757) .
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Daigre (1698–1759) .
2 CONT Anne (Daigle) Daigre (1698–abt. 1701) .
2 CONT Marie Claire Daigre (1700–1758) .
2 CONT Unknown Daigle (abt. 1701– ) .
2 CONT Charles Daigle (abt. 1702–abt. 1757) .
2 CONT Francois Daigle (1705–1759) .
2 CONT Abraham Daigre (1706–1755) .
2 CONT Unknown (Daigle) Daigre (abt. 1707– ) .
2 CONT René Daigle (1709–1757) .
2 CONT Amand (Daigle) Daigre (1712–1758)
2 CONT The Daigre family settled at Les Mines as shown in the censuses of 1693[5], 1701[6], 1703[7], and 1707[8]. They were counted again in 1714 but this time at Pisiquit.[9].
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie-Claire died in 1727 at Pisiquit.[1] Bernard died in Port-La-Joye, île Saint-Jean (Rocky Point, Prince Edward Island) on the 22nd of January 1751.[10][1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographie
2 CONT Bernard est né vers 1670, probablement â Port-Royal, Acadie (Annapolis Royal, Nouvelle Écosse, Canada). Ses parents étaient Olivier Daigre et Marie Gaudet.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Vers 1691, Bernard épousa Marie-Claire Bourg, fille de Bernard Bourg et de Françoise Brun. Entre 1692 et 1712 environ, le couple a eu 13 enfants: Bernard, Pierre, Joseph, Anne, Jean, Marie-Claire, fils inconnu, Charles, François, 
2 CONC Abraham, fils inconnu, (Louis) René, et Amand.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie-Claire est décédée à Pisiquit (Windsor, Nouvelle-Écosse Canada) en 1727. Bernard est décédé à Port-La-Joye, île Saint-Jean (Rocky Point, île-du-Prince-Édouard) le 22 janvier 1751. [10][1]
2 CONT
