1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}} 
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Parents Olivier Daigle and Marie Gaudet had a daughter whose name is unkown.  Stephen White placed her birth order as fourth, consistent with the census data. In 1671 ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at P
2 CONC ort-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census 
2 CONC microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote> at Port Royal: Olivier DAIGRE 28, wife, Marie GAUDET20; Children: Jean 4, Jacques, 2, Bernard 1; cattle 6, sheep 6.≤/b
2 CONC lockquote>≤/ref>, no daughters are listed; in 1678 ≤ref>Tim Hebert;1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.r
2 CONC ootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port-Royal: Ollvier Daigre Marie Godet 6boys the oldest 12 years 1666. 2 girls 2 years 1676 St Cristoffe at the Ste Marie Brook 4 acres 6 cattle≤/blockquo
2 CONC te>≤/ref>, two are listed. Therefore, she was presumably born after 1671 and before 1678. WhileWhite lists her birth as before 1678, it is listed here as after 1671, to make the birth order more understandable.   
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:* White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Génalogique Des Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Univ
2 CONC ersité De Moncton, 1999, Print, 447.
2 CONT
