2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category:Twins]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography ==Marie and her twin sister Madeleine were born about 1682 in Port-Royal.≤ref name=DGFA>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38 ''Dictionnaire Généalogique des F
2 CONC amilles Acadiennes''] (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p. 671 (Blanchard), 1200 (Mirande), 671 (Lavielle)≤/ref>  She was the daughter of [[Gaudet-17|Pierre Gaudet]] and [[Blanchard-186|Anne
2 CONC  Blanchard]].  
2 CONT When Marie was about 22 years of age, she married Joseph Mirande, the son of Emmanuel Mirande (a Portuguese immigrant) and Marguerite Bourgeois.≤ref name=DGFA/> Between about 1705 and 1724, they had seven children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The widowed Marie remarried in 1735.≤ref>IREL, Archives nationales d'outre mer. Etat civil, Ile Royale LOREMBEC 1735, p. 1 [http://anom.archivesnationales.culture.gouv.fr/caomec2/osd.php?territoire=ILE%20ROYALE&commune=LOREMBEC&an
2 CONC nee=1735&typeacte=AC_MA Marriage of Pierre Lavielle and Marie Gaudet 23 August 1735].≤/ref>≤ref name=DGFA/> It is mentioned in the marriage record that her husband Pierre Lavielle was from Gascogne, the son of Pierre Lavielle also
2 CONC  from Gascogne and Catherine Dumaugré from Cape Breton. Pierre and Marie had no knownchildren.  
2 CONT She passed away in January 1739 at the age of about 57.  Marie was interred on 8 January 1739 in Lorembec, Île-Royale, Acadie. ≤ref>IREL, Archives nationales d'outre-mer. Etat civil, Ile Royale LOREMBEC 1739, p. 1 [http://anom.arc
2 CONC hivesnationales.culture.gouv.fr/caomec2/osd.php?territoire=ILE%20ROYALE&commune=LOREMBEC&annee=1739&typeacte=AC_DE Marie Gaudet Burial 8 January 1739]≤/ref>≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
