2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of confusion betweensisters.  Please contact the Acadian Project before making any substantive 
2 CONC changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT :'''Marie and her sister Anne [[Blanchard-186|Marie Blanchard]] married brothers. Her sister Anne married the older Pierre (l'aîné), whileMarie married the younger Pierre (le jeune)'''
2 CONT Marie was born around 1656 in Port-Royal. She was the 6th and last child of Jean Blanchard and Radegonde Lambert. Marie was listed in the first census of Port-Royal in 1671 at the age of 15, unmarried, and living with her parents 
2 CONC and siblings.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed].  The original census can be found at [http
2 CONC ://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of theNational Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>Jean BLANCHARD, 60, wife, Radegonde LAMBERT 
2 CONC 42; Children (married): Martin 24, Madeline 28, Anne 26; (unmarried): Guillaume 21, Bernard 18, Marie 15; cattle 12, sheep 9, 5 arpents.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  
2 CONT Four years later, around 1675, she married Pierre Gaudet le jeune, sonof Denis Gaudet and Martine Gauthier. ≤ref>Stephen A. White, Patrice Gallant, Hector-J. Hébert, [http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38''Dictionnaire Généalo
2 CONC gique des Familles Acadiennes''] (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'études Acadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999) p. 143, 668. Copy in possession of  [[Girouard-4019| Jacqueline Girouard]]
2 CONT ≤/ref>   Between about 1676 and 1698 they had ten children.
2 CONT In 1678 Pierre and Marie were enumerated in the Port-Royal census withtheir two sons. Marie's parents lived next door. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. 
2 CONC Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port-Royal: Pierre Godet & Marie Blanchard. 4 acres,   6 cattle, 2 boys:   Pierre  ag
2 CONC e 3, Antoine 5 months.       ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  The family remained in Port-Royal and seemed to be doing well as shown in the censuses  in 1686≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [htt
2 CONC p://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of th
2 CONC e National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>vierre GODET, the younger,32; Marie BLANCHARD 30; Children: Pierre 10, Antoine 7, Germain 5, Guillaume 3, Denis 2 months; 2 guns, 3 arpents,
2 CONC  10 cattle, 18 sheep, 10 hogs.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, 1693≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. 
2 CONC The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote
2 CONC >	Denis GODET (widower) 70, Pierre GODET 39, Marie BLANCHARD (Pierre's wife) 37, Pierre 16, Anthoine 13, Germain 11, Guillaume 9, Denis 7, Marie 5, Jean 3; 20 cattle, 32 sheep, 15 pigs, 29 arpents, 2 guns≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, 1698≤
2 CONC ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.can
2 CONC adiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 110-150≤blockquote>Pierre GODET, the younger, 46; Marie BLANCHARD (wife) 
2 CONC 44; Pierre 22; Antoine 20; Germain 18; Guillaume 16; Denis 14; Marguerite 12; Jean 9; Bernard 7; Marie 4; 25 cattle, 35 sheep, 15 hogs, 26 arpents, 72 fruit trees, 2 guns,≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, 1700≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of 
2 CONC the 1700 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 CensusTranscribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c25
2 CONC 72/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 151-173.≤blockquote> Pierre GODET 46; Marie BLANCHARD (wife) 44; Pierre 23; Anthoine 20; Germain 18; Guilla
2 CONC ume 16; Denis 14; Jean 10; BERNARD 5; Marie 12; Marie-Anne 3; Jeanne 2; 23 cattle, 27 sheep, 25 arpents, 3 guns.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, 1701≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://free
2 CONC pages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the Nati
2 CONC onal Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote>Pierre GODET, the younger, 40, Marie BLANCHARD (wife) 35; Louis 24, Jacques 23, Clement 21, Augustin 18; 2 guns, 8 cattle, 6 sheep, 6 hogs, 9 a
2 CONC rpents.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>, 1703≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1703cens.htm 1703 Census Transcription]. The original census c
2 CONC an be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 212-220.≤blockquote>Pierre GODET, his 
