2 CONT == Biography =='''Bernard Godet''' was born about 1692. He was the son of [[Gaudet-11|Pierre Gaudet]] and [[Blanchard-488|Marie Blanchard]]. He was age 7 on the 1698 census.
2 CONT He married Marguerite Pellerin, daughter of Etienne Pellerin and Jeanne Savoy 7 February 1716 at Port Royal. The bride and groom both signedand Pierre Godet and Nicolas Daigle also signed.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de
2 CONC  la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 173) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/173?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste,
2 CONC  Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Bernard Godet and Marguerite Pellerin marriage RG 1 volume 26 page 317https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1321≤/ref>
2 CONT *Five children: Joseph Gaudet, Germain Gaudet, Marguerite Gaudet, Amand Gregoire Gaudet, Pierre Gaudet
2 CONT *Bernard died January 13, 1747 at   Port Royal/Annapolis Royal, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT
