1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Josèphe Aucoin was born about 1730, a daughter of Michel Aucoin and Marie Josèphe Henry.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents and five children were deported to France, Marie Josephe among them. She was hospitalized 24 January-1 April, but survived.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Germain Blanchard, son of Joseph Blanchard and Anne Dupuis, and widower of Marguerite Bourg, on 31 March 1761 in Langrolay, Côtes d'Armor, France.[1][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Julienne Françoise Blanchard, b. 28 Mar 1763, Langrolay, Bretagne d. 30 Mar 1763, Langrolay, Bretagne, France (Age 0 years)[5]
2 CONT Jeanne Françoise Blanchard, b. 28 Mar 1763, Langrolay, Bretagne, France d. 30 Mar 1763, Langrolay, Bretagne, France (Age 0 years)[6]
2 CONT Marie Jeanne Blanchard, b. 5 Mar 1764, La Gravelle, Pleudihen-sur-Rance, Côtes-d'Armor, France d. 6 Mar 1764, Pleudihen-sur-Rance, Côtes-d'Armor, France (Age 0 years)
2 CONT Marie Jeanne Blanchard, b. 22 Nov 1765, La Gravelle, Pleudihen-sur-Rance, Côtes-d'Armor, France d. 27 Nov 1765, Pleudihen-sur-Rance, Côtes-d'Armor, France (Age 0 years)[7]
2 CONT The family was recorded on the 1762 census in Sangrolay, France.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Germain Blanchard, 40
2 CONT wife Marie Josephe Aucoin, 30
2 CONT Jean, 16 (at hospital 17 May to 24 Jun and 31 Aug to 26 Sep 1762)
2 CONT Elisabeth Aucoin, 17 (Marie Josephe's sister, at hospital 30 Apr to 22 May 1762)
2 CONT The family was recorded on the 15 Sep 1772 census at St-Malo.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Karen Theriot Reader Marie Josèphe Aucoin citing :
2 CONT Albert J. Robichaux, THE ACADIAN EXILES IN SAINT-MALO; 1758-1785; vol. 1, pt. 1, Eunice, LA, Hebert Publications, 1981; p. 21, family #30; own copy. Also p. 66, family #83
2 CONT Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes: 1715 à 1780780 - Stephen A. White - Moncton, NB: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, draft version -University of Moncton - BLANCHARD #11 c They were 2nd cousins one time removed; - Germa
2 CONC in BLANCHARD (parents named) married 2nd on 31 Mar 1762 to Marie-Josèphe AUCOIN, daughter of Michel AUCOIN & Marie-Josèphe HENRY. There was a dispensation of 3-4 consanguinity, 3-4 affinity (Langrolay Register).
2 CONT ↑ "Rolle des habitans de l'Isle St Jean débarqués à St Malo le 23 janvier 1759 des 5 paquebots anglois le Yarmouth, la Patience, le Mathias, la Restoration et le John et Samuel," Fonds de l'inscription maritime de Saint-Servan (Fr
2 CONC ance): C-4619, MG6 C2, Library and Archives Canada, Roll of the " Five English ships " (Yarmouth, Patience, Mathias, Restoration, John Samuel) disembarked at Saint-Malo on January 23, 1759 image 165, accessed 9/9/2023
2 CONT AUCOIN Michel, 50, plowman, injured his leg, hospitalized 24 January. Lived in St Servan at the home of Catherine Denis. Died at the hospital on 8 February 1759.
2 CONT HENRY Marie Joseph, 50, his wife, at St Servan
2 CONT AUCOIN Marie Josèphe, 27, daughter, hospitalized 24 January-1 April
2 CONT AUCOIN Marguerite, 22, daughter, died 2 March 1759
2 CONT AUCOIN Geneviève, 15, daughter
2 CONT AUCOIN Isabelle, 14, daughter, hospitalized 30 March-5 April
2 CONT AUCOIN Ozite, 10, daughter, died 19 March 1759 in St Servan
2 CONT ↑ "Registres paroissiaux et d’état civil, Côtes-d'Armor, France, 1467-1920", database, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6FQZ-C389 : 21 April 2022), Marie Aucoin in entry for Germain Blanchard, 1761.
2 CONT ↑ Marcel Walter Landry Marie Josèphe Aucoin at Généalogie des Landry à travers le monde, accessed May 2020
2 CONT ↑ "Registres paroissiaux et d’état civil, Côtes-d'Armor, France, 1467-1920", database, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6FQW-VMFH : 20 April 2022), Marie Aucoin in entry for Julienne Françoise Blanchard, 1
2 CONC 763.
2 CONT ↑ "Registres paroissiaux et d’état civil, Côtes-d'Armor, France, 1467-1920", database, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6FQW-2WW9 : 20 April 2022), Marie Aucoin in entry for Jeanne Françoise Blanchard, 176
2 CONC 3.
2 CONT ↑ "Registres paroissiaux et d’état civil, Côtes-d'Armor, France, 1467-1920", database, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6FQN-STJ1 : 20 April 2022), Marie Au Coin in entry for Marie Jeanne Blanchard, 1765.
2 CONT ↑ Rieder, M. P., & Rieder, N. G. (1967). The Acadians in France, 1762-1776. s.n. Page 27, Accessed 9 Feb 2026, https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Acadians_in_France_1762_1776/ZugnAQAAMAAJ?kptab=editions&gbpv=1
2 CONT ↑ Rieder, M. P., & Rieder, N. G. (1967). The Acadians in France, 1762-1776. s.n. Page 40, Accessed 9 Feb 2026, https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Acadians_in_France_1762_1776/ZugnAQAAMAAJ?kptab=editions&gbpv=1
2 CONT Germain Blanchard, 49, laborer of St-Malo
2 CONT Marie Josephe Aucoin, 40, spins and cuts
