1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW YORK with the rank of PRIVATE.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A103396  DAR Ancestor #  A103396]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was Christened in Liverpool, England on July 8, 1750. He was a member of the English Army during the Revolutionary War of 1776, but when he came to New York he became a Colonist and fought for Independence. He was given land in
2 CONC  what is now Guernsey County, Ohio after the War as payment of service in the War. He is buried in Leatherwood Cemetery (aka Miller's Methodist Episcopal Church Cemetery). His original stone was broken in half and a new stone was 
2 CONC placed near the original. There is a "1776" marker from the DAR on his grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5073972/james-sharrock
