2 CONT **Drouin Institute (Archived marriage record - see attached in Media tab)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Born in 1742 at Beaubassin. Magdeleine is the first Landry that we can see in Kamouraska. -She married (1) Jean Cormier, b. 2 March 1733 at Beaubassin, son of Pierre and Cecile Thibodeau on 5 July 1762 at St. Louis of Kamouraska
2 CONC . -She then married (2) Jean Baptiste Levasseur, b. 1 Sept. 1752 at Kamouraska, son of Pierre and Genevieve Phocas DIT Raymond, 22 Aug. 1775 at St. Louis of Kamouraska. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-380237461/madeleine-cormier-born-landry-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 7 2018
2 CONC , 3:45:50 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT {{Acadian}}Madeleine Landry was born around 1742 at St-Joseph-de-la-Rivière-aux-Canards, Grand-Pre, Acadie (now Kings, New Brunswick) to [[Landry-3065|Alexis Landry]] and [[Aucoin-242|Marguerite Aucoin]] ≤ref name="prdh-individu">
2 CONC [https://www.prdh-igd.com/Membership/fr/PRDH/Individu/163818Programme de Récherche en Démographie Historique (PRDH)] Individual#163818 Marie Madeleine Landry.≤/ref> ≤ref name="grave">[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167127835 
2 CONC Canada, Find A Grave Index, 1600s-Current] Madeleine Cormier.≤/ref> ≤ref name="origines">Genealogy of Canada/Nos origines - Madeleine Landry [https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Landry_Madeleine&pid=1744
2 CONC 50&lng=en (English version)] [https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Landry_Madeleine&pid=174450&lng=fr (version français)]≤/ref>.
2 CONT She had a younger [[Landry-3486|half-sister]] with the same name as her who was born around 1756.
2 CONT Her family left Acadia and settled in the Kamouraska region of Nouvelle-France.
2 CONT She married Jean-Baptiste Cormier on July 5, 1762 at St-Louis, Kamouraska ≤ref name="marriage">[https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/1091/d13p_31171065/105003627 Quebec, Canada, Vital and Church Records ''(Drouin Collection)'', 16
2 CONC 21-1968] K > Kamouraska > St-Louis > 1727-1798 > Page 199. Marriage of Jean Baptiste Cormier and Marie Madeleine Landry - 5 July 1762 - St-Louis parish, Kamouraska, Province de Québec. Accessed on Ancestry.com on 26 Nov 2018.≤span
2 CONC  style="color:blueviolet"> (primary source)≤/span>≤/ref> ≤ref name="prdh-mariage">[https://www.prdh-igd.com/Membership/fr/PRDH/Acte/205039 Programme de Récherche en Démographie Historique (PRDH)] Mariage #205039  Jean Cormier and 
2 CONC Madeleine Landrille≤/ref> ≤ref name="tanguay1">[https://www.ancestry.ca/interactive/2177/32746_238408-00145/198893 Quebec, Genealogical Dictionary of Canadian Families (Tanguay Collection), 1608-1890.] Accessed on Ancestry.com on 
2 CONC 26 Nov 2018, or [http://numerique.banq.qc.ca/patrimoine/details/52327/2021541 Same document] accessed at la Bibliothèque et Archives nationales du Québec (open access). Vol 5 - Page 129. Child of Alexis Landry (Acadian).≤/ref> ≤re
2 CONC f name="tanguay2">[https://www.ancestry.ca/interactive/2177/32746_238404-00149/553027 Quebec, Genealogical Dictionary of Canadian Families (Tanguay Collection), 1608-1890.] Accessed on Ancestry.com on 26 Nov 2018, or [http://numer
2 CONC ique.banq.qc.ca/patrimoine/details/52327/2021541 Same document] accessed at la Bibliothèque et Archives nationales du Québec (open access). Vol 3 - Page 129. Wife of Jean Cormier (m. 1762).≤/ref>.
2 CONT The couple had about 14 known children together ≤ref name="origines"/>≤ref name="prdh-famille">[https://www.prdh-igd.com/Membership/fr/PRDH/Famille/39448 Programme de Récherche en Démographie Historique (PRDH)] Family #39448 Jean 
2 CONC Baptiste Cormier and Marie Madeleine Landry.≤/ref>.
2 CONT *Jean François (1763)
2 CONT *Marie Madeleine (1764)
2 CONT *Marie Françoise (1766)
2 CONT *Marie Rose (1768)
2 CONT *Roger (1768)
2 CONT *Marie-Anne (1770)
2 CONT *Jean François (1772)
2 CONT *Pierre (1773)
2 CONT *Esther (1775)
2 CONT *Victoire (1778)
2 CONT *Madeleine (1782)
2 CONT *Marie (1783)
2 CONT *Alexis (1784)
2 CONT *Marie Françoise (~1786)She died in Feb 1803 and was buried at St-Basile, Madawaska, New Brunswick ≤ref name="grave"/>.
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* Marriage: Leger, Beloved Acadia of my Ancestors (Translated by Antoine Bugeauld; Montreal: Fleuve, 1992), Family 152, Pg 316.
