1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mathurin Gaudet, private, served for three months in the American Revolutionary War, at £ 2 per month. He was the second son of Pierre (dit Pierrotte à Pitre) Gaudet and Marie-Madeleine Aucoin and was born about 17
2 CONC 55. According to his great-grandnephew Placide Gaudet (Fonds généalogique, famille Gaudet, CEA 1.98-30), he was never married, but died at Memramcook at an advanced age, perhaps in the late 1830’s or early 1840’s, when there are g
2 CONC aps in the Memramcook parish registers. See Gaudet-1 iv. http://stephenwhite.acadian-home.org/american-revolution.html
