2 CONT **"Acadian Immigrants to Lafourche des Chitimachas/Valenzuéla, 1785-86" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***At Grande-Anse, Île St.-Jean, Aug 1752, age 26
2 CONT ***Deported from Île St.-Jean to Rochefort, France, 1758-59
2 CONT ***Arrived St.-Malo, France, from Rochefort, 13 Oct 1759
2 CONT ***At St.-Suliac, France, 1759-60
2 CONT ***At Pleurtuit, France, 1760-72
2 CONT ***On list of Acadians at Nantes, France, Sep 1784, listed as Prosper Landri
2 CONT ***Sailed to la Luisiana on ''La Bergère'', age 60
2 CONT ***Valenzuela, la Luisiana census, 1788, listed as Prospere, age 64
2 CONT ***Valenzuela, la Luisiana census, 1791, listed as Prosper Landri, age 66
2 CONT ***Valenzuela, la Luisiana census, 1795, listed as Prospero, age 71
2 CONT ***Valenzuela, la Luisiana census, 1797, listed as Prospere, age 72
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana Aug 1785
2 CONT **Died two days before his wife was buried
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Prosper immigrated to P.E.I. during 1749-50. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1.  on the 23rd of Sept. 1751 at Port Lajoie (present day Charlottetown) to Anne Josette Boudrot of the Pisiquit (Windsor) area.  2.  on July 8, 1754  Port Lajoie to Marie Madeleine Bourg of Cobequid (Truro), NS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1752 census shows that they had, at that time, had an eight week old daughter, Margueritte (b.1752). The 1752 census also shows that Joseph (b.1732), Prosper's brother; and Mathurin Boudrot (b.1742), Josette's brother; were bo
2 CONC th living with Prosper and Josette.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Prosper married, m.  1761, Elizabeth Pitre. Prosper was located at Pleurtuit, France in 1763; eventually they settled at Louisiana.
