2 CONT **"Acadians Aboard English ship Britannia, 1769" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***Exiled to Province of Maryland 1755, age 31
2 CONT ***In report of Acadians at Upper Marlborough, Province of Maryland, Jul 1763, called Marie Brasseu
2 CONT ***Departed Port Tobacco, Province of Maryland, 5 Jan 1769, aboard English schooner Britannia
2 CONT ***Lost in the Gulf of Mexico & held by Spanish at La Bahia, Spanish Texas
2 CONT ***Arrived Natchitoches Post, la Luisiana, 24 Oct 1769, overland from Spanish Texas, age 46
2 CONT ***Settled below Bayou Plaquemine, St.-Gabriel District, la Luisiana with other Acadian exiles from the Britannia, Apr 1770
2 CONT ***St.-Gabriel, La Luisiana census, 1777, unnamed, age 35[sic]
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1785, unnamed
2 CONT ***On Opelousas militia list, Jul 1785, fusilier, listed as Antoine Belard
2 CONT ***In succession of her husband Olivier dated 8 Dec 1787, St. Landry Parish Courthouse
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
