2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==Jeanne Boudrot was born in 1645 in Port-Royal, Acadie. Her parents were [[Boudrot-14|Michel Boudrot]] and [[Aucoin-8|Michelle Aucoin]].  Around 1665, she married [[Thériot-103|Bonaventure Thériot]]. ≤ref>"Dictionnai
2 CONC re Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes"; Stephen A. White; 2vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p. 184≤/ref> and together  they had 4 children:
2 CONT # [[Thériot-116|Marie]]
2 CONT # [[Thériot-143|Anne]]
2 CONT # [[Thériot-663|Unnamed girl]]
2 CONT # [[Terriot-30|Marguerite]]
2 CONT Jeanne Boudrot, wife of Bonaventure Teriot, died on 8 May 1710, aged about 60 years (sic) and was buried the next day at Port-Royal, Acadia.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Por
2 CONC t-Royal, N.-É.)-1870 C-1870 (image 199) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/199?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Jeanne Boudrot buria
2 CONC l RG 1 volume 26 page 353 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1478≤/ref>
2 CONT == Sources ==
