2 CONC l 1727 in Port Royal and was buried there the same day. 2 3[2][3] Andree was 25 on the 1671 Acadian Census, taken at Port-Royal, Acadie, and married to Germaine Terriot. They had one child, age 2.[4][5] Andrée Brun and Emmanuel He
2 CONC bert or Hébert were married around 1678 and were enumerated on the 1686 Acadian Census, taken at Port-Royal, Acadie.[6] In 1694, Emanuel Hebert and Andree Brun were again enumerated with their children, living in Port-Royal.[7] So
