2 CONT Pierre Thériot aka Thériault, Terriot Born about 1671 in Port-Royal, Acadiemap ANCESTORS ancestors Son of Germain Thériot and Andrée Brun Brother of Germain Thériot II, Catherine Thériot, Guillaume Hebert [half], Marguerite Hebert
2 CONC  [half], Jean-Emmanuel Hebert [half], Jacques‎ Hébert [half], Alexandre Hebert [half] and	Martin Hebert [half] Husband of Marie Bourg — married 1695 in Port Royal, Acadiamap DESCENDANTS descendants Father of Joseph Theriot, Marie 
2 CONC Josephe Theriot, Marguerite Theriot, Cecile Terriot, Judith Theriot, Élisabeth Thériot and Marie-Josephe (Theriot) Theriault Died [date unknown] [location unknown] The Acadian flag. Pierre Thériot is an Acadian. Join: Acadians Pro
2 CONC ject Discuss: ACADIA Contents [hide] 1 Biography 1.1 Residence 2 Sources 2.1 Object Biography Pierre was born around 1671.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children's church records listed in the St. Charles aux Mines register.:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle Teriot b. 22 July 1710, bt. 24 Aug 1710 at Cobeguit.[2] Joseph Terriot wed Francoise Melancon (Pierre Melancon and Marie Blanchard) on 4 Oct. 1724. [3] Pierre Terriot b. 5 Sep 1712, bt. 20 Oct 1712 at Cobeguit. [4] Reside
2 CONC nce 1686 Acadian Census at Port-Royal: Emanuel HEBERT 30, Andree BRUN 40; children: Guillaume 6, Marguerite 5, Jean 3, Jacques 2, and a 1 month old baby not baptized; children Germain 18, Pierre 15. Catherine 12; 1 gun, 4 arpents,
2 CONC  14 cattle, 21 sheep, 8 hogs. 1693 Acadian Census at Minas: Pierre TERIOT 21, 2 arpents. Marriage Marriage 1695 Cobequid,Acadia,,[5] Marriage 1698 Port Royal, Acadie, Nova Scotia, Canada. Husband Pierre Theriot. Wife Marie Bourg.
2 CONT
