2 CONT :By 1678, seven of their children had been born.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census noting that the correlations for this censuswere done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.root
2 CONC sweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm 1678 Census]≤blockquote>Claude Terriot & Marie Gautrot
2 CONT 3 acres   5 cattle3 boys                      16  1662    Germain        1662    1663≤br>9   1669    Jean               1670   1668≤br>
2 CONT 1   1677    Claud            1678≤br>4 girls                       14   1664    Marie            1665    1665≤br>12   1666    Marguerite   1667    1666≤br>
2 CONT 8   1670    Anne              1672≤br>4   1674    Jeanne            1674≤/blockquote>≤/ref>. Four more children were born by 1686.≤ref>Tim Hebert;Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.ro
2 CONC otsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archi
2 CONC ves of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Claude TERRIOT 49, MarieGOTRO his wife 40; children: Jean 18. Claude 8, Pierre 2, Anne 14, Jeanne 12, Marie 7, Magdelaine 5, Elisabet 1; 1 gun, 13 arpents.
2 CONC  8 cattle, 6 sheep.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> By 1693 the growing family was nearly complete, with 11 of the 14 children born by then, all living in Port Royal. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Aca
2 CONC die [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-25
2 CONC 72 of the National Archives of Canada]“Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote> Claude TERRIOT 55, Marie GOUTROT 48, Jeanne 18, Claude 15, Marie 12, Madeleine 12, Pierre 9, Elisabeth 7, Joseph 6, Marie 2; 12 cat
2 CONC tle, 15 sheep, 7 pigs, 15 arpents, 1 gun≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref> Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1698 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1698cens.htm 1698 Census Transcribed
2 CONC ]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671– 1752”, Images 110-150≤blockqu
2 CONC ote>Claude TERRIOT 60; Marie GOTROT 53 (wife) 53; Marie 18; Claude 17; Magdelaine 15; Pierre 13;  Joseph10; Margueritte 8; 12 cattle, 20 sheep,12 hogs, 18 arpents, 50 fruit trees, 1 gun,≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  Just one more child was
2 CONC  to be born, probably just after the 1693 census was taken.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1700 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1700cens.htm 1700 Census Transcribed
2 CONC ]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671  1752”, Images 151-173.≤blockq
2 CONC uote>Claude TERRIOT 62; Marie GOUTROT (wife) 55; Claude 22; Pierre 16; Joseph 13; Marie 19; Madelaine 17; Elisabeth 14; Marie 9; Marguerite 7; 10 cattle, 13 sheep, 15 arpents 1gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>. All but three of these childr
2 CONC en lived to adulthood, married and had families of their own, rsulting in 93 known grandchildren.
2 CONT : Marie lived a long life all in the same village, when she died on 29NOV 1732; Port-Royal, Acadie≤ref>Nova Scotia Archives, "An Acadian Parish Remembered - The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal,1702-1755," register 
2 CONC RG 1 volume 26a page 105; online database with images,[https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1910 Marie Gautro ]≤blockquote>Marie Gautro died 29 November 1732 , about ninety years old, widow of Claude Therio≤/bloc
2 CONC kquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT == Research Notes ==Karen Theriot Reader:  Are the last two daughters, another Marie and another Marguerite, really hers? She would have been very old when theywere born.
