2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spelling, and numerous changes in relationships. Please c
2 CONC ontact the Acadian Project before making any substantive changes.Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT :Germain Theriot, the eldest child of [[Thériot-73|Claude Theriot]] and [[Gautrot-20|Marie Gautrot]], was born  about 1662, very likely in Port-Royal since the family was listed in the 1671 census at that location.≤ref>Tim Hebert;
2 CONC  Transcription of the 1671 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie. [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1671cens.htm 1671 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view
2 CONC /oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada]“Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752” Images 3-14.≤blockquote>at Port-Royal : Claude TERRIAU 34, wife, Marie GAUTEROT 24; Children: Ger
2 CONC main 9, Marie 6, Marguerite 4, Jehan 1; cattle 13, sheep 3, 6 arpents ofcultivated land.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> ≤ref name="DGFA"> White, Stephen A. Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert, ''Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadien
2 CONC nes'' (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre d'études acadiennes, Université de Moncton, 1999)   pp. 1373, 1485, 1490-1491≤blockquote>*Germain THÉRIOT, born around 1662, son of Claude & Marie GAUTROT. Note: No place given for birth.*Germain marr
2 CONC ied before the census of 1686 to Anne RICHARD ; eleven children. Note:  No place given for marriage.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>   He was also counted in the family home at age 16 in 1678.≤ref>Tim Hebert; 1678 Port Royal Acadian Census not
2 CONC ing that the correlations for this census were done by Rev. Clarence J. d'Entremont, Fairhaven, Massachusetts.[http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1678cens.htm1678 Census]≤blockquote>at Port Royal : Claude Terrio
2 CONC t & Marie Gautrot,3 acres 5 cattle, 3 boys (16 1662 Germain 1662); (9 1669 Jean 1670); (1 1678 Claude 1678) 4 girls (14 1664; Marie 1665); 12 1668 Marguerite 1667); (8 1670 Anne 1673); (4 1674 Jeanne 1675)≤/blockquote>≤/ref> 
2 CONT :Germain Theriot and [[Richard-35|Anne Richard]], daughter of [[Richard-74 |Michel Richard]] and [[Blanchard-77|Madeleine Blanchard]], were married about 1686, in Port Royal, Acadie.≤ref name="DGFA"/>
2 CONT :Children :≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=germain&n=theriot&oc=Germain Theriot] at Geneanet.≤/ref>
2 CONT # [[Terriot-3|Claude]] b: Abt 1687 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Theriot-596|Jean]]  b: Abt 1690 in Mines, Acadia
2 CONT # [[Terriot-33|Jacques]]  b: Abt 1691 in Mines, Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-168|Marie]]  b: Abt 1693 in Grand Pré, Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-274|Joseph]]  b: Abt 1695 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Terriot-75|Unknown son]] b: bef 1701 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-42|Anne]]  b: Abt 1703 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-668|Unknown son]] b: bef 1707 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-86|Madeleine]]  b: Abt 1703 in Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-88|Marguerite]] b: 8 Jun 1709 in Grand Pré, Acadia
2 CONT # [[Thériot-87|Germain]] b: Abt 1713 in Grand Pré, Acadia
2 CONT :The 1686 census shows that the newlyweds Germain, age 23 years, and  Anne, age 15, owned 1 gun, 6 arpents of worked land, 6 horned animals,and 8 sheep. No children were listed yet.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadia
2 CONC n Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 A
2 CONC cadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Germain TERRIOT 23, Anne RICHARD hiswife 15; 1 gun, 6 arpents, 6 cattle, 8 sheep.≤/blockquote>≤/ref> 
2 CONT :By 1693 the family had settled at Les Mines, where they lived for many years and raised their children, as shown in the censuses between 1693 and 1714.  ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Aca
2 CONC die [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-25
2 CONC 72 of the National Archives ofCanada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108≤blockquote>at Les Mines : 	Germain TERRIOT 30, Anne RICHARD 20, Claude 7, Jean 3, Jacques 1 1/2; 12 cattle, 12 sheep, 12 pigs, 8 arpents, 1 gun
2 CONC ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1701 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1701cens.htm 1701 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at
2 CONC  [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 174-211.≤blockquote>at Grand-Pré: Germain TERRIOT, h
2 CONC is wife, 5 boys, 1 girl, 12 arpents, 10 cattle,14 sheep, 8 hogs, 1 gun.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1703 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1703c
2 CONC ens.htm 1703 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 16
2 CONC 71  1752”, Images 212-220.≤blockquote>at Les Mines: Germain TERRIOT, his wife, 5 boys, 1 girl, 1 arms bearer.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1714 Acadian Census at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.root
2 CONC sweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1714cens.htm 1714 Census Transcription]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archi
2 CONC ves of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 239-261.≤blockquote>at Les Mines : Germain TERRIOT and wife, 2 daughters. (According to Stephen White in DGFA p. 1491, it should read 2 sons and 3 daughters)≤/blockquote>≤/r
2 CONC ef>
2 CONT :A letter dated  25 August 1714 granted permission to Germain and his family to settle at Isle Royale.≤ref name="DGFA"/> 
2 CONT :He died sometime after 17 October 1730, the date he witnessed the marriage of his granddaughter Marguerite Theriot.≤ref>"Diocese of Baton Rouge, Catholic Church Records", vol.  1a:  Acadian Records, 1707-1748 (Diocese, 1999); p. 
2 CONC 180 :"Germain TERRIOT (who signed) acted as witness to the marriage of hisgranddaughter Marguerite TERIOT, daughter of deceased Claude & Marguerite deCORMIÉ, on 17 Oct 1730 at Grand Pré (SGA-2, 219)."≤/ref>
2 CONT
