2 CONT !BIRTH: Year of birth based on 1671 Acadian census of the parish of Port Royal, Acadia (Nova Scotia); shows Marguerite, age 4, daughter of Claude Terriau, age 34, and wife Gauterot, with other children; census published in LeBlanc
2 CONC , The Acadian Miracle, page 22; Evangeline Pub. Co., Lafayette, LA, 1966, Library of Congress catalogue number 65-28646, available at the Fairfax County Library, Fairfax,VA, call number 971.6 L.
2 CONT
2 CONT !CHRISTENING: Information based on 1671 census, above.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MARRIAGE: Information on date from Doloris Desjardins, Montreal, Quebec, in a letter dated 4 October 1983 in response to an inquiry to La Societe Genealogique Canadienne-Francaise, Montreal; same information found in Bergeron, Le
2 CONC  Grand Arrangement des Acadiens au Quebec, Volume IV, La Famille des Landry, page 283; Montreal, 1981; available at the Library of Congress, Local History & Genealogy Room, call number CS88.Q4B47 (1981).
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH: Information based on birth date of last known child as listed in Bergeron.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL: Information based on birthdate of last known child as shown in Bergeron, Le Grand Arrangement des Acadiens au Quebec, Volume IV, La Famille des Landry, pages 283-84; Montreal, 1981; availableat the Library of Congress, Lo
2 CONC cal History & Genealogy Room, call number CS88.Q4B47 (1981).
2 CONT
2 CONT !CENSUS: 1671 Census of the parish of Port Royal, Acadia (Nova Scotia); shows Claude Terriau, 34, with wife Gauterot; son Germain, 9; daughters Marie, 6, Marguerite, 4, and son Jean, 1; 10 cattle and 6 sheep; census published in L
2 CONC eBlanc, The Acadian Miracle, page 22; Evangeline Pub. Co., Lafayette, LA, 1966, Library of Congress catalogue number 65-28646, available at the Fairfax County Library, Fairfax, VA, call number 971.6 L.
2 CONT 1686 Census of the parish of Port Royal, Acadia (Nova Scotia); lists Claude Landry, age 26, wife Marguerite Terio, and one daughter; census published in Leblanc, above, at page 380.
2 CONT 1714 Census of the River of Habitants, Acadia (Nova Scotia), lists a Claude Landry and his wife, one son and five daughters; census published in LeBlanc, The Acadian Miracle, page 389; Evangeline Pub.Co., Lafayette, LA, 1966, Libr
2 CONC ary of Congress catalogue number 65-28646, available at the Fairfax County Library, Fairfax, VA, call number 971.6 L.
