2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplication, variant name spellings. Please contact the Acadian Project beforemakin
2 CONC g any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT :Jean Thériot, son of Claude Theriot and Marie Gautrot, was born about 1670 at Port-Royal, Acadie. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] ≤/ref> ≤ref>Source: [[#S68]]≤/ref> He died  after 24 Nov 1727 probably in Grand Pre. This date is derived fr
2 CONC om the marriage record of his son Charle, "Charle, son of Jean TERRIOT & deceased Jeanne LANDRY, married on 24 Nov 1727to Francoise LANDRY". ≤ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese
2 CONC  of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. Personal copy;  pp. 109 & 182.≤/ref>
2 CONT :Jean Theriot and Jeanne Landry, daughter of Rene (le jeune) Landry & Marie Bernard, were married about 1691 in Acadie. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] 
2 CONT :p. 1494, THÉRIOT #9 ≤/ref>
2 CONT :[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I307 Children] All born in Acadie
