2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT :Marie Thériot was born in 1690 in Port Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France. Her parents were [[Thériot-73|Claude Thériot]] and [[Gautrot-20|Marie Gautrot]]. She married [[Beliveau-81|Antoine Beliveau]] in 1701. Antoine Beliveau m. to 
2 CONC Marie Terriot are listed on the baptismal register for their daughter Marie Beliveau.≤ref>[https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=18 Nova Scotia Archives] An Acadian Parish Remembered-The Registers of St. Jean-Bapt
2 CONC iste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755, Marie Beliveau, Register-RG 1 Vol. 26 p.6 , Priest-Felix Pain, Registration Date 24 May 1703, Event-Baptism, Name-Marie Beliveau, born 30 April 1703, Father-Antoine Beliveau, Mother-Marie Terriot,
2 CONC  Godparents-	Jean Beliveau, Marie Gautrot, https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=18≤/ref>   Together they had 8 children:
2 CONT # [[Belliveau-187|Marie Belliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Belliveau-97|Charles Belliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-104|Anne Beliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-105|Joseph Beliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-39|Jean Baptiste Beliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-106|Jean Beliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-107|Paul Beliveau]]
2 CONT # [[Beliveau-108|Madeleine Beliveau]]
2 CONT :"Marie Teriot"  died on May 04, 1753 in Port-Royal, Acadie, Nouvelle-France. She was said to have been about 63 years old and a widow of the late Antoine Beliveau. (Âgée d'environ 63 ans à son décès en 1753; naissance estimée à 1
2 CONC 690.) Her burial was witnessed by Charles Beliveau, Claude Dugast and Charles Melançon.≤ref>[https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=3436 Nova Scotia Archives-Death Record]
2 CONT : Sépulture 
2 CONT :: Register: RG 1 volume 26a page 486 
2 CONT :: Priest: Desenclaves 
2 CONT :: Registration Date: 5 May 1753
2 CONT :: Event: Burial
2 CONT :: Name: Marie Teriot:: died: 4 May 1753 , about sixty-three years old, widow of the late Antoine Beliveau:: Witnesses: Charles Beliveau, Claude Dugast, Charles Melançon ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT
