2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==Élisabeth (Terriot) Thériot was born about 1686. She was the daughter of  [[Thériot-73|Claude Thériot]] and [[Gautrot-20|Marie Gautrot]]. ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Aca
2 CONC die [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-25
2 CONC 72 of the National Archives of Canada] Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60, p. 46, Image 17.:"Claude TERRIOT 49, Marie GOTRO his wife 40; children: Jean 18. Claude 8, Pierre 2, Anne 14, Jeanne 12, Marie 7, Magdelaine 5,
2 CONC  Elisabet 1; 1 gun, 13 arpents. 8 cattle, 6 sheep.≤/ref> ≤ref>[http://collectionscanada.gc.ca/pam_archives/index.php?fuseaction=genitem.displayEcopies&lang=eng&rec_nbr=2319364&title=%5bNum%C3%A9ro%2010.%20%20%22Recensement%20fait%
2 CONC 20par%20de%20Meulles,%20Intendant%20de%20la%20...%5d.&ecopy=e002014350 Canada Archives] or [http://data2.archives.ca/e/e081/e002014350.jpg Elisabet]≤/ref>
2 CONT She is found in 1693 with her parents and two more younger siblings≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal,Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Tra
2 CONC nscribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements 1671 – 1752”, Images 62-108
2 CONC :"Claude TERRIOT 55, Marie GOUTROT 48, Jeanne 18, Claude 15, Marie 12,Madeleine 12, Pierre 9, Elisabeth 7, Joseph 6, Marie 2; 12 cattle, 15sheep, 7 pigs, 15 arpents, 1 gun"≤/ref>
2 CONT Elizabeth Teriau married Antoine Blanchard, son of Guilliaume Blanchard and Huguette Goujon 31 January 1707 at Port Royal.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Jean-Baptiste (Port-Royal, N.-É.)-18
2 CONC 70 C-1870 (image 124) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1869/124?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>An Acadian Parish Remembered The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Antoine Blanchard and Elizabeth Teriau
2 CONC  marriage RG 1 volume 26 page281 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=1218≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Marie Josephe BLANCHARD 1708-1772
2 CONT # Anne Marie BLANCHARD 1710-
2 CONT # Marie Madeleine BLANCHARD 1711-/1779
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste BLANCHARD 1714-1779
2 CONT # Honore BLANCHARD ca 1716-
2 CONT # Paul BLANCHARD 1718-
2 CONT # Elisabeth (Isabelle) BLANCHARD 1721-1773
2 CONT # Marguerite BLANCHARD 1724-1724
2 CONT # Anne BLANCHARD 1725-1800
2 CONT # Marguerite BLANCHARD 1728-
2 CONT Isabelle Terriot passed away 27 Mar 1735, aged about 48 years and was interred at Port Royal the next day. Witnesses were Guillaume Blanchard, Antoine Blanchard, Pierre Blanchard, and Claude Girouard. ≤ref>An Acadian Parish Rememb
2 CONC ered: The Registers of St. Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755 Isabelle Terriot burial RG 1 Vol. 26a p.135 https://novascotia.ca/archives/acadian/archives.asp?ID=2066≤/ref>
