2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT : Joseph Theriot, son of Claude Theriot and Marie Gautrot, was born about 1687 in Port-Royal, Acadie. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] :Joseph THÉRIOT, born around 1687, son of Claude & Marie GAUTROT. He was on the Port Royal census of 1683
2 CONC , age 6 years; in 1698, age 10 years; in 1700, age 13 years. ≤/ref>He died (Port Royal Register) in 1711, during the captivity of Father DURAND at Boston. ≤ref>Source: [[#DGFA]] :Text: Joseph died in 1711 (Port Royal Register), al
2 CONC ong with older brother Pierre, during the captivity of Father DURAND in Boston.≤/ref> ≤ref>Title: "Acadian Parish Remembered: The Registers of St Jean-Baptiste, Annapolis Royal, 1702-1755, An"; Repository: Internet; RG 1, vol. 26,
2 CONC  p. 364; Source published by Karen Theriot Reader, Rootsweb.com:Note: Scanned image of actual register. Father Durand was absent, captive in Boston, from Sep to Dec 1711.:Text: Joseph Teriot, Pierre Teriot, Germain Bourgeois, Ange
2 CONC lique Comeau [in margin]
2 CONT :Angelique Comeau femme de Jacques Laure Germain Bourgeois
2 CONT Joseph Teriot, Pierre Teriot sont morts l'an 1711 durant
2 CONT ma captivité de Boston P. Justinien Durand Recollet Missionaire
2 CONT
2 CONT :[Translation of entry]:Angelique Comeau, wife of Jacques Laure, Germain Bourgeois, Joseph Teriot, :Pierre Teriot—died in the year 1711 during my captivity in Boston. F[ather] Justinien Durand, Missionary Friar≤/ref>
2 CONT
