2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography =='''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of potential confusion with her sister of same name. Please contact the Acadian Project before 
2 CONC making any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Marguerite Theriot was born about 1689 at Port Royal, Acadia. ≤ref>Source: [[#S14]]  Page:  pp. 1389 & 1486 THÉRIOT #2 n Note:  Was mother really around age 48 when she was born? Text:  Marguerite THÉRIOT, daughter of Claude & Mar
2 CONC ie GAUTROT, born around 1693, 2nd daughter of this name in this family. [The other married Claude LANDRY.]≤/ref> She died April 1777 and was buried  28 APR 1777, at Becancour, Quebec, Canada≤ref>[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/
2 CONC 61903/3:1:3QS7-8993-ZJZF?i=403&wc=9RLD-FM9%3A13624501%2C13624502%2C16709401&cc=1321742 Burial - FamilySearch]≤/ref>≤ref>Source: [[#S14]] pp. 1389 & 1486.  Text:  Age around 97 years (sic).≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT Notes Karen Theriot Reader, Rootsweb.com, Inc.:BIRTH-PARENTS-CENSUS-MARRIAGE-BURIAL: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714 ; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999 , 2 vol
2 CONC s.; p. 1486. Marguerite THE'RIOT, born around 1693 [more likely earlier, since mother would be around age 48], daughter of Claude & Marie GAUTROT, appeared on census of 1698 as age 8 years (sic); 1700, age 7 years. She married (Po
2 CONC rt Royal Register) on 26 Jan 1712 to Rene' RICHARD dit BEAUPRE', son of Rene' & Madeleine LANDRY. She was on the 1763 census at MA. She was buried(Be'cancour Register) on 28 Apr 1777 at age around 97 years (sic).
2 CONT ::: :CENSUS: 1693, Port Royal, Acadia; household of Claude TERR IOT, age 55, & Marie GOUTROT, age 48, with eight children a ges 18 to 2. [Marguerite does not appear with family, although there is no child between Joseph, age 6 and
2 CONC  Marie, age 2. Could she be second child named Marie, age really 4, not 2? Could she have been missed? Or could she have been born just after census taken? But mother would have been too old?]
2 CONT ::: :CENSUS: 1698, Port Royal, Acadia; household of Claude TERROIT [sic], age 60 & wife Marie GOTROT, age 53, with six children age 18 to 8 years old. This girl is youngest, Margueritte, age 8 years (sic, but I believe correct).
2 CONT ::: :CENSUS: 1700, Port Royal, Acadia. The two youngest children are Marie, age 9; and Marguerite, 7 years old.
2 CONT ::: :NAME-MARRIAGE: Sometimes spelled THERIAULT. Arsenault, H&G , p. 806 spells TERRIOT, gives husband's name as Rene' RICHARD de BEAUPRE'.
2 CONT ::: :MARRIAGES: Adrien Bergeron, LE GRAND ARRANGEMENT DES ACADIENS AU QUEBEC; 1600-1889; vol. 8; p. 49; Gail Burk's copy . Marguerite TERRIAU/THE'RIAULT, born 1667, daughter of Claude & Marie GAUTEROT, married 1st at Port Royal ar
2 CONC ound 1684 to Claude LANDRY, son of Rene' & Mar. BERNARD. She marrie d 2nd [sic] on 26 Jan 1712 at Port Royal to Rene' RICHARD , son of Rene' & Magdel. LANDRY. [These were two different sisters.]
2 CONT ::: :BURIAL: Parish of La-Nativite'-de-Notre-Dame-et-St-Pierre , at Be'cancour, Quebec, Canada; Burial register. Marguerit e buried 28 Apr 1777 at age around 97 years [sic].
2 CONT
