2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !BIRTH-PARENTS-CENSUS-MARRIAGES-BURIAL: Stephen A. White, D ICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714 ; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999 , 2 vols.; p. 917; own copy. !NAME: Spelled with an
2 CONC  accent over the first E of Ce'cile. !CENSUS: 1678, Port Royal, Acadia, age 17 years (sic). !CENSUS: 1686, Les Mines [Grand Pre'], Acadia, age 22. Livi ng with Philippe [sic] TERIO, age 32, and a domestique Jacq ues MARTIN, age no
2 CONC t given. Also listed as the daughter of Rene LANDRY & Marie BER NARD, on the 1686 census of Port Royal, Cecile was age 22. !CENSUS: 1693, age 29 years. !MARRIAGE-BURIAL: Diocese of Baton Rouge [LA], CATHOLIC CHU RCH RECORDS, vol. 
2 CONC 1; 1707-1769; published by the diocese, B aton Rouge, LA, 1978; p. 73; Sutro Library F377 B3 C3 v. 1 . Two entries: Cecile LANDRY (no parents listed) married o n 12 Aug 1725 to Etienne RACOIS, called Desrosiers, maste r surgeon, (
2 CONC SGA-2, 251). [She would have been age 61, 2nd h usband only about 42 years old.She would have been a wealt hy widow. She waited only 2 1/2 months after Pierre's deat h to remarry. Etienne only lived another 6 1/2 years.] Also: In 
2 CONC the Acadian Records of St. Charles-aux-Mines , Grand Pre', Acadia, carried to St. Gabriel Church in Loui siana (SGA-3, 11b). Age 78, widow Etienne RACOIS, called De rosiere, surgeon, bur. 18 Oct 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !INFORMATION: was taken from Historire ET Généalogie Des Acadiens by Bona ARSENAULT, Tome1 page 516. THERIAULT et THERIOT aussi: TERRIAULT, TERRIO, TERRIOT, THERRIO, THERRIOT. Pierre TERRIOT né en 1655, fils de Jean et de Perrine 
2 CONC BOURG, marié vers 1684, a Cécile LANDRY, fille de René et de Marie BERNARD. Il n'eût pas de decendant. Il fut le co-fondateur de Grand Pré (avec Pierre MELANSON) et il s'est établi sur la rivière Saint Antoine, paroisse de Saint J
2 CONC oseph de la rivière aux Canards.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Cecile Landry, 1664, fille de Rene et de Marie Bernard, epousa PierreTerriot, fils de Jean et de Perrine Bourg, et,en secondes noces, le sieurEtienne Racois, chirurgien a Grand-Pre. Re: Bona ArsenaultHistorie Et Genealogie Des Aca
2 CONC diens 2 Page 624 Port Royal Annapolis Royal, Nouvelle-Ecosse
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT www.terrebonneparish.com list a Port Royal census "Taken by Monsieur De Meulles, Intendant of New France and Acadia at the beginning of 1686". Cecile's age is given as "22".
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Les Mines, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==Around 1664 Cécile Landry was born to parents René Landry (le jeune)and Marie Bernard. 
2 CONT About 1678 Cécile married Pierre Thériot, son of Jean and Perrine Rau.  Pierre was a judge. They had no children.
2 CONT On August 12 1725 Cécile married Sieur Etienne Racois dit de Rosier, son of widow Catherine Carrerot and an unnamed father.  ≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/608?r=0&s=5≤/ref> They also had no children 
2 CONT Cécile was buried at Grand Pré at St-Charles-de-Mines parish on October 18 1741. 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death Alt ===
2 CONT :October 1741 in Grand-Pré, Acadie
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT : Husband:  [[Terriot-18|Pierre Terriot]]
2 CONT : Wife:  [[Landry-176|Cecille Landry]]
2 CONT : Marriage:  
2 CONT :: Source: [[#S68]]
2 CONT : Note:  from 1678 Port Royal Census
2 CONT :: Pierre Terriot & Cecile Landry-4 acres   4 cattle
2 CONT :: Source: [[#S68]]
2 CONT : Note:  fr 1693 Port Royal Census:: Pierre TERRIOT 39, Cecile LANDRY 29, 2 servants; 22 cattle, 8 sheep, 8 pigs, 16 arpents, 1 gun
2 CONT :: Source: [[#S70]]
2 CONT
