1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **Drouin Institute (Archived marriage record - see attached in Media tab)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT LEBLANC, Pierre (Antoine & Marie BOURGEOIS, b. circa 1688, married 1711-02-16 at Grand-Pré (Saint-Charles-des-Mines) (Acadie) to LANDRY, Françoise (Antoine & Marie THIBODEAU), born between 1695 and 1707, died 1767-10-03, buried 17
2 CONC 67-10-04 Lavaltrie (Qc).
2 CONT       1) Agnès, born about 1711, married at Grand-Pré (Saint-Charles-des-Mines) (Acadie) 1731-10-15 to Pierre GAUTREAU.
2 CONT       2) Anne, born about 1717, married at Grand-Pré (Saint-Charles-des-Mines) (Acadie) 1739-01-07 to Charles DUGAS.
2 CONT       3) Augustin, married about 1752 to Françoise HÉBERT.
2 CONT       4) Françoise, married (1st) about 1745 to Louis Sylvain DUPUIS, married (2nd) at L'Acadie (Sainte-Marguerite-de-Blairfindie) (Qc) 1801-09-28 to Antoine BOUDREAU.
2 CONT       5) Joseph, married about 1754 to Anne MOÏSE.
2 CONT       6) Marguerite Monique, married about 1754 to Charles HÉBERT.
2 CONT       7) Marie, born about 1728, married at Grand-Pré (Saint-Charles-des-Mines) (Acadie) 1748-07-10 to François GAUTREAU.
2 CONT       8) Marie Angélique, married about 1746 to Germain DUPUIS.
2 CONT       9) Marie Rose, born about 1724, died 1771-05-21, buried 1771-05-22 at Bécancour (Qc), married Boston, Suffolk Co. (Massachusetts), USA 1762-08-24 to Jean Baptiste HÉBERT.
2 CONT       10) Pierre Hilaire, married (1st) at Guilford, New Haven Co. (Connecticut), USA 1762-10-13 Marie Élisabeth HÉBERT, married (2nd) at L'Acadie (Qc) 1784-10-25 to Marie GRANGER.
2 CONT       11) Théodore, married at Beaubassin (Acadie) 1740-06-04 to Marie CORMIER.
2 CONT       12) Ursule, born about 1713, married at Grand-Pré (Saint-Charles-des-Mines) (Acadie) 1740-02-29 to Joseph BROUSSARD.
2 CONT       13) Victor, married about 1740 to Marie AUCOIN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages of ancestors of that couple:Over 4 generations1500-1599 = 1 1600-1699 = 12	 Marriages of descendants of that couple:Over 9 generations 1700-1799 = 79 1800-1899 = 113 1900-1999 = 257 2000-2099 = 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes (White); Diocese of Baton Rouge, Catholic Church records; http://www.umoncton.ca/etudeacadiennes/centre/cea.html; Dictionnaire des Acadiens d'Archange Godbout; Micr
2 CONC ofilms Drouin; The Acadian Exiles in Saint Malo, 1758-1785; Histoire et généalogie des Acadiens (Arsenault); PRDH-RAB; Acadian Church Records
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Pierre LeBlanc (1675-1769) was born in Grand Pre.  He married Francoise Landry on February 16, 1711, daughter of Antoine Landry and Anne Marie Thibodeau of Grand Pre. They were expelled to Boston.  They made it back to Acadie. Fra
2 CONC ncoise died on October 3, 1767, and is buried at Saint-Antoine Cemetery, Lavaltrie, Quebec. Pierre died October 22, 1769, and is buried at Hòpital-Général, Montreal.
2 CONT --------------------
