2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Déportée au Massachussetts, décédée a Yamachiche de la variole.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogy=Marguerite_Melancon&pid=840135&lng=en
2 CONT
2 CONT ID No:		840135 Firstname:	Marguerite Name:		Melancon Gender:		F Occupation:	 Born:		1693 about Parish/City:	Port Royal, Acadie Country:		Canada Death:		12 February 1758 - Age: 65 Parish/City:	Québec Country:		Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Information, Other Kids, Notes, etc. :
2 CONT
2 CONT Décédée de la variole (petite vérole) qui a sévi au Québec dans les années 1757 et 1758.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Melanson-127
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT SA White gives her birth based on several censuses as in 1697. PRDH gives 1699 in St-Charles-des-Mines, Grand Pre Acadie. Using 1697 from White and Grand-Pre from PRDH as her older sibling was born there too.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine was born about 1697. She was in Chelmsford, Massachusetts for the 1758 Census at age 61, in 1760 (age 62). She married Jean dit Jane Landry (son of Antoine and Marie Thibodeau) in 1717 (no location available). [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine died at age 70 in Yamachiche[2]. She and her husband died of smallpox which raged in Quebec in the 1757 year and 1758. [sic] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --> She could not be in Massachusetts in 1760 if she had died in 1758. There was an epidemic in Quebec in 1769. This tends to confirm the date of death 30 APR 1769. (OJ)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ White, Stephen A. Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes” 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999. P. 1152
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Drouin Genealogical Institute (needs subscription) Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
