2 CONT The family was deported to Boston. From a list found in the Massachusetts Archives [vol.136, p.517] of the Acadians cared for in Chelmsford, dated October 24th, 1757, we can see this family: "Jean Landrie ... 62 years, Maudlin, hi
2 CONC s wife ... broken arm ..., Joseph Landrie, 26 ... healthy & able to labour Paul Landry his son 22 able to do labour, Charles, ditto, 20 sickly & unable to do labour, Simon 18 able to do labour, Asam 16 able to do labour." Joseph L
