1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **"Acadian Immigrants to Cabanocé/Cabahannocer, 1766" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***In report of Acadians at Oxford, Province of Maryland, Jul 1763
2 CONT ***Cabanocé, La Luisiana census, 1769, age 17
2 CONT ***In Second Company of Acadians, 15 Jan 1770, fusilier
2 CONT ***Ascension, La Luisiana census, 1770, age 17
2 CONT ***Ascension, La Luisiana census, 1777, listed as Joseph Landry called Bel Homme, age 24
2 CONT ***In Judice's Company, Acadian Coast Militia, Aug 1779, called Joseph dit Bellehomme, fusileer
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana in 1766, age 14
2 CONT **Lieutenant of militia, Ascension, 1794
2 CONT **Ad interim commandant of Acadians at Ascension, 1799-1803
2 CONT **Promoted to major of militia & made commander of Ascension militia, 1804
2 CONT **Title changed to justice of the peace, 1805
2 CONT **Elected to territorial legislative council, Sep 1805
2 CONT **Elected to LA State Senate, Jul 1812, from the County of Acadia (now St. James and Ascension Parishes)
2 CONT **Owned New Hope Plantation, Ascension Parish, grew sugar & corn
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
