2 CONT ***At Baie-des-Espagnols, Île Royale, Apr 1752, called Paul Boutin, ploughman, age 25
2 CONT ***In report of Acadians at Province of Pennsylvania, Jul 1763, listed as Paul Boutin
2 CONT ***In report on Acadians who settled at St.-Gabriel, 1767, listed as Pierre Bota & Pablo Botan, age 48[sic]
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1774, called Polle Boutin, no age given
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1777, called Paul, age 52[sic]
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1785, called Paul
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1788, Grand Coteau, called Paul Boutin
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1796, Grand Coteau District, called Paul Boutin
2 CONT ***Succession dated 7 Mar 1832, St. Landry Parish courthouse
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana in 1767, age 40
2 CONT **Moved to Lunenburg/Mirliguèche, colony of Nova Scotia, 1754
2 CONT **Imprisoned George's Island, Halifax, Sep1755
2 CONT **Exiled to Province of North Carolina aboard Providence, Dec 1755, age 28
2 CONT **Moved to Province of Pennsylvania, c1760
2 CONT **Moved to Providence of Maryland, c1764
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1727 Nova Scotia, Canada Death: 	Feb. 25, 1801 St. Landry Parish Louisiana, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul Boutin, born ca. 1727 in Acadie, Nova Scotia. He married Ursale Guidry on 9 Nov 1750 Acadie, Nova Scotia. Father of Marie Marguerite Catherine, Susanne, Paul Jr. Marguerite Louise & Joseph Boutin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Ursule Guidry Boutin (1731 - 1788)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Joseph Boutin (1753 - 1796)*
2 CONT   M. Marguerite Catherine Boutin Savoie (1755 - 1828)*
2 CONT   Paul Boutin (1765 - 1832)*
2 CONT   Marguerite Louise Boutin Leger (1768 - 1834)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Saint Landry Church Cemetery  Opelousas St. Landry Parish Louisiana, USA
