1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography Marie Roy was born probably after 1718 probably in Acadie, to parents Jean Roy and Jeanne Lejeune[1]. Though White says before 1735, her mother died in 1730, and her other siblings were born starting afte
2 CONC r the marriage in 1712 to 1718. So she was probably born after her brother Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Joseph Deneau/Denerro/Denicocourt around 1760. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away about 1804. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources ↑ Karen Theriot Reader Marie Roy citing Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes - Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714 - Stephen A. White - 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick:
2 CONC  Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999 - p. 1427 Mother born around 1691, so likely born before 1735. ↑ francogene Marie Roy ↑ Unsourced family tree handed down to Matthew Denico. SSDI
