2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !INFORMATION: was obtained from the book "The Acadian Exiles in Nantes (1775 - 1785), PAGE 63, PERSON # 116: Paul DUGAST was born about 1711 & married (1) about 1741 to Marguerite Marie BOUDROT who was born in 1718 & died in 1759,
2 CONC  then Paul DUGAST married (2) Helene BLANCHARD about 1760. HelenE BLANCHARD was born about 1717, daughter of Pierre BLANCHARD & Francoiss BRAUD, widow of Alexis AUCION (see family # 4), Helene BLANCHARD died at the age 65 years & 
2 CONC was buried 18 Oct 1782 (Saint Similien of Nantes): ISSUE: Marie Osite DUGAST, of Paul DUGAST & Helene BLANCHARD, his second wife, was born in 1761 at Saint Coulomb; resident of the Parish of Saint Martin of Chanteay since 2 years 
2 CONC & married on 16 Nov 1784 (Saint Martin Chantenay) to Etienne DUPUIS (see family # 122). Paul DUGAST, Helene BLANCHARD, his 2nd wife & family of 7 persons were in the Fourth Convoy leaving Chatellerault for Nantes from 6 March to 1
2 CONC 3 Mar 1776. Paul DUGAST widower, & 2 childern: Simon & Anne were passengers (Family # 62) aboard LA BERGERE, which departed France on 12 May 1785 & arrived in Louisisana on 15 Aug 1785.
2 CONT
