2 CONT {{Acadian Sticker}}Michel was born in 1707 in Acadie, Nouvelle-France ≤ref> Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; p . 207
2 CONC ; Source published by Karen Theriot Reader, RootsWeb.com, Inc. MichelBOUDROT, son of Michel & Cécile LE BLANC. He was witness to the marriage of his sister Francoise (Grand Pré Register) in 1732.≤/ref>He was among those transporte
2 CONC d to Bristol, England, and died between then and the smallpox epidemic of Sep 1756. ≤ref>Title: Dictionnaire gnéalogique des familles acadiennes, "Ajouts et corrections"; Author:Stephen A. White; Publication: University of Moncton
2 CONC , Centre d'études acadiennes; Online; corrections for p. 207: Note: Among those transported to Bristol, England, and died between then and the smallpox epidemic of Sep 1756.
2 CONT Text: Died between Sep 1755 and the end of Sep 1756.≤/ref>
2 CONT Michel married Claire Comeau, daughter of  Jean le jeune Comeau and Catherine Babin about 1742 before the deportations began.
