2 CONT :Anne Marie Boudrot, daughter of Michel and Cecile LeBlanc, was born 5Mar 1709 in Grand-Pre, Acadie and christened the same day.≤ref>Title:Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author:Diocese of Baton Rouge
2 CONC ; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. p. 33: Text: Marie BOUDROT.  (Michel and Cecille Leblanc) bn. 5 March 1709,
2 CONC bt. 5 March 1709 Sponsors: Claude BOUDROT [signed] & Catherine HÉBERT (SGA-1, 9).≤/ref>≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/31?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT :Anne Marie and Abraham Daigle were married 5 Nov 1727 in St Charles aux Mines, Grand Pre, Acadie. ≤ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol.1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999
2 CONC . The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. pp. 28-29 & 53: Text: Anne Marie Boudrot (Michel and Cecille Leblanc) m. 5 Nov 1727 Abraham Daigle (Ber
2 CONC nard Daigle and Marie Bourg) wit. Charle Hebert; Michel Boudrot; Francois Boudrot; Paul Boudrot; Jean Leber (s); sig. Abraham Daigle; Anne Marie Boudrot  (SGA-2, 231). Note: a separate entry for Abraham on p. 53.≤/ref>
2 CONT :According to the request for a dispensation to remarry at Cherbourg by her daughter Marie-Rosalie, Marie (Anne-Marie) died at sea on 16 Dec1758 in the shipwreck of the "Ruby," run aground on the rocks at Pico, in the Azores. She 
2 CONC was being transported by the British during the deportations from Acadia.≤ref> Title: Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes, "Ajouts et corrections"; Author: Stephen A. White;Publication: University of Moncton, Centre 
2 CONC d'études acadiennes; Note: Appeared in Nov 1999 & Sep 2003.;  for p. 207. Note: Cites: M. Godret, "Mariages acadiens à Cherbourg," in RACINES & RAMEAUX FRANCAIS D'ACADIE , no. 26 (2002), p. 12.≤/ref>
2 CONT :[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I3622 Children]# Marguerite DAIGLE b: 5 Jul 1729 in of Grand Pre, Acadie, Nova Scotiac: 12 Aug 1729 in St. Charles aux Mines Ch., Grand Pre, Acadie, Nova Sco
2 CONC tia# Aimable DAIGLE b: 16 Mar 1731 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie, Nova Scotia c: 15 Jun 1731 in St. Charles aux Mines Ch., Grand Pre, Acadie, Nova Scotia# Jean DAIGLE b: ABT 1733 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie, Nova Scotia#
2 CONC  Marie Rosalie DAIGLE b: 9 May 1737 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie, Nova Scotia c: 9 Jun 1737 in St Charles Des Mines,Kings,Acadie,Nova Scotia# Jean Eloi DAIGLE b: ABT 1738 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie, NovaScotia# Francoi
2 CONC s Marie DAIGLE b: ABT 1740 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie,Nova Scotia
2 CONT # Pierre DAIGLE b: ABT 1742 in , Acadie, Nova Scotia# Joseph DAIGLE b: ABT 1747 in L'Assomption, Pisiquit, Acadie, Nova Scotia
2 CONT # Nicolas DAIGLE b: ABT 1750 in Pisiquit, Acadie, Nova Scotia# Marie Madeleine DAIGLE b: 1 Sep 1752 in , of Ile-St. Jean, Acadie, Nova Scotia c: 5 Nov 1752 in St. Pierre du Nord, Ile-St-Jean, Acadie, Nova Scotia
2 CONT
2 CONT She died at sea during the crossing to France.
