2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category:Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography == :Margueritte Boudrot was born 12 Oct 1725 in Grand Pré, Acadia. Her christening was the next day at Grand-Pré. She is the daughter of Michel Boudro and Marie Cecile LeBlanc.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds d
2 CONC e la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 219): http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/219?r=0&s=4≤/ref>≤ref>Ca
2 CONC tholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; Publication: Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of 
2 CONC Iberville, LA.; p. 33: Margueritte Boudrot (Michel Boudrot and Cecille Leblanc) bn. 12 Oct.1725, bt. 13 Oct. 1725 spo. Germain Dupuis and Marie Boudrot (SGA-2, 62).≤/ref>
2 CONT :Marguerite married Antoine DUPUIS about 1746 in Acadia. Marguerite and her family were deported by the British from Acadie to the eastern seaboard of present-day New England, and made their way to Saint Domingue (Haiti) where she
2 CONC  died on 20 October 1764, not long after arrival there. She was buried at Le Mirebalais, Saint Domingue.≤ref>Donald J. Hébert, ''Acadians in Exile'' (Baton Rouge, Louisiana: Claitor's Publishing, reprinted 2010; copyright 1980), p
2 CONC . 41;: BOUDREAUX, Anne m. Antoine DUPUY d. 20 Oct. 1764 at age 30 yr. (Santo Domingo:Mirebalais)≤/ref> Conditions were very hard in the tropical climate of St. Domingue. Antoine was an infant when his mother died. ≤ref>"Dictionnai
2 CONC re Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes"; Stephen A. White; Publication: 2vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999, page 208.≤/ref>   
2 CONT
2 CONT :Children (for research purposes only, please verify)
2 CONT # Jean Baptiste DUPUIS b: Abt 1750 in Acadia
2 CONT # Marie Madeleine DUPUIS b: Abt 1752 in Riviere/Canards, Acadia
2 CONT # Felix DUPUIS b: Abt 1754 in Acadia# Pierre DUPUIS b: Abt 1757 in New England c: 12 Sep 1764 in Mirebalais, St. Domingue, Haiti
2 CONT # Simon Joseph DUPUIS b: Abt 1759 in  Acadia
2 CONT # Pierre DUPUIS# Antoine DUPUIS b: Abt Jun 1764 in New England c: 16 Sep 1764 in Mirebalais, Saint Domingue, Haiti
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
