2 CONT [[Category: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT {{Louisiana Family}}
2 CONT == Biography ==''' Olivier Boudrot''' is on the Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorialin St. Martinville, Louisiana, Plaque 1 Right. Listed with him is a son, Simon.≤ref>''The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial,'' compiledby Jan
2 CONC e G. Bulliard and the Wall of Names Committee (Opelousas, LA: Bodemuller, 2015) p. 12
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT ----'''Olivier Boudrot''', son of Michel and Marie Cecile LeBlanc, was born 20 May 1728 in Grand Pré, Acadia; christened: 20 May 1728, Grand Pré. ≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-
2 CONC Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 256): http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/256?r=0&s=4≤/ref>≤ref>''Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian R
2 CONC ecords,'' 1707-1748 (Baton Rouge, LA: Diocese, 1999) p. 34: Olivier BOUDROT, son of Michel BOUDROT & Cecile LEBLANC. Sponsors: François BOUDROT & Françoise BOUDROT (SGA-2, 84).
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne Marie Dupuis c.1752 in Grand Pré, Acadia.
2 CONT :Children:
2 CONT # Simon Firmin Boudrot (c.1753 in Acadia)≤!--
2 CONT :Title: U.S. federal census [online]{{citation needed}}:Text:  Simon Boudrau, age 57, wife Monique Dupuis, 55, unmarried son Olivier, age 22, and six unnamed slaves.{{citation needed}} This does not say that above≤ref>"United Stat
2 CONC es Census, 1820", database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XHLP-J23 : accessed 31 March 2016), Simon Boudrau, 1820. 
2 CONT ≤/ref>-->
2 CONT He arrived in Louisiana by 1766 and was counted as a widower with his son on the census of 9 April 1766 in Cabahannocer (now St. James Parish), Louisiana. ≤ref name=Cabanocey> Lillian C. Bourgeois, ''Cabanocey'' (New Orleans: Peli
2 CONC can Publishing, 1998) pp. 169, 171.: On the census of 9 Apr 1766, widower Ollivier BOUDRAU is age 29, with son Simon, age 13, no wife, living in household [#82].
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT He married Anne Gaudet on 2 October 1767 in Cabahannocer, Louisiana.≤ref>Bourgeois, Cabanocey, p. 171:On "List of the Acadians Married Since the Establishment of Kabahannossé (Cabahannocer):"
2 CONT Olivier BEAUDROS married on 2 Oct 1767 to Anne GAUDET.
2 CONT ≤/ref> 
2 CONT Three years later the census record reflected his changed situation. The census dated 14 September 1769 in Cabahannocer listed his wife, hisson and step-children.≤ref> Bourgeois, Cabanocey:
2 CONT : Left Bank, Mississippi River
2 CONT :Family #124 Ollivier BOUDREAU, 43;
2 CONT :Anne GAUDET, wife, 44;
2 CONT :Simon, son, 14;
2 CONT :Marie DUPUIS, step-daughter, 17;
2 CONT :Monique [DUPUIS], step-daughter, 14;
2 CONT :Joseph DUPUIS, nephew, 18.
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Olivier Boudreaux was only 52 when he died in Louisiana; he was buriedat the parish of St. James on the Acadian Coast on 1 November 1782.≤ref>''Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Church Records,'' Vol 2, 1770-1803 (BR, LA: Diocese of
2 CONC  Baton Rouge) p. 117  : Olivie [BOUDREAUX], age 52 years, buried on 1 Nov 1782 at St. James Catholic Church, St. James, LA (SJA-1, 63a).
2 CONT ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT
