2 CONT **Drouin Institute (Archived birth and baptismal record - see attached in Media tab)
2 CONT **Drouin Institute (Archived marriage record to Veronique Sire - see attached in Media tab)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean is the son of Rene Hébert and Marie Boudreau. He married (1) Marie-Madeleine Doiron in 1730 in Acadie and they are the parents of the following:1) Catherine (1731-1772) md Victor Boudreau2) Pierre (1732-1759) md Anne Benoit3)
2 CONC  Marie (1734-1788) md Pierre Arcement4) Marguerite-Blanche (1737-1758)5) Anne (1740-) md Pierre Robichaud6) Rosalie-Dite-Rose (1745-) md Pierre-Olivier Pitre7) Ignace (1747-1821) md (a) Anne Dugas and (b) Marguerite Pitre8) Jean-B
2 CONC aptiste (1749-1819) md Anne-Josephe DugasHe married (2) Veronique Cyr on 20 January 1752, in Port-Lajoie, PEI. They are the parents of the following:1) Marguerite-Tarsille (1754-1759)Jean and Veronique were part of the Acadian exp
2 CONC lusion to France. Traveling together were:Jean Hébert, age 52, of l'AcadieVeronique Cyr, age 27 (died)Rosalie, age 14 (eventually married Pierre-Olivier Pitre)Joseph-Ignace, age 12 (eventually married (a) Marguerite Pitre (b) Anne
2 CONC  Dugas)Jean-Baptiste, age 10 (eventually md Anne-Josephe Dugas)Marguerite-Tarsile, age 5 (died)Marguerite-Blanche, age 22 (died)They were on the ship "Supply", which arrived and disembarked at Saint-Malo on 9 March 1759. HEBERT Je
2 CONC an, de l'Acadie, 52 ansSIRE Véronique, 27 ans (died at Saint Servan le 30 avril 1759)HEBERT Rosalie, 14 ans, filleHEBERT Joseph Ignace, 12 ans, filsHEBERT Jean Baptiste, 10 ans, filsHEBERT Marguerite Tarsile, fille (died 10 mai 17
2 CONC 59)HEBERT Marguerite Blanche, fille, died at sea
