1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Les Mines, Acadie]]
2 CONT [[Category:Port-Royal, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography ==Jacques was born about 1677 to father Jacques and Catherine Hebert≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=jacques&n=le+blanc Jacques LeBlanc] citin
2 CONC g Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes: 1715 à 1780780 - Stephen A. White - Moncton, NB: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, draft version - Centre d'Études Acadiennes - Centre d'Études AcadiennesUniversity of Moncton - Centr
2 CONC e d'Études Acadiennes - 1 University of Moncton - p. 529≤/ref>
2 CONT He was listed at the age of 9 in the 1686 census of Port-Royal with his parents and 8 siblings.≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription of the 1686 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancajun/genealogy
2 CONC /1686cens.htm 1686 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the NationalArchives of Canada] “Acadie Recensements
2 CONC  1671 – 1752”, Images 15-60.≤blockquote>Jacques Leblanc, 35, Catherine Hébert, 23, Jean, 12,Marguerite, 11, Jacques, 9, Marie, 6 years old, Anne, 5 years old, Catherine, 3 years old, Pierre, 2 years old, René, 1 month old. 3 rifle
2 CONC s, 6 arpans in plowing, 25 bestes with horns, 30 sheep, 15 pigs. ≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  The census showed that the family owned a large numberof animals, 3 rifles, and 6 arpents of cultivable land.
2 CONT By 1693 Jacques' parents had moved to Les Mines, by then a village just a little smaller than Port Royal.  ≤ref>Tim Hebert; Transcription ofthe 1693 Acadian Census, at Port-Royal, Acadie [http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~acadiancaju
2 CONC n/genealogy/1693cens.htm 1693 Census Transcribed]. The original census can be found at [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c2572/2?r=0&s=1 Acadian Census microfilm C-2572 of the National Archives of Canada] “Acadie 
2 CONC Recensements 1671 – 1752, Images 62-108≤blockquote> Jacques LEBLANC 42, Caterine HEBERT 32, Jean 19, Jacques 17, Marie 15, Antoine 13, Caterine 11, Genevieve 9, Madeleine 7, Francois 5, Pierre 3, Ignace 1; 12 cattle, 6 sheep, 6 pi
2 CONC gs, 11 arpents, 1 gun≤/blockquote>≤/ref>  All of their 11 children were born and ten were still living at home, with Ignace just a toddler.  Jacques was the second oldest child in the busy household at 17 years of age.
2 CONT When he was about 38 years of age, he married Elisabeth Boudrot, age 19,  around 1715 in Acadie≤ref name=DGFA>Karen Theriot Reader [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=jacques&n=le+blan
2 CONC c Jacques LeBlanc] citing Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes - Dictionnaire Généalogique des FamillesAcadiennes, Première Partie 1636-1714 - Stephen A. White - 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadie
2 CONC nnes, 1999 - p. 986 - Jacques married around 1715 to Élisabeth (Isabelle) BOUDROT, daughter of Claude & Anne-Marie THIBODEAU.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques passed away some time between 1719 and 1723.≤ref name=DGFA/>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT See also:* [http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogy=Pierre_Leblanc&pid=908383&lng=en&partID=908384
