2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT François LeBlanc (1688-1761) was born in Grand-Pré, Acadie (Port Royal). On September 19, 1712, he married Marguerite Boudreaux in Grand-Pré.  They had twelve children, including one set of twins, all born in Grand-Pré between 171
2 CONC 4 and 1739.  In 1755 they were exiled to Massachusetts.  The deportation record shows his name plus Marguerite and ten children including his son Charles’ family.  He died while in exile in Needham, Norfolk, Massachusetts, at the 
2 CONC age of 73.
2 CONT --------------------
