2 CONT History of Francois LeBlanc from The LeBlanc Genealogy
2 CONT Francois was 12th child of Jacques, born at The Mines, at the River of the Habitants in 1692. he married at Grand Pre, 19 September 1711 to Marguerite Boudreaux, daughter of Claude Boudreax and Anne Thibodeau. In 1755 he was depor
2 CONC ted to Massachusetts with his 12 c children. He landed at Point Shirley, Winthrop, Mass (caudet, Famlle Acadiennes, p. 105) and from there he asked permission to go to Massachusetts to live with his family. From there he returned 
2 CONC to Dudley in that same locality in 1766. Finally settled at Needham near to Boston where he died in 1770. (Caudet p 130).
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Deported to Massachusetts in 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !INTERIM SOURCE NOTE: This person is part of the generation that came to Acadia from France or was a member of the first few succeeding generations who lived in Acadia in the 1600s and early 1700s.
2 CONT Information on this person is from one or more of the secondary sources listed below. Until I find the time to add the specific source information (volume/page and exact source) this interim note willhave to suffice. The sources a
2 CONC re:
2 CONT Denis Beauregard's Dictionnaire Genealogique de la Ancienne Acadie is located at http://www.francogene.com/dgaa/index.php (explanation in both English and French at viewer's option; dictionnaire in French). His Francogene, an exte
2 CONC nsive list of Acadian genealogical sources and bibliography is located at http://www.francogene.com/acadia/resources.php (in English).
2 CONT Acadian History and Genealogy website (gives brief history of Acadia and some selected Acadian family trees), at http://www.craftconn.com/genealogy/acadianh.htm (in English).
2 CONT Acadian and French Canadian Ancestral Home (a searchable data base of web sites with information on early Acadian families, at http://www.acadian.org/ (in English).
2 CONT Center for Acadian Studies, University of Moncton (New Brunswick), has short genealogies of 37 Acadian families, at http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/55 (in French).
2 CONT See also, Stephen White's Dictionnaire Genealogique des Familles Acadiennes (in French, but available with an English supplement), the best and most recent secondary source for Acadian family information, described and available f
2 CONC or purchase at http://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/38
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''François Leblanc''' was born in Grande-Pre, Acadie about 1688 to [[LeBlanc-70|Jacques LeBlanc]] and [[Hébert-3425|Catherine Hébert]].≤ref name=SW94 /> He married Marguerite Boudrot, daughter of Claude Boudrot an
2 CONC d Anne Marie Thibodeau, in Grand-Pre on 19 September 1712.≤ref>"Catholic Church Records", vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Diocese of Baton Rouge; Diocese, 1999. The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré
2 CONC , carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA.; pp. 18 & p. 90;  :Francois LEBLANC, son of Jacque [sic] & Catherine HEBERT, married on 19 Sep 1712 to Marguerite BOUDROT, daughter of Claude & Anne Marie TIBAUDO, decea
2 CONC sed. Recorded at St. Gabriel church (SGA-1, 12 & 48).≤/ref>≤ref name ="Marriage"/>≤ref name=SW94 /> Together they had 12 children:
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2638|François LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2640|Marie LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2502|Joseph LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2641|Elisabeth LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-517|Charles LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-520|Pierre LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2644|Etienne LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-1928|Amand LeBlanc]]
2 CONT # [[Leblanc-798|Jacques Leblanc]]
2 CONT # [[Leblanc-808|Simon Leblanc]]
2 CONT # [[Leblanc-7624|Marguerite Leblanc]]
2 CONT # [[LeBlanc-2647|Elisabeth LeBlanc]]:During the great deportation of 1755, François, Marguerite and theirfamily were deported to Point Shirley, Massachusetts. François petitioned the Governor of the Massachusetts Bay Colony to be 
2 CONC removed from Point Shirley and moved to Needham, Massachusetts.
2 CONT ≤blockquote>To his Excellency the Governor, the Hon'ble Council and Representatives of the Province of the Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT :François Le Blanc a poor french Inhabitant of Accaday humbly shew That he and his family five of which are men were placed at Port Shirley that they have with great, difficulty supported themselves since the provision allowed by 
2 CONC the Province ceased but now they cannot find work and they have a Winter before them and no prospect of any opportunity of labour during that season and all necessaries of life are excessivedear, there and your Petitioner's family
2 CONC  must perish with hunger and cold. Your Petitioner has relations placed in the town of York and is known to Col. Donnell and Capt.Donnell and has traded with them, and he thinks he could support his family, tho he is 63 years old 
2 CONC with the help of his sons and some little relief from the Publick and as there is but 8 French in that Town he hoped there will be no exception and humbly prays he may be placed there with his family.
2 CONT :FRANCOIS LEBLANC
2 CONT :CHARLES LEBLANC
2 CONT :François died in Needham, Massachusetts in 1761.≤ref name="L.Consentino">Lucie Consentino; acadian-home.org;  [http://www.acadian-home.org/genealogy-daniel-leblanc1.html Descendants of Daniel LeBlanc]:"FRANÇOIS3 LEBLANC (JACQUES2
2 CONC , DANIEL1) was born Abt. 1688 in Les Mines, Acadia, and died 1761 in Massachusetts. He married MARGUERITE BOUDREAU 19 September 1712 in Grand-Pré, Acadia, daughter of CLAUDE BOUDREAU and ANNE-MARIE THIBODEAU. She was born Abt. 169
2 CONC 8 in Les Mines, Acadia-(DBIM), and died 15 May 1767."
2 CONT :Notes by Consentino:
2 CONT :Les Mines Census 1693 5a, Neddham, Massachusetts census 1760.
2 CONT :Marriage: Grand-Pré Register:Date of death is according to an inscription made on his gunpowder holder by his son Jacques - part of the collection at the Acadian Museumat Moncton University, Moncton, New Brunswick.≤/ref>
2 CONT :Marguerite with four sons and a daughter, Simon and Marguerite being still in her household, were repatriated onto Miquelon Island near Newfoundland in 1763. Four years later, she was able to return to Nova Scotia. removed to Mem
2 CONC ramcook, New Brunswick with the families of her sons Charles and François.≤ref name="L.Consentino"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographie ==
2 CONT ≤blockquote>Jacques LeBlanc, né à Port-Royal vers 1651, était le fils aîné deDaniel. Il convola vers 1673 avec Catherine Hébert, fille d'Antoine Hébert et de Geneviève Lefranc, qui lui donna treize enfants, dont '''François''', né
2 CONC  vers 1688. Celui-ci prit pour femme, à Grand-Pré, le 19 septembre 1712, Marguerite Boudrot, fille de Claude Boudrot etd'Anne-Marie Thibodeau.≤ref name ="Marriage"> [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/563?r=0&
2 CONC s=5 Marriage]≤/ref> Lors de la Déportation de 1755, François et Marguerite furent transportés avec leur famille au Massachusetts, où François est décédé en 1761.≤ref name=SW94> Stephen A. White, ''La généalogie des trente-sept fam
2 CONC illes hôtesses des "Retrouvailles 94", Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne,'' vol. 25, nos 2 et 3 (1994). (LeBlanc)  ≤/ref>≤/blockquote>
2 CONT TRANSLATON: 
2 CONT ≤blockquote>Jacques LeBlanc, born in Port-Royal about 1651, was the eldest son of Daniel.  He and Genevieve Lefranc had thirteen children, one of which,'''François''', was born about 1688. The latter took as spouse in Grand-Pre on
2 CONC  the 19th September 1712, Marguerite Boudrot, daughter of Claude Boudrot and Anne-Marie Thibodeau.≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/563?r=0&s=5≤/ref>   During the Deportation of 1755, François and Margue
2 CONC rite were moved with their family to Massachusetts, where François died in 1761.≤ref name=SW94 />--''S. Sturm, translation.''
2 CONT ≤/blockquote>
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT '''See Also:'''*BIRTH-PARENTS-CENSUS-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-DEATH: Stephen A. White, DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; pp. 986 & 1019; #19:
2 CONT *List of children [http://www.acadian-home.org/genealogy-daniel-leblanc1.html acadian-home] and [https://gw.geneanet.org/katheriot?lang=en&pz=frederick+joseph&nz=theriot&ocz=1&p=marguerite&n=boudrot&oc=2 Karen Theriot Reader Famil
2 CONC y Tree-Marguerite Boudrot]* http://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/françois-leblanc_118059032
2 CONT *http://www.peterandsally.com/Docs/DescendantReport.pdf
