1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Source:'''
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/LeBlanc-517 WikiTree]
2 CONT [https://gw.geneanet.org/nicleb33?lang=fr&p=charles&n=le+blanc&oc=4 Geneanet]
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Leblanc (1723-1806) was born in Grand-Pré, Acadie, Nova Scotia Province.  He married Marie Josephine Barrieau in Saint-Charles, Acadie, in 1748.   This was a time of mass upheavals.  Grand-Pré was under siege in 1749. Thei
2 CONC r movements can be traced by the births of their nine children. Pierre, Joseph, and Marie were born in Pisiquit, Acadia, in 1751-1755.  The expulsions began in 1755.  In 1759, the family was exiled to New England. Marguerite, Eliz
2 CONC abeth, and Anne were born in Massachusetts in 1759-1762.  Later in 1762, they were on the island of Miquelon off the coast of Newfoundland where the child Marie died.  Charles and Francoise were born there in 1765 and 1767.  The l
2 CONC ast child, Anastasie, was born in New Brunswick or Nova Scotia about 1769.  Charles (Sr.) died in December 1814 at Memramcook, Acadie.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
