2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Brief history of Charles from LeBlanc Genealogy
2 CONT Charles, fifth child of Francois, born at Grand Pre, the same as all his brothers and sisters. He married Marie Barrillot and with her and all their children he was deported in 1755 to New England where he followed his father from
2 CONC  Point Shirley to Dudley and Needham. About 1763 Charles took refuge at the Island of Miquelon with all his family. Four years afterward, in 1767, Charles and his brothers, Pierre, Jacques and Simon, left Miquelon (Gaudet, pp. 159
2 CONC  and 175) and returned to Nova Scotia where he took the oath of allegiance to the British Crown. A few of them settled near Halifax at Birch's Cove; the others, with Charles, preferred to settle at Windsor at The Mines, near to th
2 CONC eir ancient home. After a few years, they joined a few others from that locality and, together, they went to settle on the left bank of the Memramcook River where Charles died about 1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT He accompanied his mother from Massachusetts to Miquelon in 1763 and then to Nova Scotia in 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Information per: Carroll and Dolores Hamlet 586 Tulip Ct.; Uniondale, NY 11553
2 CONT
