2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}                                                           
2 CONT [[Category: Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT == Biography == :'''Jacques Leblanc''' was born  30 Nov 1732 to [[LeBlanc-1927|François LeBlanc]] and [[Boudrot-61|Marguerite Boudrot]]. ≤ref>Institut Généalogique Drouin: Le Lafrance: Baptêmes 1621-1861≤blockquote>Baptême - 
2 CONT St-Charles-les-Mines - 
2 CONT 1732-11-30 - 
2 CONT Naissance : 1732-11-30 - 
2 CONT '''LEBLANC, JACQUES''', 
2 CONT Sujet - 
2 CONT FRANCOIS, 
2 CONT Père - 
2 CONT BOUDROT, MARGUERITE, Mère≤/blockquote> [https://www.genealogiequebec.com/Membership/LAFRANCE/acte/6147018 Baptism]≤/ref>He was baptized the day he was born at Saint Charles des Mines, Grand-Pré, Acadia. His godparents were PierreB
2 CONC oudrot and Marie Leblanc, his sister.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 322): ht
2 CONC tp://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/322?r=0&s=4≤/ref>
2 CONT :Jacques married Nathalie Breau and had 5 children. He passed away on 1772 in Chezzetcook.
2 CONT :JACQUES LEBLANC, his wife NATHALIE DITE ANASTHASIE BRAULT(Breau), andhis family were exiled to Massachusetts in 1755. In 1767, he was at Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon. JACQUES LEBLANC was the son of FRANCOIS LEBLANC and MARGUERITE BOU
2 CONC DREAU. NATHALIE BRAULT(BREAU) was the daugther ofPIERRE BRAULT and ANNE-FRANCOISE DUPUIS. [http://www.acadian-home.org/leblanc-exiles.html]
2 CONT :Children per Stephen White: ≤ref>[https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/55 37 Families]≤/ref>#Marie, n Stoughton (Mass) 28 juil 1759; m v 1774 Charles MAILLET (Antoine-Salomon & Marie Saulnier); fosse bénite Richibouctou-Villag
2 CONC e 12 avril 1825.  #Simon dit Simon à Nathalie, n Stoughton 26 déc 1760; m v 1783 Marie-Madeleine RICHARD (René & Perpétue Bourgeois).  #Isabelle, n Dorchester (Mass) 20 déc 1762; m v 1780 Jean-Baptiste JOHNSON (Guillaume & MarieJo
2 CONC sèphe Aucoin).  #Marguerite, b Miquelon 25 déc 1763; m v 1790 Raymond-Jean-Baptiste LANDRY (René & Madeleine Boudreau).  #Anne-Marie, b Miquelon 16 juil 1766; m v 1782 Jean-David THIBODEAU (Germain & MadeleineBlanche Préjean).  #A
2 CONC nastasie, n Halifax 30 mai 1768; m v 1785 Jean dit Petit Jean à Jani RICHARD (Jean-Baptiste & Françoise Girouard); d Richibouctou-Village 24 juin 1796.  
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research ==
