2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Exiled in 1755
2 CONT The LeBlanc Genealogy indicates he was exiled in 1755 to New England. He afterwards took refuge at Miquelon from where he went to Chezzetcook near Halifax, where he took the name of White. He settled definitely at St Louis, Kent C
2 CONC ounty, where he died in 1815. He was the father of Olivier LeBlanc, the first Acadian Deputy to the provincial Parliament. Note: It was from that generation that belongedthe LaBlanc Martyrs, found amont the Martyrs of Quimper, exe
2 CONC cuted at Brest, 1 July 1794. They were the widow of Sylvain LeBlanc (Anne LePrince) and her daughter, Anastasie LeBlanc: Anne was born in Acadian in 1721 and her daughter in exile, perhaps in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Simon Le Blanc & Marie Madeleine Comeau - no child Agnes
2 CONT Stephen A. White, lists 8 children belonging to this couple. Marcelline, Marie-Madeleine, Anne (dit Nannon), Bruno, Fabien, Isabelle, Francois, Germain. There is no Agnes Le Blanc. In Agnes' person page she has the same birth/chr.
2 CONC  date as Marcelline.
