2 CONT == Biography ==Marguerite Comeau was born in Acadia in about 1696≤ref name="DGFA-378">White, Stephen A., Patrice Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert. [[Space:Dictionnaire_généalogique_des_familles_acadiennes|''Dictionnaire Généalogique D
2 CONC es Familles Acadiennes.'']] Moncton, N.-B.: Centre D'étudesAcadiennes, Université De Moncton, 1999, Print, p.378.≤/ref>.  She married Jean Baptiste Landry in Grand Pre on 17 October 1718.≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/ooci
2 CONC hm.lac_reel_c1870/594?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref> Diocese of Baton Rouge Catholic Church Records: Acadian Records 1707-1748 (Baton Rouge, LA, Diocese of Baton Rouge, 1999), Personal Collection, Marriage of Marguerite Comeaux (Jean ≤u>Comea
2 CONC ux and Catherine Babin≤/u>) m. ≤u>17 Oct.≤/u> 1718 Jean Baptiste Landry (Claude Landry and Catherine ≤u>Thibodeau≤/u>) wit. Jean Commaux (s); Claude Babyn (s); Pierre Doucet (s); J. Mouton (s); Claude Landry (s); Claude Babin. Not
2 CONC e: part of page 259 is missing, underlined text is from 1895 transcription. (SGA-2, 258-259)."≤/ref>
2 CONT She was expelled to Southampton England where she was in 1763, when the Acadians were sent to St-Malo, France.≤ref name="DGFA-378" /> She was still in St-Malo at the time of the 1772 census there, but died in Nantes, France on 17 
2 CONC May 1779 and was buried at St-Jacques de Nantes eleven days later.≤ref name="DGFA-378" /> 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
