1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Grand-Pré, Acadie]] 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Biography =='''Marguerite Labove Landry''' was born about 1714. She was the adopted daughter of [[Landry-979|Claude Landry]] and [[Doucet-58|Madeleine Doucet]]. When she was about 21, she married Augustin Hebert, age 23, son of
2 CONC  Augustin Hebert and Anne Boudrot 6 Aug 1736 at Saint Charles desMines, Grand-Pré, Acadia. ≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds dela paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) -1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Pa
2 CONC rish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 708): http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/708?r=0&s=4≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustin Hébert, Marguerite et leurs enfants furent déportés au Massachussetts à l'automne de 1755. Au mois de juillet 1760 ils furent placés dans la ville de Watertown, Mass. Augustin et sa famille s'établit à Trois-Rivières en 1
2 CONC 767. 
2 CONT
2 CONT English translation via google translate:Augustin Hébert, Marguerite and children were deported to Massachusetts in the fall of 1755. In the month of July 1760 they were located inthe city of Watertown, Mass. Augustin and his fami
2 CONC ly moved to Trois-Rivières in 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogy=Marguerite_Landry&pid=18767&lng=en
