2 CONT Claire LeBlanc Born about 1700 in Mines, Grand-Pré, Acadie, Nouvelle-France
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of René LeBlanc [uncertain] and Anne Bourgeois
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Jacques LeBlanc, François (Leblanc) LeBlanc, René (Leblanc) LeBlanc, Pierre LeBlanc, Joseph Leblanc, Étienne Leblanc, Claude LeBlanc, Marie Marguerite LeBlanc and Jean Baptiste LeBlanc
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Jean Landry — married about Jan 1717 in Grand-Pré, Acadie, Colony of Nova Scotia [uncertain].
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Marie Landry, Marguerite Landry, Alexis Landry, Angelique Landry, Bonne Landry, Marguerite Landry, Madeleine Landry, Mathurin Landry, Mathurin Landry, Estienne Landry, Osite Rosette Dorotea Landry, Ursule Landry, Anne La
2 CONC ndry, Claire Landry, Osithe Landry and Joseph Dominique Landry
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 1763 in Pennsylvania Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Claire LeBlanc, daughter of Rene LeBlanc and Anne Bourgeois, was born about 1700 in Grand-Pré, Acadie.[1] Claire married Jean Landry in Grand-Pré in January or February 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie LANDRY 1717- Marguerite LANDRY 1720- Alexis LANDRY 1721-1798 Angelique (Bonne) LANDRY 1723-/1754 Marguerite LANDRY 1725- Madeleine LANDRY 1727-1798 Mathurin LANDRY 1729- Mathurin LANDRY 1730-/1761 Etienne LANDRY 1731- Ursule
2 CONC  LANDRY 1733- Anne LANDRY 1737- Claire LANDRY 1739- Osite Dorothee Rose Josette LANDRY 1743-1810 Joseph Dominique LANDRY 1744-1824
2 CONT
2 CONT She was on the 1763 census at PA, a widow. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after the census of 1763.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Stephen A. White, "DICTIONNAIRE GENEALOGIQUE DES FAMILLES ACADIENNES"; 1636-1714; Moncton, New Brunswick, Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, 1999, 2 vols.; pp. 925 & 988. BIRTH-PARENTS-NAME-MARRIAGE-CENSUS: Claire was on
2 CONC  the 1763 census at PA, a widow. Jean LANDRY, (according to P. GAUDET) son of Claude & (Marie-) Catherine THIBODEAU, married (according to P. GALLANT) at Grand Pré in Jan or Feb 1717 to Claire LE BLANC, daughter of René & Anne BOU
2 CONC RGEOIS.
