2 CONT == Biography ==:'''Marguerite Landry''' was born 12 May 1720. She was the daughter of[[Landry-36|Jean Landry]] and [[LeBlanc-68|Claire LeBlanc]]. She was baptized the day after she was born at Saint Charles des Mines, Grand-Pré, A
2 CONC cadia. Her godparents were Rene Babin and Jeanne Hebert.≤ref>Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748748 - Diocese of Baton Rouge - Diocese, 1999, - The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand 
2 CONC Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. - p. 113 :Sponsors: René Babin and Jeanne Hébert (SGA-2, 19).≤/ref>≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pr
2 CONC é, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia : C-1869 (Image 129): http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/129?r=0&s=4≤/ref>≤ref>Marguerite Landry, born 12 May 1720 in St-Charles-les-Mines 
2 CONC Is the daughter of Jean Landry and Claire Leblanc. [https://www.genealogiequebec.com/Membership/LAFRANCE/acte/6146218 Baptism]≤/ref> Another Marguerite was baptised in this family on 28 Feb. 1725. That could mean that this Marguer
2 CONC ite died very young, but a death record hasn't been found for her.
2 CONT == Sources ==
