2 CONT == Biography =='''Madeleine Landry''' was born 3 May 1727. She was the daughter of [[Landry-36|Jean Landry]] and [[LeBlanc-68|Claire LeBlanc]]. She was baptized the following day at Saint Charles des Mines, Grand-Pré, Acadia. Her 
2 CONC godparents were Jacques Leblanc and Marie Madeleine LeBlanc.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada, Fonds de la paroisse catholique Saint-Charles-des-Mines (Grand-Pré, N.-É.) - 1869;  Canadiana, Heritage, Parish registers: Nova Scotia :
2 CONC  C-1869 (Image 242): http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/242?r=0&s=4≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Name ===
2 CONT : Name:  Madeleine /Landry/
2 CONT :: Given Name:  Madeleine:: Surname:  Landry≤ref>Source: [[#S233]]  Page:  Source number: 1063.000; Source type: Electronic Database; Number of Pages: 1; Submitter Code: SMB TMPLT  FIELD  Name:  Page VALUE Source number: 1063.000;
2 CONC  Source type: Electronic Database; Number of Pages: 1; Submitter Code: SMB≤/ref>
2 CONT She married Pierre Arseneau≤ref>Karen Theriot Reader [https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I25331 Pierre] citing FATHER-BIRTH-MARRIAGE-CHILD-RESIDENCES: Placide Gaudet, REPORT CONCERNING CANADIAN ARCHIVES
2 CONC  FOR THE YEAR 1905; 1600-1800; vol. II, part A, original a Sessional Paper no. 18 of the Archives, reprinted Heritage Books, 1994; p. 154; own copy. ≤blockquote> Pierre ARCENAUD, son of Jacques, ploughman, native of l'Acadie, age 
2 CONC 27 years, has been in the country 11 years. Married to Magdelaine LANDRY, native of l'Acadie, age 25, they have a daughter age one year. Land and livestock listed.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
