2 CONT Osite Rosette Dorotea "Rosette Dorotea" Landry aka Broussard, Castille Born 5 May 1733 in Grand-Pre, Acadie, Nouvelle-Francemap ANCESTORS ancestors Daughter of Jean Landry and Claire LeBlanc Sister of Marie Landry, Marguerite Land
2 CONC ry, Alexis Landry, Angelique Landry, Bonne Landry, Marguerite Landry, Madeleine Landry, Mathurin Landry, Mathurin Landry, Estienne Landry, Ursule Landry, Anne Landry, Claire Landry, Osithe Landry and Joseph Dominique Landry Wife o
2 CONC f Jose Rafael Ignacio Bonventura Castille — married 1755 in Baltimore, Marylandmap DESCENDANTS descendants Mother of Joseph Ignace Castille, Marie-Magdeleine Castille and Jean Baptiste Castille Died 16 Oct 1810 in St Martinville, 
2 CONC St Martin, Louisiana, United Statesmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Osite Landry is on the Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial in St. Martinville, Louisiana.[1] Biography "Among the Acadians established by the Spanish government at St. Gabriel, 1767. Extant documents indicate that her 
2 CONC household included her husband, Joseph Castille, and the following children: Pierre, Joseph, Marguerite, and Marie (Marie Marthe). She is mistakenly identified as Rose in the 1767 census of St. Gabriel. Witnessed her son Jean Bapt
2 CONC iste's marriage contract at the Opelousas District, July 16, 1797. (She was illiterate in 1797.) Placed her mark on her son Manuel's marriage contract at the Opelousas District, May 11, 1800."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources ↑ Title: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial; Author: Wall of Names Committee; Jane G. Bulliard, Chair; second edition, 2015; Bodemuller The Printer, USA; Personal copy in possession of Jacqueline Girouard ↑ Title: E
2 CONC nsemble Encore, "Life Lines"; Author: Acadian Memorial Foundation. Database of Acadian Immigrants to Louisiana (Internet Entry for Osite (sometimes Dorothée, Rose Osite) Hebert, Rev. Donald J., Southwest Louisiana Records (1750-19
2 CONC 00), CD-ROM, Rayne LA: Hebert Publications, n.d., “CASTILLE, Marie Magdeleine - veuve de dec. Joseph RICHARD (major daughter of dec. Joseph CASTILLE & Ositte LANDRY) m. 27 June 1807 Francois POITIERS - of Nantes (major son of dec.
2 CONC  Pierre & Agnes BROUSSARD) Wits: Charles POITIERS, Vallery BARA, Hypolite BARA. Fr. Gabriel ISABEY (SM Ch.: v.5, #90)“ Hebert, Rev. Donald J., Southwest Louisiana Records (1750-1900), CD-ROM, Rayne LA: Hebert Publications, n.d., “
2 CONC CASTILLE, Joseph (min. son of Joseph & Hostitte [Osite] LANDRY) m. 29 March 1785 Scholastique BORDA (min. daughter of Antoine & Marguerite MARTIN) Fr. GEFFROTIN (SM Ch.: v.3, #54)”
2 CONT
