2 CONT ==Biography=='''Jean Daigre''' was born about 1698. He was the son of [[Daigre-38|Bernard Daigre]] and [[Bourg-39|Marie Claire Bourg]]. He married Marie Magdeleine Landry, daughter of Claude Landry and the late Catherine Tibodeau 
2 CONC 6 Nov 1721 at Saint Charles des Mines.≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/606?r=0&s=5≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriages===:Marriage 1 Marie Madeleine Marguerite LANDRY  6 Nov 1721 in Grand Pr, Acadia ≤ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese of Baton Rouge; 1999; Note: The Registers of St
2 CONC . Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. Personal Copy; p. 55; Note(KTR): Discrepancy with date in DGFA following citation.:Text: Jean Bapt. DAIGLE, son of Bernard D
2 CONC AIGLE & Marie BOURG, married10 [sic] Nov 1721 Marie Magdeleine LANDRY, daughter of Claude LANDRY & deceased Catherine THIBODOT. Witnesses: Claude LANDRY [signed]; Bernard DAIGRE [signed]; Charle DAIGRE; Pierre DOUCET [signed] (SGA
2 CONC -2, 252).≤/ref>≤ref>Title: Dictionnaire Généalogique des Familles Acadiennes; Author: Stephen A. White; Publication: 2 vols., Moncton, New Brunswick: Centre d'Études Acadiennes, 1999; p.  448. Source published by Karen Theriot Rea
2 CONC der, RootsWeb.com:Text: Jean married 1st (Grand Pré Register) 6 [sic] Nov 1721 to Marie-Madeleine LANDRY, daughter o f Claude & Catherine THIBODEAU.≤/ref>
2 CONT :[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I3545 Children]# Madeleine DAIGRE b: 4 Sep 1722 in Grand Pré, Acadia c: 4 Sep 1722 in Grand Pré, Acadia# Judith DAIGRE b: 2 Nov 1723 in Grand Pré, Acadia c: 
2 CONC 2 Nov 1723 in Grand Pré, Acadia# Marie Rose DAIGRE b: 15 Feb 1725 in Grand Pré, Acadia c: 14 Mar 1725 in Grand Pré, Acadia
2 CONT :Marriage 2 Marie Anne BREAU  3 Feb 1727 in Grand Pré, Acadia≤ref>http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c1870/626?r=0&s=5≤/ref>≤ref>Title: Catholic Church Records, vol. 1a: Acadian Records, 1707-1748; Author: Diocese o
2 CONC f Baton Rouge; 1999; Note: The Registers of St. Charles aux Mines in Acadia, from Grand Pré, carried into exile to St. Gabriel Church of Iberville, LA. Page: pp. 43 & 54-55
2 CONT :Text: (Consanguinity 3rd degree) (SGA-2, 233).≤/ref>
2 CONT :[http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=katheriot&id=I3545 Children]# Francoise DAIGRE b: 1727 in Pisiguit, Acadia c: 4 Jan 1728 in Grand Pré, Acadia
