1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **"Acadian Immigrants to Bayou des Écores, New Feliciana, 1785-86" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***At Rivière-de-l'Ouest, Île St.-Jean, Aug 1752, age 29
2 CONT ***Deported from Île St.-Jean to St.-Malo, France, aboard one of the Five Ships 25 Nov 1758, arrived St.-Malo 23 Jan 1759, listed as Charles Tibodeau, age 35
2 CONT ***Sailed to la Luisiana on ''La Ville d'Archangel'', age 63
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana Dec 1785
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT {{Louisiana Family}}
2 CONT [[Category: Acadian Immigrants to Louisiana]]
2 CONT [[Category: Louisiana First Families]]
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT [[Category: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial]]
2 CONT == Biography ==:Charles Thibodeau is on the Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial in St. Martinville, Louisiana Plaque 12 Left, ''La Ville D'Arcangel''.  Listed with him is his wife Magdelaine Henry and five children: Pierre Charl
2 CONC es, Jeanne Tarsile, Marguerite, Helene and Marie Victoire.≤ref> Title: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial; Author: Wall of NamesCommittee; Jane G. Bulliard, Chair; second edition, 2015; Bodemuller The Printer, USA; Personal
2 CONC  copy in possession of  [[Girouard-4019| Jacqueline Girouard]]; p. 12≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Thibodeau was born  in 1723, in Pisiquit, Acadia, to Philippe Thibodeau and Elizabeth Isabelle Vincent.  He was the 6th of 10 siblings.
2 CONT In 1751, Charles married Madeleine Henry, daughter of Jean Henry and Marie Hebert, at Port Lajoie, Ilse St. Jean, Acadia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *Helene THIBODEAU 1 b: 11 Feb 1752 in , Isle St. Jean, , Acadia c: 27 Feb 1752 in Port Lajoie, Isle St. Jean, , Acadia*Anastasie THIBODEAU b: 30 Aug 1755 in , Isle St. Jean, , Acadia c: 30Aug 1755 in Port Lajoie, Isle St. Jean, , 
2 CONC Acadia*Francois THIBODEAU b: 9 Feb 1760 in La Moisias, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 10 Feb 1760 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France*Marguerite Josephe THIBODEAU b: 25 Apr 1762 in la Moisias, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 25 Apr
2 CONC  1762 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France*Pierre Charles THIBODEAU b: 2 Jul 1764 in la Moisias, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 3 Jul 1764 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France*Jeanne Tarsille Anne THIBODEAU b: 2 Jul 1764 in la
2 CONC  Moisias, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 3 Jul 1764 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France*Helene THIBODEAU b: 1 Nov 1766 in St. Antoine, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 2 Nov 1766 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France*Marie Victoir
2 CONC e THIBODEAU b: 23 Apr 1769 in St. Antoine, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 24 Apr 1769 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France
2 CONT In 1758, they were exiled to France as part of the expulsion of the Acadians.  Charles, Madeleine and their 2 young daughters, Helene and Anastasie were on one of the "five ships".  The two daughters both died at sea during the vo
2 CONC yage.  On 23 jan 1759, Charles and Madeleine disembarked at St. Malo alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 6 more children while in France
2 CONT In 1785, they traveled aboard "La Ville d'Archangel" to New Orleans. ≤ref> The 7 Ships Passenger Lists (Note: also has scans of actual ship manifests); Published by Acadian-Cajun Genealogy & History; Internet; [http://www.acadian-
2 CONC cajun.com/7ships.htm Seven Spanish Ships]≤/ref>On the Spanish debarkation list he is listed as Carlos TIBODEAU, and received 1 each of knife, large knife ; 2 of axe, hoe; 4 shovels.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles died in Louisiana, location unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==Notes: Immigration: 3 Dec 1785 New Orleans, Orleans, LA 1 Note: !BIRTH-MARRIAGE: Arsenault, H&G, p. 1499.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT
2 CONT *Bona Arsenault, 
2 CONT *:HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS; 162 5-1810; 
2 CONT *:Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, 6 vols.; 
2 CONT *:p. 1437 (Pisiguit); own copy. *:Charles dit Charlie THIBODEAU, born 1723, son of Philippe & E'lizabeth VINCENT, married at Port-Lajoie on 1 Feb 1751 to Madeleine HENRY, daughter of Jean & Marie HÉBERT; two daughter listed. Charl
2 CONC es was at Port-Lajoie, Isle St. Jean, in 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Janet Jehn, 
