2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT == Biography ==:'''NOTICE''': this profile is protected by the [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Project:Acadians Acadian Project] because of frequent duplicatio and variant name spellings. Please contact the Acadian Project before m
2 CONC aking any substantive changes. Thanks for helping make WikiTree the best site for accurate information.
2 CONT Germain was born around 1734.  He married Madeleine-Blanche Préjean, daughter of Jean-Baptiste Préjean and Marie Gaudet.  They  were amongthe Acadians who were deported in 1755 and were still in exile in Massachusetts when some of
2 CONC  their children were born.  After the Treaty ofParis of 1763, Germain Thibodeau returned to Acadia. Having lost his wife, he married a second time around 1767 with Marie Babineau, daughter of Jean Babineau and Isabelle Breau, and 
2 CONC widow of Charles Maillet. ≤ref name=White94>Stephen A. White, “La généalogie des trente-septfamilles hôtesses des ‘Retrouvailles ‘94’” in ‘’Les Cahiers de la Société historique acadienne,’’ vol. 25, nos 2 et 3 (1994) THIBODEAU, p.
2 CONC  1,  [https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/node/55  37Families] ≤/ref>≤ref name=Frenchmen>White, Stephen A. “The Company of Frenchmen in the County of Cumberland, Province of Nova Scotia.” accessed at [http://stephenwhite.acadian-ho
2 CONC me.org/american-revolution.html acadian-home.org] hosted by Lucie LeBlanc Consentino ≤/ref>  
2 CONT He died  in 1809. Burial (3 Jan 1809)  Saint Thomas RC Church, Memramcook, Westmorland, New Brunswick, CAN≤ref name=burial>Memramcook, Nouveau-Brunswick, Régistre de la paroisse St-Thomas, catholique, Sépultures, 1806-1870, ( F.M.
2 CONC  9, A 11, volume 8), p. 660, Image  992 [http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_reel_c3018/992?r=0&s=1 entry forGermin Tibodau] Burial 3 January 1809, digital images, Héritage, Genealogy collection, Library and Archives Cana
2 CONC da, reel C-3018, Parish Registers: New Brunswick : C-3018, accessed 12 November 2019≤/ref>≤ref> "Family Tree," database, ≤i>FamilySearch≤/i> (http://familysearch.org : modified 11 June 2017, 01:16), entry for Germain à Jean Thibod
2 CONC eau(PID https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:L8PY-P8Z); contributed by various users.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biographie==
2 CONT Germain est né vers 1734. Il se maria en premières noces à Madeleine-Blanche Préjean, fille de Jean-Baptiste Préjean et de Marie Gaudet.   En 1755 ils ont été déportés au Massachusetts où plusieurs deleurs enfants sont nés. Après 
2 CONC le traité de Paris de 1763, ils revinrent  en Acadie. Ayant perdu sa femme, il convola en secondes noces vers 1767 avec Marie Babineau, fille de Jean Babineau et d'Isabelle Breau, et veuve de Charles Maillet. Germain Thibodeau est
2 CONC  décédé dans la paroisse de Memramcook le 2 janv 1809.  ≤ref name=White94/> ≤ref name=Frenchmen/> ≤ref name=burial/>
2 CONT
2 CONT
