2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT :Anne Thibodeau, born about 1721 in the parish of Ste. Famille of Pisiguit in Acadie, daughter of [[Thibeaudeau-17|Philippe]] & [[Vincent-414|Elizabeth Vincent]], widow of [[Pitre-2057|Charles Pitre]].≤ref> White, Stephen A. Patri
2 CONC ce Gallant, and Hector-J Hébert, ''Dictionnaire généalogique des familles acadiennes'' (Moncton, N.-B.: Centre d'études acadiennes, Université de Moncton, 1999) p. 1322≤/ref> She married 2nd on 7 Aug 1759 at Pleurtuit, Ille-et-Vil
2 CONC aine [France] to [[Henry-6|Pierre Henry]], son of Jean & Marie Hébert. They had three children. They lived at Pleurtuit from 1759-1772. ≤ref>Title: Acadians in Exile in Saint Malo 1758-1785; Author: Albert J. Robichaux; Publicatio
2 CONC n: Hebert Publications, Eunice, Louisiana 1981; Vol 2; Personal Copy; p. 501
2 CONT :Text: Family #560≤/ref>
2 CONT :According to the list of persons who died crossing to France in 1758 {http://froux.pagesperso-orange.fr/St_malo_arrivees/Tamerlan.htm], family #188 Anne Tibodeau, widow of Charles Pitre, age 38 had the following children: 
2 CONT #Marie Marthe Pitre age 12, died in hospital 24 April 1759 
2 CONT #Jean Baptiste Pitre age 8, died at sea 
2 CONT #Josephe Pitre age 5, died at sea 
2 CONT #Ozite Pitre age 9, died at sea 
2 CONT #Anne Pitre age 6, died at sea 
2 CONT
2 CONT ::Also with her was Charles Pitre's nephew, Olivier Pitre. 
2 CONT ::Only Anne and Olivier survived.
2 CONT :After Charles Pitre's death, Anne married Pierre Louis Henry 7 Aug 1759 in Pleurtuit, ancient province of Bretagne (present-day département of Ille-et-Vilaine).≤ref> Thot, Archives en ligne, Ille-et-Vilaine, Registres paroissiaux
2 CONC  et état civil, 10 NUM 35228 103, Pleurtuit, 1759, Baptêmes/Mariages, COMMUNE, p. 14/23 [http://archives-en-ligne.ille-et-vilaine.fr/thot_internet/FrmLotDocFrame.asp?idlot=121343&idfic=0345252&ref=0345276&appliCindoc=THOPWREG&resX
2 CONC =1280&resY=800&init=1&visionneuseHTML5=0 Marriage Pierre Henry & Anne Thibeaudau 7 August 1759]≤blockquote>Marriage between Pierre Henry, son of deceased Jean and widower of Magdeleine Pitre, from the parish of St-Pierre and St-Pa
2 CONC ul of Cobeqit, diocese of Quebec and resident of Pleurtuit and of Marie Hébert, and Anne Thibeaudau, daughter of Philipe and Elisabeth Vincent, and widow of Charles Pitre, from the parish of Sainte-Famille of Pesiguit, diocese of 
2 CONC Quebec, Canada and living in this parish. Special dispensation granted for 4th degree filiation. Witnesses: Jean Henry, Charles Thibeaudau, Simon Henry, Charles Henry.≤/blockquote>≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :Children# Marie Helene HENRY b: 14 May 1760 in la Moissias, Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 14 May 1760 in Pleurtuit, , Ille-et-Vilaine, France# Francoise HENRY b: 2 Nov 1761 in Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 2 Nov 1761 in Pleurtuit, Ille
2 CONC -et-Vilaine, France# Angelique HENRY b: 15 May 1763 in La Moysias, Ille-et-Vilaine, France c: 15 May 1763 in Pleurtuit, Ille-et-Vilaine, France
2 CONT
