1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Source:'''
2 CONT [https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Beriault_Marguerite&pid=445315 Nosorigines]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Acadia, we farmed the lowlands using the methods of our homeland, from the coast of France. In 1755 we were forced out of our homes and land and driven away. My husband and I landed in Boston with our four children. Life w
2 CONC as difficult because we were Catholic. There was great animosity at this time against foreigners; the Acadians were not well received. One of my sons went to Louisiana and became part of the Cajun society. We wandered until we ret
2 CONC urned to Canada, to Québec. We joined other expatriate Acadians. A good study would be to see which of our descendants returned to Québec. Married  1745 in Grandpre, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Grand-Pré, Acadie]]
2 CONT {{Acadian}} [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT :Marguerite is the daughter of Nicolas Barrieau and an unknown mother.She married Alexis Breau, son of  Francois Breau and Marie Comeau, in1746, location not given, but in Acadie.<ref> White Stephen A., Dictionnaire Généalogique d
2 CONC es Familles Acadiennes (Moncton NB: Centre d'Etudes Acadiennes, Universite de Moncton, 1999), page 279.
2 CONT :note: location of marriage not given.</ref> :Marguerite and Alexis were exiled to Massachusetts in 1755. They wereliving back in Canada by 1805, where she passed away 17 Dec 1805. <ref>Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ET GENEALOGIE DES A
2 CONC CADIENS; 1625-1810; Ottawa, Editions Lemeac, 1978, 6 vols.; p. 1128 (Grand Pré); Source citedby Karen Theriot Reader, Rootsweb.com. :Alexis BREAUX, born 1721, son of Francois & Marie COMEAU, married around 1745 to Marguerite BARIO
2 CONC T [no parents given]; eight children. He lived at the River aux Canards; deported to Massachusetts, he was at St. Philippe of Laprairie [Canada] in 1767. He was buried at L'Acadie on18 Jul 1811. His son Firmin settled in Louisiana
2 CONC .</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT : Birth:  About 1726-1730 : L'Acadie : Quebec, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT : Death:  Dec. 17, 1805 : L'Acadie : Quebec, Canada :  : Burial: about 17 Dec 1805 : Sainte-Marguerite L'Acadie Cemetery : L'Acadie : Monteregie Region : Quebec, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born'''  1730L'Acadie, Quebec, Canada. <ref>Source: [[#S45]]  Certainty: 0</ref><ref>Source: [[#S46]]  Certainty: 0</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died'''  17 DEC 1805.  Lacadie, Quebec, Canada. Age: 74-75. <ref>Source: [[#S45]]  Certainty: 0</ref><ref>Source: [[#S46]]  Certainty: 0</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Buried''' L'Acadie, Monteregie Region, Quebec, Canada. <ref>Source: [[#S46]]  Certainty: 0</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage''' Husband @I227@.  Wife @I226@.  Child: @I280@.  Child: @I282@.  Child: @I289@.  Child: @I287@.  Child: @I286@.  Child: @I284@.  Child: @I217@.  Child: @I288@.  Child: @I283@.  Child: @I281@.  Child: @I285@.  Marriage
2 CONC  1745Grande Pre, Kings, Nova Scotia, Canada. <ref>Source: [[#S47]]  Certainty: 0</ref> Marriage Acadie, Nova Scotia, Canada.  Marriage 1750 Pisiquit, Acadia, Nova Scotia, Canada. 
