2 CONT '''Jean Baptiste Cormier''' was born 2 Mar 1734. He was the son of [[Cormier-77|Pierre Cormier]] and [[Thibodeau-22|Cecile Thibodeau]]. He was baptized 5 Apr 1734 at Beaubassin. His godparents were Pierre Tibaudaut and Hermine Cor
2 CONC mier.≤ref>Library and Archives Canada Fonds des Archives départementales de la Charente-Maritime [La Rochelle, France] : C-1207 Registres de Beaubassin - reel_c1207 MG 6 A 2 (Image 46) http://heritage.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.lac_
2 CONC reel_c1207/46?r=0&s=6≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternatively: Jean-Baptiste Cormier was born the 2nd of March 1733≤ref name="Cormier">White, Stephen A. ''La généalogie des trente-sept familles hôtesses des "Retrouvailles 94"'' [https://www.umoncton.ca/umcm-ceaac/files/umcm-cea
2 CONC ac/wf/wf/pdf/37fam-cormier.pdf Cormier], Les Cahiers, La Socité Historique Acadienne, Vol. 25, #2-3, 1994; Université de Moncton, p. 1 .:: Jean-Baptiste CORMIER, son of Pierre & Cécile THIBODEAU, born at Beaubassin on 2 Mar 1733, 
2 CONC married at Kamouraska 5 Jul 1762 to MadeleineLANDRY, daughter of Alexis & Marguerite AUCOIN. He died at St-Basile on 14 Feb 1822.≤/ref>≤ref name="Leger">Leger, Yvon, Beloved Acadia of my Ancestors (Translated by Antoine Bugeaud), 
2 CONC Montreal: Fleuve, 1992, Family 152, Pg 316.≤/ref> in Beaubassin, Acadia to parents Pierre Cormier and Cécile Thibodeau. 
2 CONT He married Madeleine Landry the 5th of July 1762≤ref name="Cormier" />≤ref name="Leger" />≤ref>Quebec, Canada, Vital and Church Records (Drouin Collection), 1621-1968 [https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/1091/d13p_31171065/150036
2 CONC 27?backurl=https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/12463865/person/190090261050/facts/citation/680292979906/edit/record]≤/ref> in Kamouraska, Quebec, Canada. 
2 CONT
