2 CONT
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]] [[Category: Louisiana First Families]] [[Category: Acadian Immigrants to Louisiana]] [[Category: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial]] [[Category: Louisiana Acadian Coast Settlers]]
2 CONT {{Louisiana Family}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==:Joseph Cormier is on the Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial in St.Martinville, Louisiana Plaque 2 Right. Listed with him is Marguerite Saulnier, his wife; their three daughters Susanne, Marie Louise & Felicite and
2 CONC  his brother Michel Cormier.<ref> Title: The Wall of Names at the Acadian Memorial; Author: Wall of Names Committee; Jane G. Bulliard, Chair; second edition, 2015; Bodemuller The Printer, USA; Personal copy in possession of  [[Gir
2 CONC ouard-4019|Girouard-4019]]. p. 15.</ref>
2 CONT ----:'''5th Generation- From Ouescoque Heights (Amherst Point Nova Scotia Canada) to Prison, and Louisiana, USA''' :'''1740:''' Joseph Cormier is born, the fifth child of Pierre Cormierand Cecile Thibodeau.<ref name="SW">{{SW94}}<
2 CONC /ref>   His family has afarm nearby on the Ouescoque Heights (Amherst Point, Nova Scotia, Canada). By the time he is 10 years old, the world he knows will be shattered and he will lose or become separated by all but one of his fam
2 CONC ily members.     :'''1750-55:''' 10 year old Joseph and his family are refugees from their burnt-out home and move across the French-English boundary to Le Lac (Aulac NB)<ref>Surette, Paul. Atlas of the Acadian Settlement of the B
2 CONC eaubassin 1660 to 1755. Tintamarre and Le Lac.  Tantramar Heritage Trust. 2005</ref>. His father dies within the year.<ref>Acadian Census1750, 1752, 1755 Accessed at Acadian and French Canadian Ancestral Home http://www.acadian-ho
2 CONC me.org/frames.html</ref><ref>Surette, Paul. Atlas of the Acadian Settlement of the Beaubassin 1660 to 1755. Tintamarre and Le Lac.  Tantramar Heritage Trust. 2005</ref>   :'''1755:''' Some of the Cormier brothers are taken prisone
2 CONC rs at Jolicoeur (Jolicure New Brunswick) and are able to escape and rejoin their mother and siblings<ref>White, Stephen. “Pierre Cormier”. In Dictionary of Canadian Biography Online.  Accessed July 2011 at: http://www.biographi.ca
2 CONC /009004-119.01-.php?BioId=36465&PHPSESSID=73cd94f0sto8ap6bp2uml5u6l6</ref>. :Joseph and his brother Michel and a younger first cousin, Jean-Baptiste become separated from the rest of the family.   :According to Steven Cormier<ref>
2 CONC Cormier, Steven. Acadians in Grey. Accessed July 2011 at http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-CORMIER.htm .</ref>: ''"They either fell into British hands during the family's wanderings from Chignecto to Québec and back, 
2 CONC or they became separated early and joined the Acadian resistance in the Petitcoudiac area led by Joseph Broussard dit Beausoleil.  Joseph and Michel's mother was a Thibodeau, the family into which the Broussard dit Beausoleil brot
2 CONC hers had married.  Jean-Baptiste Cormier, fils's mother was a Richard, another family close to the Broussard clan.  So the Cormier boys may have been part of the Broussards' large, extended family.  Joseph,Michel, and Jean-Baptist
2 CONC e, fils surrendered to the British probably in the early 1760s when the Broussards surrendered.  And, like hundredsof other captured Acadians, they spent the next few years in a Halifax prison waiting for the war to end."''  :Afte
2 CONC r the war, Joseph and Michel sail to Opelousas Louisiana and prosper as cattlemen<ref>Cormier, Steven. Acadians in Grey. Accessed July 2011 at http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-CORMIER.htm .</ref>.   :Around '''1759:'
2 CONC '' Joseph marries Marguerite Saulnier, daughter of Jacques Saulnier and Anne Hebert and widow of Michel Brun and Victor Comeau.<ref name="SW"/>      :'''1771:''' Joseph marries Anne Michel, daughter of Jacques Michel and Jeanne Br
2 CONC eau. The nuptials takes place on April 25 at Pointe-Coupee,Louisiana, USA. .<ref name="SW"/>     
2 CONT
2 CONT :Joseph served under Galvez during the American Revolution. :'''1795:''' Joseph died on August 5 at the age of 55 in Opelousas, Spanish Louisiana.<ref name="SW"/>     
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <references />
2 CONT * Hebert, Rev. Donald J., Southwest Louisiana Records (1750-1900), CD-ROM, Rayne LA: Hebert Publications, n.d., “CORMIER, Joseph  de l'Acadie, now of Opelousas (Pierre C., widr. of  Marguerite SAUNIER  & Cecile THIBAUDEAU)  m. 25 
2 CONC April  1771 Anne MICHEL, of Acadie, wid. of Victor COMMAUT of  Attakapa (Jacques & Jeanne BREAUD) Wits: Jean BERARD, J.  GAIGNARD, GREVEMBER, MERCIER.  Fr. IRENEE (SM Ch.:  v.1, p.20)“
2 CONT * MARRIAGES-BURIAL: Donald J. Hebert, SOUTHWEST LOUISIANA RECORDS; 1750-1800; vol. 1-A, rev. ed., Rayne, LA, Hebert Publications, 1996; p. 207; own copy; contains church and civil records. ::Joseph CORMIER of l'Acadie, now of Opel
2 CONC ousas, son of Pierre C., widower of Marguerite SAUNIER & Cecile THIBAUDEAU, married on 25 Apr 1771 to Anne MICHEL of Acadie, widow of Victor COMMAUT of Attakapa [sic], daughter of Jacques & Jeanne BREAUD. Witnesses: Jean BERARD; J
2 CONC . GAIGNARD; GREVEMBER; MERCIER. Recorded by Fr. IRENEE at St. Martin of Tours Catholic Church, St. Martinville, LA (SM Ch.: v.1, p.20). ::Also: Joseph CORMIER buried 6 Aug 1795 at St. Landry Catholic Church, Opelousas, LA (Opel.Ch
2 CONC .: v.1, p.25).
2 CONT * BIRTH-NAME-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN-RESIDENCES: Bona Arsenault, HISTOIRE ETGENEALOGIE DES ACADIENS, vols. 1-6; 1630-1775; Quebec, Le Conseil de la Vie Francaise en Amerique, 1965; p. 920-921; ::Born 1742, with his brother Michel was de
2 CONC ported to South Carolina, and settled in Louisiana. ::Also on p. 2464 (Louisiana), Joseph CORMIER, born 1742, son of Pierre & Cécile THIBODEAUX of Beaubassin, Acadia, married 1st around 1760 to Marguerite SAUNIER; three daughters.
2 CONC  He married Anne MICHEL, daughter of Jacques & Jeanne BREAUX and widow of Victor COMEAUX; three children. He died at Opelousas, LA in 1795.
2 CONT
