1 NAME Zacharie Amable /Doiron/
2 GIVN Zacharie Amable
2 SURN Doiron
2 _MARNM Doiron
2 NICK Aimable
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1744
2 PLAC Asomption De Pisiguit
2 ADDR
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 APR 1816
2 ADDR
3 CITY Caraquet
3 STAE NB
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Zacharie, orphaned at age 13, was raised by his uncle, Honore Doiron.  His residence at this time in unknown.  It is believed he migrated with fishermen friends to the Baie des Chaleurs.  He married in Caraquet, N.
2 CONC B. and settled on a land grant east of Isabelle Stream in 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three years later he sold 300 acres of the original 500 grant of the Pointe de Roche to the brothers Francois and Jean-Baptiste Legere.  He was also owner of a small island near Pokesudie named Ile a Zacharie.  It was later named 
2 CONC Ile des Doiron which was given to his sons Hilaire and Isaac.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE:  This information taken from Les Familles de Caraquet by Fidele Theriault.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
2 CONT @R-1247644566@  Ancestry Family Trees  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members. 
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Ancestry Family Tree  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=69230950&pid=291 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Acadian}}
2 CONT [[Category: Great Upheaval]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT : Birth:  
2 CONT :: Date:  1744
2 CONT :: Place:  Assomption De Pisiguit, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT Death
2 CONT :: Date:  28 APR 1816
2 CONT :: Place:  Caraquet, New Brunswick, Canada
2 CONT Zacharie is the pioneer of the family in Caraquet.  He was the owner of a small island located close to Pokesudie called the Island of Zacharie, later named the Island of Doiron which was divided between his sons, Hilaire and Isaa
2 CONC c.  In this day it is also called the island of Pokesudie.
2 CONT :CENSUS: Placide Gaudet, REPORT CONCERNING CANADIAN ARCHIVES FOR THE YEAR 1905; 1600-1800; vol. II, part A, original a Sessional Paper no. 18 of the Archives, reprinted Heritage Books, 1994; p. 27.≤ref>REPORT CONCERNING CANADIAN A
2 CONC RCHIVES FOR THE YEAR 1905; 1600-1800; vol. II, part A, original a Sessional Paper no. 18 of the Archives, Printed by Order of Parliament, Ottawa, Canada, S. E. Dawson, Printer to the King's most excellent Majesty 1906; digitized a
2 CONC nd available online; personal copy downloaded [https://archive.org/details/reportconcerning01publ here].≤/ref>
2 CONT :Marriage 1 Marie Anne VICAIRE b: 4 Mar 1752 in Pabos, Quebec, Canada c: 9 Apr 1752 in Pabos, Quebec, Canada:Married: Abt 1770 in Caraquet, Gloucester, New Brunswick, Canada ≤ref>Title: Programme de recherche en démographie histor
2 CONC ique; Note: Individual information.
2 CONT Repository:Internet
2 CONT :Text: They were married before 31 Dec 1776 (place unknown).≤/ref>
2 CONT In 1784 the governor of Nouvelle-Ecosse, known as l’Acadie, gave 14150 acres of land to the first inhabitants, 34 families of Caraquet of which Zacharie Doiron was one of those families.*
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Les descendants de Zacharie Doiron et Anne LeVicaire by Odette Hache.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dictionnaire Biographique du Nord- Est du Nouveau - Brunswick 
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT
2 CONT *Caraquet village au Soleil by J Antonin Friolet, p. 31.
2 CONT *Recueil de souvenirs par Monique Thériault Leger page 40
