2 CONT **"The BROUSSARD dit Beausoleil Party to the Attakapas District, 1765" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***Deported to Province of South Carolina aboard HMS Syren 13 Oct 1755, age 27, arrived Charles Town 27 Nov 1755 in chains, with his father
2 CONT ***Escaped from workhouse at Charles Town, Feb1756, age 28, with his father & made his way across country, perhaps via Québec, to present-day southeastern NB, where he served with his father & uncle in the Acadian resistance
2 CONT ***On list of Acadian prisoners at Halifax, Aug 1763, called Victor Brousare
2 CONT ***Signed DAUTERIVE agreement in New Orleans, 4 Apr 1765
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1766, Bayou Queue[sic] de Tortue, listed as Victor Broussard
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana in Feb 1765, age 37
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Gregoire Broussard was born in 1728 in Port Royal, Acadia. Victor and his wife Isabelle LeBlanc were among the first Acadians to arrive in Louisiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
