2 CONT **"The First Nominal Census (1769) of Colonial Settlers in Southwest Louisiana"; compiled by Donald Joseph Arceneaux; Provincial Press, Claitor's Publishing Division, Baton Rouge, Louisiana; www.ProvincialPress.us & www.Claitors.c
2 CONC om.
2 CONT **"The BROUSSARD dit Beausoleil Party to the Attakapas District, 1765" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***Exiled to Province of Massachusetts 1755, age 11, with grandfather Jean Semer & uncle Amand Semer?
2 CONT ***Moved to Colony of Nova Scotia, 1763, age 18?
2 CONT ***On list of Acadians who exchanged card money in New Orleans, Apr 1765, called Jean SEMÈRE
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1766, Bayou Queue[sic] de Tortue, listed as Juan Baptista, no surname given
2 CONT ***Exchanged letters with his father in France, including a letter sent to his father at Le Havre from New Orleans, dated 20 Apr 1766, a copy of which survived in the French naval archives
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1769, listed as Jean B Semer, age 25
2 CONT ***Took oath of allegiance to Spanish monarch 9 Dec 1769 & made his mark, called Jean Baptiste Semer
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1771, listed as Jean Seymer, age 23[sic]
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1774, listed as J. Bte. Semer
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1777, age 34
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1781, listed as Baptiste
2 CONT ***Attakapas, La Luisiana census, 1785, listed as Semer
2 CONT ***On Attakapas militia list, Aug 1789, called Juan Batista Semer
2 CONT ***Succession dated Nov 1809, St. Martin Parish courthouse
2 CONT ***Succession land sale dated 4 May 1840, St. Martin Parish courthouse
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana in Feb 1765, age 21
2 CONT **Depicted in Dafford Mural, Acadian Memorial, St. Martinville, embracing his father [actually his uncle] soon after the latter reached Attakapas
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Article by Jean-François Mouhot, "Une ultime revenante ? Lettre de Jean-Baptiste Semer," in ACADIENSIS, vol. 34, no. 2 (spring 2005), pp. 124-129. Text of copy of the long letter Jean-Baptiste sent to his father Germain SEMER in H
2 CONC avre, France, from New Orleans dated 20 Apr 1766. Jean-Baptiste was on his way to the Attakapas. He states he arrived in New Orleans in Feb 1765 with 202 other Acadians led by Joseph Brossard [sic]. 
