1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LEBLANC, Alexis (Come & Isabelle BROUSSARD - of Acadia) b. 6 Jan. 1797, bt. 9 April 1797 Pats: Simon LEBLANC & Marguerite GUILLEBAUT - of Acadia; Mats: Thomas BROUSSARD & Anne BOURGEOIS - of Acadia; Spons: Isidore 
2 CONC ROUSSARD & Eugenie LOUVIERE. Fr. Michel Bernard BARRIERE (SM Ch.: v.4, #845)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Fausse Pointe, LEBLANC, Alexis - native of this parish (major son of dec. Come LEBLANC - inhabitant at La fausse pointe & Isabelle BOUSSARD) m. 7 Feb. 1820 Marie LANDRY - native of this parish (minor daughter of Hubert - inhabita
2 CONC nt at la fausse pointe & Anne Euphrosine LEGROS) Wits: Joseph Fortune PENNE, Louis DUSOUCBET, Agricole LEBLANC, Emile USSILLON, Hubert LANDRY. Fr. abriel ISABEY (SM Ch.: v.6, 173)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexis married Marie Sidonise, Sidonie, or Edonise, daughter of fellow Acadian Hubert Landry of Fausse Pointe, at the St. Martinville church, St. Martin Parish, in February 1820.  They settled at Fausse Pointe and in St. Mary Pari
2 CONC sh.  Their son, name unrecorded, died at his parents' home at age 1 month in December 1820, Alexis, fils was born in April 1823 but died at age 2 in April 1825, and Désiré was born in November 1833.  They also had sons named Aurel
2 CONC ien, Joseph, and Hubert.  Their daughters married into the Hébert, Landry, LeBlanc, Legnon, and Louvière families.  Alexis's succession record was filed at the Franklin courthouse, St. Mary Parish, in July 1846; he would have been
2 CONC  49 years old that year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Désiré married cousin Donatille, Adonatile, or Adonathilde, daughter of fellow Acadian Pierre Landry, at the New Iberia church, then in St. Martin but now in Iberia Parish, in February 1854.  Their son Désiré Nises was born near N
2 CONC ew Iberia in December 1854, Martinus in July 1856, and Pierre near Patoutville, now Lydia, in December 1868.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aurelien married Aurelia or Auresia Stevens, Stevin, or Stivens at the Charenton church, St. Mary Parish, in September 1858.  Their son Louis Stevens was born near New Iberia, then in St. Martin but now in Iberia Parish, in March 
2 CONC 1860, Paule in June 1861, and Pierre near Charenton in March 1869. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married cousin Julie Félicie or Félicite, daughter of French Creole Jules Pellerin, at the New Iberia church, then in St. Martin but now in Iberia Parish, in February 1860; Julie's mother, also, was a Landry.  Their son Ale
2 CONC xis le jeune was born near New Iberia in March 1861, Joseph Olidon in July 1862, Calix in November 1866, and Paul near Patoutville, now Lydia, in April 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hubert married cousin Élizabeth, daughter of fellow Acadian Gédéon Landry, at the New Iberia church, then in St. Martin but now in Iberia Parish, in December 1860.  Their son Duprélom was born near New Iberia in May 1864, and Jean
2 CONC  Armogène in March 1866 but may have died at age 2 1/2 in August 1868.
2 CONT
2 CONT !SOUR: http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-LEBLANC.htm
