2 CONT **"Acadians Aboard English ship Britannia, 1769" - http://www.acadiansingray.com
2 CONT ***In report on Acadians at Port Tobacco, Province of Maryland, Jul 1763, listed as Jean Benoist
2 CONT ***Departed Port Tobacco, Province of Maryland, 5 Jan 1769, aboard English schooner Britannia
2 CONT ***Lost in the Gulf of Mexico & held by Spanish at La Bahia, Spanish Texas
2 CONT ***Arrived Natchitoches Post, la Luisiana, 24 Oct 1769, overland from Spanish Texas, age 15[sic]
2 CONT ***Settled below Bayou Plaquemine, St.-Gabriel District, la Luisiana with other Acadian exiles from the Britannia, Apr 1770
2 CONT ***St.-Gabriel, La Luisiana census, 1777, unnamed, age 18
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1785, unnamed
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1788, Plaquemines Brûlé, called Jn. Cho.
2 CONT ***Opelousas, La Luisiana census, 1796, Bellevue District, listed as Jean
2 CONT ***Moved to Attakapas District, settled at La Petite-Anse, now Avery Island, Iberia Parish, & Grand Bois
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes:'''
2 CONT **Arrived in current day Louisiana on 24 Oct 1769, age 10
2 CONT ----
