2 CONT __________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT August Brasseux native of this Parish and son of Joseph Brasseux, deceased, and Theodore GAUTRAU married October 4, 1825 to Susanne PRIMAU native of this Parish. Susanne was the minor daughter of Francoise PRIMAU and Justine BAUDO
2 CONC IN. Witnesses were Ambroise TOUCHET, Joseph BRASSEUR and Francois CORNER (Comeaux?) Father Laurent Peyretti
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-BRASSEAUX.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Auguste or Augustin BRASSEAUX (1800-1862; Mathieu dit La Citardy, Cosme, Pierre)
2 CONT
2 CONT Auguste or Augustin, second son of Joseph Brasseaux and Théodose Gautreaux, born at St.-Gabriel on the river in August 1800, followed his older brother and a sister to the western prairies and married Susanne, daughter of French C
2 CONC anadian François Primeaux and Justine Baudoin, at the Vermilionville church, Lafayette Parish, in October 1825.  They moved south to the Abbeville area of Vermilion Parish by the 1840s.  Their daughter married into the Desormeaux 
2 CONC family.  In October 1850, the federal census taker in Vermilion Parish counted 6 slaves--2 males and 4 females, all black, ranging in age from 30 to 5--on Auguste Brasseux's farm in Ward Two of the parish's western district.  Augu
2 CONC ste died near Abbeville in November 1862, age 62.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Oldest son Aladin, born in Lafayette Parish in May 1828, married Belzire, daughter of fellow Acadian Don Louis Broussard and Madeleine Benoit of Lafayette Parish, at the Abbeville church, Vermilion Parish, in March 1856. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Joachim, baptized at the Vermilionville church, Lafayette Parish, age 8 months, in June 1830, married fellow Acadian Aurelia Broussard.  Their son Gustave le jeune was born near Abbeville, Vermilion Parish, in March 1856.  They al
2 CONC so had an older son named Benjamin.  Their daughter married into the Nunez family.  Joachim died by July 1867, when he was listed as deceased in a daughter's marriage record. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin married Azéma or Alzena, daughter of French Creole Philemon Dubois and Sylvanie Thibodeaux, at the Abbeville church, Vermilion Parish, in November 1867.  Their son Armance Joseph was born near Abbeville in January 1869. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Adrien, baptized at the Vermilionville church, Lafayette Parish, age 7 months, in December 1839, married fellow Acadian Azéma Trahan at the Abbeville church, Vermilion Parish, in February 1858.  Their son Cléopha was born near Abb
2 CONC eville in February 1859, Osea in April 1861, and Auguste in May 1866.  Adrien may have remarried to Isabelle François and settled near New Iberia, on lower Bayou Teche, in the late 1860s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph le jeune, born near Abbeville, Vermilion Parish, in September 1845, married French Creole Marie Sylvanie, called Sylvanie, Langlinais at the Abbeville church, Vermilion Parish, between April and September 1864. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Youngest son Gustave, born near Abbeville, Vermilion Parish, in January 1851, married Émilie, daughter of fellow Acadian Pierre Thibodeaux and Celanie Boudreaux, at the Abbeville church, Vermilion Parish, in April 1870.  
