0 @N6000000003087568674@ NOTE Sources:
1 CONT Genealogical Dictionary of Early Acadia,
1 CONT http://www.cam.org/~beaur/dgaa/index.html(Denis Beauregard).
1 CONT Acadian-Cajun mailing list:
1 CONT Lucie LeBlanc Consentino, (LucieMC@aol.com), http://www.geocities.com/Heartland/Pointe/6106.
1 CONT Melba Gaultier, (mgaultier@eatel.net).
1 CONT Whitney Dartez, (wdartez@juno.com). (says Martin's DOB 1647)
1 CONT Carol Thibodeux, (Cajuncolen@aol.com):
1 CONT Bona Arsenault, Histoire et Genealogie des Acadiens.
1 CONT Don Boudreaux, Lafayette, LA, (donboudreaux@earthlink.net)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Arsenault says Martin's DOB 1647.
1 CONT Also refers to 3 more children, dates are questionable:
1 CONT Augustin, b. March 13 1682/83, Grand Pre.
1 CONT Cecile, b. 1686, Grand Pre.
1 CONT Francoise, b. 1688, Grand Pre, Married abt. 1720 to Jean Baptiste Bourg, b. 1683, Cobequid.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT From Lucie LeBlanc Consentino, (LucieMC@aol.com),
1 CONT written by MGR Louis Richard Cahier "C" pp 34, 35:
1 CONT
1 CONT The Aucoin family goes back to the first census of Acadia... however, it is
1 CONT necessary to go down to the one of 1686 to find a male ancestor of this family
1 CONT in the person of Martin married to Marie Gaudet who at this census accounted
1 CONT for 8 children: 4 sons 4 daughters.
1 CONT
1 CONT Martin Aucoin was among the first settlers of Mines (La Grand-Pré tranlated means "The great meadow") and it is here that his descendants settled as well.. so much so that within the acadian sense they formed "a whole village" tha
1 CONC t bore their name of Aucoin.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1755, there were 18 Aucoin in Mines, 2 at Memramcook and 1 at Chipoudy. The Aucoin of the Trois-Rivières area desend from this last one whose name was
1 CONT Jean-Baptiste married to Marie-Anne Saulnier.
1 CONT
1 CONT Other spellings for the name Aucoin:  Coing - Aucoing and Aucouin
1 CONT
1 CONT The first ancestor's name in France was spelled AUCOUIN.
