0 @N6000000003087562664@ NOTE Sources:
1 CONT http://www.erols.com/someday/Blanchard.html (Steve & Natalie Fleming).
1 CONT Bona Arsenault, Histoire et Genealogie des Acadiens, Vol 2, Port Royal, p. 431.
1 CONT Genealogical Dictionary of Early Acadia,
1 CONT http://www.cam.org/~beaur/dgaa/index.html(Denis Beauregard).
1 CONT Acadian-Cajun Mailing List:
1 CONT Don Boudreaux, Lafayette, LA, (donboudreaux@earthlink.net)
1 CONT Christine Thomas,(ct9965@gte.net).
1 CONT
1 CONT Also referred to as: Marie Anne Blanchard
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Taken from: "The New Brunswick Magazine",  Vol. I, number 4 , published by W.K.Reynolds, St. John, NB, - "Our First Families", written by James Hannay., his "Second Paper", 1898.
1 CONT ---------------------------------------
1 CONT "First on the list of names in the census of 1671, if we take them alphabetically; is Aucoin, and this without a doubt is one of the oldest in Acadia.  There was no male head of a family of that name when the census was taken, Fra
1 CONC ncois Aucoin having been dead a year or two, leaving a widow 26 years old and five children, two sons and three daughters.  The widow Aucoin probably understated her age, for  her oldest child was 12, and if she was only 26 in 167
1 CONC 1, this child must have been born when she was only 14.  She, I think, was Ann Blanchard, a daughter 
1 CONT of Jean Blanchard, another of the ancient inhabitants of the country...
