0 @N6000000003087545273@ NOTE Anselme Aucoin was the son of Pierre Aucoin and Félicité LeBlanc. He was born (in captivity) in England just before his parents were brought to France. On his return to Acadia, he was married at P.E.I. in 1787 to Rose Chiasson, da
1 CONC ughter of Paul. At Chéticamp he owned a boat fit for the open seas, and the account books of the Robins in 1788 indicate that he was a relatively important business man. Anselme had a family of at least 10 children, six boys and f
1 CONC our girls.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: "CHÉTICAMP - IT'S PIONEERS", by Jean-Doris LeBlanc, Published by:
1 CONT La Société St. Pierre, January 1983
0 @N6000000003087545320@ NOTE Marie Doucet, widow.
