0 @N6000000002316428551@ NOTE He was a Lieutenant in DeClouet's Regiment in the War of 1812.  Henry was
1 CONT adopted by General Schyler from New York during the Revolutionary War,
1 CONT educated in Scotland.  He came to Louisiana in 1794 and married twice.
1 CONT His second wife was Bridget Belander.  He became a doctor, plantation
1 CONT owner and slave owner.  He became a trader, State Senator for three terms
1 CONT and president of the Senate for 2 terms and is listed as the 4th Governor
1 CONT of Louisiana when he replaced Governor Thomas B. Livingston.  His sons
1 CONT from his 1st wife and his widow had numerous court fights over his estate
1 CONT which the entire fortune ($185,000) was lost to taxes.
0 @N6000000003087559978@ NOTE Source:
1 CONT http://www.erols.com/someday/Richard.html (Steve & Natalie Fleming):
1 CONT Janet Jehn, Acadian Descendants, Vol I.
1 CONT St. James Parish Records Civil Extracts 1782-1787, p. 1.
